        { id = 94201, name = "Pristine White Sand", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Morell's Castle [zone=757]\n**Who:**\n- Alisia Sandweaver [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 90\n**Maximum Level:** | 90\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Faction\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Dream Delvers +?\n**Factions Lowered:**\n**Quest Items:**\n- Pristine White Sand [item=94201]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a sandman [npc=36594]\n- a sandman timekeeper [npc=36600]\n- an enraged sandman [npc=36595]\n**Era:** | !House of Thule\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Fri Dec 10 04:09:28 2010\nModified: Sun Jan 26 23:04:03 2025 | | _This is a solo kill task that begins with Alisia Sandweaver in Morell's Castle. She's located at the zone-in._\nYou say, 'Hail, Alisia Sandweaver'\nAlisia Sandweaver says 'Dreamer, you've come [too far]. I advise you turn back.'\nYou say, 'Too far?'\nAlisia Sandweaver says 'You've touched the edge of dreams themselves. The [mysteries] of the mind are better not left unraveled.'\nYou say, 'What mysteries?'\nAlisia Sandweaver says 'Why does one dream far differently than another? Why can some remember their dreams in the waking world, and some believe they do not dream at all? Why are hopes and dreams so closely matched? They are better unanswered than to be stumbled upon in the [grains] of sand ahead.'\nYou say, 'Grains?'\nAlisia Sandweaver says 'You are very persistent. Sand is part of the life of all things, from how it is created to how we interact with it. Hundreds, thousands, millions of years ago, it may have made up a being, or a large rock, and finely sifted to such miniscule granules over time. Then such can be transformed by man to sculptures, to glass, or within that glass, even more sand to display the passing of time. Sand is comforting, sand is how many beings are born of Norrath, and how we all [rest].'\nYou say, 'It helps us rest?'\nAlisia Sandweaver says 'You're unaware of that mystery of sand? With your insistence on remaining and inquiring about these mysteries, then I shall send you on a [quest] of knowledge if you wish.'\nYou say, 'Send me on a quest...'\nAlisia Sandweaver says 'The sandmen hold your answer, but they will not give it up easily. Fight them for it, then bring it here, and I shall explain some more on the significance of it.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Bring Me a Dream'.\n\n---\n\nKill the sandmen and search for what they hold 0/7 (Morell's Castle)\nLoot Pristine White Sand from the fallen sandmen 0/5 (Morell's Castle)\n_There are three sandman spawns in the zone-in area, east of the marionette room. There are many more in the sand castle._\n_To get to the sand castle, you have to go through to the northeast part of the forest and into the shellscale area, up and to the second level of the water maze and use the whirlpool to port to the ship. Then from atop the ship, click the ship's wheel to port to the beach area._\n_Note: These are not pre-lootable._\nBring the sand back to Alisia Sandweaver for more information 0/5 (Morell's Castle)\nAlisia Sandweaver muses over the samples you've given her, her lips twitching into a curl as she brings a small portion of the sand above your head, sprinkling it over you. 'With luck, you will remember this as a dream now. Sleep, and dream, so that the mysteries remain mysteries.'\n_Task rewards:_\nExperience (about 1 AA worth)\nMinor Faction with Dream Delvers",
    },
