      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Bixie Warfront [zone=941]\n**Who:**\n- Naturalist Yrelia [ _Heroic Adventures_]\nRating:\n0/2**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(Average from 2 ratings)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 75\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Adventure\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 03:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Bixie Knock-Out Gas [item=113737]\n- Spider Venom Sample [item=114105]\n- Stolen Supplies [item=114104]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Bixie Warfront: They've Gone Too Far This Time [zone=956]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Cassyndra, Challenger of Fear [npc=45134]\n- Curtis Fig [npc=44973]\n- Fear Scavenger Anse the Lucky [npc=45135]\n- Giliferd the Spider [npc=44974]\n- Grelia, Ender of Fear [npc=45136]\n- Oreginald the Tableflipper [npc=45137]\n- Spider muncher [npc=44975]\n- Tleroth, Mistress of the Web [npc=44084]\n- a bixie eater [npc=44943]\n- a careful watcher [npc=44944]\n- a corpse swarmer [npc=44945]\n- a desperate cleaver [npc=44946]\n- a desperate dissuader [npc=44947]\n- a desperate medic [npc=44948]\n- a dying hunter [npc=44949]\n- a fleeing spider hunter [npc=44950]\n- a flesh eater [npc=45015]\n- a frightened bixie [npc=44951]\n- a hastily built barricade [npc=44952]\n- a hole filler [npc=45472]\n- a home wrecker [npc=44953]\n- a mole driver [npc=45474]\n- a mole poker [npc=45475]\n- a nervous digger [npc=45473]\n- a pack spiderling [npc=44954]\n- a provoked sleeper [npc=44955]\n- a shadow lurker [npc=45476]\n- a spider wrestler [npc=44956]\n- a spider youngling [npc=44957]\n- a stalwart defender [npc=44958]\n- a sticky spider [npc=44959]\n- a stirred up tunneler [npc=44960]\n- a trapped hunter [npc=44961]\n- a triumphant spider [npc=44962]\n- a venomous swarmer [npc=44963]\n- a voice mimic [npc=44964]\n- a wild crawler [npc=44965]\n- a youngling guardian [npc=44966]\n- an agile thief [npc=44967]\n- an arachnid harrower [npc=44968]\n- an emboldened snatcher [npc=44969]\n- an enraged killer [npc=44970]\n- an infested bixie [npc=44971]\n- an infester [npc=45016]\n- an outraged trapper [npc=44972]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Daily Task: Heroic Adventures [quest=7988]\n- Yrelia #1: The Great Hunt [quest=7266]\n- Yrelia #3: They're Everywhere! [quest=7268]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Oct 8 06:03:20 2013\nModified: Fri Dec 13 10:01:26 2024 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n**About Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Heroic adventures in Call of the Forsaken scale in level: As low as **Level 75** and up to current maximum level.\n\\- Scale is based on the highest level player **present in the zone** and affects difficulty, loot quality, and mob levels.\n\\- There is some variation/randomization in the task steps you'll be assigned as you progress through the task.\n\\- Time of completion will vary by your group's makeup (anywhere from 30-90+ minutes).\n\\- Collection items appear as ground spawns midway through tasks (you'll see an emote indicating their appearance).\n\\- Named mobs (or their PHs) spawn midway through tasks (usually, but always, at the same time collection items appear).\n\\- These tasks have individual **3-hour lockout timers** (timer gained upon completion).\n**Experience in Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Mobs in these instances grant some experience, but the bulk of experience is **earned upon task completion**.\n\\- As of a patch in November 2014, less difficult tasks were tuned to reward less experience and more difficult ones were tuned to reward more.\n\\- For an added experience bonus, check out **Guard Hamarn's \"Daily Tasks\"** [quest=7988].\n\n---\n\n_This is a heroic adventure (1-6 players) that begins with Naturalist Yrelia ( **map image**) in the Bixie Warfront. She is located at about -790, -2120, 50 (up the ramp just east of the portal to the Ethernere Tainted West Karana)._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Level 75\n\\- Completed \"The Great Hunt\" (heroic adventure)\n\n---\n\n**TASK SUMMARY**\n\\- Say \"embark on an adventure\" to get the task and \"ready\" to zone in.\n**Step #1:**\n\\- Speak with a fleeing spider hunter 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- \"run\" updates the task\n**Step #2:**\n\\- Rescue frightened bixies 0/5\n\\-\\-\\- Clear the spiders and killer bixies around the \"a frightened bixie\" mobs\n\\- Help stalwart defenders kill aggressors 0/5\n\\-\\-\\- Kill the hostile mobs around the frightened bixies, and hail the stalwart defenders for updates\n\\- Kill enraged bixies 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update (\"an enraged \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\" bixies).\n**Step #3:**\n\\- Destroy tunnel walls 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- Kill the makeshift barricades that lead to the spider nest (some of these may spawn ambush adds)\n\\- Activate spider traps 0/7\n\\-\\-\\- Click on the traps (they look like little trampolines); note you can get 1-4 adds upon each click\n\\- Kill triumphant spiders 0/8\n\\-\\-\\- Simple kill updates\n**Step #4:**\n\\- Save, then knock out spider wrestlers 0/4\n\\-\\-\\- Clear the spiders around each \"a spider wrestler\", then click the gas on the wrestler\n\\- Give antivenin to dying hunters 0/4\n\\-\\-\\- Kill venomous swarmers (aggro-linked 10 at a time; weak mobs), loot their venom, click it to turn it into antivenin, which you turn in to dying hunter NPCs\n\\- Kill digging moles 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- Simple kill update\n**\\- At this point in the task, collectibles spawn in the zone (ground spawns) and a named (or its PH) has a chance to spawn.**\n**Step #5:**\n\\- Scare spiderlings into their dens 0/30\n\\-\\-\\- Kill 10x \"a youngling guardian\" (each aggro-linked with three spiderlings) to update the task\n\\- Gather stolen supplies 0/10\n\\-\\-\\- Kill sticky spiders and agile thieves on the ramps and in the rooms, and loot supplies from their corpses\n\\- Kill infested bixies 0/10\n\\-\\-\\- These spawn \"an infester\" at 50% (normal trash mob) or 4x \"a flesh eater\" (lower difficulty)\n\\- Take back stolen supplies 0/10\n\\-\\-\\- In an odd turn of events, you stumbled across a large pile of goods missing from the Bixie neighborhood. The sticky spiders seem to be stealing them, both intentionally and without realizing it. Kill the nearby spiders and secure any supplies they have taken.\n**Step #6:**\n\\- Kill Curtis Fig, the bixie avenger, and his mole 0/2\n\\-\\-\\- Kill the two nameds at the top of the spider nest (aggro-linked)\n\\- Kill the enraged adventurers 0/4\n\\-\\-\\- Kill the four NPCs at the top of the nest (splittable)\n\\- As soon as the objective for Step #6 is done, the task completes.\n\n---\n\n**NAMED MOBS**\n_\"Tleroth, Mistress of the Web\" (or its PH) has a chance to spawn after the fourth step is completed. Known loot from this named:_\nLevel 100\nBixie Summoner's Stone\nHelm of Latent Ether\nMistress's Web\nTleroth's Ring\nLevel 95\n???\nLevel 90\nDaelai's Dandy Brush\nLevel 85\n???\nLevel 80\n???\nLevel 75\n???\n\n---\n\n**TASK IN DETAIL**\n========================================================================\nTRIGGERING THE TASK\n========================================================================\nYou say, 'Let's embark on an adventure...'\nNaturalist Yrelia says 'Excellent. There's an urgent matter that suits you perfectly. Let me know when you're [ready] to confront it.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'They've Gone Too Far This Time'.\nA group of paticularly bloodthirsty bixies have broken off from the hive to hunt deadly spiders that have nested nearby. Their aggression has caused the spiders to strike out against nearby bixie homes. Help save the town and push your way into the next to subdue the spider threat.\nYou say, 'Ready!'\nNaturalist Yrelia says 'May cool winds carry you and soft ground catch you. Fight well, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Bixie Warfront.\n========================================================================\nSTEP #1\n========================================================================\nSpeak with a fleeing spider hunter 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Something bad must've happened in the spider hunters' camp east of this community. The bixie spider hunters are fleeing through the town, being chased by giant spiders. Stop one of them and find out what's going on. You may need to wait a few moments for them to make it through the town safely.\n_If You Get This Step: When you zone in, you'll see spiders and bixies already fighting each other. You can leave them alone for now and hail one of the \"a fleeing spider hunter\" mobs that path down the ramp to the zone-in area._\nYou say, 'Hail, a fleeing spider hunter'\na fleeing spider hunter stops long enough to grab your shoulders and shake you vigorously while shouting, '[Run], little \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_! Run for your life!'\nYou say, 'Why run?'\na fleeing spider hunter says 'The spiders were too much for us. We tried to stop them, but we--' The hunter looks over its shoulder and starts screaming again as it runs off.'\n========================================================================\nSTEP #2\n========================================================================\nRescue frightened bixies 0/5 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The nearby bixie neighborhood has descended into chaos in the wake of the spider attacks. Some of the most vulnerable have been cornered by spiders. Kill the spiders cornering any frightened bixies to save them.\n_If You Get This Step: Head east from the zone-in, where you'll find multiple \"a frightened bixie\" (both outside and inside homes) with spiders and enraged killers around them. All of the mobs must be killed to \"rescue\" the bixies. Note that the corpse swarmers have less hitpoints and hit for less (~2,500) than the others. The larger spiders and the bixie killers hit for a max ~13,000 and have regular hitpoints (all mobs stunnable, mezzable, splittable). Hail the frightened bixie to rescue it._\nYou say, 'Hail, a frightened bixie'\na frightened bixie peaks through its fingers and asks, genuinely confused, 'I'm alive?'\n==========================\nAssist the defenders 0/5 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill the hostile mobs around the frightened bixies (of which there are many), and hail the stalwart defenders for updates._\n==========================\nKill enraged bixies 0/6 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill the hostile \"an enraged \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\" bixie mobs around the residential area._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #3\n========================================================================\nDestroy tunnel walls 0/6 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The spider hunters seem to have constructed quick-fix barricades in the tunnel to the spider nest. You hear screams for help coming from inside. Break down the walls.\n_If You Get This Step: Head east from the residential area and into the tunnel that leads to the spider nest. There, destroy the barricades that have been put in place. When a barricade is destroyed, you are AE'd (3-second stun + minor damage) and one of three things happens: Nothing spawns, 1x \"a voice mimic spawns (hits for a max ~7,500), or 4x \"a shadow lurker\" spawn (hit for a max ~2,500 each)._\na voice mimic calls in a perfect female high elf voice, 'Oh help me, help me! Please!'\n==========================\nActivate spider traps 0/7 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Click on the spider traps (they look like little trampolines). Note that after each click, you can get either 1x \"a careful watcher\" (standard trash mob) or 4x \"an outraged trapper\" (weaker variety)._\n==========================\nKill triumphant spiders 0/8 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: This is a simple kill update._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #4\n========================================================================\nSave, then knock out spider wrestlers 0/4 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Once you got inside the spider nest, it became apparent the bixies aren't trying to stop the violence. Some of the most muscular bixies you've ever seen are inside the nest, wrestling spiders in order to make them more angry and violent. Dispatch them before they incite more violence. You can use the Bixie Knock-Out Gas, but you'll want to kill the spiders they're wrestling first, so the spiders don't eat them.\n_If You Get This Step: You receive \"Bixie Knock-Out Gas\" in your inventory. Around the floor of the central spider nest area will be several bixie wrestlers and spiders. Kill the spiders around each bixie, and then use the gas on the bixie._\n==========================\nGive antivenin to dying hunters 0/4 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill venomous swarmers (aggro-linked 10 at a time; weak mobs). These drop \"Spider Venom Sample\" that, when clicked, results in \"Small Dose Antivenin\" which you can then turn in to one of the \"a dying hunter\" NPCs around the nesting area._\n==========================\nKill digging moles 0/6 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: This is a simple kill update._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #5\n========================================================================\nScare spiderlings into their dens 0/30 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ There are a lot of small spiders being grown in the nest, making it hard to traverse safely. Most of them are protected by a larger spider. If you kill the large youngling guardians, the hatchlings should run back to their den, where they won't hassle you.\n_If You Get This Step: Note: At this step in the task, collection ground spawns become available and a named has a chance to spawn. Pull and kill the \"a youngling guardian\" spiders (hit for a max ~16,000; AE rampage) on and around the ramps. Each guardian is aggro-linked (cannot be split) with 3x \"a spider youngling\" (hit for a max ~1,000; AE rampage). All mobs here are mezzable and stunnable. When you kill a guardian, the younglings flee._\n==========================\nGather stolen supplies 0/10 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill spiders (\"an agile thief\" and \"a sticky spider\") on the ramps and in the rooms, and loot supplies from their corpses (it's not a guaranteed drop, so you may need to kill more than 10 mobs)._\n==========================\nKill infested bixies 0/10 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Around the spider nest area, you'll find infested bixies. Attack these, and at 50%, you'll get one of two spawns: 1x \"an infester\" (normal trash mob) or 4x \"a flesh eater\" (lower hitpoints; hits for less)._\n==========================\nTake back stolen supplies 0/10\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You get This Step: In an odd turn of events, you stumbled across a large pile of goods missing from the Bixie neighborhood. The sticky spiders seem to be stealing them, both intentionally and without realizing it. Kill the nearby spiders and secure any supplies they have taken._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #6\n========================================================================\nKill Curtis Fig, the bixie avenger, and his mole 0/2 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ At the top of the spider nest, you discovered a mighty bixie warrior who's gone mad with bloodlust as he attempts to slay everything in sight to avenge his fallen comrades. You'll have to put him down.\n_If You Get This Step: In the cave at the top of the spider nest are two mobs: Curtis Fig, a bixie, and \"Spider muncher\", a mole. These two mobs are aggro-linked, so you'll have to fight them both at once. They are mezzable and stunnable, but not rootable/snareable. The mole hits for a max ~13,000 and has an average amount of hitpoints (no special abilities reported). Curtis Fig hits for a max ~15,500; casts short-term melee/spell mitigation buffs; and warps onto random targets on his hate list. Kill them both to complete the task._\nCurtis Fig says 'Have you come to kill me? We could've hunted spiders together. But, alas, you share their bloodthirst.'\nCurtis Fig has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nSpider muncher has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nSpider muncher's corpse says 'Well, at least we totally stomped those bixies.'\n==========================\nKill the Enraged Adventurers 0/4 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill the four NPCs at the top of the nest (splittable). They are \"Cassyndra, Challanger of Fear\"; \"Fear Scavenger Anse the Lucky\"; \"Grelia, Ender of Fear\"; and \"Oreginald the Tableflipper\"._\n\n---\n\n**TASK REWARDS**\n\\- a varying amount of platinum\n\\- a varying amount of experience\n\\- a varying number of Marks of Valor (currency used to buy group gear)\n- Daelai's Dandy Brush [item=94553]\n- Helm of Latent Ether [item=113264]\n- Mark of Valor [item=113459]\n- Mistress's Web [item=114054]\n- Tleroth's Ring [item=113213]",
    },
