      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- The Hero's Forge [zone=1328]\n**Who:**\n- Elmara Emberclaw - The Hero's Forge [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 110\n**Maximum Level:** | 130\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n**Quest Items:**\n- Phoenix Feather Quill [item=148131]\n- Piece of Orchidium [item=148129]\n- Pyreberries [item=148130]\n- Shard of Illumiaz [item=146513]\n- Sliver of Glitterine [item=148428]\n- Transfrogifying Hoops [item=148399]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a phoenix fledgling [npc=59115]\n- a reborn berserker [npc=59117]\n- a reborn warrior [npc=59118]\n- a reborn wizard [npc=59119]\n- a rekindled phoenix [npc=59120]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Partisan of The Hero's Forge (15 Points) [quest=12662]\n**Era:** | !Laurion's Song\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Fri Nov 3 02:37:43 2023\nModified: Mon Aug 17 02:10:39 2026 | | **Laurion's Song Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\nYou can obtain this solo task from Elmara Emberclaw [npc=59617] in Hero's Forge. You can find Elmara at /waypoint +541, -1296, +328, near the Laurion Inn door. She is on the find tool as well CTRL-F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Elmara Emberclaw'\nElmara Emberclaw says, 'Ah! It's the Dark Elf I've heard so much about. I didn't believe it when I heard there are newcomers at Laurion Inn. It's been centuries since anyone joined us. I was reluctant to let you enter my domain, but you've proven to be a friend to my allies. Welcome to the Hero's Forge, Renana. It's nice to finally meet you, although I suspect you've already met me. A [version] of me, at least.'\nYou say, 'I have seen a version of you in others' memories.'\nElmara Emberclaw says, 'The residents of Laurion Inn love to revel in past memories, so you are sure to see former versions of us all. I, however, am not so fond of reliving the past. I'd much rather anchor myself in the present and in my duties at the [Hero's Forge].'\nYou say, 'What is the Hero's Forge?'\nElmara Emberclaw says, 'The Hero's Forge is my passion and purpose. I believe anyone can be a hero, but not everyone has the tools to do so. I design armor, weapons, and other tools to help empower those people. There is one design I've made more than any other -- maybe you've come across it in your travels. I heard that it's been dubbed '[defiant gear]' outside of my realm.'\nYou say, 'I've seen defiant gear.'\nElmara Emberclaw says, 'That makes my heart soar. My forgebound workers craft it, then my phoenixes [deliver] it to Norrath and beyond. Although people have, for a long time, been unable to enter the Realm of Heroes, there is a small crack in my domain above the mountain. My phoenixes travel through that gap for their deliveries.'\nYou say, 'Who do they deliver to?'\nElmara Emberclaw says, 'My phoenixes leave defiant gear in all corners of your world. There is always someone in need. Enjoy the Hero's Forge, and be careful around the creatures. They get combative when they think someone's interfering with operations. Every creature in my realm resurrects itself, so I don't mind you sparring with them. Let me know if you have any questions, or are looking for [work] to do.'\nYou say, 'What work do you need done?'\nElmara Emberclaw says, 'It would be a big help if you gathered raw [materials] for a new design I'm drafting. Everything I need can be found around the area. As a bonus for helping me, I'll let you be the first to test my new item!'\nYou say, 'What materials do you need?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Heroic Errand Runner'.\nElmara Emberclaw beams at you. 'We're going to get along, Renana. I need a handful of components for my design: A piece of orchidium, a sliver of glitterine, and a shard of illumiaz. You can find all of these minerals in the mine to the west. The mine is filled with creatures I call 'gemforms.' They usually collect the minerals and send them up in a minecart, but I haven't received any lately. It should be easy for you to find what I need. Orchidium is a purple gem, glitterine is gold, and illumiaz is clear. Fragments can be found along the ground in the mine. The gemforms might put up a fight, but I'm sure it's nothing you can't handle.'\n\n---\n\nElmara Emberclaw is delighted by your offer to help with her latest creation. She needs a variety of materials to finish the design, and as a reward for helping her, she'll let you be the first to try the new item.\nElmara Emberclaw needs a piece of orchidium, a sliver of glitterine, and a shard of illumiaz. All of these materials are in the mine to the west.\n1\\. Obtain a piece of orchidium 0/1 Hero's Forge\n_Piece of Orchidium can be found throughout the caves. They are a glowing white little crystal ground spawn near the big purple crystals._\nHere are some ground spawn locations:\n/waypoint +1093, +639, +40\n/waypoint +1263, +743, +54\n/waypoint +1357, +882, +53\n/waypoint +1559, +951, +54\n2\\. Obtain a sliver of glitterine 0/1 Hero's Forge\n_Sliver of Glitterine can be found throughout the caves. They are a glowing yellow color that looks almost like corn sticking up, it looks sharp like a knife._\nHere are some ground spawn locations:\n/waypoint +1101, +685, +35\n/waypoint +1403, +929, +53\n3\\. Obtain a shard of illumiaz 0/1 Hero's Forge\nShard of Illumiaz [item=146513] can be found throughout the caves. They are a glowing white color among other white glowing crystals on the ground. They almost look like corn sticking up, it looks sharp like a knife.\nHere are some ground soawn locations:\n/waypoint +1674, +1101, +53\n4\\. Deliver the piece of orchidium to Elmara Emberclaw 0/1 The Hero's Forge\nYou offered 1 Piece of Orchidium to Elmara Emberclaw.\nYour task 'Heroic Errand Runner' has been updated.\nYou complete the trade with Elmara Emberclaw.\n5\\. Deliver the piece of glitterine to Elmara Emberclaw 0/1 The Hero's Forge\nYou offered 1 Sliver of Glitterine to Elmara Emberclaw.\nYour task 'Heroic Errand Runner' has been updated.\nYou complete the trade with Elmara Emberclaw.\n6\\. Deliver the piece of illumiaz to Elmara Emberclaw 0/1 The Hero's Forge\nYou offered 1 Shard of Illumiaz to Elmara Emberclaw.\nYour task 'Heroic Errand Runner' has been updated.\nYou complete the trade with Elmara Emberclaw.\n7\\. Speak to Elmara Emberclaw 0/1 The Hero's Forge\nYou say, 'Hail, Elmara Emberclaw'\nElmara Emberclaw says, 'These are all perfect. Thanks, Gebb! It will take me some time to put everything together, so could I trouble you with another request while I work? There are a couple other [items] I'd like.'\nYou say, 'What items?'\nYour task 'Heroic Errand Runner' has been updated.\nElmara Emberclaw smiles sheepishly. 'It's selfish. I love journaling, but I'm almost out of ink and my quill has gotten dull. I've been so busy that I haven't replenished my supplies. I make ink using red pyreberries that grow on bushes all over the forest. For quills, I use phoenix feathers. Phoenix fledglings have the best sized ones for writing. Unfortunately, they don't let you simply pluck one. You'll have to fight a few to get a good feather....' She looks embarrassed. 'Don't look at me like that! Phoenixes always come back to life after you fight them. Nothing to feel guilty about.'\n8\\. Obtain pyreberries 0/1 The Hero's Forge\n_Pyreberries are red berries found on bushes that grow around the foilage in the forest. They are a mix of green and red._\nHere are some ground spawn locations:\n/waypoint +288, -166, +35\n/waypoint -323, -824, +3\n/waypoint +273, -667, +3\n/waypoint -1086, -1138, +8\n/waypoint +291, -168, +36\n9\\. Obtain a phoenix feather quill 0/1 The Hero's Forge\n_Pheonix Feather Quill drop off the Phoenix's in the upper west side of the zone going up the winding road._\n/waypoint -1558, +724, +934\n10\\. Deliver the pyreberries to Elmara Emberclaw 0/1 The Hero's Forge\nYou offered 1 Pyreberries to Elmara Emberclaw.\nYour task 'Heroic Errand Runner' has been updated.\nYou complete the trade with Elmara Emberclaw.\n11\\. Deliver a phoenix feather quill to Elmara Emberclaw 0/1 The Hero's Forge\nYou offered 1 Phoenix Feather Quill to Elmara Emberclaw.\nYour task 'Heroic Errand Runner' has been updated.\nYou complete the trade with Elmara Emberclaw.\n12\\. Ask Elmara Emberclaw about her progress 0/1 The Hero's Forge\nYou say, 'Hail, Elmara Emberclaw'\nElmara Emberclaw says, 'Gebb, you're just in time! Introducing the latest and greatest Hero's Forge invention...' She reveals three objects from behind her back. 'Ta-dah! I call them 'transfrogifying hoops.' You put the hoop around a creature and that creature should transform into a frog. The keyword in that sentence is 'should.' I haven't tested the [hoops], but I'm hoping you'd be interested in helping?'\nYou say, 'I can try using the hoops.'\nYou have been given: Transfrogifying Hoops\nYour task 'Heroic Errand Runner' has been updated.\nElmara Emberclaw says, 'Fabulous. Would you mind testing them on the reborn soldiers that wander the forest? Once you've picked your target, try putting the hoop around them. Ideally, they'll turn into little frogs. Much easier to fight, right? I implore you to not put them on yourself or any of my workers. We don't know what side effects the hoops will have.'\n13\\. Test the transfrogifying hoops on reborn creatures 0/3 The Hero's Forge\n_Test the transfrogifying hoops on reborn warriors, wizards, or berserkers in the area. Three repeated trials should be enough data for Elmara._\nPick any of the three, it can be 3 of the same. Right click the item on them, it turns them into a frog and then kill them.\nIf you right click on an already transformed reborn, it will not allow it and you will see, \"Elmira told you to only use these on reborn warriors, wizards or berserkers!\"\nIf you dispel the frog illusion, then you can right click anyone's hoops again to get credit for this step.\n14\\. Return the transfrogifying hoops to Elmara Emberclaw 0/1 The Hero's Forge\nYou offered 1 Transfrogifying Hoops to Elmara Emberclaw.\nYour task 'Heroic Errand Runner' has been updated.\nElmara Emberclaw appears pleased.\nYou receive 7 copper .\nYou receive 6 silver .\nYou receive 6 gold .\nYou receive 141 platinum .\nElmara Emberclaw listens intently while you describe your experiences with the transfrogifying hoops. She makes notes on some paper with her new phoenix feather quill and red ink. 'You've been such a big help, Gebb! I can't wait to work on the next iteration of these hoops.'\nYou complete the trade with Elmara Emberclaw.\nYou have successfully been granted your reward for: Heroic Errand Runner\nYou can now click Elmara`s Journal in The Hero's Forge on the table behind her to start the next quest, The Emberclaw Sisters.\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n141 platinum 6 gold 6 silver 7 copper\nExperience\n**Submitted by:** Gidono\n- Progression, Experience",
    },
