      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "",
      repeatable = false,
      group_size = "",
      npc = "Elmara's Journal",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Elmara Emberclaw",
        "I do have a question",
        "I looked at your journal.",
        "What about your entries about Kasha?",
        "I don",
        "Hail, Thormir Helmsbane",
        "I",
        "What changed?",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "for you to be here", count = 1 },
        { name = "her a little space", count = 1 },
        { name = "Elmara a gift to apologize for upsetting her", count = 1 },
        { name = "encouragement", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 148430, name = "Elistyl's Writings", type = "item" },
        { id = 148432, name = "Empty Gift Box", type = "item" },
        { id = 148429, name = "Fudge Chip Cookie", type = "item" },
        { id = 147831, name = "Gift for Elmara", type = "item" },
        { id = 148431, name = "Pressed Pink Daisy", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
        { name = "Elmara Emberclaw", change = -300 },
        { name = "Elmara Emberclaw", change = 300 },
      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- The Hero's Forge [zone=1328]\n**Who:**\n- Elmara's Journal [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 120\n**Maximum Level:** | 130\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 00:30:00\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Elmara Emberclaw +300\n**Factions Lowered:**\n- Elmara Emberclaw -300\n**Quest Items:**\n- Elistyl's Writings [item=148430]\n- Empty Gift Box [item=148432]\n- Fudge Chip Cookie [item=148429]\n- Gift for Elmara [item=147831]\n- Pressed Pink Daisy [item=148431]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Laurion Inn [zone=1329]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Baker Hylda [npc=59189]\n- Elistyl Kanghammer [ _Quest and Raid_]\n- Elmara Emberclaw - The Hero's Forge [ _Quests_]\n- Thormir Helmsbane - Laurion Inn [ _Raid_]\n- Thornel Grayleaf - Laurion Inn [ _Raid_]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Partisan of The Hero's Forge (15 Points) [quest=12662]\n**Era:** | !Laurion's Song\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Mon Nov 27 01:12:49 2023\nModified: Tue Feb 27 07:06:23 2024 | | **Laurion's Song Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n**Prerequisite Task: Heroic Errand Runner [quest=12610]**\n\n---\n\nYou can obtain this solo task from Elmara's Journal [npc=59128] in Hero's Forge. You can find Elmara's Journal on the table near the Laurion Inn door. It is on the find tool CTRL F.\nGet near the journal on the table and click on the left page. A popup shows a journal entry.\n\"My beloved sister,\nThis is dum, isn't it? Writing journal entries as if you'll ever read them? It's been exactly 2,451 days since I last saw you, Kasha. I've met dozens of interesting people on my journey. I'm traveling with a boisterous bard named Shalowain --- I think you'd like her. She's far too loud, in my opinion, but you have a way of getting along with everyone. I'm also journeying with an honorable dwarf, a kind Elddar, a moody dark elf, and even a bookish ogre, however, no matter how many people I meet, not a single one compares to you. I feel out of place among my companions. While they celebrate every victory we have over bandits or monsters, I find myself growing more discontent about the world. Why are we so surrounded by evil? What I wouldn't give for you to be here, reassuring me in the way you always do: a big grin and a slap on the back while you say, 'Don't make a storm out of a drizzle!' Although you are lost right now, Kasha, I swear you will be found.\"\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Emberclaw Sisters'.\n\n---\n\nYou read an interesting passage in Elmara Emberclaw's journal about her sister, Lasha. It seems Kasha was lost at some point, but the journal entry is short. The only way to learn more would be talking to Elmara about it.\nSpeak to Elmara Emberclaw about her journal.\n1\\. Ask Elmara Emberclaw about her journal entry 0/1 The Hero's Forge\nYou say, 'Hail, Elmara Emberclaw'\nElmara Emberclaw says, 'Hi again, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. How's life treating you? I don't have any errands for you right now, but if you have any [questions], I'm happy to chat! It's been a while since anyone was interested in hearing more about the work I do.'\nYou say, 'I do have a question'\nElmara Emberclaw says, 'What do you want to know about? More about the things I create? More about my realm? I was reading my [journal] earlier and reminded of so many fun stories from my past.'\nYou say, 'I looked at your journal.'\nElmara Emberclaw raises an eyebrow. 'You looked through my journal? There are some stories I'm happy to share, but there are plenty more [entries] that are very personal. You ought to ask people for permission before rummaging through their belongings.' She smiles awkwardly. 'I hope you didn't read anything too embarrassing. Let's change the subject, shall we?'\nYou say, 'What about your entries about Kasha?'\nElmara Emberclaw's smile is wiped away in an instant. Her eyes narrow and ears twitch. 'I told you to [drop] the subject.' Her voice is low and threatening.\nYou say, 'I don't want to drop it.'\nElmara Emberclaw shouts, 'Kasha is my sister! She's gone. Dead.' Her hands become tightly curled fists. 'Are you happy now? Is that what you wanted to hear? I couldn't save her. When she needed me the most... I wasn't there.' She glares at you. 'You should go, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Perhaps you shouldn't come back.'\nYour faction standing with Elmara Emberclaw has been adjusted by -300.\nElmara Emberclaw goes from threatening to aggressive. Her lips curl into a snarl, showing her sharp teeth.\n2\\. Return to Laurion Inn 0/1 Laurion Inn\n_At Elmara's request, leave the Hero's Forge and return to Laurion Inn._\nThis step updates right at the front door of the Laurion Inn at /way -765,-143,-2.\n3\\. Seek Thormir Helmsbane's advice at Laurion Inn 0/1 Laurion Inn\nThormir Helmsbane [npc=59220] is located in the first floor of the house. He is not far from the front door to the right.\nYou say, 'Hail, Thormir Helmsbane'\nThormir Helmsbane says, 'Ye got into a tiff with Elmara? Oh, ye asked about Kasha? That's Elmara's sister, aye? Yer openin' a whole can o' worms askin' about that. It's no wonder Elmara kicked ye out o' her forge. It's a sad story. I s'pose I can tell ye what I know if yer so [curious].'\nYou say, 'I'm curious.'\nThormir Helmsbane says, 'None of us ever met Kasha, but from what I gather, she and Elmara were thick as thieves. They lost their parents at a young age and had to rely on each other for everythin'. They lived a simple, nomadic life. They were talented anglers 'n' made their money catchin' 'n' sellin' fish. One day, everythin' [changed].'\nYou say, 'What changed?'\nThormir Helmsbane says, 'Elmara went to run errands, and when she returned to camp, Kasha had simply disappeared. It had a mighty big effect on Elmara. Ye can't blame her. That was her last family member 'n' Elmara blames herself for not bein' 'round to protect Kasha from... whatever happened. When we met, Elmara spoke of Kasha as though she were still alive somewhere, waitin' to be found. I thought it was admirable at first, but it got sadder as years went by. The rest o' the party 'n' I knew Kasha was probably [gone], but we indulged Elmara. Couldn't bear to see the pain on her face when anyone suggested that it might be time to stop lookin' for Kasha.'\nYou say, 'By 'gone,' you mean 'dead'?'\nYou have been given: Empty Gift Box [item=148432]\nThormir Helmsbane says, 'Aye. Sounds like ye reopened a wound that's never healed for Elmara. Ye couldn't have known, though. She'll cool off if ye give her a little space. She's always touched by thoughtful gifts, 'n' that'd go a long way in makin' a sincere apology. Yer in luck because I happen to have a gift box. I had it for somethin' else, but I think ye need it more than I do. How about ye collect some nice things and wrap 'em up in this? Since Elmara hardly ever visits Laurion Inn, might I suggest ye check the kitchen for a treat? If my nose is correct, they just baked a batch o' cookies.'\n4\\. Ask Baker Hylda about fresh-baked cookies 0/1 Laurion Inn\n_Thormir Helmsbane suggested that you give Elmara a gift to apologize for upsetting her. He suggested that you speak to two other friends, Elistyl Kanghammer and Thornel Grayleaf in Laurion Inn, for ideas about could be put into the gift box. He's also mentioned that Elmara might enojoy a fresh-baked cookie from the inn's kitchen. Once you obtain all the items you need, wrap them together in the empty gift box that Hormir provided you with._\nBaker Hylda [npc=59189] can be found in the kitchen on the first floor of the house. She is at /way -1036, -252, -2 and is on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Baker Hylda'\nBaker Hylda says, 'Mate, I got no time ta chit-chat with ya. I've got too much flyin' 'round the ol' noggin.' She begins muttering to herself, 'The pie's got five minutes left in the oven. The bread dough needs ta proof 'nother half hour. The [cookies] should cool down fer seven.''\nYou say, 'I heard you have cookies?'\nYou have been given: Fudge Chip Cookie [item=148429]\n5\\. Speak to Elistyl Kanghammer at Laurion Inn 0/1 Laurion Inn\nEliistyl Kanghammer [npc=59621] is on the first floor of the house right near the front door on the left at /way -835,-261,0. He is on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Elistyl Kanghammer'\nElistyl Kanghammer says, 'Hm? Elmara is upset with you? I'm sorry to hear that, but I don't know what you expect me to do about it. I'm sure you'll think of [something].'\nYou say, 'Do you know something that would help?'\nElistyl Kanghammer appears vexed. 'I don't like being roped into the drama of other people, but I suppose one thing I dislike even more is seeing Elmara sad.' Elistyl Kanghammer crosses his arms, clearly displeased. 'So, what did you do? I don't [know] how to help unless you tell me the details.'\nYou say, 'I asked to know more about Kasha.'\nElistyl Kanghammer says, 'I see. You pushed Elmara to talk about a painful memory. A simple 'sorry' won't cut it, but Thormir is right. A gift might help her get her mind off it.' Elistyl ponders quietly, but soon frustration takes over. With a huff, he says, 'I can only think of [one] thing that may help, but I'm not pleased about it.'\nYou say, 'What is the one thing?'\nElistyl Kanghammer says, 'Elmara loves to read, but we don't get many new books around here; rarely does a writer show up and decide to pen a novel during their stay. By now, I'm sure Elmara's read everything on the shelves here. I happen to know of some literature that she has certainly never read.' His jaw clenches before he finally says, 'That is because... I [wrote] it.'\nYou say, 'You wrote a book?'\nElistyl Kanghammer says, 'You sound surprised. I do have hobbies, you know.' He leans forward and whispers, 'Do not breathe a word of this to anyone other than Elmara. If I hear my name and the word 'wrote' in the same sentence, we'll have a problem.' He straightens himself. 'Exit the main door of the inn. Turn left. There's a garden with a fountain. You'll find a brown box with a notebook inside, hidden between two flower bushes. Wrap that in your gift box, then take it to Elmara. Do not read it. Got it? Now, let's pretend this conversation never happened.'\n6\\. Find Elistyl's writings somewhere in the inn's garden 0/1 Laurion Inn\nTo the west of the house in the shrubs you will see a box at /way -1005,+236,-9. Click on it to get Elistyl's Writings [item=148430].\nYou find the notebook Elistyl spoke of earlier. He asked that you don't read his writing, but... would he know if you took a peek? Either way, this item should be wrapped up with other presents in the gift box Thormir Helmsbane provided you with.\n7\\. Speak to Thornel Grayleaf at Laurion Inn 0/1 Laurion Inn\nThornel Grayleaf [npc=59452] is on the 2nd floor of the hour in Laurion Inn. He can be found at /way -913,-40,+25. He is on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Thornel Grayleaf'\nThornel Grayleaf says, 'Greetings. Ah, Elmara is troubled? Yes, she's cagey about her past. Like trees shedding their leaves and growing anew in the spring, I believe people, too, can set down their past and grow in new directions. Unfortunately, Elmara hasn't been able to [let go] of what she views as her former shortcomings.'\nYou say, 'Can we help her let go?'\nYou have been given: Pressed Pink Daisy [item=148431]\nThornel Grayleaf says, 'If only it were so easy. We can give encouragement, but we can't heal her wounds for her. It's incredible how much a mood can be lifted when you know your friends are supporting you, though. Take this gift to her. She and I loved observing the world around us, and maybe this will remind her how much beauty there is in the present. Hopefully this also reminds her how much I cherish her friendship, even if we haven't spoken in a while.'\n8\\. Accept Thornel's pressed pink daisy 0/1 Laurion Inn\nThis updates automatically from the previous step.\n9\\. Wrap three presents in the empty gift box 0/1 ALL\nPut the three items in the Empty Gift Box [item=148432]:\nFudge Chip Cookie [item=148429]\nPressed Pink Daisy [item=148431]\nElistyl's Writings [item=148430]\nHit combine.\nYou have fashioned the items together to create something new: Gift for Elmara. [item=147831]\n10\\. Deliver the gift for Elmara in the Hero's Forge 0/1 The Hero's Forge\nYou offered 1 Gift for Elmara to Elmara Emberclaw.\nElmara Emberclaw becomes less tense after accepting the gift.\nYour faction standing with Elmara Emberclaw has been adjusted by 300.\nYou receive 7 copper .\nYou receive 6 silver .\nYou receive 6 gold .\nYou receive 141 platinum .\nElmara Emberclaw says, 'What's this?' She opens the gift box and peers inside. A small smile appears on her face as she looks at the cookie and daisy. The smile turns into an incredulous grin as she flips through Elistyl's writings. 'You brought all this just to cheer me up? Thank you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. I'm sorry for getting so angry earlier. When you have a moment, can we talk?'\nYou complete the trade with Elmara Emberclaw.\nElmara Emberclaw says, 'I want to apologize again for the way I behaved. I'm not happy that you read my private journal, but that's no excuse for me to hiss at you. I was thinking about the situation while you were gone, and I realized that I snapped because I don't like to [let people in]'\nYou have successfully been granted your reward for: The Emberclaw Sisters\nYou have gained 21 ability point(s)!\nYou have gained 9 mercenary ability point(s)! You now have 20 mercenary ability point(s).\nYou gain experience!\nYou have completed achievement: Partisan of The Hero's Forge [quest=12662]\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n141 platinum 6 gold 6 silver 7 copper\nIncreases your faction with Elmara Emberclaw.\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
    },
