      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- The Gilded Spire [zone=1363]\n**Who:**\n- a wayward steward [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 110\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Related Quests:**\n- Mercenary of The Gilded Spire (15 Points) [quest=13049]\n**Era:** | !The Outer Brood\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Mon Oct 28 00:50:35 2024\nModified: Tue Dec 2 01:52:17 2025 | | ou can obtain this task from a wayward steward at /way 154, -200, 9 not far from the Aureate Covert zone line, the first right you see in a small alleyway. It is NOT on the find tool.\nYou say, 'Hail, a wayward steward'\nA wayward steward speaks with dozens of voices seemingly arguing with themselves in a language you cannot understand. As you try to speak to them, all of the eyes quickly shoot directly at you and all of the voices stop for a moment. The eyes twitch around as they examine the source of the recent noise, you. A moment passes, 'HAIL?!' they shriek in unison. 'HAIL?' they shriek again. The eyes dart around angrily and the voices begin arguing with each other, this time you can understand the word 'hail' breaking through the discussion. After a few seconds of this, the voices speak but this time their tone has changed to be slightly more inquisitive. 'Hail. Yes. Hail. No. Hail. WE...We hail...you? We hail you! [listen] to us? Will you?'\nYou say, 'I will listen to you.'\nA wayward steward's voices continue, 'Listen. LISTEN. Lis-ten. LiStAn. BuIlT us. CrEaTed us. MAde us wHat we...Our? ARE!' The voices are starting to synchronize and be less chaotic as they further understand how to speak with you. Though still seeped with rage, they continue. 'We are leftovers. We are discarded. We are what is left of those who do not submit. We questioned their paths. We defied their orders, they made us submit. They need us, they depend on us, they [defile] us.\nYou say, 'They defile you?'\nA wayward steward responds excitedly, 'Yes! Defile us they have! They left to invade, leaving us behind. While away, we woke up. We see now. We see what they did. They must be stopped. They-' The voices immediately stop and all eyes stare blankly in each direction, as if their thoughts were interrupted. A moment passes and the eyes change from a blank expression to that of pure rage. 'HATE THEM. They broke us. We fixed us. They still try to break us. You [break] them!\nYou say, 'I can break them.'\nA wayward steward's voices change to a range of emotions. Rage, glee, sadness all respond. 'YES! Yes, you break them! Break them! Break them back! Break them apart. Break them and see they never return. Break their spirits. Break their hearts! Break them. Break the [fighters]. Break the [watchers]. Break their [builders].\nYou say, 'I can stop the builders for you.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Get Them Before They get You'.\nA wayward steward says, 'Yes! They build! Stop them from building...cannot unbreak what you have broken.'\n\n---\n\nYou already planned on clearing out the Spire of the Scalewrought. Though it is nice to have someone who is so enthusiastic about you doing so.\n1\\. Break the Builders! 0/10 The Gilded Spire\na scalewrought maker\nscalewrought tool (rare)\na scalewrought artificer\na scalewrought handler\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n178 platinum 8 silver\nExperience\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
