    {
      id = "13015",
      title = "Eye Eye, Captain!",
      exp = "31",
      exp_name = "The Outer Brood",
      min_lvl = 1,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "",
      repeatable = false,
      group_size = "",
      npc = "Koredi Onalen",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Koredi Onalen",
        "I also want to figure it out.",
        "A leash?",
        "I wonder where they came from.",
        "Dreamweaver?",
        "Cancel Reinforcement Protocols",
        "Cancel Return Contingency",
        "_Quests_",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "him the eye", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 151041, name = "Dreamweaver Incense", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- The Gilded Spire [zone=1363]\n**Who:**\n- Koredi Onalen [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 110\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Dreamweaver Incense [item=151041]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Far Flung Flora [quest=13014]\n- Partisan of The Gilded Spire (15 Points) [quest=13050]\n**Era:** | !The Outer Brood\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Oct 31 02:08:34 2024\nModified: Sun Dec 22 20:23:13 2024 | | **Prerequisite Task:** Far Flung Flora [quest=13014]\n\n---\n\nYou can obtain this task from Koredi Onalen in The Gilded Spire at /way 354, 412, 275 up the ramp, on the west side of the 2nd floor. He is on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Koredi Onalen'\nKoredi Onalen spots you as you enter the room and gives an audible 'Psst!' to get your attention. He waves you over to him in the corner. You are surprised that he is even speaking to you in the first place, but you don't question it right now. Allies in here are rare, and you figure it would be better to hear him out and greet him with a hail. He adjusts whatever he is chewing on to one side of his mouth before addressing you. 'Hey, the name's Koredi Onalen. I've seen you around here and can tell you have an eye for the curious.' He looks around the room while speaking. 'Ain't you curious as to how this thing ticks? How it moves? How it functions? I do and want your help with [figuring it out].'\nYou say, 'I also want to figure it out.'\nKoredi Onalen's mouth grows into a mischievous grin, revealing a gold tooth. You're dealing with a real scoundrel here. 'Yeah, I knew you'd be down for a little sab-oh-tage. But we can't go out and do a sab-oh-tage without having some more information about what it is we are sab-oh-taging.' He puts his hands on his belt and adjusts it side to side. 'Now, I know we got ourselves a giant animal that we find ourselves in. And if there is one thing we know about giant animals that are forced into servitude, it's that there is probably a [leash] somewhere.'\nYou say, 'A leash?'\nKoredi Onalen snaps his fingers and points at you. 'You got it. Every beast that has to be used for war has to be broken down and then rebuilt, psy-coal-logically speaking. They call that training where I come from.' You notice that you cannot place his accent. You are not sure where he comes from. 'Let me tell you what I noticed. I noticed that there are a bunch of dragons sleeping in beds in these parts. I bet you a platinum that those dragons are sleeping because their energy has been exhausted traveling here. Which means they know a few things on how to get here and, more importantly, how to get back to [where they came from].'\nYou say, 'I wonder where they came from.'\nKoredi Onalen shrugs 'That's what I'm trying to figure out as well! Through my work, I have come across many, let's say, useful folks. One that goes by the name of Kwilrz Vn`Ycxa gave me an incense made with spores found from the Deepshade that helps one get into a trance and see what something is dreaming. Now, you may be asking, \"Why not use that on the beast we are inside of?\" And I will answer you with a \"Where is its nose, genius?\" And you will feel like a fool and we will continue our con-ver-sation. The only issue is that, with this being an incense, it has to be inhaled. We have come to call this incense \"[Dreamweaver].\"'\nYou say, 'Dreamweaver?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Eye Eye, Captain!'.\nYou have been given: Dreamweaver Incense\nKoredi Onalen looks at you sheepishly. 'Oh, don't look at me like that. If it works well, it should have a fun name for it. Maybe we can sell it someday, who knows? That's not important to the current pre-dik-ah-ment.' What is important to the current pre-dik-ah-ment is you taking the Dreamweaver to these sleeping dragons and learning what they know. You gotta light it and inhale it at the same time as the dreamer, if you are to get anything useful out of this. Now go on, git! Come back to me when you've learned something useful.'\n\n---\n\nYou have come across a scoundrel named Koredl Onalen. He has a plan to sab-oh-tage the transport that the Aurelians used to get to Norrath. He has an incense called \"Dreamweaver\" that he wishes to employ on the sleeping dragons in the higher levels of the Gilded Spire. Doing so will help with understanding how to pilot the beast and, in turn, cripple the Aurelians even further than you already have.\nUse the Dreamweaver incense on Narthu.\n1\\. Use the Dreamweaver incense on Narthu 0/1 The Gilded Spire\nNarthu is a sleeping dragon on the upper floors at /way 227, 151, 860\nRight click the Dreamweaver Incense when you target Narthu. It will not cast anything and won't break invis.\nNarthu inhales the incense at the same time as you do. You feel your mind slip away from you and into the dreams of Narthu. You witness flashes of the journey through the void as stars streak past the window you are looking out of. You get a glimpse of Narthu's reflection in the window. She turns and walks toward one of the blue crystals where a strange language with images is flashing on it. You stare at the screen for a few moments before returning to a tome that she is holding. You can hear Narthu's thoughts as she reads. It is a log of commands that can be used on the console. You can't fully make out the words, but her thoughts are understandable by you. She thinks about how she one day will not need Ballafore to do her job anymore, and once he is out of the way, she will be able to work unbothered. A loud, piercing sound crescendos. You blink and return to your body, staring back at Narthu sleeping soundly.\nYour task 'Eye Eye, Captain!' has been updated.\n2\\. Use the Dreamweaver incense on Quirin 0/1 The Gilded Spire\nSame thing, target Quirin and right click the item. Quirin is next to Narthu.\nQuirin takes a deep breath at the moment you light the incense, inhaling a huge noseful of the smoke. You lean in to inhale what you can and find your mind slipping into Quirin's dream. You watch Quirin sitting in front of the blue crystals with an unknown language being displayed. You can't read the runes, but you can understand Quirin's thoughts at the time. He appears to be trying to get the device to work how he wants it to by speaking commands out loud. Red words blip on the screen after every command. The dream state that you are in makes it difficult to understand what is being said, but one command is very clear: 'Cancel Reinforcement Protocols.' The lights in front of you flash red and you feel Quirin curse in frustration. Just then, Ballafore appears and consoles the frustrated Quirin. He looks intently at the blue crystal and the red flashes surrounding two squares with runes in them. He presses one of the squares while Quirin thinks the word \"Yes.\" The red lights get brighter and brighter until you flash back into the Gilded Spire, staring intently at a sleeping Quirin.\nYour task 'Eye Eye, Captain!' has been updated.\n3\\. Use the Dreamweaver incense of Valanor 0/1 The Gilded Spire\nValanor is next to Quirin.\nValanor exhales just as you attempt to use the incense, causing it to dissipate. You wait for a moment for the smoke to reform and be thick enough to be inhaled. You both inhale and you feel your mind slipping into a trance. Valanor is talking directly to Ballafore in a lift. It is just these two in the lift talking with each other about what they are doing for the day. During the conversation, Valanor looks Ballafore directly in the eyes and notices that one of his eyes is fake. She notes internally how it makes him look intimidating, yet handsome. Much of the conversation can be heard, but due to this being a dream, understanding what is being said is a challenge. You note that the conversation is cordial as the both of them continue their preparations in the invasion. The lift's doors open and a bright light flashes. You find yourself back in the leviathan, looking at Valanor as she snores peacefully.\nYour task 'Eye Eye, Captain!' has been updated.\n4\\. Use the Dreamweaver incense on Lysara 0/1 The Gilded Spire\nLysara is next to Valanor.\nLysara breathes in as you light the incense. You inhale the thick, blue smoke at the same time and feel yourself slip into a dreamlike trance. You are viewing everything from the perspective of Lysara. She is sitting in the bathing pools. You can feel the warm water rejuvenate you and the feeling is similar to the feeling you had when you were collecting the healing magics earlier. She is not alone as she turns to face Narthu, another Aurelian who is also resting. Lysara and Narthu continue their conversation and you are having a hard time focusing on what is being said. It feels as though they are quizzing each other. One statement sticks out to you. 'Remember...' The dream fades in and out. '...ever say \"Cancel Return Contingency.\"' The Dream fades again. '...an be catastroph...' The dream fades and you are back in your body, in the familiar surroundings of the Gilded Spire.\nYour task 'Eye Eye, Captain!' has been updated.\n5\\. Return the incense to Koredi 0/1 The Gilded Spire\nYou offered 1 Dreamweaver Incense to Koredi Onalen.\nYour task 'Eye Eye, Captain!' has been updated.\nKoredi Onalen takes the Dreamweaver from you and smiles a wicked smile. 'I see by the look on your face that the Dreamweaver worked. Good, now we got ourselves a bone-ah-fide pilot on our hands, don't we? I'll let Kwilrz know how well this worked. He will be pleased with this revelation. With that being said, we now have some of the tools we need to make sure that we stop this attack and prevent more from happening. There ain't no way they are going to get back from here. Norrath is their tomb. With that being said, it appears this Ballafore is someone who has access to the level of authority that we need. They seem to use their eye to control this beast. I think your best bet would be to kill Ballafore and take their eye. Then you can try and use the commands in the control room at the top of this spire.'\nYou complete the trade with Koredi Onalen.\n6\\. Kill Ballafore and retrieve his eye 0/1 The Gilded Spire\nBallafore is on the upper decks at /way 250, -255, 952. It's really easy to kill despite its size.\n--You have looted a Ballafore's Eye from Ballafore's corpse.--\nYou pull the eye out of Ballafore's socket with a disgusting squish. The front of the eye looks like what you would expect. Iris, pupil, sclera, all the normal parts. However, the back of the eye has a clear shell that attaches to the front of the eye. Within the shell you see the most pristine, pure golden clockwork spinning around like the inside of a watch. The gears and springs are still moving, seemingly perpetually in motion. Within the center of the clockwork you spot a small blue diamond-shaped crystal.\nYour task 'Eye Eye, Captain!' has been updated.\n7\\. Sabotage the call for Reinforcements 0/1 The Gilded Spire\nYou will need to go up even further until you get to a room full of crystal like objects at /way 597, 267, 1157. The command microphone will be on your right at a big crystal guarded by 2 mobs at /way 409, 337, 1157.\nTarget it and /say Cancel Reinforcement Protocols\nYou say, 'Cancel Reinforcement Protocols'\nYou point the eye at the crystal and say the words. The gears within the eye speed up and make the eye feel like it is vibrating in a way that acknowledges the command. The screen lights up red with runes and shapes with two boxes on them. You touch the one that you remember is the word \"Yes.\" The eye vibrates twice in quick succession and the facet returns to how you found it, none the wiser to what you have just done.\nYour task 'Eye Eye, Captain!' has been updated.\n8\\. Sabotage the return home 0/1 The Gilded Spire\nSame thing, target the microphone and /say Cancel Return Contingency\nYou say, 'Cancel Return Contingency'\nAs you speak the words, the crystal's facet flashes red and two squares appear again with runes on them. You feel the eye vibrate in acknowledgement. You press the \"Yes\" button again, knowing that this will cripple the Aurelians forever. The eye vibrates twice quickly to acknowledge the command has been accepted. Return to Koredi Onalen and give him the eye. Let him know the plan worked.\nYour task 'Eye Eye, Captain!' has been updated.\n9\\. Bring Ballafore's eye to Koredi 0/1 The Gilded Spire\nYou offered 1 Ballafore's Eye to Koredi Onalen.\nYour task 'Eye Eye, Captain!' has been updated.\nYou were able to get enough information to sabotage the beast that the Aurelians used to transport to Norrath. Your work has made it to where they will have a difficult time with a quick egress, if any egress is made at all.\nYou receive 2 silver .\nYou receive 1 gold .\nYou receive 267 platinum .\nYou gain experience!\nKoredi Onalen grins wildly as you hand him the eye, his gold tooth glistening with spit. 'Excellent, we got ourselves a bon-a-fide sab-oh-tage! Great work, Gebb. I'm going to take some time to gather my belongings and get out of here. I'll take this eye to where it needs to go. I'm sure someone in the Ring of Scale would be interested in it. I'll also tell Kwilrz that his Dreamweaver worked like a charm. Thanks again, I'll be seeing ya around, kid.'\nYou complete the trade with Koredi Onalen.\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n267 platinum 1 gold 2 silver\nExperience\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
    },
