      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Scarred Grove [zone=1381]\n**Who:**\n- Marshal Gulpin [ _Quest Giver_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 115\n**Maximum Level:** | 130\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Faction\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Verdant Guardians +150\n**Factions Lowered:**\n- The Burning Host -30\n**Quest Items:**\n- Innoruuk Camp Supplies [item=153179]\n- Invader's Ammunition [item=153178]\n- Rallos Zek Camp Supplies [item=153180]\n- Solusek Ro Camp Supplies [item=153181]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a war caller [npc=60780]\n- a warbringer [npc=60782]\n- a warmonger [npc=60817]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Missing Scout [quest=13389]\n- Storm Chasing [quest=13394]\n**Era:** | !Shattering of Ro\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Oct 21 04:08:13 2025\nModified: Tue Dec 9 06:33:26 2025 | | **Prerequisite Tasks: Missing Scout [quest=13389]**\n\n---\n\nYou can obtain this task from Marshal Gulpin [npc=60807] in Scarred grove at /way -200, -388, -3. He is on the Find tool (Ctrl+F).\nYou say, 'Hail, Marshal Gulpin'\nMarshal Gulpin says, 'To turn this battle in our favor, we will need to gain an advantage over the invading forces. I have a plan, but I will need your [help] in buying us some time.'\nYou say, 'What did you need my help with?'\nMarshal Gulpin says, 'Rallos Zek's forces brought several siege engines and used them to punch several holes in the defensive walls that were constructed. For now, they have stopped their barrages, but we need to disable their weapons by destroying the [equipment] they use to rearm them.'\nYou say, 'What kind of equipment?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Take the Offensive'.\nMarshal Gulpin glances at another report on the table. \"From our reports they keep the equipment in large crates around the siege engines and while you are out there it looks like we could use additional ammunition for the rangers on the walls. Collect some from the invading forces.\"\n\n---\n\nThe Burning Hosts siege has taken its toll on the defenders and their stronghold. Marshal Gulpin believes that the only way to turn the battle in the Verdant Guardians' favor Is to take the offensive.\nYou may not be able to destroy the siege engines, but destroying the equipment used to rearm and use them is just as good.\nThe archers on the wall need ammunition Collect some from the invading forces.\n1\\. Destroy the invading force's siege equipment 0/3 Scarred Grove\nYou'll see boxes around all the war equipment where you see mobs and little fires. Target invader siege equipment and kill it.\nOnly one in the group needs to do this, it updates for all in the group.\n2\\. Collect ammunition from invading forces 0/5 Scarred Grove\nInvader's Ammunition drops from various mobs. Each person in the group needs 5 of these.\nMobs that drop it:\na warbringer\na warmonger\na war caller\n3\\. Deliuver ammunition to one of the rangers on the wall 0/5 Scarred Grove\nGive the Invader's Ammunition to a grove sentinel.\nThey are on top of the wall. There are vine ladders you can climb on the wall inside of the fort or you can go to an opening in the wall and walk up it easily, even though it looks steep.\nYou offered 5 Invader's Ammunition to a grove sentinel.\nYour task 'Take the Offensive' has been updated.\nYour task 'Take the Offensive' has been updated.\nYour task 'Take the Offensive' has been updated.\nYour task 'Take the Offensive' has been updated.\nYour task 'Take the Offensive' has been updated.\nA grove sentinel says, 'Thank you. I will make sure this gets shared with everyone on the wall.'\nYou complete the trade with a grove sentinel.\n4\\. Report back to Marshal Gulpin 0/1 Scarred Grove\nYou say, 'Hail, Marshal Gulpin'\nMarshal Gulpin places a small figure on the war table. \"Our archers have arrows, and it sounds like the siege engines are out of commission. You did well, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, but I have something [else] for you to do.\"\nYou say, 'else'\nMarshal Gulpin nods. \"The invaders did not take our attacks lightly and they managed to break through our lines and destroy our [supply stores].\"\nYou say, 'supply stores'\nMarshal Gulpin stifles a croak. \"Food, medicine, and weapons were all burned. We started preparations to get more supplies, but it will be slow. We will need to take more drastic [action].\"\nYou say, 'What kind of action did you have in mind?'\nMarshal Gulpin's face turns sour. \"We need supplies, and we need them now. The [enemy] beating down our doors has supplies.\"\nYou say, ' I see, you want me to take the supplies from the enemy forces.'\nYour task 'Take the Offensive' has been updated.\nMarshal Gulpin nods. \"It will be dangerous, but taking supplies from each of the camps will not only help us but will also hurt their ability to continue this conflict, and if what you found in the tunnels is true, this may help to further drive a wedge between their forces. When you have gathered the supplies deliver them to Templar Davrin. He will ensure they are distributed to those that need them most.\"\n5\\. Collect supplies from Innoruuk tunnels 0/2 Scarred Grove\nGo back into the tunnels, you'll see what looks like brown cardboard boxes (Innoruuk Camp Supplies) in several spots, click them to loot them.\n6\\. Collect supplies from Rallos Zek's camp 0/3 Scarred Grove\nGo to Rallos Zek's camp, you'll see the same boxes (Rallos Zek Camp Supplies) around the outside of certain tents. Click them to loot them.\n7\\. Collect supplies from Solusek Ro's camp 0/3 Scarred Grove\nSame thing at Solusek's camp. Loot Solusek Ro Camp Supplies by clicking on the boxes.\n8\\. Deliver Innoruuk supplies to Templar Davrin 0/3 Scarred Grove\n9\\. Deliver Rallos Zek supplies to Templar Davrin 0/3 Scarred Grove\n10\\. Deliver Solusek Ro supplies to Templar Davrin 0/3 Scarred Grove\n11\\. Return to Marshal Gulpin 0/1 Scarred Grove\nYou say, 'Hail, Marshal Gulpin'\nYour task 'Take the Offensive' has been updated.\nMarshal Gulpin salutes you with pride. \"Templar Davrin has already sent word that you gathered the supplies we need. They will go a long way to helping the defenders. Also, while you were gone a messenger stopped by and requested you speak with [Lady Quellious].\"\nYou say, 'Lady Quellious'\nMarshal Gulpin says, 'They did not say what this was about, but it is best not to keep the goddess waiting. Thank you again, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'\n12\\. Speak with Lady Quellious 0/1 Scarred Grove\nYou say, 'Hail, Quellious'\nYour task 'Take the Offensive' has been updated.\nDestroying the Burning Host's siege equipment and taking their supplies may not have sent them away, but your actions have directly slowed their progress and with any hope driven a wedge between their combined forces.\nYour faction standing with Verdant Guardians has been adjusted by 150.\nYour faction standing with The Burning Host has been adjusted by -30.\nQuellious smiles warmly. \"Thank you for coming, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. We have much to discuss.\"\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\nIncreases your faction with Verdant Guardians by 150.\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
