      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Ruined Relic [zone=1384]\n**Who:**\n- Tsikut - Ruined Relic - SoR [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 115\n**Maximum Level:** | 130\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Era:** | !Shattering of Ro\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Nov 9 19:04:43 2025\nModified: Sun Jun 21 20:28:08 2026 | | You can obtain this partisan task from Tsikut in Ruined Relic. Tsikut can be found at /way 28, 429, 311 on the upper levels.\nYou'll need to make your way south to the platform portal which takes you up to the upper levels and then work your way up, crossing the blue glowing invisible bridges to reach the platform Tsikut is on.\nYou say, 'Hail, Tsikut'\nTsikut says, 'So we meet again, Gebb. When I heard you had made your way to the Plane of Magic once more, I had to summon you. These wild accusations against you aside, I know the power you had shown when you bested me prior. And I see you have only grown in power since. I hope you're done with your petty squabbling with higher beings, because I debase myself now by making [this request].'\nYou say, 'What is this request?'\nTsikut says, 'I know what rippled across the plane. I know what ripped through Skylance and tore through these platforms that honor her mighty dragons. I know what caused the coalescence of power within the Hall of Mirrors. It broke mind and magic, both, of the life here, including that of my brethren. I felt it.' Every word is punctuated by his hefty bass voice. 'It could be nothing but the [Tears of Veeshan], our Mother.'\nYou say, 'How could it be the Tears of Veeshan?'\nTsikut says, 'That is the mystery.' The slow gaze of ice-frosted golden eyes shift over his platform. 'I must stay here, to guard and maintain the portal to the great Vortex. As much to protect it from nefarious adventurers like you...' The lack of trust continues to drip through his words. '...As to protect the greater Relic from what is inside.' Narrowing his eyes, he asks, 'Will you [find any] that may remain of her Tears? It is the first step to determining how it happened.'\nYou say, 'I will do my best to find any remains of the Tears.'\nTsikut says, 'You aren't just a murderer, after all. Or you simply will do anything for the chance of a reward from a dragon, whether willingly given or taken by the sword. We'll start with the [first fragment].'\nYou say, 'The first fragment. Got it.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Shattered Tears: The First Fragment'.\nTsikut says, 'Our story begins in the marketplace. If there are any young scrykin still maintaining a level of sanity, they are likely there among the storefronts of the Artifact City.'\n\n---\n\nJust within the first steps from Arcstone into the ruined Artifact City and a young and slightly scatterbrained messenger named Tilahn had advised the adventurer to see the great Tsikut in the upper levels of the city. The formerly aggressive dragon has been working tirelessly to keep a portal open between Relic and the center of the storm open, as well as protect the sides from each other until the situation could be determined.\nTsikut knows the level of power that it took to shatter the city, and the familiar twang of draconic power had to have been the Tears of Veeshan. It could not have survived the blast but he would like to find what sections he can to investigate what had occurred.\nIf there are any young and relatively able-minded scrykin left within Relic, one has to be somewhere in the remains of the Marketplace.\n1\\. Explore the Relic Marketplace in search for a scrykin that may be coherant 0/1 Ruined Relic\nThis is a location update at /way 1185, 563, -273 which is in the northwest section of the map on the base level of the zone, to the north of the Arcstone zone line.\n2\\. Speak with Thress to see if he's seen a fragment of the Tears of Veeshan 0/1 Ruined Relic\nThress is in the same area back in a corner near some cages at /way 1209, 891, -273\nYou say, 'Hail, Thress'\nThress isn't immediately hostile, and his awareness of his environment allows him to immediately look to Gebb upon being addressed. 'Cage is empty. [Cages] are empty. But cage is full.'\nYou say, 'These cages?'\nThress blinks once and replies a nondescript, 'The cages!' Running his malformed hand upon the slick metal bars of the smaller cage, he stares at it as though to will the previous contents back into place. 'My elementals are gone.' But you're here on [behalf of Tsikut] and there is still information to obtain.\nYou say, 'I'm here on behalf of Tsikut.'\nThress widens his eyes. 'Great Tsikut!' Bang, bang, bang -- the scrykin's hand slaps against the same bars, and his attention turns strictly to the adventurer. 'What can I do for the honored master of ice? I didn't [break] the Plane. I didn't. Let him know, please. Please, please.'\nYou say, 'Regarding another break, have you seen any part of the Tears of Veeshan?'\nThress blinks again. 'Veeshan! Great Wyrmqueen. Not caged. No cage. She's caged.' A little twiddle of his fingers, and he replies, 'If you can help me with a task or two, I may [know something]. Maybe.'\nYou say, 'If you know something, I have the time to help.'\nA fire tamer begins casting Legion of Ogna.\nThress says, 'Good! Elementals gone; my [elementals] left me. I can't make money or feed them. I ask that you kill them, and then their defiance will be paid back.'\nYou say, 'I'm not sure what it will accomplish, but I can kill the elementals.'\nYour task 'Shattered Tears: The First Fragment' has been updated.\nThress says, 'Good. Good! Do it and I will help Tsikut.'\n3\\. Kill four elementals that broke loose 0/4 Ruined Relic\nMobs that count:\na cresting wave\na fiery sorcerer\na living vortex\nan animated flamespout\nan aqueous healer\nan earthen construct\n4\\. Check in with Thress after fulfilling his request 0/1 The Vortex\nYou say, 'Hail, Thress'\nThress says, 'My elementals are gone? They were already gone. Already. Empty cages. Full cage.' Shifting from one foot to another and shielding something beneath the waistline of his robe, he continues, 'Now get my crazed [brethren] who let them out.'\nYou say, 'Are you quite sure it was your brethren?'\nYour task 'Shattered Tears: The First Fragment' has been updated.\nThress says, 'Yes. Yes, very much so.' Giving no leeway to decline the request, he swiftly adds, 'Do it and I will help Tsikut.'\n5\\. Kill several scrykin that may have let his elementals loose 0/6 Ruined Relic\nMobs that count:\na cunning scrykin\na devious scrykin\na fire tamer\na frigid Mage\na storming scrykin\na sweltering scrykin\nan enraged scrykin\nan impetuous scrykin\nan impulsvile scrykin\n6\\. Check in with Thress after fulfilling his second request 0/1 Ruined Relic\nYou say, 'Hail, Thress'\nYour task 'Shattered Tears: The First Fragment' has been updated.\nThress says, 'You're back, and they're not! Ha ha ha ha ha! Now, you, fetch me a simple covered tome from the bookshelf. Simple cover. Black. Top shelf. It was stolen from me.' And like an echo, he says, 'Get it and I will help Tsikut.'\n7\\. For his third request, check the bookshelf for Thress' missing book 0/1 Ruined Relic\nThis bookshelf is north of the Arcstone zone line near /way 1308, 524, -273\nClear out around the bookshelf because a book mob will spawn and attack. The first one was yellow to me, after we killed it and went back to the bookshelf a 2nd book spawned and attacked. This one was white con to me at 130.\nOnce it dies, everyone in the group will get a Dusty and Torn Tome (Itemid 107398) on their cursor.\n8\\. Return the missing book to Thress 0/1 Ruined Relic\nYou offered 1 Dusty and Torn Tome to Thress.\nYour task 'Shattered Tears: The First Fragment' has been updated.\nThress picks up the corpse of the rather dangerous book, looking it over. 'A maze. A maze. Amazing, you found it! Now --' It's best to cut him off before he continues, because he owes you [answers] a few times over.\nYou complete the trade with Thress.\n9\\. See if Thress is ready to give more information 0/1 Ruined Relic\nYou say, 'Hail, Thress'\nThress picks up the corpse of the rather dangerous book, looking it over. 'A maze. A maze. Amazing, you found it! Now --' It's best to cut him off before he continues, because he owes you [answers] a few times over.\nYou say, 'That's enough for now. I need answers for Tsikut.'\nThress says, 'But... but...' The spindly arms wrap about his waist in an insecure hug, holding the hidden object closer to himself. With a pout, he asks, '[One more thing]? ...Please?'\nYou say, 'Okay. One more thing.'\nYour task 'Shattered Tears: The First Fragment' has been updated.\nThress says, 'A lapis lazuli! So precious. I've always wanted one.'\n10\\. Placate Three' final request with a simple, but beautiful stone 0/1 Ruined Relic\nYou'll need a Lapis Lazuli for this step.\nYou offered 1 Lapis Lazuli to Thress.\nYou have been given: Cloudy Remnant of the Tears\nYour task 'Shattered Tears: The First Fragment' has been updated.\nThress excitedly curls his long fingers around it. 'Lapis! Huzzah! I trade the Tear part to you in return; it's not as pretty. Not anymore. Not anymore... My elementals are gone!' He had the Remnant of the Tears the whole time, but yet was willing to trade it for a common but fancy gemstone. It's best to take it quickly to Tsikut.\nYou complete the trade with Thress.\n11\\. Bring the Cloudy Remnant of the Tears to Tsikut 0/1 Ruined Relic\nYou offered 1 Cloudy Remnant of the Tears to Tsikut.\nYour task 'Shattered Tears: The First Fragment' has been updated.\nUsing the reduced power of the Remnant of the Tears of Veeshan, Tsikut keeps the icy portal to the Vortex open. This wasn't the only remnant, and perhaps Tsikut knows more.\nTsikut rumbles curiously as he takes possession of the broken segment of the Tears of Veeshan. 'There is no doubt this was used to power the destruction, but yet not alone, and not just the whole Tears. There is something sinister tainting the divine object. I will keep hold of it, and utilize it to help keep the portal to the Vortex open.'\nYou complete the trade with Tsikut.\n\n---\n\n_**Reward:**_\nExperience for your level\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
    },
