      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Ruined Relic [zone=1384]\n**Who:**\n- Tsikut - Ruined Relic - SoR [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 115\n**Maximum Level:** | 130\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Items:**\n- Living Magma [item=151746]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Shattered Tears: The First Fragment [quest=13412]\n**Era:** | !Shattering of Ro\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Nov 11 04:03:14 2025\nModified: Thu Dec 25 17:11:02 2025 | | You can obtain this partisan task from Tsikut in Ruined Relic. Tsikut can be found at /way 28, 429, 311 on the upper levels. It is on the find tool CTRL F but if you are on the lower levels, it won't help.\nYou'll need to make your way south to the platform portal which takes you up to the upper levels and then work your way up, crossing the blue glowing invisible bridges to reach the platform Tsikut is on.\nYou say, 'Hail, Tsikut'\nTsikut restrains himself from a roar of frustration, knowing that \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ was only just a messenger for the state of the Tears of Veeshan. It was a confirmation, in the worst way, of what he had felt rippling through the blast. 'I summoned you before, but your presence is a reminder of the sick abuse of Mother Veeshan's power. I absolutely cannot have you in my sight. Go, and find the [second fragment] before I thrust you off the ledge.'\nYou say, 'Yes, I will seek out the second fragment.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Shattered Tears: The Second Fragment'.\nTsikut stares at \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, conveniently forgetting to give the adventurer a target of their search.\n\n---\n\nTsikut appeared rather irritated at the knowledge that the Tears of Veeshan have been shattered with the power of the explosion they caused. It's quite\npossible there's another fragment available out there, and without any clues granted from the great ice dragon, it's time to search it out.\nTsikut really gave no indication of where to go. Perhaps you can stumble across a clue.\n1\\. Without direction, start searching for the next fragment of the Tears 0/1 Ruined Relic\nThis is a location update not far from Tsikut at /way 197, 206, 318 right next to the blue glowing bridge.\nA voice whispers from above your right shoulder, a small shimmer of sound where no being or object exists. 'Char. Burn. Fry. Hot. Are her bars radiating heat? Do they burn? What does ice know of fire, anyways? Char. Scorch. Want to see? Does it burn you, too?'\nYour task 'Shattered Tears: The Second Fragment' has been updated.\n2\\. A voice recommend searching the fire, but is it for the Tears? 0/1 Ruined Relic\nThis is a location update at /way 365, -162, 303 on a broken up ramp on the upper levels northeast of Tsikut.\nThe voice whispers again. If sound could have a temperature, it would sear at your senses. 'Yes. Here. Smart. Does it burn? Does she burn? Do they burn? Do [Tears] burn? Will you burn? Can you summon me, and we can find out?'\nYour task 'Shattered Tears: The Second Fragment' has been updated.\n3\\. Seek out a dialogue with a disembodied voice 0/1 Ruined Relic\nThis is tied to the [Tears] dialogue from the previous step. There can only be one person in the vicinity of the fire (/way 329, -172, 300) Back everyone else away and kill nearby mobs while one person completes the dialogue to get this step updated.\nYou say, 'What do you know of the Tears?'\nA voice replies with an uncomfortable heat at the edge of your skin. 'The Tears of Veeshan. The ice seek. But the ice doesn't care. No care. Where is she? Does [she] burn?\nYou say, 'Who is she?'\nYour task 'Shattered Tears: The Second Fragment' has been updated.\nA voice hisses softly. 'Char.Burn. Storm. Retch. Spark. Summon me.'\n4\\. Kill five elementals and fire-based scrykin 0/5 Ruined Relic\nMobs that count for this:\nan animated flamespout\na blazing flamespout\na fiery scrykin\n5\\. Collect ten pieces of Living Magma to try to summon the voice 0/10 Ruined Relic\nThe same fire-based mobs drop Living Magma (ItemId: 107399). Usually 3 at a time.\nThis is also a ground spawn in the Fire circle (/way 715, -300, 315) . They look like black collection items.\nThe magma is pre-lootable.\n6\\. Summon and kill Magmath 0/1 Ruined Relic\nYou need to be on the lava platform at /way 713, -303, 312 which is not far from Tsikut.\nClear out the mobs around the center area and then stand right in the center and click Living Magma.\nMagmath spawns (lvl 130-131) and attacks. It doesn't have the hit points that a rare has and didn't hit all that hard. It's a mage, you can see what spells it casts by clicking on the related npc creatures link on the left.\nMagmath is stunnable and slowable.\n7\\. Pull the Remnant of the Tears of Veeshan from Magmath's corpse 0/1 Ruined Relic\nWhen Magmath dies, it drops Charred Remnant of the Tears (ItemId 106686) for each member of the group.\n8\\. Return the Charred Remnant of the Tears to Tsikut 0/1 Ruined Relic\nYou offered 1 Charred Remnant of the Tears to Tsikut.\nYour task 'Shattered Tears: The Second Fragment' has been updated.\nTsikut growls, 'Ashenback!'\nYou complete the trade with Tsikut.\n9\\. Speak with Tsikut about the findings so far 0/1 Ruined Relic\nYou say, 'Hail, Tsikut'\nTsikut says, 'You found the second piece. I...' Once again he appears visibly disgusted with his next words, but shares them in spite of that. 'I apologize for casting you away with this task and limited knowledge.' The two parts of the tear now resting together in front of him, he continues, 'I believe you know by now that to find any level of [sanity left] in this realm is like trying to find a sliver of peace under the tools of Saryrn. Not impossible though.'\nYou say, 'Do you think there's any sanity left?'\nYour task 'Shattered Tears: The Second Fragment' has been updated.\nNow with two pieces to help maintain the gateway to the Vortex, Tsikut believes there may be another hidden amongst some sanity left in the broken walls of Relic.\nTsikut repeats, 'Not impossible. But to hear what has become of Magmath is painful. It was never much of a trickster. I was hoping to hear one of Ashenback's minions was aware enough to nudge Ashenback back. That said, I have a feeling. Come to me in a bit, and I may have more to share on an idea of another part of her Tears.'\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\nEXP for your level\n**Submitted by:** Gidono, Veludeus",
    },
