      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Labyrinth of Spite [zone=1386]\n**Who:**\n- Drew Xiomar [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 115\n**Maximum Level:** | 130\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Confirmed Patroller's Key [item=154101]\n- Patroller's Key [item=151742]\n- Polished Coin [item=151741]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Heloise Alston [npc=61015]\n- Tyrwin [ _Quests_]\n**Era:** | !Shattering of Ro\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 13 02:37:47 2025\nModified: Tue Jul 14 19:27:23 2026 | | You can obtain this task from Drew Xiomar near the entrance of the zone at /way 491, 340, 163. He is on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Drew Xiomar'\nDrew Xiomar regards Gebb with a small grunt, proving to be the best greeting you'll get out of him at the moment. The vague acknowledgement out of the way, he gets down to business. 'Did you have a chance to see when they brought the [prisoner] in?'\nYou say, 'Which prisoner is that?'\nDrew Xiomar furrows his brow as though the question presented is absurd, and shares a look briefly with Gebb. In acknowledgement of a very much vague description for a place with as many cells as this one has, he clarifies, 'The one in the central, floating cage. They seem to be a very [special] prisoner.'\nYou say, 'Special how?'\nDrew Xiomar says, 'It's a unique enclosure, to start. It's also been brought down into the central room so rarely, and always under guard. I believe whomever it is, they are a key or THE key to, well...' He flicks a few fingers vaguely in the direction of the top of the endless staircase in figurative emphasis. '...all this. Do you have eyes on the figure [in there]?'\nYou say, 'I can't see who is in there.'\nDrew Xiomar slams a palm against the stone railing. 'Damn! I was hoping on having some eyes up there.' With another moment to clear his thoughts, he replies with newfound control, 'I have to say my interest is piqued. If you're the adventuring type, would you want to [investigate] this mysterious cage for me?'\nYou say, 'I can investigate it.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Spiteful Machinations'.\nDrew Xiomar nods once, and slips a coin out of a belt pocket and extends it to Gebb. 'There are some below who may be friendly enough to accept this. If you find a denizen of the Labyrinth who will cooperate, you may be able to ask some questions. It's quite vague, but if I had more information, I wouldn't be asking for help now.'\nYou are given: Polished Coin\n\n---\n\nThe mysterious floating cage, levitating high above the middle of the Labyrinth of Spite, is rumored to have a VIP prisoner. From paladin Drew Xiomar's\nposition overlooking the Labyrinth, he seeks additional information about its occupant, and is sending you forth to find out more.\nSupplying you with a polished coin with a notable signet on its face, Drew advised finding a friendly-enough denizen to gather information from.\n1\\. Find a denizen who will cooperate when they see the coin 0/1 Labyrinth of Spite\nYou are looking for Heloise Alston. She can be found at /way -142, 349, -23 on the west side of the zone on the base floor.\nYou offered 1 Polished Coin to Heloise Alston.\nYour task 'Spiteful Machinations' has been updated.\nHeloise Alston says, 'Oh. Oooooh.' Her expression eases into a faint smile before slipping neutral to maintain the facade of the labyrinth. 'I presume you have a [question] to approach me so brazenly publicly?'\nYou complete the trade with Heloise Alston.\n2\\. See if you can get a lead from Heloise Alston 0/1 Labyrinth of Spite\nHeloise Alston can be found at /way -141, 351, -24 on the west side of the zone.\nYou say, 'Hail, Heloise Alston'\nHeloise Alston says, 'Oh. Oooooh.' Her expression eases into a faint smile before slipping neutral to maintain the facade of the labyrinth. 'I presume you have a [question] to approach me so brazenly publicly?'\nYou say, 'Yes, I have a question. Can you tell me of the central prisoner?'\nHeloise Alston says, 'You... don't know? You can't feel it?' Despite her friendly-enough, quiet demeanor, she quietly snorts. Using a term that's been perhaps overused in a short few moments, she adds, 'I can only tell you that the prisoner is quite [special].'\nYou say, 'I have heard they're quite special.'\nHeloise Alston says, 'Oh, very much yes. But what good is knowing who is there without knowing how or why they got there?' Her smile grows, exposing her thick fangs. Nonchalantly, she seems to change subject. 'Why don't you focus on the poor [husks] instead?' Voice dripping, she adds, 'No one thinks of the husks. Poor things.''\nYou say, 'The husks?'\nYour task 'Spiteful Machinations' has been updated.\nHeloise Alston says, 'Perhaps they have more in common than you think.' Checking her sharpened nails, her eyes focus away from Gebb. 'Go find yourself an assortment of them and do what you do best. It will make itself known.' Wait, what? The vampire seems to have lost her interest in talking to you, for now.\n3\\. Find a common thread with some of the husks 0/1 Labyrinth of Spite\nHere are the different named husks and vessels I've come across. This step is based upon killing a husk or vessel mob in each of the sections of the zone. North, South, East, West.\nThe mob that counts for this step is \"an envious husk\" or \"an envious vessel.\"\n4\\. Find a common thread with some of the husks 0/1 Labyrinth of Spite\nThe mob that counts for this step is \"a jealous husk\".\n5\\. Find a common thread with some of the husks 0/1 Labyrinth of Spite\nThis mob that counted for this step is \"a malicious husk\".\n6\\. Find a common thread with some of the husks 0/1 Labyrinth of Spite\nThe mob that counts for this step is \"a contemptuous husk\".\n7\\. Seek out any additional leads from the Husks 0/1 Labyrinth of Spite\nFind Tyrwin /way -471, -176, -24\n8\\. Speak with the semi-lucid husk 0/1 Labyrinth of Spite\nSpeak with Tyrwin /way -471, -176, -24\nYou say, 'Hail, Tyrwin'\nTyrwin doesn't look to be fully present. 'O-o-oh? You're not them, and... y-you're not us. You're, umm, an [adventurer]? Uh, Norrathian?'\nYou say, 'Yes, I'm an adventurer.'\nTyrwin says, 'Oh n-no. Go, don't [stay here].'\nYou say, 'Why not stay here?'\nTyrwin says, 'Y-y-y-you can't be-become [one of us].' He shakes his head in minute little sways. 'H-h-hold onto y-yourself.'\nYou say, 'What do you mean 'one of us'?'\nTyrwin answers a single word: '[Husks].'\nYou say, 'What are husks?'\nTyrwin says, 'W-we are.' The pain is present in his hood-darkened eyes as he tilts his head to look at Thorque, the first time he has made real eye contact since beginning the discussion. 'W-w-we are e-empty vessels. W-we had h-her spite. It is gone. Gone... She t-[took it].'\nYou say, 'Took it?'\nTyrwin blankly echoes, 'Took it.' There is little more you could get from that line of discussion. Does he, perhaps, have the same [marks] on his head or neck, like the other husks?\nKinathar tells the guild, 'i'm in NC we dodged yet another storm'\nYou say, 'May I check for marks on you?'\nTyrwin shifts his eyes about as he takes the request under consideration. Fear trembles his fingers as they reach up to his hood, and drop the fabric long enough to share the bruising behind one of his ears, matching that of similar husks. Out of security, it's swiftly put back into place before it could be examined in detail. Perhaps something can be done [to help].\nYou say, 'Is there anything I can do to help you?'\nTyrwin tightens his grasp on his hood, the knuckles whitening under his already-pale grip. It's a few long moments before he replies, 'Help me? No. N-no. No no. Not me. [Others]?... Perhaps so, still.'\nYou say, 'What others?'\nYour task 'Spiteful Machinations' has been updated.\nTyrwin says, 'D-do something for me. A key. A key from the d-d-d-drachnids. Bring it, and... I c-can share more.'\n9\\. Find a key from one of the patrolling drachnids 0/1 Labyrinth of Spite\nKill the wandering drachnids that see through invis. They will drop a Patroller's Key for everyone doing this task. The key is NOT pre-lootable.\n10\\. Show the key to the husk 0/1 Labyrinth of Spite\nGive the Patroller's Key to Tyrwin /way -471, -176, -24\nYou offered 1 Patroller's Key to Tyrwin.\nYou have been given: Confirmed Patroller's Key\nYour task 'Spiteful Machinations' has been updated.\nTyrwin insists Thorque holds onto the key. 'Release my... wife. P-please.' There's no indication of which cell holds her, but there's only one way to find out.\nYou complete the trade with Tyrwin.\n11\\. Find the door somewhere in the Labyrinth, and release its occupant 0/1 Labyrinth of Spite\nRight click they key on the door\nThe key produces an echoing click as it turns in the lock. A husk emerges immediately upon the door opening, and pays no mind to the adventurer as she takes off for her target.\n_When too far away_\nThe key doesn't seem to apply to any locks around here.\n12\\. Give the key back to the husk 0/1 Labyrinth of Spite\nGive the key to Tyrwin /way -471, -176, -24\nYou offered 1 Confirmed Patroller's Key to Tyrwin.\nYour task 'Spiteful Machinations' has been updated.\nThe husk, Tyrwin, sent you to find his wife, and she was swiftly released, but he believes it was too late. With new resolve to do something about it, he now seeks your assistance further.\nTyrwin says, 'We're t-too late. No. No...' There's distress in his manner, but he cannot find the anger that aches to come out. 'We have t-t-to change this.'\nYou complete the trade with Tyrwin.\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n23 platinum 7 gold 6 silver\nExperience for your level\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
    },
