      id = "13698",
      title = "Through the Breach",
      exp = "32",
      exp_name = "Shattering of Ro",
      min_lvl = 1,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "",
      repeatable = false,
      group_size = "",
      npc = "Flameshaper Severyn",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Flameshaper Severyn",
        "What do you mean, what reinforcements?",
        "If you need more troops for the frontline, I could join the next assault.",
        "better use",
        "And you want me to be this someone.",
        "Hail, Flameseeker Onkrin",
        "What is the mission?",
        "How big are these gaps?",
      },
      items_required = {
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 153177, name = "Ambusher's Orders", type = "item" },
        { id = 153176, name = "Flamespeaker's Orders", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
        { name = "The Burning Host", change = 225 },
      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Scarred Grove [zone=1381]\n**Who:**\n- Flameshaper Severyn [ _Quest Giver_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 105\n**Maximum Level:** | 130\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Ambusher's Orders [item=153177]\n- Flamespeaker's Orders [item=153176]\n**Era:** | !Shattering of Ro\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Nov 30 20:52:30 2025\nModified: Tue Dec 9 06:35:40 2025 | | You can obtain this Partisan task from Flameshaper Severyn in Scarreg Grove in the Solusek Grove camp in the southwest part of the zone. She is on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Flameshaper Severyn'\nFlameshaper Severyn turns her fiery gaze toward you. \"So, you are the [reinforcements] that they sent?\"\nYou say, 'What do you mean, what reinforcements?'\nFlameshaper Severyn eyes narrow. \"Our initial assault met with more resistance than we had anticipated and with the intervention of Mithaniel Marr and his sycophants we need more [troops].\"\nYou say, ' If you need more troops for the frontline, I could join the next assault.'\nFlameshaper Severyn takes your measure. \"No, you look more capable than the blockheads Rallos Zek has been sending forward. I think I have a [better use] for you.\"\nYou say, 'better use'\nFlameshaper Severyn nods sternly. \"Our lord grows impatient with the current battle and ordered me to find [someone] to take a less direct approach.\"\nYou say, ' And you want me to be this someone.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Through the Breach'.\nFlameshaper Severyn smirks. \"Capable and smart. Yes, you are just the right someone. Report to Flameseeker Onkrin, they will have the details.\"\n\n---\n\nThe Burning Host's initial assault was met with more resistance than they anticipated, but the Flameshaper believes that you will be better served taking a less direct approach than charging headlong toward the defender's lines.\nReport to Flameseeker Onkrin for your orders.\n1\\. Report to Flameseeker Onkrin 0/1 Scarred Grove\nYou say, 'Hail, Flameseeker Onkrin'\nFlameseeker Onkrin looks up from a report with a rigid look on her face. \"The Flameshaper already sent word. She believes that you will be able to complete this [mission]. We will see.\"\nYou say, 'What is the mission?'\nFlameseeker Onkrin points towards the wall. \"The defenders may have held us off initially, but they did not do so unscarred. Rallos Zek's siege engines gouged several [gaps] in their walls.\"\nYou say, 'How big are these gaps?'\nFlameseeker Onkrin says, 'Large enough to move a squad through, but they have already moved troops to shore up those defenses. So, it is unlikely we will be able to breach their walls with numbers. That is where you come in. Where a squad would fail, I believe that one clever soldier could [breach] the wall and do some real damage.'\nYou say, 'breach'\nFlameseeker Onkrin grins. \"I want you to investigate the breaches and find a more subtle approach to get into their camp. Find a small breach or one that has fewer guards and make your way [inside]. Do your best not to raise any alarms.\"\nYou say, 'Once I'm inside then what?'\nYour task 'Through the Breach' has been updated.\nFlameseeker Onkrin grin becomes a sinister smile. \"That is when then fun begins. I want you to destroy their supplies. Burn them all to the ground and when you are done report back to me.\"\n2\\. Investigate the western breaches 0/1 Scarred Grove\nThis is a location update at /way -392, 213, -33 at the 2nd break on the wall from the left on the north part of the zone.\n3\\. Investigate the eastern breaches 0/1 Scarred Grove\nThis is a location update at /way -418, -213, -34 on the same wall, just down further to the east.\n4\\. Locate the small breach 0/1 Scarred Grove\nThis is a location update at /way -299, -600, -14 further east down the wall on a smaller opening.\n5\\. Destroy defender's weapon racks 0/3 Scarred Grove\nThese are located inside the wall on the north side of the zone. You can find them along the walls on the west end and east end. They have little to no hit points, they won't count if a pet kills it.\nKilling these counts for the whole group.\n6\\. Destroy defender's food stores 0/1 Scarred Grove\nThese are in the huts. One is in a hut up in a tree by itself on the west end.\n7\\. Destroy defender's supply cache 0/1 Scarred Grove\nThese are in the huts as well. When you kill this a npc will spawn and attack.\n8\\. Defeat the ambush 0/1 Scarred Grove\na lightbearer ambusher spawns, kill it. If you don't get to it in time, kill the defender's supply cache again.\n9\\. Collect the ambusher's orders 0/1 Scarred Grove\n--You have looted an Ambusher's Orders from a lightbearer ambusher's corpse.--\n10\\. Deliver orders to Flameseeker Onkrin 0/1 Scarred Grove\nYou offered 1 Ambusher's Orders to Flameseeker Onkrin.\nYour task 'Through the Breach' has been updated.\nFlameseeker Onkrin reads through the orders. \"I never trusted Innoruuk's forces, but to outright attack one of our own seems foolish. The Flameshaper will need to know of this. Report to her at once.\"\nYou complete the trade with Flameseeker Onkrin.\n11\\. Report to Flameshaper Severyn 0/1 Scarred Grove\nYou say, 'Hail, Flameshaper Severyn'\nFlameshaper Severyn says, 'Word of your success has already [reached] my ears. Congratulations are in order, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'\nYou say, 'Has word of Innoruuk's betrayal reached your ears?'\nFlameshaper Severyn intently listens to your explanation. \"I do not believe that Innoruuk's forces are bold enough to double cross us, but to be sure I will have [Commander Roknik] investigate the matter. It is time his forces proved themselves to be more than just a blunt object.\"\nYou say, 'Commander Roknik'\nYour task 'Through the Breach' has been updated.\nFlameshaper Severyn quickly pens a message and seals it in an envelope. \"Yes, he commands Rallos Zek's forces. Take this letter to him.\"\nYou are given: Flamespeaker's Orders (Itemid 113513)\n12\\. Deliver message to Commander Roknik 0/1 Scarred Grove\nYou offered 1 Flamespeaker's Orders to Commander Roknik.\nYour task 'Through the Breach' has been updated.\nYou dealt a devastating blow to the defenders by destroying their supplies, but the ambush by Innoruuk's forces may have thrown a wrinkle into things. While Flameshaper Severyn's attention is turned toward the destruction of the defenders she expects Commander Roknik to look deeper into this matter.\nYour faction standing with The Burning Host has been adjusted by 225.\nYour faction standing with Verdant Guardians could not possibly get any worse.\nYou receive 36 platinum .\nYou gain experience!\nCommander Roknik tears open the envelope and quickly glances through the message a sour look crossing his face. \"If you want work, I give.\"\nYou complete the trade with Commander Roknik.\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\nMoney - At Level 130 - 36 platinum\nExperience\nIncreases your faction with The Burning Host.\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
    },
