      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- East Freeport 2.0 [zone=1]\n- North Qeynos [zone=4]\n**Who:**\n- Artisan Tar Cordell [ _Tradeskill Quests_]\n- Artisan Vivian Selgan [ _Trade Skill Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 20\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Armour Set\n- Tradeskill\n**Quest Items:**\n- Ancestral Human Armor [item=33976]\n- Arachnid Eye Cluster [item=34761]\n- Blessed Book of Human Culture [item=33991]\n- Burned Out Lightstone [item=3614]\n- Crystallized Marrow [item=14760]\n- Deepwater Ink [item=17621]\n- Drop of Mercury [item=5709]\n- Elaborate Sagacious Swatch [item=34597]\n- Elaborate Stargazer Swatch [item=34601]\n- Eminent Book of Human Culture [item=34036]\n- Fire Beetle Carapace [item=18350]\n- Golden Bandit Tooth [item=16924]\n- Huge Block of Clay [item=34078]\n- Intricate Sagacious Swatch [item=34596]\n- Intricate Stargazer Swatch [item=34600]\n- Jade Shard [item=5953]\n- Lake Pebble [item=20318]\n- Large Darkhollow Geode [item=45104]\n- Lightstone [item=2976]\n- Lion Tail [item=11966]\n- Mold for Human Boots [item=34103]\n- Mold for Human Chestplates [item=34104]\n- Mold for Human Gloves [item=34105]\n- Mold for Human Helms [item=34106]\n- Mold for Human Leggings [item=34107]\n- Mold for Human Sleeves [item=34108]\n- Mold for Human Wristguards [item=34109]\n- Old Dragon Horn [item=17662]\n- Ornate Sagacious Swatch [item=34595]\n- Ornate Stargazer Swatch [item=34599]\n- Pattern for Human Boots [item=34110]\n- Pattern for Human Gloves [item=34111]\n- Pattern for Human Helms [item=34112]\n- Pattern for Human Leggings [item=34113]\n- Pattern for Human Sleeves [item=34114]\n- Pattern for Human Tunics [item=34115]\n- Pattern for Human Wristguards [item=34116]\n- Revered Book of Human Culture [item=34006]\n- Rough Patch of Goblin Skin [item=34763]\n- Sacred Book of Human Culture [item=34021]\n- Shark Skin [item=3115]\n- Simple Sagacious Swatch [item=34594]\n- Simple Stargazer Swatch [item=34598]\n- Stalwart Human Cultural Smithing [item=86743]\n- Zombie Skin [item=7772]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Befallen 2.0 [zone=23]\n- Dragon Necropolis 2.0 [zone=121]\n- Erud's Crossing [zone=28]\n- Kedge Keep 2.0 [zone=64]\n- Ruins of Old Paineel 2.0 (The Hole) [zone=99]\n- Toxxulia Forest 2.0 [zone=65]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Darkhollow Geode (Human) [quest=4322]\n- Dragons of Norrath Cultural Equipment [quest=3056]\n- Eminent Impressions (Human/Freeport) [quest=4323]\n**Era:** | !Dragons of Norrath\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- Bard\n- Berserker\n- Cleric\n- Druid\n- Enchanter\n- Magician\n- Monk\n- Necromancer\n- Paladin\n- Ranger\n- Rogue\n- Shadowknight\n- Warrior\n- Wizard\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- Human\nEntered: Mon Feb 21 13:15:30 2005\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Click here** [quest=3056] for an overview of cultural armor introduced with Dragons of Norrath.\n_(If you are starting in Qeynos, click here [quest=3038].)_\n_Find Vivian Selgan in East Freeport (location -1015, -865)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Vivian Selgan'\nVivian Selgan says 'Hello \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. What brings you back 'ere? Wanted to be round yer own [kind] again?'\nYou say, 'Kind?'\nVivian Selgan says 'Aye. A lot of us have returned home these past few months. Seems distrust is brewing among them other races. Now, I don't want to be accused of bigotry, some of those other races are okay--dwarves and elves are pretty reliable in a fight--but the rest: you can't trust 'em. Like them blasted dark elves: always plotting something. And those lizard things. . . don't even get me started with those. Folks don't feel safe out there anymore so they come back here for protection. Why do you think I came back to the city! To be 'round more humans, folks I can [trust]!'\nYou say, 'Trust?'\nVivian Selgan says 'Aye, you know what I mean. We need to stick together, form a unified front and let our enemies know we mean business. In fact, right now I'm making armor for the city militia. Hmm, you look like you'd be good in a fight. Perhaps you'd be [interested] in these armor designs. Or maybe you want to know more about the military and scholarly [symbols] we humans have used over the ages? I can share my patterns for either the symbols or the armor with you provided you don't go blabbing my trade secrets to no dark elves. Can't trust those kind!'\nYou say, 'I am interested.'\nVivian Selgan says 'Excellent, I can make you a pattern book, but first I'm gonna need some materials. Bring me a raw-hide belt for the cover, a low quality cat pelt for the pages, a snake venom sac for the ink, and a cutthroat insignia ring for the binding. I have heard most of these items can be found in the Oasis of Marr, South Ro and the Commonlands. Bring them to me and the pattern book shall be yours.'\n_On handing in the items:_\nArtisan Vivian Selgan says 'Aye, well done, my friend! As promised, 'ere is the pattern book. It may take some practice to get a hang of those designs, but they should serve you well. Don't forget about us if a war breaks out. I want you up on those city walls with me, aye!'\n_You receive your book of Ancestral Human Armor._\nYou say, 'What symbols?'\nVivian Selgan says 'Once ye've got yer armor, ye might want ta reinforce it with these symbols. Fetch me a few things so I can make the symbol patterns. There's reagents I need in [Befallen], [The Hole], [The Dragon Necropolis], and the [valley] beyond the Lavastorm Mountains.'\n**Journeyman's Book of Human Culture**\nYou say, 'Befallen.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Into Befallen'.\nVivian Selgan says 'Deep in Befallen lay Ice Boned Skeletons. Their crystallized marrow is what I need to inscribe this pattern. Hunt around down there for a bit and bring me four of them.'\n**Task given to get your Journeyman's Book:**\n1) Kill 20 Ice boned skeletons in Befallen\n2) Loot four Crystalized Marrow\n3) Hand Vivian the marrow\n4) Kill 10 willowisps\n5) Loot one Burned Out Lightstone\n6) Return Lightstone to Vivian\n_Receive Journeyman's Book._\n**Expert's Book of Human Culture**\nYou say, 'The Hole.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Searching Old Paineel'.\nVivian Selgan says 'You think you're ready for the hole do you? This place is ripe with magical energies. I need you to put some of the elemental warriors to rest and bring me twenty drops of mercury.'\n**Task given to get your Expert's Book:**\n1) Kill 50 elemental warriors in The Hole\n2) Loot 10 Drops of Mercury\n3) Return Mercury to Vivian\n4) Kill 5 Elemental Monstrosities in The Hole\n5) Loot 1 Drop of Mercury\n6) Return Mercury to Vivian\n_Receive Expert's Book._\n**Master's Book of Human Culture**\nYou say, 'The Dragon Necropolis.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Delve the Necropolis'.\nVivian Selgan says 'Within the tomb of the Dragon Necropolis you will find a race of rat creatures.. In order to create this symbol I need lots of their old dragon horns. Return to me when you have acquired these items.'\n**Task given to get your Master's Book:**\n1) Kill 80 Chetari-aligned NPCs in Dragon Necropolis\n2) Loot 2 Old Dragon Horns\n3) Return Horns to Vivian\n4) Kill 5 Phase Spiders\n5) Loot 1 Phase Spider Silk\n6) Return 1 Phase Spider Silk to Vivian\n_Receive Master's Book._\n**Grandmaster's Book of Human Culture**\nYou say, 'What valley?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Ripples in Stillmoon'.\nVivian Selgan says 'Ready for something more challenging, eh? Very well. The goblins in stillmoon temple are known for their resilient skin. For this next pattern I need four of the thickest rough goblin skins you can find. Go collect a large quantity and bring me the finest of the haul. You may wish to seek out some operatives in Lavastorm to aid you in tracking down these rare items.'\n**Task given to get your Grandmaster's Book:**\n1) Kill 120 Denizens of Stillmoon in Stillmoon Temple\n2) Loot 80 Rough Patches of Goblin Skin\n3) Return Skins to Vivian\n4) Kill 10 Denizens of Stillmoon Temple\n5) Loot 1 Stone Necklace\n6) Return 1 Stone Necklace to Vivian\n_Receive Grandmaster's Book._\n..................................................................................\n**QEYNOS**\n_Find Tar Cordell in North Qeynos by the Priest of Discord, at +230, +395._\n**Ancestral Human Armor**\nYou say, 'Hail, Tar Cordell'\nTar Cordell says 'Hello \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. What brings you back 'ere? Wanted to be 'round yer own [kind] again?'\nYou say, 'My kind?'\nTar Cordell says 'Aye. A lot of us 'ave returned 'ome these past few months. Seems distrust is brewing among them other races. Now, I don't want to be accused of bigotry, some of those other kind are okay--dwarves and elves are pretty reliable--but the rest . . . you can't trust 'em. Like them blasted dark elves always plotting something. And those lizard things . . . don't even get me started with those. Folks don't feel safe out there anymore so they're coming back to the cities for protection. Why do you think I came back to 'ere! To be 'round more 'umans, folks I can [trust]!'\nYou say, 'Trust?'\nTar Cordell says 'Aye, you know what I mean. We need to stick together, form a unified front and let our enemies know we mean business. In fact, right now I'm making armor for the city militia. Hmm, you look like you'd be good in a fight. Perhaps you'd be interested in these armor designs. I can share my pattern [book] or even my armor [patterns] with you provided you don't go blabbing my trade secrets to no dark elves. Can't trust those kind!'\nYou say, 'What book?'\nTar Cordell says 'Excellent, I can make you a pattern book, but first I'm gonna need some materials. Bring me a fire beetle carapace for the cover, a patch of zombie skin for the pages, a golden bandit tooth for the clasp, and a lion tail to grind down and make a salve which will protect and preserve the finished product. I hear these resources can be found in Western Karana. Once I have these things, I can create the pattern book for ya.'\n_On handing in the items:_\nTar Cordell says 'Aye, well done, my friend! As promised, 'ere is the pattern book. It may take some practice to get a 'ang of these designs, but they should serve you well. Don't forget about us if a war breaks out. I want you up on those city walls with me, aye!'\nYou say, 'What patterns?'\nTar Cordell says 'Aye, I can give you these patterns provided you can help me with some missions for Qeynos. What do ya say? Can you help ol' Tar out? I need someone to spearhead expeditions to [Erud's Crossing], [Kedge Keep], the [Dragon Necropolis] or, if you've got the metal for it, the [valley] on the other side of the lavastorm mountains. I can reward you with some armor patterns for yer efforts. You know the drill. The more the danger, the more the reward! Choose wisely, now.'\n**Journeyman's Book of Human Culture**\nYou say, 'Erud's Crossing.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Clearing the Western Sea Lanes'.\nTar Cordell says 'Ha ha! I knew I could count on ya! Seems our ocean trade routes are in trouble again, my friend. I need ya' to travel over to Erud's Crossing and kill twenty o' dem sharks. That should clear the way a bit for our sailors! Bring me three lake pebbles from their stomachs as proof of your kills. Not that I don't trust ya, I just need something to show the boys when I let 'em know the way is clear.'\nTask details\n1) Kill 15 Sharks in Kerra Isle\n2) Loot three Lake Pebbles\n3) Return and hand in pebbles to Tar Cordell\n4) Kill 10 Will-O-Wisps\n5) Loot one Lightstone\n6) Return and hand in Lightstone to Tar Cordell\nWell done. Lucky I found you or that job never would have gotten done. As promised, 'ere's those armor runes. Let me know if you need any more of these [patterns]. Sure as the sunrise, there's always more work to be done 'round here.\nYou have been given: Journeyman's Book of Human Culture\n**Expert's Book of Human Culture**\nYou say, 'Kedge Keep.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Clearing the Eastern Sea Lanes'.\nTar Cordell says 'Our ocean trade routes still aren't as secure as we need 'em to be. Several of Qeynos' finer cargo vessels have disappeared while sailing from `ere to Freeport and Faydwer. Sure enough, the wreckage always turns up floating around Kedge Keep. Get over there an' wreck the place. Kill fifty mermaids and return to me with four vials of deepwater ink. That should clear the way for our ships.'\n**Name of task and hand-in dialogues needed.**\n1) Kill 40 Mermaids in Kedge Keep\n2) Loot 15 Deepwater Inks\n3) Deliver four Deepwater Inks to Tar Cordell\n4) Kill any five Cauldron Sharks in Kedge Keep\n5) Loot one Shark Skin\n6) Deliver one Shark Skin to Tar Cordell\n**Master's Book of Human Culture**\nYou say, 'Dragon Necropolis.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Scale and Bone'.\nTar Cordell says 'We've lost several expeditions into the dragon necropolis over the past few months. It's the rats that have been sneaking upon our ranks in those dark tunnels. Kill eighty of those things and return to me four old dragon horns. That should clear the depths out a bit.'\n**Hand-in dialogues and task details needed.**\n**Grandmaster's Book of Human Culture**\nYou say, 'Valley.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Lair of the Lavaspinner'.\nTar Cordell says 'Aye, glad you volunteered! Our scouts have been having a heap o' trouble in the dragon lands north of Lavastorm. Seems the spiders there have been tracking our movements and ambushing our scouts. I need you to lead an expedition into the Lavaspinner's Lair and slay six score denizens of the delve. Bring me four arachnid eye clusters as proof of your kills. You may wish to seek out some operatives in Lavastorm to aid you in tracking down these rare items.'\n**Dialogues and task details needed.**\n**Types of Armor**\n_Claviger - Berserker, Ranger, Rogue_\n_Sagacious - Druid, Monk_\n_Stalwart - Bard, Cleric, Paladin, Shadowknight, Warrior_\n_Stargazer - Enchanter, Magician, Necromancer, Wizard_\n- Elaborate Claviger Armband [item=37197]\n- Elaborate Claviger Boots [item=39179]\n- Elaborate Claviger Cuirass [item=37198]\n- Elaborate Claviger Gloves [item=39234]\n- Elaborate Claviger Greaves [item=36713]\n- Elaborate Claviger Helm [item=37199]\n- Elaborate Claviger Sleeves [item=55448]\n- Elaborate Sagacious Armband [item=38341]\n- Elaborate Sagacious Boots [item=38518]\n- Elaborate Sagacious Cuirass [item=36901]\n- Elaborate Sagacious Gloves [item=48579]\n- Elaborate Sagacious Greaves [item=36788]\n- Elaborate Sagacious Helm [item=38517]\n- Elaborate Sagacious Sleeves [item=37828]\n- Elaborate Stalwart Armband [item=36456]\n- Elaborate Stalwart Boots [item=37852]\n- Elaborate Stalwart Cuirass [item=37853]\n- Elaborate Stalwart Gloves [item=37854]\n- Elaborate Stalwart Helm [item=37855]\n- Elaborate Stalwart Sleeves [item=37856]\n- Elaborate Stargazer Armband [item=56609]\n- Elaborate Stargazer Boots [item=56610]\n- Elaborate Stargazer Breeches [item=56613]\n- Elaborate Stargazer Cap [item=56614]\n- Elaborate Stargazer Gloves [item=56612]\n- Elaborate Stargazer Robe [item=56611]\n- Elaborate Stargazer Sleeves [item=56615]\n- Elegant Sagacious Armband [item=71581]\n- Elegant Sagacious Boots [item=71580]\n- Elegant Sagacious Cuirass [item=71579]\n- Elegant Sagacious Gloves [item=71587]\n- Elegant Sagacious Greaves [item=71584]\n- Elegant Sagacious Helm [item=71589]\n- Elegant Sagacious Sleeves [item=71586]\n- Elegant Stalwart Armband [item=71208]\n- Elegant Stalwart Boots [item=71033]\n- Elegant Stalwart Cuirass [item=71020]\n- Elegant Stalwart Gloves [item=71620]\n- Elegant Stalwart Greaves [item=71528]\n- Elegant Stalwart Helm [item=71621]\n- Elegant Stalwart Sleeves [item=71560]\n- Intricate Claviger Armband [item=55449]\n- Intricate Claviger Boots [item=55450]\n- Intricate Claviger Cuirass [it