Stillmoon warlord [npc=17783]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Dragons of Norrath Progression (Dark Reign) [quest=3062]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 1a: Burning Arrows [quest=3108]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 1a: Creating an Antidote [quest=3107]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 1a: Greed of the Goblins [quest=3103]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 1b: Children of Gimblax [quest=3072]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 2a: Defend the Kirin Contact [quest=3126]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 2a: Recover the Lost Map [quest=3127]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 2a: Turn the Tides of the Sand [quest=3128]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 2b: Sickness of the Spirit [quest=3071]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 2c: Calling Emoush [quest=3060]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 3a: Protect the Waters [quest=3288]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 3a: Snowfoot Revenge [quest=3287]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 3a: The Sacred Scrolls [quest=3289]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 3b: History of the Isle [quest=3262]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 3b: Trial of Perseverance [quest=3067]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 3b: Volkara's Bite [quest=3059]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 4a: Goblin Dojo [quest=3076]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 4a: Guardian of the Sands [quest=3058]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 4b: An End to the Storms [quest=3089]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 5a: Origins of the Curse [quest=3263]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 5a: The Curse of Ju`rek [quest=3290]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tier 5b: In the Shadows [quest=3063]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tokens [quest=3134]\n- Norrath's Keepers: Forbin's Elixir [quest=3558]\n- Norrath's Keepers: Storming the Goblin Temple [quest=4230]\n**Era:** | !Dragons of Norrath\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Mar 13 18:29:08 2005\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n!**Faction with Norrath's Keepers**\n_The Norrath's Keepers camp can be found in the Lavastorm Mountains tunnels that lead to The Broodlands (they are in the tunnels west of the Broodlands). In order to begin more advanced tasks within the Norrath's Keepers camp, you must be of \"indifferent\" faction or higher._\n_There will be faction requirements as you move along in progression:_\n\\- Tier 1 requires \"indifferent\"+\n\\- Tier 2 requires \"amiable\"+\n\\- Tier 3 requires high \"amiable\"+\n\\- Tier 4 requires \"kindly\"+\n\\- Tier 5 requires \"warmly\"+\nDoN progression faction amounts for Norrath's Keepers\nYou start at -100: apprehensive (good toons)\nor start at -600: mid-threatening (evil toons)\n+100 (good toons): 5 tasks\n+600 (evil toons): 30 tasks\n0: indifferent. Start Tier 1.\n+30: 3 solo tasks\n+20: Children of Gimblax (group)\n+60: 3 extra tokens from junk missions\n110: amiable. Start Tier 2\n+30: 3 solo tasks\n+20: Sickness of the Spirit (group)\n+20: Calling Emoush (raid)\n+120: 6 extra tokens from junk missions\n300: mid-amiable (+400 on the faction window). Start Tier 3\n+30: 3 solo tasks\n+20: History of the Isle (group)\n+20: Trial of Perseverance (raid)\n+20: Volkara's Bite (raid)\n+120: 6 extra tokens from junk missions\n510: kindly.(+600 on the faction window) Start Tier 4\n+20: Guardian of the Sands (raid)\n+20: Goblin Dojo (raid)\n+20: An End to the Storms (raid)\n+180: 9 extra tokens from junk missions\n750: warmly. (+850 on the faction window) Start Tier 5\n+20: Origins of the Curse (group)\n+20: The Curse of Ju'rek (raid)\n+20: In the Shadows (raid)\n_There are several ways to increase faction:_\n\\- Kill Dark Reign guards (+1 per kill).\n\\- Wayfarer Mercenary Elanye's solo tasks (available at apprehensive **or lower**):\n\\-\\-\\- Blood of the Winged (+20)\n\\-\\-\\- Goblin Broth (+20)\n\\- Wayfarer Mercenary Bitral's solo tasks (available at apprehensive **or lower**):\n\\-\\-\\- Population Control (+20)\n\\-\\-\\- Gathering Silk (+20)\n\\- \"Norrath's Keepers Tokens\" are rewarded from all group missions and raids (LORE item, so turn it in each time you get one):\n\\-\\-\\- Turned in to Wayfarers Mercenary Youra (at apprehensive or lower) or Tatsujiro the Serene (in the Norrath's Keepers camp at indifferent+) (+20 faction each)\n\\- There are 37 non-progression group missions (the first eight are available at apprehensive):\n\\-\\-\\- Boldger Bristlebeard (Lavaspinner's Lair & Tirranun's Delve):\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Grounding the Drakes (apprehensive)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Lavaspinner's Locals (apprehensive)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Diving for Lavarocks (indifferent)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- The Drake Menace (indifferent)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Infested (amiable)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Lavaspinner Hunting (amiable)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Storming the Goblin Temple (kindly)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Forbin's Elixir (kindly)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- A Goblin's Escort (warmly)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- A Halfling's Greed (warmly)\n\\-\\-\\- Bianca Galbraith (Thundercrest Isles):\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Simple Task (apprehensive)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Throes of Contagion (apprehensive)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Scions of Thundercrest (indifferent)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Splitting the Storm (indifferent)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Holy Hour (amiable)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- The Creator (amiable)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Behind Closed Doors (kindly)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Lair Unguarded (kindly)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- House of the Autumn Rose (warmly)\n\\-\\-\\- Kanetheus Forestwalker (Stillmoon Temple & The Ascent):\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Animated Statue Plans (apprehensive)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Tracking the Kirin (apprehensive)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Death Comes Swiftly (indifferent)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Diseased Pumas (indifferent)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Best Laid Plans (amiable)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Storm Dragon Scales (amiable)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Scales of Justice (kindly)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Tea for Thy Master (kindly)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Signal Fires (warmly)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Sudden Tremors (warmly)\n\\-\\-\\- Gordish Frozenheart (Accursed Nest):\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Lair of the Blackwing (apprehensive)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Scrap Metal (apprehensive)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Spider's Eye (indifferent)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Dragon's Egg (indifferent)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Lost Comrades (amiable)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Web of Lies (amiable)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Clues (kindly)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Rivals (kindly)\n\\- There are two non-progression mini-raids:\n\\-\\-\\- Gordish Frozenheart:\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Circle of Drakes (amiable+)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- The Rampaging Monolith (amiable+)\n\\- There are three non-progression full-size raids:\n\\-\\-\\- Captain Areha Burina:\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Fanning the Flames (amiable+)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Reflections of Silver (high amiable+)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Kessdona's Perch (high amiable+)\n\\- You'll also gain faction regularly as you go through the progression itself.\n\n---\n\n**Tier 1: Gift of the Keepers**\n_Upon reaching indifferent faction (and if Level 65+), you can begin progression by speaking with Chieftain Relae Aderi:_\nYou say, 'Hail, Chieftain Relae Aderi'\nChieftain Relae Aderi nods his head in acknowledgement and smiles. 'Welcome to the Norrath's Keepers' enclave. We are busy protecting the way of the right and honorable now. Our world is at a crossroads and we must endeavor to ensure we maintain order as much as we can. Should you wish to [help] us, do say so.'\nYou say, 'I wish to help you'\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'Those are encouraging words and we will gladly take your offer. Please see Nylaen Kel`Ther, my trusted friend. While his tasks may not seem glorious, they are necessary for us to gain a foothold against the Dark Reign, the followers of Lanys T`Vyl, the Child of Hate. They have their grim eyes set on seeing the end of us all. To begin, from the volcano, we need ingredients to create an antidote, help collecting Delvian teeth for our arrowheads, and handling goblin greed in the Stillmoon Temple. When you satisfy these needs, then we shall speak again.'\nYou have received a character flag!\n_Now talk with Private Nylaen Kel`Ther, next to Chieftain Relae Aderi to receive three different solo tasks:_\nCreating an Antidote\nBurning Arrows\nGreed of the Goblins\n_After completing these tasks, speak with Chieftain Relae Aderi again:_\nYou say, 'Hail, Chieftain Relae Aderi'\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'Welcome back, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. News of your good deeds is passing quickly through our ranks. I wish we could say your work is done here, but it is not. The goblins of Tirranun's Delve heard of your efforts against their kin in the Stillmoon Temple and they have vowed revenge. One in particular, Gimblax, plans to hunt you down. We know where he is now and if you move quickly, perhaps you can reach him first. Speak to Dilar Nelune and he will give you further guidance.'\nYou have received a character flag!\n_Next, speak with Keeper Dilar Nelune to receive a single-group task:_\nChildren of Gimblax\n_After completing this task, speak with Chieftain Relae Aderi again:_\nYou say, 'Hail, Chieftain Relae Aderi'\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'It is time to repay you for all you have done. Firiona Vie has chosen to share a divine gift with you that will only grow stronger if you continue to help us. This magic to be instilled with you is a fitting reward, but you will fast lose it should you ever aid the Dark Reign -- in fact, it will disappear instantly!'\nYou have received a character flag!\nYou have gained the ability \"Gift of the Keepers\" at a cost of 0 ability points.\n_The new ability \"Gift of the Keepers\" gives a maximum stats increase of 10 per stat._\n\n---\n\n**Tier 2: Valor of the Keepers**\n_You must have amiable faction standing or better to request Tier 2 tasks. You can raise faction by doing the miscellaneous missions offered by the NPCs in the camp (each mission results in a Token which can be turned in for +20 faction). First speak with Chieftain Relae Aderi again:_\nYou say, 'Hail, Chieftain Relae Aderi'\n_If below amiable, you see:_\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'Your contributions certainly do shine, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, but to further help us is a matter of trust. You must prove that you are ready for the higher levels of confidentiality by aiding us with more work.'\n_If amiable or higher, you see:_\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'I am delighted to see that you got to Gimblax before he was able to get to you. It would be a great loss to us if he were to find you and carry out his plans! You have done so well for us that we have much more for you to do if you are still willing. If you wish to help us turn the sand goblins' anger, recover the lost map, and protect our kirin contact, please speak to Nylaen Kel`Ther and he will give you more [work]. May the light of the world shine upon you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!'\nYou say, 'What work?'\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'This may be presumptuous and I'm not certain the kind of company you keep, but should you find the will and way, there are stories of a dragon of lava that goes by the very name of that volcano, Tirranun. We have found an entrance that would seem to lead to its lair, but none of us have found the numbers or bravery to attempt to find it. With your associations, perhaps you would have better luck, at your leisure of course. We must learn all we can about the dragons for we fear that the Dark Reign wish to gain control over them to use against us. In the meantime, we have bestowed upon you a reward for your assistance. Safe travels, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'\nYou have received a character flag!\n_(This flag grants you access to the non-progression raid \"Fanning the Flames\".)_\n_Now, speak with Private Nylaen Kel`Ther (need to be Level 67+) to receive three solo tasks:_\nTurn the Tides of the Sand\nRecover the Lost Map\nDefend the Kirin Contact\n_After completing these three tasks, speak with Chieftain Relae Aderi again:_\nYou say, 'Hail, Chieftain Relae Aderi'\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'Your advancement and accomplishments are many and you have our gratitude, but I must implore you to continue to help us. There are few as capable as you to accept the challenges that lie ahead. Dilar Nelune has been charged with giving you the information needed to making an offering of peace and reassurance to our kirin contact. Also, I have permitted Ekiltu Verlor to give you access to all the information you would need to bring an end to the terrible dervish, Emoush. Bring me evidence you have overcome this challenge.'\nYou have received a character flag!\n_Next, hail Keeper Dilar Nelune to receive a group mission:_\nSickness of the Spirit\n_After that, speak with Lieutenant Ekiltu Verlor for your first raid event:_\nCalling Emoush (6-24 players)\n_Loot the \"Glowing Stone Fragment\" from Emoush the Destroyer, and bring it to the Chieftain to complete Tier 2 progression:_\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'Norrath's Keepers acknowledges your steadfastness and resolve in our name and Firiona herself wishes to strengthen the gift she has bestowed upon you so you may serve us with greater power.'\nYou have received a character flag!\n_You get 1-2 AAs and the Special AA \"Valor of the Keepers\" which adds 250 hp/mana/end to your base stats. You also receive your 69th level spell/tome:_\nBard - Spell: Storm Blade\nBeastlord - Spell: Growl of the Panther\nBerserker - Tome of Destroyer's Volley\nCleric - Spell: Blessed Touch (scribes as \"Ward of Retribution\")\nDruid - Spell: Serpent Vines\nEnchanter - Spell: Rune of Rikkukin\nMagician - Spell: Summon: Molten Orb\nMonk - Tome of Dragon Fang\nNecromancer - Spell: Shadow Orb\nPaladin - Tome of Guard of Righteousness\nRanger - Spell: Earthen Shackles\nRogue - Tome of Assassin's Feint\nShadowknight - Tome of Soul Shield\nShaman - Spell: Spirit of the Panther\nWarrior - Tome of Cyclone Attack\nWizard - Spell: Claw of Vox\n\n---\n\n**Tier 3: Embrace of the Keepers**\n_To request Tier 3 content, you must be at least high amiable with Norrath's Keepers (+400) and be at least Level 68._\nYou say, 'Hail, Chieftain Relae Aderi'\nChieftain Relae Aderi bows as he recognizes you. 'Your good deeds in the name of the Keepers is gaining you a great reputation and the requests for your assistance come from more and more places. I would ask you to continue with your good work and we still have several tasks you may be interested in. Your skill and prowess have earned you entrance into the more [lauded] circles of our ranks, so what we ask now is of greater importance.'\nYou have received a character flag!\n_(This flag grants you access to the non-progression raids \"Reflections of Silver\" & \"Kessdona's Perch\".)_\nYou say, 'Lauded?'\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'Indeed. The people who now know and respect you are some of the closest to Firiona Vie, the Chosen of Tunare, and the leader of Norrath's Keepers. If you wish to stand alongside those who support and serve the Chosen, then you must continue to prove your worth as they all did. There are many [quests] that must be undertaken. You must speak to Nylaen Kel`Ther for those. And you must meet Areha Burina. She has uncovered a path to the [wyrms] of Stillmoon Temple, though our interest in them right now isn't immediate or required.'\nYou say, 'What quests?'\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'You must protect the purity of the waters of Stillmoon Temple, secure the knowledge of the scrolls of the temple, and thwart the attack of the Snowfoot goblins. Speak to Nylaen again and he will give you more information. When you are successful, return to me and I will direct you to my officers for more challenging work.'\nYou say, 'What wyrms?'\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'There are two dragons that protect and serve in the Stillmoon Temple and Ascent -- Rikkukin and Kessdona. They are mates of a breed of dragon made of precious metals. They are believed to be the first children of Veeshan on Norrath. They are dragons of great wisdom and knowledge, but don't be fooled by their sleek beauty. Once in the past, I believe dragons of their kind had betrayed our own Firiona. We fear they intend to betray the good of Norrath too if we lend our minds and hearts to them. You will nearly need an army of your own to overcome these dragons and we have no requirement of you to that end, but they are yours to discover.'\n_Speak with Private Nylaen Kel`Ther to receive three solo tasks:_\nProtect the Waters\nThe Sacred Scrolls\nSnowfoot Revenge\n_Once done those tasks, speak with the Chieftain again for a flag:_\nYou say, 'Hail, Chieftain Relae Aderi'\nChieftain Relae Aderi nods. 'We are always on the defensive and must continue to keep our minds and spirits up and charging ahead. The tasks we present to you now are more daunting. Having proven yourself and gained our trust brings greater challenges to you. We ask you to learn the history of Thundercrest Isle, endure a Trial of Perseverance issued by the goblins in the Stillmoon Temple, and take on the great spider queen, Volkara. You'll need to speak to Ekiltu Verlor for particulars and then you must return to me and give me proof you have overcome these tasks. And do introduce yourself to Areha Burina.'\nYou have received a character flag!\n_Next, speak with Keeper Dilar Nelune for a group mission:_\nHistory of the Isle\n_You'll also need to complete two progression raids from Lieutenant Ekiltu Verlor:_\nTrial of Perseverance (6-24 players)\nVolkara's Bite (6-42 players)\n_Loot \"Goblin Warlord's Beads\" from the warlord in the \"Trial of Perseverance\", and loot \"Lava Spider Spinners\" from Volkara in \"Volkara's Bite\". Hand in these two items to Chieftain Relae Aderi:_\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'You've become a great contributor to our cause, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. There will be gifts bestowed upon you for this!'\nYou have received a character flag!\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'Your deeds continue to astound and impress us, even Firiona Vie has taken notice of you as we carry on about your good work. She has decided to grant you greater power once again.'\nYou have received a character flag!\n_You get 1-2 AAs and the Special AA \"Embrace of the Keepers\" which increases your buff slot limit._\n\n---\n\n**Tier 4: Power of the Keepers**\n_In order to continue on in Tier 4, you must, again, have kindly faction. Hail Commander Zaerr Ty`Dar for another flag:_\nYou say, 'Hail, Chieftain Relae Aderi'\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'Every day we learn more about the Nest and, sadly, the intentions of the Dark Reign toward the good folk of Norrath. These are indeed troubling times, but I have no doubt that we will prevail with Firiona at our side. Go speak to Ekiltu Verlor. With your skills and talents, we believe you may have a good chance to overcome Shogurei, the Guardian of the Sands. With a smaller force, you may be able to accept the challenge issued by the goblins of Thundercrest Isles. We must attempt to beat this trial ahead of the Dark Reign so that perhaps the goblins may favour us and ease their anger towards us. You must bring proof you have conquered both of these tasks.'\nYou have received a character flag!\n_Now, you need to complete two progression raids from Lieutenant Ekiltu Verlor:_\nGuardian of the Sands (6-42 players)\nGoblin Dojo (6-24 players)\n_Loot \"Quintessence of Sand\" and \"Meditation Stone\" from those two raids (respectively), and give them to Chieftain Relae Aderi:_\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'You are indeed rising in everyone's estimation as you continue to overcome great odds Your efforts will not go unnoticed.'\nYou have received a character flag!\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'You have done a great service to Norrath's Keepers. What you have learned may have given us the edge we need over the Dark Reign. They are forever sending spies and doing all they can to undermine our efforts to bring peace and harmony in Norrath. While you have risen in our estimation since we first set eyes upon you, you would like to put your [dedication] to the test before we admit you as a Keeper.'\nYou say, 'My dedication?'\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'Lanys T`Vyl and her Dark Reign lackeys grow stronger each day and there is little time to waste. Areha Burina has some extremely challenging work for you, particularly a meeting with the dragon of [storms].'\nYou say, 'What dragon of storms?'\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'We expect that Yar`Lir, the storm dragon, is exceedingly powerful and unique. We have learned from you and the scrolls obtained from the temple, that Yar`Lir is the dragon responsible for casting a veil of magic and storms over the Nest to protect it from view and keep it hospitable for the wyrms. You must go to see her, but I would expect her to be none-to-pleased to see you there and you will likely need to [defend] yourself. However, we would not be the keepers of these lands if we did not at least attempt to approach her civilly.'\nYou say, 'Defend myself?'\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'Should she attack you and you are forced to draw your weapons, know this -- killing her will disrupt the veil she casts here. This might be the opportunity that the Dark Reign looks for, but we will contend with that from here. There is more, we believe, as we haven't found where most of the dragons eggs are kept in the Nest. This is why we are sending you -- to learn what you can. Also, if you can, retrieve one of Yar`Lir's fangs. Areha Burina will lead you to her.'\nYou have received a character flag!\n_Now, speak with Captain Areha Burina to request another progression raid:_\nAn End to the Storms (6-54 players)\n_Loot \"Yar'lir's Fang\" from this raid, and hand it to Chieftain Relae Aderi:_\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'Our efforts to keep the Dark Reign at bay have been furthered by your honor and prowess, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. And once more Firiona wishes to grant you even greater magic and strength to carry you forward.'\n_You get 1-2 AAs + the Special AA \"Power of the Keepers\" (increases chance of critical hits/spells, heals, and DoTs)_\n\n---\n\n**Tier 5: Sanctity of the Keepers**\n_In order to continue on in Tier 5, you must have at least warmly faction. Speak with Chieftain Relae Aderi:_\nYou say, 'Hail, Chieftain Relae Aderi'\nChieftain Relae Aderi says, 'As we feared, Yar'lir was not kind to us, but it is to be expected. This fang will be treasured and protected while our researcher study it. It is not time to dawdle though. I'm sure you're already aware that the death of Yar'Lir caused a great disturbance in the Nest. Each time the storm dragon's magic is interrupted, the Nest and resting place of the eggs of the Nest's dragons become darker and we're not sure why. In order to learn more, please talk to Dilar Nelune and Ekiltu Verlor. They have new work for you -- to investigate a curse in the Nest and to learn about a dark drake by the name of Ju'rek. You will need to bring me proof of your success.'\n_Next, speak with Keeper Dilar Nelune for a group mission:_\nOrigins of the Curse\n_You'll also need to complete another progression raid from Lieutenant Ekiltu Verlor:_\nThe Curse of Ju'rek (6-24 players)\n_Loot \"Diseased Wing Fragment\" from this raid, and hand it to Chieftain Relae Aderi:_\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'Gracious, that curse certainly seems to run deep. You have accomplished what very few have been able to and we'd like to reward you. As you may have already ascertained, there is a [dragon] in the Nest that we have yet to confront. That falls to you now.'\nYou have received a character flag!\nYou say, 'What dragon?'\nChieftain Relae Aderi says 'We hear that the dragon in the Nest was Yar'Lir's mate, also a dragon of storms. But as you confronted Yar'Lir and disrupted her magic, the twisting caverns of the Nest were fully bared and a sickly darkness washed over them. It seems the curse you investigated was somehow unleash\n\n...[Walkthrough truncated for in-game performance]...",
