      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Lavastorm Mountains 3.0 [zone=31]\n**Who:**\n- Lieutenant Ekiltu Verlor [npc=17798]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 70\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Faction\n- Loot\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Faction Required:**\nNorrath's Keepers (Min: Kindly)\n**Related Zones:**\n- Thundercrest Isles: Goblin Dojo [zone=1051]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Disciple of Earth [npc=17993]\n- Disciple of Fire [npc=17994]\n- Disciple of Metal [npc=17995]\n- Disciple of Water [npc=17996]\n- Disciple of Wood [npc=17997]\n- Grandmaster Beetle [npc=17998]\n- Grandmaster Puma [npc=17999]\n- Grandmaster Snake [npc=18006]\n- Master of Contentment [npc=18002]\n- Master of Deceit [npc=18003]\n- Master of Doubt [npc=18004]\n- Master of Rage [npc=18005]\n- Silk [npc=18000]\n- Steel [npc=18001]\n- Storm Reach Sensei [npc=17820]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Dragons of Norrath Progression (Dark Reign) [quest=3062]\n- Dragons of Norrath Progression (Norrath's Keepers) [quest=3061]\n- Norrath's Keepers Tokens [quest=3134]\n**Era:** | !Dragons of Norrath\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Raid\n**Min. # of Players:** | 6\n**Max. # of Players:** | 24\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Apr 20 17:10:55 2005\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**For an overview of the Dragons of Norrath expansion, see this wiki article.**\n**For an overview of progression, see quest entries for Norrath's Keepers [quest=3061] and the Dark Reign [quest=3062].**\n\n---\n\n_This raid task begins with Lieutenant Ekiltu Verlor ( **click for map image**) in the Norrath's Keepers camp of the Lavastorm Mountains._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting this task:_\n\\- Minimum 6 players; maximum 24 players\n\\- Must be kindly faction with Norrath's Keepers\n\\- Completion of all Tier 3 tasks and flags\n\\- **This raid requires six live players present in the zone**\nYou say, 'Hail, Lieutenant Ekiltu Verlor'\nLieutenant Ekiltu Verlor says 'Those faithful to the way of Norrath's Keepers may take on the greatest challenges and prove their worth to Firiona Vie.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Goblin Dojo'.\nIt is peculiar that the goblins in Thundercrest Isles have issued a challenge to Norrathians. As much as we don't often bend to threats and arrogance, we are curious what the outcome of this challenge might be -- and it's better that we find out and be prepared for it, rather than the Dark Reign. Be on your guard. It could very well be a trap.\n\n---\n\n**Task Steps**\nTouch the portal to Thundercrest Isles 0/1 (The Broodlands)\nEnter the Dojo 0/1 (Thundercrest Isles)\n**TASK LOCKS HERE**\nOvercome the Stormreach Challenge 0/1 (Thundercrest Isles)\n\n---\n\n**Entry**\n_Approach the Storm Reach Sensei, who opens the doors to the Dojo and enters._\nStorm Reach Sensei says 'Welcome to the Storm Reach Dojo. I am pleased that you have taken up our humble challenge. As soon as you are ready, bring at least six of your fellows into the dojo and we shall begin. Be aware that this is a contest to the death. Do not enter the dojo unless you are prepared to pay that price.'\n_Six players must be inside the Dojo before this event activates. Don't enter the Dojo until you're ready._\n\n---\n\n**The Event: Waves of Goblins & The First Wave**\n_In this event, you will be fighting against waves of goblins. Six people must be present in the dojo in order to activate the event._\n_The numbers in the waves:_\n\\- 1st wave: five goblins\n\\- 2nd wave: four goblins\n\\- 3rd wave: three goblins\n\\- 4th wave: two goblins\n\\- 5th wave: one named\n_Upon zoning in, you are dropped at the portal to the dojo. Enter it, and approach Storm Reach Sensei in the middle of the opposite wall. Your would-be opponents are all spawned already, but aren't attackable yet. You'll see the following:_\nThe Storm Reach Sensei says, 'Good, you have decided to meet the challenge. I will not bore you with unworthy tales of our training methods or our meager accomplishments, certainly your own deeds far outshine our own. We are but meager servants to the Strom Mistress, Yar`Lir, and are of little consequence. We have been asked to test you and, certainly, ourselves in a battle to the death. The residents of this place are away at tasks beyond those such as we, and for a short while we have this room to ourselves. We must finish our contest before they return, and so there is little time for pleasantries.'\nThe Storm Reach Sensei says, 'A winner will be declared if they are the only combatants alive in this room. Your first challenge will be to defeat the Disciples of The Five Elements. Certainly they will be easily defeated by such mighty beings, but it is within their hearts to try. Your battle will begin in one minute. Prepare yourselves.'\nIn a clear, ringing voice, The Disciple of Metal says, 'Please forgive my poor humor, but I am very eager to test your mettle.'\nThe Disciple of Earth rumbles, 'When we have defeated you, I shall see that your corpses rot in the soil as is proper.'\nThe Disciple of Fire shouts, 'I make no apologies. I shall burn your hearts out!'\nThe Disciple of Water says, 'Ah, yes. You must forgive Fire, for he cares little for pleasantries. It is part of his charm. You most certainly will be worthy opponents. I am honored to face you.'\nThe Disciple of Wood says, 'May our efforts here earn favor with those that watch over us all.'\n_The first wave attacks: Five disciples:_\n\\- Disciple of Earth: hits 240-1500, average 630, ~83,000 hitpoints\n\\- Disciple of Fire: hits 100-700, average 350, ~57,000 hitpoints\n\\- Disciple of Metal: hits 300-1300, average 690, ~60,000 hitpoints\n\\- Disciple of Water: hits 100-700, average 300, ~65,000 hitpoints\n\\- Disciple of Wood: hits 170-900, average 460, ~78,000 hitpoints\n_Upon the death of the fifth disciple, you see:_\nThe Storm Reach Sensei says, 'Congratulations! You have defeated the Disciples of the Five Elements. You have proven yourself worthy to face the Four Emotions. They have mastered their emotions and from them they gain strength. Each has become a conduit for the emotions of our kind, a paradigm, if you will. Certainly you shall defeat them, for you are the champions of your people and they are slaves. We shall begin again in two minutes. Rest and consult with each other, if you have need.'\n\n---\n\n**The Event: The Second Wave**\n_Two minutes after completion of the first wave, the Masters attack:_\nThe Master of Rage shouts, 'I hate you! I will rend you into bite-sized chunks of flesh and feed them to the puma!' Rage's face darkens with blood and flecks of spittle fly from his mouth as he pants and stares at his enemies.\nThe Master of Deceit smiles broadly. 'You certainly will find Rage difficult to stop. I see it boiling up inside many of you. Allow it to take over, and Rage will ruin you.'\nThe Master of Doubt mutters, 'I. . . You. . . ' he sighs, 'I do not know what will happen next. I see the same misgiving in some of you. Could it be that you are like me? No, that seems unlikely.'\nThe Master of Contentment drawls, 'Ah! I am pleased to meet you all. This is a fine challenge for us, is it not? I find this sort of exercise invigorating, though rarely do I find invigoration to be a good thing.'\n_The four masters attack:_\n\\- Master of Contentment: hits 190-990, average 490, ~100,000 hitpoints\n\\- Master of Deceit: hits 310-1500, average 770, ~110,000 hitpoints\n\\- Master of Doubt: hits 240-1020, average 500, ~101,000 hitpoints, casts \"Doubt\" and \"Mental Discord\"\n\\- Master of Rage: hits 80-1200, average 540, ~98,000 hitpoints, rampages\n_Upon the death of the fourth master, you see:_\nThe Storm Reach Sensei says, 'Well done. It is rare that an opponent is able to defeat the goblin Emotions. Your next test will be greater, I fear. You must face our three Animals. These are grandmasters of our arts and have never suffered defeat against opponents outside of these grand islands of the sky. You look weary. You shall have three minutes to prepare for the next contest.'\n\n---\n\n**The Event: The Third Wave**\n_Three minutes after the previous wave, the three Grandmasters attack:_\n\\- Grandmaster Beetle: hits 150-850, average 510, ~152,000 hitpoints, casts \"Whirling Beetle Strike\"\n\\- Grandmaster Puma: hits 150-800, average 400,~140,000 hitpoints\n\\- Grandmaster Snake: hits 120-730, average 280, ~126,000 hitpoints, casts \"Venomed Mist\"\n_Upon the death of the third grandmaster, you see:_\nThe Storm Reach Sensei says, 'Amazing, simply amazing! Never before have our grandmasters been defeated by anyone other than your next opponents. Prepare yourself, for next you must face Silk and Steel. You have four minutes to prepare, use those minutes wisely.'\n\n---\n\n**The Event: The Fourth Wave**\n_Four minutes after the third wave, \"Steel\" and \"Silk\" attack:_\nIn a voice more fluent and soft than any you've heard a goblin use, Silk says, 'Forgive my brother. He has a keen mind but a blunt mouth. We look forward to this test of our skills. Thank you for honoring us by accepting the challenge.'\n\\- Steel: hits 130-830, average 350, ~221,000 hitpoints, highly resistant to weapons\n\\- Silk: hits 30-420, average 210, ~202,000 hitpoints, flurries, casts \"Corporeal Torment\"\n\n---\n\n**The Event: The Final Wave**\n_Upon the death of Steel and Silk, you see:_\nThe Storm Reach Sensei says, 'Wonderful! You have defeated all of the students of the Storm Reach Dojo! Celebrate your victory. Remember this day.'\nThe Storm Reach Sensei says, 'You have beaten all of my students, and have only had an advantage in numbers. Experience has taught me that such advantages usually lead to disaster caused by overconfidence or reliance on the lesser skills of others. Today you have proven that my experience is not always correct, a humbling moment.'\nThe Storm Reach Sensei says, 'You should return to those that sent you and tell them of your success. It will be a moment of shame for me to return to my mistress and explain the defeat of my students. I offer you my humble congratulations.'\nThe Storm Reach Sensei says, 'However, our challenge is not over. You were to defeat all of the members of the Storm Reach Dojo to prove your worth. You have indeed defeated all of the students of my humble dojo, but you have not defeated the master of this insignificant school. To complete the challenge, you must defeat the school's master.'\n_Now, Storm Reach Sensei attacks._\n_Storm Reach Sensei hits for a max ~3,100; has ~336,000 hitpoints; casts \"Whirling Smash\" and \"Fist of Mastery\"; and single-target rampages._\n\n---\n\n**Completion & Loot**\nStorm Reach Sensei has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nStorm Reach Sensei's corpse falls slowly to the floor, a small smile on his face.\nYou've done well. Thank you for representing us.\n_The Storm Reach Sensei drops 6x \"Meditation Stone\" (progression item) + 1 item from this loot table:_\nKilt of the North Winds\nLeaguewalker Leggings\nThunderheart\nVestment of the Far Horizon\n_Rewards:_\n15 Radiant Crystals\n1x \"Norrath's Keepers Token\" (faction **turn-in** [quest=3134] item)\n_Note: If doing this raid as part of progression, you'll want to check in with some NPCs to make sure your flags are up to date. See **this quest entry** [quest=3061] for more details._\n**Submitted by:** Saraban of Darkwind\n- Kilt of the North Winds [item=36008]\n- Leaguewalker Leggings [item=36791]\n- Meditation Stone [item=34992]\n- Radiant Crystal [item=34988]\n- Thunderheart [item=35008]\n- Vestment of the Far Horizon [item=39052]",
