      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- North Ro 2.0 [zone=24]\n**Who:**\n- Tak`Valnakor [npc=20551]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 70\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Loot\n- Spell\n**Quest Items:**\n- Broken Section of a Sandstone Tablet [item=47358]\n- Part of a Sandstone Tablet [item=47356]\n- Piece of a Sandstone Tablet [item=47355]\n- Portion of a Sandstone Tablet [item=47357]\n- Sandstone Tablet Chunk [item=47354]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Root of Ro: The Key to the Past [zone=346]\n- Ruins of Takish-Hiz [zone=345]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Beau`Dril The Queen`s Defender [npc=20550]\n- Krylin [npc=20552]\n- a chest - The Key to the Past [npc=21583]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Access to the Theater of Blood/Plane of Music [quest=3444]\n- PoR Level 70 Spell #2: The Burning Prince [quest=3391]\n**Era:** | !Prophecy of Ro\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Mon Mar 6 16:23:33 2006\nModified: Wed Sep 10 06:45:32 2025 | | This task has at least 3 available difficulties: Levels 58, 63, and 66+. Each have different possible loot rewards associated with them.\nTak`Valnakor [npc=20551] may be found at +6885, -1350.\nYou say, 'Hail, Tak`Valnakor'\nTak`Valnakor says 'Hello fair adventurer. I wonder what brings a Human way out here? Could you be a student of [Archeology] like myself?'\nYou say, 'I am a student of Archeology.'\nTak`Valnakor says 'Yes, I am studying an ancient race of Elves that thrived eons ago near this area. Why, look at these many trinkets I have discovered. Here, take a look at this. This is some sort of diary etched into this stone tablet. So far I've translated that the owners name was [Krylin].'\nYou say, 'Krylin?'\nTak`Valnakor says 'Hmm, yes, that is his name. He apparently was the queen's footman. Oh how I wish I could only meet him as I have so many questions to ask him. It seems he was beginning to record some sort of disaster that befell his city. Alas, I have so far [failed] to translate the rest of this tablet.'\nYou say, 'Failed?'\nTak`Valnakor says 'Correct. I am missing some key glyphs that prevent me from deciphering any more of his texts. But perhaps I could [convince] you to explore an area that I am now turning my interest towards.'\nYou say, 'You can convince me.'\nTak`Valnakor says 'Wonderful! Then I shall let you in on a secret. I have in fact, just discovered this [ancient city]! It lay undisturbed for untold centuries till a massive storm came and unearthed it before my very eyes!'\nYou say, 'Ancient city?'\nTak`Valnakor says 'Yes, go there now and look for any trace of this Krylin. I have a feeling the mystery shall unravel once we find out more about him.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Key To The Past'.\nHead to the Ruins of Takish-Hiz.\nYou have entered Ruins of Takish-Hiz.\nThe direction to the entry to your instanced zone(s) have been marked on your compass.\nKrylin [npc=20552] is in a shattered building just past the Ghost along the wall, at -415, -25.\nYou say, 'Hail, Krylin'\nKrylin says 'Who seeks to disturb my [endless toiling]? Is it another specter of my past? . . .Or perhaps a figment of my long forgotten memory that now seeks to haunt my tortured existence. . .'\nYou say, 'What endless toiling?'\nKrylin says 'Cursed are we. Forever between life and death we are forced to labor away the ages. We do not know why or for what purpose other than this was our decree. If only [she] could be summoned. . .she would surely help to end our woes.'\nYou say, 'Who is she?'\nKrylin says 'The one who has not forgotten us. She was sure she was just about to [discover] the evil that lurked behind the veil.'\nYou say, 'Discover?'\nKrylin says 'Yes. . .she had begun to chronicle her discoveries when disaster struck. . .now the pieces of her journal remain scattered within the remains of the Root.'\nThe entrance to the instanced zone is in the North East of Ruins of Takish-Hiz at +725, -575.\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered The Root of Ro.\nYou have to loot four chunks of a tablet, which can drop from any mob: a Sandstone Tablet Chunk [item=47354], a Piece of a Sandstone Tablet [item=47355], a Part of a Sandstone Tablet [item=47356], and a Portion of a Sandstone Tablet [item=47357].\nThe last piece, a Broken Section of a Sandstone Tablet [item=47358], drops off Beau`Dril The Queen`s Defender [npc=20550] at the far end of the zone **(/loc?)**. She will attack, enrage, and flurry, hitting for up to 1200.\nBeauDril The Queens Defender has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\n--You have looted a A Broken Section of a SandStone Tablet.--\nYour task 'The Key To The Past' has been updated.\nReturn to Tak`Valnakor in North Ro and hand in all five pieces of the tablet.\nAfter handing the fragments to Tak'Valnakor, he gingerly places them upon his work table. Deftly he assembles an ancient sandstone tablet all complete but for a few missing chunks. He scans over the glyphs and smiles wildly. 'Yes, yes. This explains much. Thank you for your help. An answer is slowly beginning to emerge but it appears we are not done yet my friend!'\nA chest will spawn with one item of loot. You have unlocked the next quest in the series: The Burning Prince.\n_Chest loot level 58_\nSand-Covered Axe [item=132708]\nSand-Covered Epaulettes [item=132710]\n????\n_Chest loot level 63_\nSand-Encrusted Cloak [item=132705]\n????\n????\n_Chest loot level 66+_\nSand-Blasted Axe [item=48505]\nSand-Blasted Plate Sleeves [item=49237]\n????\n**Need confirmation as to what loot drops from each tier chest, there are also likely rewards from this mission that are not linked to this quest page yet.**\n**Submitted by:** Jolo\n- Root Tender Totem [item=47473]\n- Sand-Covered Axe [item=132708]\n- Sand-Covered Epaulettes [item=132710]\n- Sandswirled Mask [item=48807]",
    },
