      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- North Ro 2.0 [zone=24]\n**Who:**\n- Tak`Valnakor [npc=20551]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 70\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Loot\n- Spell\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Related Zones:**\n- Ruins of Takish-Hiz: The Burning Prince [zone=377]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Priest Coltrolin [npc=21585]\n- Priest Detrituss [npc=21586]\n- Priest Kaltricor [npc=21587]\n- Priest Nalmon [npc=21588]\n- Priest Taslin [npc=21589]\n- Prince Tak`Salir [npc=21590]\n- Queen Tak`Yaliz [npc=20324]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Access to the Theater of Blood/Plane of Music [quest=3444]\n- PoR Level 70 Spell #1: The Key To The Past [quest=3390]\n- PoR Level 70 Spell #3: Message to the Past [quest=3497]\n**Era:** | !Prophecy of Ro\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Mon Mar 6 16:29:21 2006\nModified: Sat Aug 17 07:51:07 2024 | | **This task has at least 3 available difficulties: Levels 58, 63, and 66+. Each have different possible loot rewards associated with them.**\n_Tak`Valnakor may be found at +6885, -1350._\nYou say, 'Hail, Tak`Valnakor'\nTak`Valnakor says 'Welcome back \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. I've spent some time looking over the tablets you brought me and I believe I am begging to understand them. They seem to make references to rumors of a group of acolytes of the Burning Prince within the elven community that met in secret in the years leading up to the destruction of Takish`Hiz. I'm uncertain as to the author, but I suspect these could have in fact been inscribed by the last Queen of Takish`Hiz, Tak`Yalir. Tragic indeed if the Queen suspected the influences of the Burning Prince and failed to act. I've had previous reports of the ghost of an elven queen near the ruins along the coast that I had dismissed, but if her soul believes she had failed her city perhaps it really is her ghost. Perhaps we can lay her spirit to [rest].'\nYou say, 'Rest?'\nTak`Valnakor says 'Find the spirit of the wayward queen and try to find a way to put her weary soul to rest. Good luck \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Burning Prince'.\n_Speak with Queen Tak`Yaliz in order to be ported into an instanced version of the Ruins of Takish-Hiz. In this zone, everything sees invisibility, everything is mezzable, charmable, and lullable._\n_A detailed map courtesy Weake can be found here._\n_You must search out and kill five priests in various points of the zone:_\n_\\- One in each of the three outer towers._\n_\\- Two in the main building (through the main entrance to the building the back and down to the twin towers underground in the back)_\n_Prince Tak`Salir will spawn in the center of the zone with a few friends. He hits for 1850, AEs Curse of Silir (30 seconds after landing, DDs for 8000), and has a single-target lifetap called Death's Beckon._\n_You will get one piece of loot from the Prince's corpse based on the mission level._\n_Prince possible loot level 58_\nSleeves of the Stone Trunk\nBelt of the Stone Trunk\nBow of the Stone Trunk\n_Prince possible loot level 63_\n????\n????\n????\n_Prince possible loot level 66+_\nStoneleaf Staff\nStone Leaf Wrist Bands\n????\n_After killing the Prince, return to North Ro and see the Queen._\nUpon completing this task, you will be offered a final task in the series -- a 54 person raid.\n**Need confirmation as to what loot drops from each tier mission, there are also likely rewards from this mission that are not linked to this quest page yet.**\n**Submitted by:** Jolo",
    },
