      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Cooling Chamber [zone=706]\n**Who:**\n- Rodrick Cleanheart [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 85\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n- Spell\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Dark Gem of the Underbelly [item=85916]\n- Frozen Dark Gem Fragment [item=85914]\n- Jagged Dark Gem Fragment [item=85908]\n- Rough Dark Gem Fragment [item=86581]\n- Scuffed Dark Gem Fragment [item=85915]\n- Smooth Dark Gem Fragment [item=85912]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Cooling Chamber: Tasnise Underbelly [zone=717]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Dark Spectre [npc=34488]\n- Darkbone Skeleton [npc=34490]\n- Darkcloth Mummy [npc=34487]\n- Darklight Ghoul [npc=34489]\n- Darksoul Ghost [npc=34491]\n- Grunkuck the Beast [npc=40847]\n- Tasnise Underbelly [npc=34207]\n- a frost-encrusted chest [npc=35257]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Alphabet Goop [quest=6726]\n- Rodrick #1: Investigate the Dead [quest=4921]\n- Rodrick #2: Hunt the Dead [quest=4922]\n- Tasnise Underbelly Challenge of Toughness [quest=6725]\n- Tasnise Underbelly Time Trial [quest=6724]\n**Era:** | !Underfoot\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sat Dec 12 16:38:47 2009\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | _This group task begins with Rodrick Cleanheart in the Cooling Chamber at location -170, -320, -25._\n_In order to request this task, you must have first completed Rodrick's two previous tasks._\nYou say, 'Hail, Rodrick Cleanheart'\nRodrick Cleanheart says 'Brell's eyes must shine down on you from below his [heavy] brows, my friend. Your discovery of that [device] and removal of the threat to the [Coldain] has been of great service to Brell and all of us in the Underfoot. But even that appears to have opened the way for an even more deadly [threat].'\nYou say, 'Coldain?'\nRodrick Cleanheart says 'I would have never thought that one of us could fall into the path of necromancy, but it seems one has. The one behind all of this is Tasnise Underbelly, as hard as that is to believe. Now I need you to find and destroy him. His foolishness has grown too dangerous and could result in the final breakdown of the Cooling Chambers. I need you to stop him. If you're [willing], let me know and I'll send you to the right place to begin.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Tasnise Underbelly'.\nTasnise has been proven to be corrupted beyond redemption. He has embraced necromancy and has been using his power to disrupt the workings of the Cooling Chambers. Rodrick believes that his power must be vast. The number of undead in the area alone proves this. He has asked you to see if you can defeat Tasnise and end his evil.\nFinding Tasnise might be difficult enough. If he knows that his veil of lies has been pierced, he may hide himself.\nYou say, 'We're willing'\nRodrick Cleanheart says 'May Brell's beard be soft for you!'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered The Cooling Chamber. _(an instanced version of the zone)_\n\n---\n\nDefeat Tasnise Underbelly 0/1 (Cooling Chamber)\n_As you zone in, you'll see a rather annoyed Tasnise Underbelly shouting at his workers._\nTasnise Underbelly shouts 'You WILL do as I say.'\n_He is located just below the zone-in point and is aggro._\nTasnise Underbelly says 'Hah! Now you know why you can never hope to defeat me! My life can never be taken!'\nTasnise Underbelly says 'I have traded some fraction of my power to creatures that never die, and I have taken from them their unliving essence. You can never hope to defeat me!'\nTasnise Underbelly says 'I will take your lives as I have so many others. I shall drain what little power you have and add it to my own.'\n_At 70%, he will heal to full and translocate group to random locations (the zone-in or the undead tunnels):_\nTasnise Underbelly says 'Enough of this foolishness. I haven't the time to kill you. After all, that's why I have mindless minions! Besides, I have a portal to build and a kingdom to usurp!'\n_This updates the step._\n\n---\n\nFind a way to defeat Tasnise! 0/1 (Cooling Chamber)\n_Task Window Says:_ It appears that hiding isn't something that Tasnise needs to do. His body recovers from serious wounds instantly! You must regroup and find a way to defeat his necromantic healing.\n_In the five deadends of the undead tunnels are five different named \"Dark\" mobs. Kill these and loot their gems._\n_Darkcloth Mummy is at the \"Rags\" location and drops Scuffed Dark Gem Fragment. It uses:_\nDark Reasoning: Single Target, (-120)\n1: Decrease Attack Speed by 40%\n2: Decrease Movement by 60%\n3: Increase corruption counter by 3\nDeathcloth Spore: Single Target, Magic (-450)\n1: Hitpoints unknown calc: 1999 range: 1000 -> 0\n2: Increase Poison Counter by 8\n_Darklight Ghoul is at the \"Tatters\" location and drops Rough Dark Gem Fragment. It uses:_\nDark Watchman: Single Target, Chromatic (-1000)\n1: Summon Pets: CCHMissDarkWatchmenPet x 1 for 60 sec\nDeath's Light: Single Target, Magic (0)\n1: Blindness (0)\n_Darksoul Ghost is at the \"Bonechips\" location and drops Frozen Dark Gem Fragment. It uses:_\nDark Reasoning: Single Target, (-120)\n1: Decrease Attack Speed by 40%\n2: Decrease Movement by 60%\n3: Increase corruption counter by 3\nDeathshock: Single Target, Magic (0)\n1: Decrease AC by 1500\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 1200 per tick\n_Darkbone Skeleton is at the \"Shrieking Death\" location and drops Smooth Dark Gem Fragment. It uses:_\nBoneshards: Directional 150', Chromatic (-500)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 20000\nDark Leeching: Lifetap 0', Magic (-500)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 16000\n_Dark Spectre is at the \"Rampaging Ghoul\" location and drops Jagged Dark Gem Fragment. It uses:_\nDark Repulsion: Single Target, Magic (-500)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 14000\n2: Unknown #380 (100/4/0)\nScything Slice: Single Target, Chromatic (-450)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 5000 per tick\n\n---\n\nThe Dark Gem fragment is obviously magical. Discover its secret. 0/1 (Cooling Chamber)\n_Click any of the fragments and it will assemble into a Dark Gem of the Underbelly._\n\n---\n\nDestroy the Dark Gem after weakening Tasnise Underbelly 0/1 (Cooling Chamber)\n_Task Window Says:_ The gem cannot be broken while Tasnise's body is whole, but when he draws from the gem to heal himself, you may be able to destroy it.\n_Tasnise Underbelly has relocated to the undead area but does not aggro you. You can clear if necessary and pull him when ready._\n_He casts some or all of the following \"Dark\" spells (how many of these you see may depend on how long you take to kill him):_\nDark Daze: Single Target, Magic (-500)\n1: Stun (8.00 sec)\nDark Leeching: Lifetap 0', Magic (-500)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 16000\nDark Reasoning: Single Target, (-120)\n1: Decrease Attack Speed by 40%\n2: Decrease Movement by 60%\n3: Increase corruption counter by 3\nDark Repulsion: Single Target, Magic (-500)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 14000\n2: Knockback (4) and Toss Up (6)\nDark Watchman: Single Target, Chromatic (-1000)\n1: Summon Pets: CCHMissDarkWatchmenPet x 1 for 60 sec\n_Click the Dark Gem any time between 70% and 60% of his health. He regenerates to full health and will now be killable._\nTasnise Underbelly shouts 'Fools! You may have returned to me my mortal weakness, but with that weakness also comes all of my power! You have returned to me that which I gave to my undead agents in exchange for their immortal life. With it I shall crush you! What matter that I will need to rebuild the gem. Time for that once you are all dead!'\n\n---\n\nKill Tasnise now, while he is vulnerable 0/1 (Cooling Chamber)\n_NOTE: The task locks as soon as Tasnise dies._\n_Finish him off._\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Rodrick 0/1 (Cooling Chamber)\n_You may or may not be able to do this with Rodrick in the instanced zone. If not, say \"return\" to exit, then hail Rodrick Cleanheart in the regular zone to complete the task._\nDefeating Tasnise will help the workers in the Cooling Chambers very much. At least it will if the necromancer remains dead...\n_A frost-encrusted chest spawns with loot (1 item per task). Known drops:_\nBleakburn Goo\nDeathmaker's Bane\nEchoing Shriek\nEmpowered Boneshards\nFoehatchet\nOwl's Wisdom\nRatskull Earring\nRobe of Mulberry Essence\nSleet\nTower of Gold\n_Rewards (everyone in task):_\n20 Silver Tokens\n105 platinum\nExperience (1.1 AAs at Level 85)\n\n---\n\n_Some (not all) classes also receive a spell for completion of this mission:_\nBard - You'll get nothing and like it!\nBeastlord - You'll get nothing and like it!\nBerserker - You'll get nothing and like it!\nCleric - You'll get nothing and like it!\nDruid - Spell: Surge of Ironvines\nEnchanter - You'll get nothing and like it!\nMagician - Spell: Chaotic Boon\nMonk - You'll get nothing and like it!\nNecromancer - You'll get nothing and like it!\nPaladin - You'll get nothing and like it!\nRanger - You'll get nothing and like it!\nRogue - You'll get nothing and like it!\nShadowknight - Spell: Dire Constriction\nShaman - You'll get nothing and like it!\nWarrior - You'll get nothing and like it!\nWizard - Spell: Malediction of Havoc\n- Silver Token [item=85837]\n- Spell: Chaotic Boon [item=86455]\n- Spell: Dire Constriction [item=86502]\n- Spell: Malediction of Havoc [item=86560]\n- Spell: Surge of Ironvines [item=85920]",
