      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Convorteum [zone=733]\n**Who:**\n- Delth [npc=35252]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 85\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Related Zones:**\n- Convorteum: The First Corruption [zone=736]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Argnus [npc=35417]\n- Belsa [npc=35418]\n- Crushing Apexus [npc=35426]\n- Delth [npc=35415]\n- Gorgex [npc=35425]\n- Grodnis [npc=35416]\n- Keeper Veilyn [npc=35427]\n- a bellikos assassin [npc=35420]\n- a greken spawn [npc=35424]\n- a mephit servant [npc=35423]\n- a telmiran servant [npc=35422]\n- an apexus enforcer [npc=35421]\n- an ornate chest - The First Corruption [npc=35419]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Delth #1: Different Point of View [quest=5045]\n- Delth #2: I, Bellikos [quest=5056]\n- Delth #3: Convorteum Coercion [quest=5057]\n- The First Corruption Challenge of Toughness [quest=6748]\n- The First Corruption Time Trial [quest=6747]\n- We Interrupt the Following Spellcast [quest=6749]\n**Era:** | !Underfoot\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 12\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Fri Apr 30 15:24:13 2010\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | _This is a group/mini-raid task (3-12 players) given by a bellikos named Delth in the Convorteum. She is located in the zone-in area, below the fortress at about -1380, 365, -65._\n_KOS mobs wander close to her, so keep a lookout while speaking with her._\n_In order to request this task, you must first have completed Delth's three solo tasks._\nYou say, 'Hail, Delth'\nDelth says 'Greetings outsider, your endeavors have helped greatly and now the sense of self has spread throughout the others. Now we must [strike]. I could also use your assistance to [investigate] the teachings of the first, locate and assemble Bellikos [parts], or to [reach] certain members of the elite creations and deliver the truth to them.'\nYou say, 'Strike?'\nDelth says 'Yes, I will lead the rebellion against our creator, but I fear that I will need more help. You see, I have become a target and I am expecting them to come after me first. If they capture me it may cause the rest of the rebels to give up. But you helped us find all of this and, as such, are just as committed to this all as I am. Please, won't you [join] us?'\nYou say, 'I'll join you'\nDelth says 'Come now, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Our rage will be the weapon we use to break down the walls and find the truth. Tell me when you are [ready] to go.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The First Corruption'.\nDelth, a trainer for Bellikos envoys, now knows the truth about The First Creation's teachings, thanks to your previous efforts. And now that you have begun to spread the cult of the self inside the pyramid, Delth thinks that it is time to call upon your new allies and attack Keeper Veilyn, who holds the key to the records room.\nDelth has gone on ahead, but you still need to gather your allies for the assault on the Keeper. Talk to Argnus first.\n_NOTE: You'll zone into an instanced version of the Convorteum and land on the first level of the fortress in aggro range of wandering mobs. Up to three mobs can aggro you at the zone-in point if you are not invis._\nYou say, 'Ready!'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\n\n---\n\n_This is an escort task with waves of mobs that must be killed. It is recommended that you clear a path up to the third floor of the temple prior to hailing Argnus._\nSpeak With Argnus 0/1 (The Convorteum)\n_Argnus is found on the first floor of the temple._\nYou say, 'Hail, Argnus'\nArgnus says 'Is me convinced. First to Underfoot teaches freedoms and self; to Convorteum teaches slaveries and sacrificers. I bring self to Convorteum! You me go smash face of Keeper, see in room of records what really true! And we go gets Belsa and Grodnis!'\n_He'll walk to the second floor to Belsa's location._\nTake Argnus with you and hail Belsa 0/1 (The Convorteum)\nYou say, 'Hail, Belsa'\nBelsa says 'Now is our time to strike. The First has been careful about keeping knowledge of the self away from those of us in the pyramid. But now that we have it, we must carry it out to its fullest extent. If we can catch Keeper Veilyn off guard, we can breach the records room and disseminate the truth about the First to all of the First's creations, and to all of the Underfoot.'\n_The two will walk to Grodnis's location (also on the second floor)._\nTake your allies with you and hail Grodnis 0/1 (The Convorteum)\nYou say, 'Hail, Grodnis'\nGrodnis says '\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, you bring Argnus and Belsa! Good! I see Delth go being drugged up to jails. We make big fight, get Delth, go bash Keeper! Grodnis no afraid; have strong self!'\n_The three of them will walk up the next ramp, to the second set of prison cells where you'll find Delth._\nTake your allies with you and hail Delth 0/1 (The Convorteum)\nYou say, 'Hail, Delth'\nDelth says 'You see, what the First does to those who dare to question, who dare to think? The moment I start believing what I preach, he locks me away. There are many secrets in here, Painlord, but we will lay them bare. We will strip the stones from this pyramid if need be. If I can charge up my powers, I might be able to cast a spell powerful enough to dispel the Keeper's cloak of protection. Come, let us make our assault on the records room while there is still time.'\n_The four of them will walk up to the Reclamation room (the lava room with the platforms)._\nGather in the Reclamation Room 0/1 (The Convorteum)\nLet your allies get into position and challenge Keeper Veilyn 0/1 (The Convorteum)\n_Once the four NPCs you've been escorting reach their positions, they'll go through some dialogue. After this point, the first wave of mobs spawns._\nDelth says, 'We are near the Keeper. Let us take up defensive positions while I charge the spell that will make her visible.\nKeeper Veilyn says, 'Who are you to challenge the First? His servants will deal with you.'\nDefeat the first wave of enemies 0/1 (The Convorteum)\n_About 12 mobs in total spawn here (a mix of Bellikos and Apexi) and charge the platforms. They'll attack players as well as the NPCs. They are all mezzable._\n_Keep the mobs off Delth while she casts a long spell. Then kill them. (Those you kill before she's done casting will respawn instantly.) As she completes her spell, you'll see:_\nDelth shouts 'I have gained sufficient power to proceed. Get rid of those creatures quickly!'\n_Note: You'll only see this emote if you're in close proximity to Delth. It's not a zonewide emote._\n_Be ready for another large wave of mobs once you kill the last of those._\nKeeper Veilyn says, 'The First is our master. Reject the beliefs of our enemies.'\nDefeat the second wave of enemies 0/1 (The Convorteum)\n_Once the above wave is dead, a second wave spawns nearby: 6-8 telmiran mobs (mezzable) immediately charge and attack players and the NPCs. In addition to those, about 10 fire mephits spawn at the windows around the large halls. They AE for damage and gravity-flux. They are mezzable and permanently rooted._\n_Keep them off Delth while she casts, wait for her emote, and then kill them._\n_Be ready for another large wave of mobs once you kill the last of those._\nKeeper Veilyn says, 'Belief in self only leads to destruction. The Gorgex will feast upon you.'\nDefeat the third wave of enemies 0/1 (The Convorteum)\n_10 grekens spawn nearby and charge you (some spawn on the platforms; some spawn in the lava). They are mezzable and do not see invis. A named spawns in the center of the lava. It may be permanently rooted or tethered to the floor of the lava. It sees invis and SOS and will target players at random._\n_Kill the named before killing the other grekens as they respawn if they die before the named._\n_Be ready for a named mob once the last of those dies._\nKeeper Veilyn says, 'The kiln brings forth your doom. When the crusher reaches you, Delth, you will die.'\nDefend Dealth from Crushing Apexus 0/1 (The Convorteum)\n_A Crushing Apexus spawns in the hallways outside the lava room. It slowly walks up towards Delth. You must kill it before it reaches Delth or the task fails._\n_For the most part, you can beat on it without it aggroing you, but it will occasionally turn around and melee (hits quite hard). It is lurch-able and highsun-able until around 30%._\nCrushing Apexus has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nCrushing Apexus falls, shaking the pyramid.\nKeeper Veilyn says, 'I will kill you traitors myself!'\nKeeper Veilyn says, 'You might have torn my cloak, but I will unravel the thread of your lives!'\nKeeper Veilyn says, 'Do you see what your love of self has brought you? You have lost the love of the Master... And your life.'\nKeeper Veilyn says, 'Adventurers, you may speak to me in the throne room if you dare.'\nDefend your allies from Keeper Veilyn 0/1 (The Convorteum)\nHail Keeper Veilyn in the throne room 0/1 (The Convorteum)\nYou say, 'Hail, Keeper Veilyn'\nKeeper Veilyn says 'You are fools to come here and try to turn the children of the First against each other. He permits no dissent, and there is no self. We are his creations, and he is our master and lord. You either serve Brell or the First; there is no other path. The self is but an illusion in the sight of your god. His will is an ocean; you are but the smallest vessel. And you will drown'\nKeeper Veilyn says 'You will be consumed by the wrath of the First.'\nKill 1 Keeper Veilyn 0/1 (The Convorteum)\n_This is a relatively simple kill, except she occasionally AEs \"Lava Ball\":_\nLava Ball: Targeted AE 120', Fire (-650)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 35000\nKeeper Veilyn has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nKeeper Veilyn's corpse will be turned to clay by the First.\nSpeak with Delth 0/1 (The Convorteum)\n_Delth is back on the lava platform. Hailing her spawns a chest._\nAlthough your allies were injured, you have defeated Keeper Veilyn and gained access to the records room. Delth will continue her search for answers and will spread the Cult of Self among the servants in the Convorteum.\nSee what reward has been offered 0/1 (The Convorteum)\n\n---\n\n_The chest contains 1 item of loot. Known drops:_\nEverburning Jewel\nEye of the Spitting Firebug\nFallen Leviathan's Runic Hatchet\nIgnited Heart of the Firebug\nJewel of the Self\nLabrys of the Twisted\nPainblade\nPunisher's Guard\nTear of the Bellikos\nTorment\n_Rewards (everyone in task):_\n240 Platinum\n~160 Brellium Tokens\nExperience (2.2 AAs at Level 85)\n- Brellium Token [item=88944]\n- Everburning Jewel [item=88741]\n- Eye of the Spitting Firebug [item=88559]\n- Fallen Leviathan's Runic Hatchet [item=88552]\n- Ignited Heart of the Firebug [item=88532]\n- Jewel of the Self [item=88583]\n- Labrys of the Twisted [item=88596]\n- Painblade [item=88748]\n- Punisher's Guard [item=88561]\n- Tear of the Bellikos [item=88588]\n- Torment [item=88591]",
