      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Al'Kabor's Nightmare [zone=754]\n**Who:**\n- Dreezil Stickens Pocketdip [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 90\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Money\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Dream Delvers +10\n**Factions Lowered:**\n**Quest Items:**\n- Stored Food [item=93639]\n- Stored Medicine [item=93640]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Dabner Drednever [npc=36449]\n- a halfling bandit - Al'Kabor's Nightmare - 1 [npc=36421]\n- a halfling guard [npc=36420]\n- a halfling lookout [npc=36422]\n- a klaknak beetle [npc=36412]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Faydark's Shadow [quest=5210]\n- Wastelands of Everfrost [quest=5209]\n**Era:** | !House of Thule\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 10 06:49:32 2010\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | _This solo task is the first in a series of three that will grant you access to the different islands in Al'Kabor's Nightmare (as well as lead into the group progression mission for the zone)._\n_This task begins with Dreezil Stickens Pocketdip who's located at the zone-in._\nYou say, 'Hail, Dreezil Stickens Pocketdip'\nDreezil Stickens Pocketdip sighs and kicks at the ground. 'Nothing matters anymore. I should have been grateful for what I had. If I had known this would happen, I wouldn't have wasted my life with stealing stuff. Now, there isn't anything to do but wait to [die], or chat up goblins!' Dreezil rolls his eyes. 'So, did you want something, or were you just [passing] through?'\nYou say, 'Die?'\nDreezil Stickens Pocketdip scoffs at your sudden interest, 'Why does a goblin like you care, anyway? Rivervale is in ruins, the Misty Thicket is no more. It's the end of the world! We're out of [supplies], most of the halflings have turned to backstabbing and thievery, and the Runnyeye clan has got us all dancing on the edge of a blade.\nYou say, 'Supplies?'\nDreezil Stickens Pocketdip says 'There are stores of food near the wall on the opposite side of this 'island,' but we can't even get to them thanks to the giant animals and the more hostile goblins. You're welcome to [try], but you're wasting your time!'\nYou say, 'I will try...'\nDreezil Stickens Pocketdip says 'Good luck then. I guess I won't be seeing you again. If you can knock some sense into some of those halflings that are causing even more problems before you get yourself killed, I'd appreciate it.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Rivervale Ruins'.\nYou've been asked to stop the Klaknak beetles and halfling bandits from causing trouble and stealing all the food and medicine.\n\n---\n\nKill klaknak beetles 0/3 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\nSubdue halfling bandits 0/3 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\nCollect food stored at the wall and give it to Dreezil 0/3 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\nCollect medicine stored at the wall and give it to Dreezil 0/3 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\n_These are groundspawns inside the wall and around it (some medicine spawns are found on the southwest side of the wall while food spawns are found on the north side)._\n_Medicine (looks like a red/sparkling potion bottle):_\n-130, 902\n-201, 921\n-245, 891\n_Food (looks like a brown box):_\n-135, 866\n245, 1007\n304, 966\n106, 946\nTalk to Dreezil 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\nYou say, 'Hail, Dreezil Stickens Pocketdip'\nDreezil Stickens Pocketdip appears shocked and quite grateful. 'I didn't think you'd come back. Thank you. You know, I think you are right. We might be in a bad way, but we aren't all dead yet. Maybe there is hope. Could you talk to Dabner? Maybe you can help him, too.'\nConvince Dabner not to give up 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\n_Dabner Drednever is found a little ways east of the wall inside some ruins at 110, 360, -30._\nYou say, 'Hail, Dabner Drednever'\nDabner Drednever looks up as you inform him of your success in driving back the goblins and securing food and medicine. 'Really? You've done a lot to help us. I may never get over what has happened here with Al'Kabor's magic, but I owe it to my friends that are still alive that I push on. You have my deepest appreciation.'\nReturn to Dreezil 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\nYou say, 'Hail, Dreezil Stickens Pocketdip'\nDreezil Stickens Pocketdip manages a slight smile. 'I think you've reminded Dabner and I what courage and hope is all about. I won't wallow in the past any longer. I'll do what I can to make something better of this mess! Listen, if you by any chance get to what remains of Everfrost, I've heard Dagda Icefury needs some help. I have a little magical trinket here that might be able to get you there. If you do go, be sure to dress warmly. It's still cold as ever!'\nYou've helped give the halflings a second chance and given Dreezil and Dabner some peace of mind. You can now go to the wastelands of Everfrost whenever you wish.\nYour faction standing with Dream Delvers got better.\n_Rewards:_\n315 platinum\nFaction with Dream Delvers\nExperience\n30 Dream Motes\n_Note: You also gain access to the second island in the zone (Everfrost). To get there, say \"Everfrost\" to Dreezil._\n- Dream Mote [item=90255]",
    },
