      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Al'Kabor's Nightmare [zone=754]\n**Who:**\n- Gimble Shamrook [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 90\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Money\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Dream Delvers +?\n**Factions Lowered:**\n**Quest Items:**\n- Goblin Goulash [item=93450]\n- Large Chunk of Bone [item=93741]\n- Magnetic Metal Detector [item=93687]\n- Pristine Ice Bear Pelt [item=94611]\n- Ruined Cloak of the Ice Bear [item=94612]\n- Ruined Robe of Discord [item=94616]\n- Ruined Runnyeye Warbeads [item=94607]\n- Ruined Wraith Bone Hammer [item=94624]\n- Staff Fragment [item=94614]\n- Tender Ice Goblin Meat [item=93646]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Helda Varesh [npc=36445]\n- Hilnie [npc=36475]\n- Ogrol [npc=36464]\n- Priest of Discord - Al'Kabor's Nightmare [npc=36472]\n- Snugum Witgone [npc=36427]\n- Zisak [npc=36493]\n- a plaguebone skeleton - Al'Kabor's Nightmare - 1 [npc=36477]\n- an ice bear [npc=36723]\n- an ice goblin thief [npc=36439]\n**Era:** | !House of Thule\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 11 07:09:53 2010\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | _This shared task (1-6 players) begins with Gimble Shamrook in Al'Kabor's Nightmare. He's found in a ruined hut a little ways east of the wall (in the same spot as Dabner Drednever from the \"The Rivervale Ruins\" task)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Gimble Shamrook'\nGimble Shamrook looks you over with curious suspicion before he speaks, 'I have a quick and keen eye, you know, and I can tell with one glance that you don't belong here. If you're attempting to retrieve [relics], then you'd better be warned that I am one step ahead of you!'\nYou say, 'What relics?'\nGimble Shamrook says 'I can sense your shenanigans, oh yes. I see that you're trying to steal my brilliant idea! While these islands may be a figment of someone's imagination, they still contain all the same [treasures] the original lands hold.'\nYou say, 'Treasures?'\nGimble Shamrook says 'Oh, such wondrous treasures! Sure, they may be rusty and ruined, but if I shine 'em up a bit, no one will ever know the difference. The simpletons of Norrath will pay me a hefty sum for my faux relics! I just need to find a way to travel to the other [islands]...'\nYou say, 'The other islands?'\nGimble Shamrook says 'There are several other islands in this space, and I'm positive there must be a way to travel between them. Since we both seem to have the same goal, we might as well work together. If you can help me [recover] these relics, I'll make sure it's worth your effort.'\nYou say, 'I'll help you recover them'\nGimble Shamrook says 'Splendid! I'll give you whatever information I have pertaining to the relic's whereabouts. Happy treasure hunting!'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Ruined Relic Recovery'.\nYou have partnered up with Gimble Shamrook to recover relics from the surrounding islands in order to earn a hefty profit!\n\n---\n\n_The four \"Speak to...\" and four \"Deliver...\" steps are open from the start of the task, so you can handle the islands in any order you'd like._\nSpeak to Snugum Witgone 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\n_Snugum Witgone is found within the wall on the Rivervale isle._\nYou say, 'Hail, Snugum Witgone'\nSnugum Witgone clears his throat before responding, 'You're here for the beads? Boss must have sent you. Boss knows he can count on me! I hid the beads in the most secret of hiding spots. No one will ever [find] them, not even me!'\nYou say, 'How can I find them?'\nSnugum Witgone says 'You use a magnetic metal detector to find the beads, but that fat-fingered Hilnie stole it! You'll take it from her and find the beads? And not tell Boss that I hid them so good?'\nRecover the Magnetic Metal Detector from Hilnie 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\n_Hilnie spawns in the north-central halfling bandit camp. Her difficulty is on par with the rest of the mobs on the island (hits for a max ~7,000)._\nHilnie has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nHilnie's corpse crumples to the floor.\nFind the spot where the beads are buried 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\n_The beads are buried in the southeastern part of the island at approximately -270, -400, -40._\nUse the Magnetic Metal Detector to retrieve the warbeads 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\nThe metal detector makes a loud clanking noise as it pulls Ruined Runnyeye Warbeads from the ground.\nSpeak to Helda Varesh 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\n_Helda Varesh is found in a building in the northeastern part of the Everfrost Wastelands._\nYou say, 'Hail, Helda Varesh'\nHelda Varesh says 'Greetings, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. You're looking for the cloak of an ice bear? What an odd request. It's so old and tattered. If you insist, I can help restore it to a suitable condition, but I'll need a pelt from the elusive ice bear. I can help you lure it out of hiding with my delectable goblin goulash, but you'll need to collect some tender goblin meat for me first.'\nLoot Tender Goblin Meat from ice goblins 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\n_This is a common drop from ice goblins on the isle._\nGive the Tender Goblin Meat to Helda Varesh 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\nHelda Varesh says 'Doesn't it smell delicious? Head right outside of this building, and use the goulash to attract an ice bear.'\nUse the goulash to lure an ice bear and take its pelt 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\n_Right-click the Goblin Goulash while standing in front of Helda's building to spawn \"an ice bear\" (on par with difficulty of the mobs on the isle)._\nA ferocious roar rumbles behind Helda's ice hut.\nan ice bear has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nan ice bear's corpse falls to the ground with a loud crash.\nGive the Pristine Ice Bear Pelt to Helda Varesh 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\nHelda Varesh says 'This should do it. The cloak won't provide much protection, but it's yours nonetheless.'\nSpeak to Ogrol 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\n_Ogrol spawns in a set of abandonned huts in the central part of the Faydark island._\nYou say, 'Hail, Ogrol'\nOgrol says 'You want a robe? What for? You're not going to wear it, are you? Never mind, I don't want to know... I have no use for a robe, but since you seem to want it so badly, I'm sure you're willing to trade far more than what it's worth! Bring me a fragment from the Staff of Discord, and the robe is yours to do whatever you want with.'\nKill the Priest of Discord and loot a fragment of his staff 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\n_You'll find the Priest of Discord a little ways west of Ogrol's location, beneath the ruins of Kelethin. He has two guards with him (they are mezzable), but can be split away from them. Fight difficulty is on par with the rest of the isle's mob population._\nPriest of Discord has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nPriest of Discord's corpse lets out a gasp before falling silent.\nGive the Staff Fragment to Ogrol 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\nOgrol says 'The ruined robe is all yours. Just don't try squeezing it on over that fat head of yours, you hear?'\nSpeak to Zisak 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\n_Zisak spawns in the northeastern pyramid on the Dreadlands isle._\nYou say, 'Hail, Zisak'\nZisak says 'All of our weapons have deteriorated, much like our home here. I will do my best to repair the hilt of the wraith bone hammer if you bring me a large chunk of bone from one of the plaguebone skeletons that linger around here.'\nLoot a Large Chunk of Bone 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\n_This item drops from plaguebones on the Dreadlands isle._\nGive the Large Chunk of Bone to Zisak 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\nZisak says 'I do not believe it will hold up in battle, but regardless, here is the hammer you requested.'\nDeliver Ruined Runnyeye Warbeads to Gimble 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\nDeliver a Ruined Cloak of the Ice Bear to Gimble 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\nDeliver a Ruined Robe of Discord to Gimble 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\nDeliver a Ruined Wraith Bone Hammer to Gimble 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\nSpeak to Gimble Shamrook 0/1 (Al'Kabor's Nightmare)\nYou say, 'Hail, Gimble Shamrook'\nGimble Shamrook says 'Brilliant job, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_! These relics should make me filthy rich! Oh... um, I mean they'll make us rich, of course.'\nYou collected numerous ruined relics for Gimble Shamrook and received what you hope is half of the profits...\nYour faction standing with Dream Delvers got better.\n_Rewards:_\n262 platinum\nExperience\nFaction with Dream Delvers\n25 Dream Motes\n- Dream Mote [item=90255]",
