      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Morell's Castle [zone=757]\n**Who:**\n- Gurroth Aberrine [npc=36814]\nRating:\n0/2**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(Average from 2 ratings)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 90\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Dream Delvers +?\n**Factions Lowered:**\n**Quest Items:**\n- Gouzah Teleportation Gem [item=94187]\n- Rabbit Carcass [item=94183]\n- Speckled Hare Carcass [item=93818]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Morell's Castle: Gouzah Safari [zone=779]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Gurroth Aberrine [npc=36987]\n- Snibbles The Grand Gouzah [npc=36990]\n- The Smart Gouzah [npc=36995]\n- a chaos gouzah [npc=36992]\n- a grizzly gouzah [npc=36991]\n- a rabbit - Morell's Castle [npc=36988]\n- a shade gouzah [npc=36994]\n- a sorcel gouzah [npc=36993]\n- a speckled hare [npc=36989]\n**Era:** | !House of Thule\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Nov 21 07:11:26 2010\nModified: Wed Jan 29 09:00:29 2025 | | _This is one of five tasks leading up to \"The Staff Retreat\" and the group progression mission for Morell's Castle, \"Hippity Hoppity Kill\"._\n_Of the five tasks, this is the only group task and the only one that takes place in its own instance. It begins with Gurroth Aberrine who is found at location 860, 1200, 60 (inside the house in the candy land area)._\n_There are no pre-requisites for requesting this task._\n_NOTE: Depite what the timer says, you may be limited to two hours to complete this task._\n_NOTE: Unlike most instances in this expansion, all mobs in this instance (including named) DO respawn._\nYou say, 'Hail, Gurroth Aberrine'\nGurroth Aberrine says 'Hello there. I don't suppose you've brought along any spare food for a [stranded] soul, have you?'\nYou say, 'Stranded?'\nGurroth Aberrine says 'Yes, marooned here. I have been lost in this crazy place for days... Or is it weeks?? I found my way here, as here is where I came to find myself tolerated, not attacked by every living (or unliving) thing in the area. I have bound my wounds up as best I could, and set to work finding food in this [wretched] place.'\nYou say, 'Wretched?'\nGurroth Aberrine says 'Yes, it is truly dismal. The folks living here are clearly out of their minds. All there is to eat is this oversized candy, which I have done until half my teeth have fallen out. I am starved for some good, solid food, but I fear I will need [help] with this as I am too weak to exert myself. I broke a bone in my hand when I fainted from hunger yesterday, and can no longer wave a sword.'\nYou say, 'How can I help?'\nGurroth Aberrine says 'If you could lend assistance, I could let you have something of mine which I'll no longer be needing to lug around. All I need you to do is go and kill some hares and [rabbits] as are loping around nearby, bring me back their carcasses, and I will have my first real meal in a long time.'\nYou say, 'Rabbits?'\nGurroth Aberrine says 'Three of the speckled hares and three of the ordinary brown rabbits, what do you say? Are you [ready], willing, and able?'\nYou say, 'I'm ready'\nGurroth Aberrine says 'Splendid, I will get the cookpot ready while you go back out there to hunt. Let me know when you'd like to [go].'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Gouzah Safari'.\nPrevent Gurroth from dying of malnutrition by collecting the rabbit meat he needs to finish making a pot of rabbit stew.\n_Say \"go\" to zone into the instance._\nYou say, 'I'd like to go...'\nGurroth Aberrine says 'Good luck! Let me know if you need anything.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\n_Mobs in this instance hit for a max ~8,500 (or more, if you're low on mitigation)._\n\n---\n\nKill three speckled hares for Gurroth's rabbit stew 0/3 (Morell's Castle)\nAcquire three speckled hare carcasses 0/3 (Morell's Castle)\nKill three rabbits for Gurroth's rabbit stew 0/3 (Morell's Castle)\nAcquire three rabbit carcasses 0/3 (Morell's Castle)\n_Speckled hares spawn around the northern part of the candy land while regular rabbits spawn out in the forest._\nDeliver three speckled hare carcasses to Gurroth 0/3 (Morell's Castle)\nGurroth Aberrine says 'Yes, this will do spendidly, there's enough speckled hare meat here to bring me back from death's door, assuming I can find a cookpot.'\nDeliver three rabbit carcasses to Gurroth 0/3 (Morell's Castle)\nGurroth Aberrine says 'The more rabbit meat, the better. If only I had some herbs and spices. I'll find some around here somewhere.'\nFind out when Gurroth's stew will be ready 0/1 (Morell's Castle)\nYou say, 'Hail, Gurroth Aberrine'\nGurroth Aberrine says 'Did... Did you hear that? That commotion outside? What is going on out there? Strange, horrible giant rabbits! What could they want? I'm still too weak to lift a weapon, could you run out there and try to... persuade them not to kill us all?'\nTalk to the Grand Gouzah, whose name is Snibbles. Find out what the Gouzahs want 0/1 (Morell's Castle)\n_A giant rabbit, the Grand Gouzah, spawns outside the house along with several smaller gouzahs._\nYou say, 'Hail, Snibbles The Grand Gouzah'\nSnibbles The Grand Gouzah says 'Not often are we ready and able to intervene in your mortal matters, not always are the mystical barriers which normally separate our worlds so chaotically weakened as they are in this place. We shall take this opportunity to punish you for your crimes against our inferior, less-developed brethren. We are Gouzahs. You are killers of our distant relatives. You must die! Your civilization, your creatures, your gods - all shall be destroyed in favor of our new order!'\n_Snibbles and the surrounding gouzahs attack. If you're able to fade, FD, escape, or otherwise remove your aggro from the initial attack (your death also works), you can split these mobs from one another._\nIt behooves you to resolve the dispute with the Gouzahs in a way that permits your survival. Kill the Grand Gouzah 0/1 (Morell's Castle)\nKill the attacking Gouzahs 0/6 (Morell's Castle)\n_Task Window Says:_ Kill Snibbles, the Grand Gouzah, and at least eight members of his vanguard force.\n_\"a sorcel gouzah\" casts \"Sorcelling Gouzah-spray\":_\nSorcelling Gouzah-spray: PB AE 30', Chromatic (-600)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 2816 (L1) to 4000 (L149)\n2: Decrease Mana by 1316 (L1) to 3000 (L212) per tick\n3: Decrease Hitpoints by 1316 (L1) to 12000 (L1337) per tick\n_\"a shade gouzah\" casts \"Shadowlocking Gouzah-blast\":_\nShadowlocking Gouzah-blast: PB AE 0', Chromatic (-600)\n1: Mesmerize (1/90)\n2: ? ? ?\n3: Stun (12.00 sec/90)\n4: Decrease All Resists by 140\n5: Increase corruption counter by 20\n_\"a chaos gouzah\" casts \"Chaos Gouzah-bolt\":_\nChaos Gouzah-bolt: Single Target, Chromatic (-600)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 19816 (L1) to 30000 (L1274)\n_Grizzly gouzahs and Snibbles appear to be straight melee._\nSpeak to the Smart Gouzah 0/1 (Morell's Castle)\n_Task Window Says:_ Speak to the Smart Gouzah. Perhaps a resolution can be found to this situation.\n_The Smart Gouzah spawns with a few gouzahs in the southeastern corner of the candy land area._\nYou say, 'Hail, The Smart Gouzah'\nThe Smart Gouzah says 'You cannot destroy us. Killing us only banishes our life energy for a time, returning us to our home plane. As long as we possess our planar teleportation gem, we are free to return here as we please, as many times as it takes to lay waste to those who have harmed our kin. Now you will pay for your crimes against our brethren, mortal!'\n_NOTE: The task locks at this point. The Smart Gouzah also attacks. It hits for a max ~9,000 (maybe more) and appears to be straight melee._\nThe only way to prevent Gouzahs from invading the castle is to kill the Smart Gouzah and take its teleport gem 0/1 (Morell's Castle)\nDeliver the Gouzah Teleportation Gem to Gurroth, then return from the Gouzah Safari 0/1 (Morell's Castle)\nGurroth Aberrine says 'What's this? A 'planar teleportation gem', you say? I wouldn't know what to do with this, but I suppose I could hang on to it for you if you ever decide you need it. Nice work on capturing this from those horrid Gouzah creatures, whatever they were. They looked like they were about to cause a real problem for us! I'd hate to die hungry at the hands of giant extra-planar rabbits.'\nYou say, 'Hail, Gurroth Aberrine'\nGurroth Aberrine says 'Hey, if it's getting too gnarly in the candy forest for you, say the word, and I'll pretend I never gave you this quest... You can [return] to your normal schedule. I still won't have a decent thing to eat, but I'll get by.'\nYou say, 'Return me...'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Morell's Castle.\nFind out if Gurroth really wants to continue making rabbit stew, now that he knows the Gouzahs are always watching 0/1 (Morell's Castle)\n_Task Window Says:_ After the planar breach returns you to the original dimension of Morell's Castle, speak to Gurroth and see if he still wishes to continue making rabbit stew, with the threat of the Gouzahs' retribution now hanging over him.\nYou say, 'Hail, Gurroth Aberrine'\nGurroth Aberrine says 'I suppose I could lay off hunting rabbits around here, never know when those Gouzahs might be able to return. I'll pray that the others of their kind remain unaware of our deeds, even if they still possess the ability to come here. Here, you've done much more than you bargained for, here's a reward.'\n_Rewards:_\n315 platinum\nExperience _(about 4 AAs worth)_\nFaction with Dream Delvers\n40 Dream Motes\n- Dream Mote [item=90255]",
    },
