      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Sarith, City of Tides [zone=808]\n**Who:**\n- Governor Parrin Wenst [ _Quests & Missions_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 91\n**Maximum Level:** | 95\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Archon Eries' Documents [item=100049]\n- City of Bronze Equipment Chest [item=97990]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Guard Captain Naraind Reles [npc=38384]\n- Quartermaster Gilles [npc=38431]\n- Rebel Leader Ain Kavus [npc=38383]\n- an Orator`s Army assassin [npc=39951]\n- an Orator`s Army beast master [npc=39183]\n- an Orator`s Army death knight [npc=39177]\n- an Orator`s Army life knight [npc=39184]\n- an Orator`s Army nature mage [npc=39181]\n- an Orator`s Army primal mage [npc=39182]\n- an Orator`s Army ranger [npc=39180]\n- an Orator`s army archmage [npc=39179]\n- an Orator`s army battlemage [npc=38466]\n- an Orator`s army beast trainer [npc=38477]\n- an Orator`s army bishop [npc=39175]\n- an Orator`s army commander [npc=39178]\n- an Orator`s army conscript [npc=38467]\n- an Orator`s army dark mage [npc=38481]\n- an Orator`s army lieutenant [npc=39952]\n- an Orator`s army scout [npc=38470]\n- an Orator`s army soldier [npc=38469]\n- an Orator`s army strategist [npc=39176]\n- an Orator`s army warpriest [npc=38468]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Fri Nov 18 22:03:54 2011\nModified: Sat Feb 8 15:50:13 2020 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This task is the first in a series of three; a solo task that begins with Governor Parrin Wenst in Sarith. He's found in a building at location -600, -685, 4 (the northern room of the large building in the far southwestern part of the zone)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- No tasks\n\\- 70 Skill Level in Alaran\n\n---\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Governor Parrin Wenst'\nGovernor Parrin Wenst says, in Alaran, 'Oh, hello there, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. I'm always glad to see another of you outsiders here. It gives me hope. I'm not ashamed to say that [Sarith] needs your [help]. Once we get the more pressing matters settled, we'll be ready for a big [mission] that I hope you will be a part of. I will do everything in my power to see that you are rewarded for your efforts.'\nYou say, 'Sarith?'\nGovernor Parrin Wenst says, in Alaran, 'I was proud to serve as this city's Governor. Sarith is the greatest city state in the region, with a robust export of ocean commodities. Well, that's how it used to be. Now [Guard Captain Reles] and I are just the puppets of [High Priest Vyers] and [Archon Eries].'\nYou say, 'Who is Guard Captain Reles?'\nGovernor Parrin Wenst says, in Alaran, 'Guard Captain Reles is the only thing keeping [Sarith] together. I know al's frustrated being under [Archon Eries]' control, but I keep telling ali to be patient. The people need ali. If al were to be killed, what little al can do in delaying or preventing the suffering of [Sarith]'s people will be destroyed.'\nYou say, 'Who is Archon Eries?'\nGovernor Parrin Wenst says, in Alaran, 'A frightening person. For your own safety, please do not make ali angry. Al took this city in mere days. It was horrific.'\nYou say, 'Tell me about High Priest Vyers'\nGovernor Parrin Wenst says, in Alaran, 'High Priest Vyers is a very intimidating fellow. If al truly is powered by [Oseka], do we have any chance to win? That other god-creature, Prexus, will destroy this city trying to get at ali. We'll be caught in the middle.'\nYou say, 'Oseka?'\nGovernor Parrin Wenst says, in Alaran, 'Oseka, Prexus. All these ocean gods are going to destroy my city! Is this what it is all about? A god-war? When the Orator took over the City of Bronze, I knew things were going to get worse!'\nYou say, 'I'll help you'\nGovernor Parrin Wenst says, in Alaran, 'Ah, yes! I'm so glad to hear you say that. It just so happens [Guard Captain Reles] and I were planning something. Well, it was mostly alis idea, but I'm doing what I can to help. Please go speak to ali to find out what you need to do. I'll send a messenger along so al will be expecting you.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Governor's Plot'.\nSabotage the efforts of the Orator's army by working with Governor Wenst and Guard Captain Reles.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Governor Parrin Wenst 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, Governor Parrin Wenst'\nGovernor Parrin Wenst says, in Alaran, 'You have no idea how happy I am to hear that you want to help! I believe the Guard Captain and the rebels are formulating a plan to take back the city before the one called Prexus and his Kedge destroy it. Please, go speak to the Guard Captain. I'll be sending a messenger along with information vital to the success of their mission, and telling the Guard Captain to expect you.'\nReport to Guard Captain Naraind Reles 0/1 (Sarith)\n_The captain is found in the northwestern building (location 10, 620, 0)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Guard Captain Naraind Reles'\nGuard Captain Naraind Reles says, in Alaran, 'The Governor's aide arrived shortly before you. This mission is the start of something big, and I personally want to thank you, as an outsider, for helping our city state. I want to get this taken care of before Prexus destroys our home. I know he's after High Priest Vyers, and to get to Vyers, we need to take out the City of Bronze military. For the rebels to have a chance, you'll need to take their equipment and give it to their leader, Ain Kavus. Find the quartermaster, defeat ali, and take what you need. I have good intelligence suggesting the quartermaster has an important missive from Archon Eries aleself. If you find anything like that, give it to Ain Kavus as well, at the drydock.'\nDefeat Orator's army troops 0/8 (Sarith)\nCollect City of Bronze equipment chests from the Orator's army 0/4 (Sarith)\nDefeat the Orator's army quartermaster, Gilles near the barracks 0/1 (Sarith)\nTake Archon Eries' plans from Quartermaster Gilles 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Quartermaster Gilles spawns in a building just west of the city's front gate (once inside, head right; he's in the first building on your right). He drops one_\nDeliver equipment to Rebel Leader Ain Kavus at the drydock 0/4 (Sarith)\nGive Archon Eries' documents to Rebel Leader Ain Kavus at the drydock 0/1 (Sarith)\n_The Rebel Leader is in the far northeastern part of the city at about 145, -845, -4)._\nTalk to Rebel Leader Ain Kavus 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, Rebel Leader Ain Kavus'\nRebel Leader Ain Kavus says, in Alaran, 'This equipment could be the catalyst that changes this entire fight, and these plans contain all the information we could have hoped for. You've been a great help. Let the Governor know we appreciate alis help as well.'\nReport to Governor Parrin Wenst at the City Hall 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, Governor Parrin Wenst'\nGovernor Parrin Wenst says, in Alaran, 'I'm so relieved to hear things went through without a hitch. I, Captain Reles, the rebels, and all of Sarith owe you a debt of gratitude. I will make sure you are rewarded properly for your efforts. If you would be willing, we'd like your help with the next phase of this operation. Please speak to Ain Kavus at the drydock, whom you've met. Let Ain know you want to help.'\nYou've set the Orator's army back, assisted the citizens of Sarith, and weakened the control Archon Eries has over the city. The rebel leader Ain Kavus is said to be preparing the next strike against Archon Eries and High Priest Vyers if you'd wish to assist further.\n_Rewards:_\n273 platinum, 3 gold, 3 silver, 4 copper\nExperience\nEltarki's Diary - Time and Tides\n_If you're a Wizard, you can also choose your Sarith port spells as a reward._\n- Eltarki's Diary - Time and Tides [item=98630]\n- Scroll: Sarith Gate [item=100711]\n- Scroll: Sarith Portal [item=100547]\n- Scroll: Translocate Sarith [item=100548]",
