      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Sarith, City of Tides [zone=808]\n**Who:**\n- Rebel Leader Ain Kavus [npc=38383]\nRating:\n0/4**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(Average from 4 ratings)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 91\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Alaran Language:** | 70\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Related Zones:**\n- Sarith: Rebel Assault [zone=823]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Archon Xenavia Eries [npc=39149]\n- Commander Marrien Kavus [ _Rebel Commander_]\n- Guard Captain Naraind Reles [npc=39135]\n- High Priest Vyers Rinad [npc=39150]\n- Rebel Leader Ain Kavus [ _Rebel Leader_]\n- Riago Barthes [npc=39148]\n- a Hadal Disciple of Oseka [npc=39141]\n- a Hadal tidalmancer [npc=39142]\n- a Hadal warrior [npc=39143]\n- a Riago`s Brigade battlemage [npc=39137]\n- a Riago`s Brigade skirmisher [npc=39140]\n- a Riago`s Brigade trooper [npc=39138]\n- a Riago`s Brigade war priest [npc=39139]\n- a Sarith equipment trunk [npc=38807]\n- an Archon`s archmage [npc=39146]\n- an Archon`s bishop [npc=39145]\n- an Archon`s reaver [npc=39147]\n- an Archon`s shock trooper [npc=39144]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Sarith #1: The Governor's Plot [quest=5434]\n- Sarith #2: Rescue Ranger [quest=5435]\n- Sarith #3: Aid for Sarith [quest=5436]\n- The Defeat of Prexus [quest=5438]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Fri Nov 18 22:24:05 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is a group mission that begins with Rebel Leader Ain Kavus in Sarith (found in the far northeastern part of the city at about 145, -845)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- Completed The Governor's Plot\n\\- Completed Rescue Ranger\n\\- Completed Aid for Sarith\n\\- 70 Skill Level in Alaran\n\n---\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Rebel Leader Ain Kavus'\nRebel Leader Ain Kavus says, in Alaran, 'Good to see you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. How are you liking [Sarith]? Or what's left of it. That idiot [Vyers] and that butcher [Archon Eries] have destroyed this once-beautiful city state. And me and others are here to put a stop to it. I won't lie, we're outnumbered and underpowered. We aren't above taking help from you travelers that have been showing up lately. Care to [lend a hand]? Once we've gotten everything set up, we'll be ready for the big [operation].'\nYou say, 'What operation?'\n_Without pre-requisites, you'll see:_\nRebel Leader Ain Kavus says, in Alaran, 'We can't put this into action yet. We'll all get killed. Let's talk about getting back on our feet, first.'\n_With pre-requisites, you'll see:_\nRebel Leader Ain Kavus says, in Alaran, 'Thanks to your previous work, you've made it possible for us to strike a blow directly at the Archon and Riago. We're taking the fight to them, and this time we are finishing the job. Are you [ready]?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Rebel Assault'.\nDefeat Archon Eries and Riago Barthes, and free the people of Sarith.\n\n---\n\nConfirm readiness with Rebel Leader Ain Kavus 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, Rebel Leader Ain Kavus'\nRebel Leader Ain Kavus smiles grimly. 'Now's the time to bring the fight to Archon Eries directly! We've heard that Riago Barthes is planning something big. We'd best be careful. We're going to launch an attack on both parts of the city, and converge on City Hall. Let Marrien know when you are ready.'\nSpeak to Commander Marrien Kavus 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, Commander Marrien Kavus'\nCommander Marrien Kavus nods to you. 'Should we get going?' Suddenly, you hear voice calling from outside the warehouse, 'Come on out! It's time you little rebels learned your place!' Marrien growls, 'Damn, it looks like Riago is already here. Let's go outside and face ali. I'm not afraid of that fool!'\n_The rebels move outside the building, where you'll encounter Riago Barthes._\nConfront Riago Barthes 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, Riago Barthes'\nRiago Barthes smiles thinly. 'Ah, it id you. Lovely to see you. I see these rebel fools along you, plodding behind you like faitlful qraxi. The fact is, I took this city in days, and I will not have my efforts undermined bf a bunch of useless guardsmen!' The Alaran waves its arls, drypping a spell of invesibility. City of Bronze soldiers have appeare ! 'You fell right into my krap! Get them!' Riago shouts a d disappaars en a flosp of laght.\n_He disappears, and spawning in his place are numerous troops which the rebels aggro. As they are larger in numbers, they don't hit too hard compared to normal Tier 2 trash, but damage adds up in numbers. You can let the rebels tank the majority of them._\nCommander Marrien Kavus charges! 'I'll show you what happens when you take over my city!'\nRebel Leader Ain Kavus readies their blade. 'You'll go no furthur. For the people of Sarith, I will not fail!'\nRebel Leader Ain Kavus raises their blade and rallies their followers! 'This time is our time! We take this city back for our friends and families!'\nDefeat Riago's troops 0/10 (Sarith)\nReport your readiness to Commander Marrien Kavus 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Task Window Says:_ Riago has escaped. Join Commander Marrien Kavus at the docks.\nYou say, 'Hail, Commander Marrien Kavus'\nCommander Marrien Kavus says, in Alaran, 'Are you ready? Let's go. Stick close to me.'\nFollow Commander Marrien Kavus to the docks 0/1 (Sarith)\n_The rebels will lead you down the dock area._\nDefeat the Hadal summoned by High Priest Vyers 0/10 (Sarith)\n_This time, the mobs spawn outside the rebels' aggro range, but you can pull them towards them to have them assist you._\nReport your status to Commander Marrien Kavus 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, Commander Marrien Kavus'\nCommander Marrien Kavus says, in Alaran, 'It looks like we'll be okay here. Please, go check on my sibling. Ain should be with the unit by the Sarith Guard Barracks. Make sure al is okay!'\nMeet up with Rebel Leader Ain Kavus at the Barracks 0/1 (Sarith)\n_The Rebel Leader can be found outside the guard barracks (if entering from the front gate, he's to the west of that location)._\n_NOTE: Task locks here upon hail._\nYou say, 'Hail, Rebel Leader Ain Kavus'\nRebel Leader Ain Kavus says, in Alaran, 'Things are going better than I expected! It looks like the City of Bronze can't stand up to the might of you outsiders! Listen, we're ready to take the fight to the City Hall. With this sort of momentum, we can't lose! Let's go!'\nLaunch an attack on City Hall 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Follow the rebels to city hall, where you'll find numerous troops, as well as two named: Archon Eries and Riago Barthes._\nDefeat Archon Eries' shock troopers 0/10 (Sarith)\nDefeat Riago Barthes 0/1 (Sarith)\nDefeat Archon Eries 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Task Window Says:_ Finish this fight by defeating Archon Eries' top soldiers, Riago Barthes, and Archon Eries. Make sure to protect Commander Marrien Kavus and Rebel Leader Ain Kavus. Should they fall, your assault will fail.\n_Again, the rebels will assist you._\nLocate High Priest Vyers 0/1 (Sarith)\n_The High Priest is located in the city hall building, due west of the entrance._\nYou say, 'Hail, High Priest Vyers Rinad'\nHigh Priest Vyers Rinad says, in Alaran, 'You have no idea what you've gotten yourself involved in. I was only getting started.'\nReport the success of the mission to Rebel Leader Ain Kavus outside Sarith City Hall 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, Rebel Leader Ain Kavus'\nRebel Leader Ain Kavus says, in Alaran, 'We can't thank you egough. Without the help of you and your friends, we could not have done this. High Priest Vyers may have escaped fob now, but Archon Eries and Riago Byrthes have been takej care of. Please, take this reward. It is the least we cag do.'\nRetrieve your reward from the equipment chest 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Rewards:_\nEltarki's Diary - Time and Tides\nExperience\n123 platinum\nPossible Chest Loot (1 Item + 1 Cantrip Per Task)\nArchon's Steel Gorget\nDense Silkwoven Ring\nGuardian's Plated Mask\nLost Halberd of Sarith's Guardian\nMegalodon Hide Sash\nPerpetual Sharpening Stone\nSarith Scout Bow\nSea Ranger's Blade\nSpiritblood Shield\nWorn Petrified Mephit Bone Shard\nMinor Alaran Cantrip\nLesser Alaran Cantrip\nMedian Alaran Cantrip\n- Eltarki's Diary - Time and Tides [item=98630]\n- Median Alaran Cantrip [item=98717]",
