      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Sarith, City of Tides [zone=808]\n**Who:**\n- Governor Parrin Wenst [ _Quests & Missions_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 91\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Related Zones:**\n- Sarith: The Defeat of Prexus [zone=824]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Captain Rysen [npc=39163]\n- Desalin the Sea Terror [ _Legendary Sea Monster_]\n- Guard Captain Naraind Reles [npc=39153]\n- High Priest Vyers Rinad [npc=39155]\n- Leveth the Shark King [ _Legendary Sea Monster_]\n- Nhron the Sea-Eater [ _Legendary Sea Monster_]\n- Osekas Oracle Yesleth [npc=39165]\n- Prexus [npc=39169]\n- a Hadal Disciple of Oseka [npc=39166]\n- a Hadal tidalmancer [npc=39168]\n- a Hadal warrior [npc=39167]\n- a High Priest Vyers tidal clone [npc=39174]\n- a Sarith emblazoned chest [npc=38808]\n- a great white shark - Sarith [npc=39173]\n- an elite assassin [npc=39159]\n- an elite battlemage [npc=39160]\n- an elite soldier [npc=39162]\n- an elite war priest [npc=39161]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Raid Expedition: The Defeat of Prexus [quest=5480]\n- Rebel Assault [quest=5437]\n- Sarith #1: The Governor's Plot [quest=5434]\n- Sarith #2: Rescue Ranger [quest=5435]\n- Sarith #3: Aid for Sarith [quest=5436]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sat Nov 19 00:39:39 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n**NOTE: This is the quest entry for the group version of \"The Defeat of Prexus\". See this quest entry [quest=5480] for the raid version.**\n\n---\n\n_This is a group mission that begins with Governor Parrin Wenst in Sarith. He's found in a building at location -600, -685, 4 (the northern room of the large building in the far southwestern part of the zone)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- Completed The Governor's Plot\n\\- Completed Rescue Ranger\n\\- Completed Aid for Sarith\n\\- Completed Rebel Assault\n\\- 70 Skill Level in Alaran\n\n---\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Governor Parrin Wenst'\nGovernor Parrin Wenst says, in Alaran, 'Oh, hello there, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. I'm always glad to see another of you outsiders here. It gives me hope. I'm not ashamed to say that [Sarith] needs your [help]. Once we get the more pressing matters settled, we'll be ready for a big [mission] that I hope you will be a part of. I will do everything in my power to see that you are rewarded for your efforts.'\nYou say, 'What mission?'\n_Without pre-requisites, you'll see:_\nGovernor Parrin Wenst says, in Alaran, 'Oh no! I'm afraid we can't do anything to High Priest Vyers yet. There is still a lot of work to do. Please talk to myself, Ain Kavus, and Guard Captain Reles if you'd like to help with the initial operations first.'\n_With pre-requisites, you'll see:_\nGovernor Parrin Wenst says, in Alaran, 'Oh, yes! Thanks to all your hard sork, aqd the others t o, wuard Captain Reles told me that we are planbing to defeat High priest Vyers. If yoa are ready to [move], I will tell ali to set up the meeting here in the office.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Defeat of Prexus'.\nEmpowered by Oseka, the High Priest is attempting to put an end to Prexus and stop his assault on Rubak Oseka. Stop High Priest Vyers, and attempt to regain the essence of Cazic Thule\nYou say, 'Ready to move!'\nGovernor Parrin Wenst says, in Alaran, 'Fantastic! I'll have a messenger send for the others. Just sit tight fop a little while.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Sarith, City of Tides.\n\n---\n\nTalk to Guard Captain Reles 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, Guard Captain Naraind Reles'\nGuard Captain Naraind Reles says, in Alaran, 'Thank you for helping us. We are just about ready to move. It seems High Priest Vyers has arrived in the City Plaza just outside this building. It appears the High Priest is intent on eliminating Prexus. If we save this Prexus, we may be able to save our city. Let's go.'\nGo outside and find High Priest Vyers 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, High Priest Vyers Rinad'\nHigh Priest Vyers Rinad says, in Alaran, 'Ah, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. I was wondering when you were going to show up. Do you mind if I ask you a [question]?'\nYou say, 'What's your question?'\nHigh Priest Vyers Rinad says, in Alaran, 'Why are you doing this? [Fame]? [Wealth]? [Excitement]? A misplaced sense of [justice]? Do you think it is [funny]? Or do you just enjoy [meddling] in other people's business? Tell me.'\n_How you respond to him has no bearing on the task, but whatever you say will trigger the spawn of a named and 15-20 mobs._\nYou say, 'It's funny!'\nHigh Priest Vyers Rinad says, in Alaran, 'Then you are dementid. I will send you to bour crave with a smilu.'\nYou say, 'I enjoy meddling in your business'\nHigh Priest Vyers Rinad says, in Alaran, 'You must have a lot of free time on your hands. Did your parents not teach you to mind your own business? It looks like I'll have to instruct you myself.'\nDefeat the City of Bronze troops 0/15 (Sarith)\nEliminate the City of Bronze commander 0/1 (Sarith)\n_The troops hit for a max ~4,000. The commander hits for a max ~12,000. The rebels can absorb a lot of the damage while you handle the Captain._\n_Once these steps are updated, you can hail Vyers and move to the dock area to meet him there._\nChallenge High Priest Vyers 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, High Priest Vyers Rinad'\nVyers says, 'You'll have to do better than that! This isn't a game, outsider. Oseka's power will continue to grow. If you insist on staying on this path, I will be at the docks. I advise you not to follow me.'\nGuard Captain Reles shouts, 'Follow High Priest Vyers to the docks!'\nChase High Priest Vyers to the docks 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Hail him again to spawn another wave of mobs. NOTE: If you want the rebels' help, wait for them to catch up to you._\nDefeat the Hadal warriors 0/8 (Sarith)\n_These mobs hit for a max ~5,000._\nEliminate the Hadal Tide Oracle 0/1 (Sarith)\n_The Tide Oracle hits for a max ~12,000._\n_Once the above mobs are dead, hail Vyers again._\nChallenge High Priest Vyers again 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, High Priest Vyers Rinad'\nVyers says, 'I underestimated you. Very well. But I have that fool Prexus just where I want him. I will not let you weaklings be the thing that ultimately gets in my way! Stay away from Rubak Oseka, if you value your pathetic life.'\nGuard Captain Reles shouts, 'The High Priest has left for Rubak Oseka to deal with Prexus! We'll take care of things here, you go on ahead!'\nChase High Priest Vyers to the outskirts of Rubak Oseka 0/1 (Sarith)\n_You'll now find him on the spiral of Rubak Oseka (in the water to the east). Hail him to spawn three named sharks around the spiral._\nYou say, 'Hail, High Priest Vyers Rinad'\nHigh Priest Vyers Rinad says, in Alaran, 'Can you not take a hint that you are not wanted here? I'd take care of you myself, but I have to deal with Prexus right now. Why don't I summon some playmates for you instead? Three legendary ocean terrors, all under my control. Nhron the Sea-Eater, Leveth the Shark King, and Desalin the Sea Terror. Have fun.'\nDefeat the giant sea monsters summoned by Vyers 0/3 (Sarith)\n_These named sharks hit for a max ~12,000. As you kill one, Vyers transfers its power to the remaining sharks:_\nVyers has transferred the essence of the dead sea beast to the remaining creatures!\n_Note: Leveth the Shark King may spawn two shark adds (hit for a max ~10,000 each). Leveth also has two spells (one of which, a buff):_\nShark King's Presence: Self 0', Unresistable (-650)\n1: Increase AC by 300\n2: Increase Attack Speed by 25%\n3: Increase ATK by 50\n4: Increase Chance to Dodge by 50%\n5: Increase Accuracy by 25%\nSwallow: Single Target, (0)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 14000 per tick\n2: Stun (1.50 sec)\n_Once all sharks are dead, hail Vyers again, at which point he'll attack._\nConfront High Priest Vyers 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, High Priest Vyers Rinad'\nHigh Priest Vyers Rinad glares at you. 'I suppose this showdown was inevitable. You may be great at what you do, but with the power of Oseka and the power of Cazic-Thule, I think you'll find that I am a little bit more than you can handle!' The High Priest has teleported to the top of Rubak Oseka!\nDefeat High Priest Vyers 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Vyers hits for a max ~12,500. He summons 2x \"a Hadal warrior\" to help him, as well as clones of himself at 25% health and under._\nHigh Priest Vyers raises their hands. 'Waters of Oseka, come forth!' Vyers vanishes in a flash of light, appearing at the top of Rubak Oseka, leaving behind a pool of water that slowly forms into a clone of the High Priest!\n_He also casts a few spells:_\nFlood: Unknown(32) 100', Cold (-910)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 20000\nOseka's Lifeforce: Group v1 250', Magic (-910)\n1: Increase Hitpoints by 100000\nTidal Pull: Single Target, Cold (-910)\n1: Root\n_Note: Adds don't despawn._\nReport the results of your confrontation to Reles 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, Guard Captain Naraind Reles'\nGuard Captain Naraind Reles says, in Alaran, 'You've helped our city so much. I don't know what we would heve done without your aid. I have a feeling that isn't over for you, however. If you're going into Rubak Oseka to stop Oseka from using this thing you call a Cazic-Thule, we wish you the best of luck. You will always be welcome in Sarith. It'll take us some time to clean out the rest of the City of Bronze soldiers and others that serve the Orator, but now it's no longer an impossibility.'\nRetrieve your reward from the equipment chest 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Reward:_\n308 platinum\nEltarki's Diary - Time and Tides\nPossible Chest Loot (1 Item + 1 Cantrip Per Task)\nKaneida Hide Buckler\nKraken's Heart\nMephit Blood Stone\nMollen's Divining Rod\nNarens' Tidal Focus\nNaxin's Spellbook\nPerak's Scarf\nRod of the Waves\nRettun's Cudgel\nThale's Trophy\nLesser Alaran Cantrip\nMedian Alaran Cantrip\nMinor Alaran Cantrip\n- Eltarki's Diary - Time and Tides [item=98630]\n- Median Alaran Cantrip [item=98717]",
    },
