      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Sarith, City of Tides [zone=808]\n**Who:**\n- Coraln Seagazer [npc=38394]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 100\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Vial of Soothing Water [item=99544]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Rubak Oseka, Temple of the Sea [zone=809]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a churning water spirit [npc=38540]\n- a disturbed water spirit [npc=38541]\n- a soothed water spirit [npc=39203]\n- an agitated water spirit [npc=38543]\n- an angry water spirit [npc=38542]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Mon Nov 21 20:57:27 2011\nModified: Wed Jul 22 03:56:55 2020 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This solo task begins with a Kedge named Coraln Seagazer in Sarith, located in the northeastern part of the dock area (35, -1090, -4)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- No tasks\n\\- 73 Skill Level in Alaran\n\n---\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Coraln Seagazer'\nCoraln Seagazer says 'Such sorrow the [water spirits] feel.'\nYou say, 'Water spirits?'\nCoraln Seagazer says 'The water spirits in the Temple of Rubak have become innocent casualties of the conflict between us and Oseka and nobody seems to notice, or care. I however do care and wish to [soothe] them.'\nYou say, 'How can we soothe them?'\nCoraln Seagazer says 'I am unable to enter the Temple, but you can. Will you take these vials of soothing [water] and give them to the water spirits?'\nYou say, 'I'll take some water'\nCoraln Seagazer says 'War is an inevitable part of life, but it is not right that the water spirits needlessly suffer. Take these vials of water and give them to the agitated water spirits. If you are successful in this endeavor, return to me and let me know so my mind can be at ease.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Soothing the Spirits'.\nCoraln Seagazer is concerned about water spirits in the Temple of Rubak. They have become agitated by the ongoing conflct between Prexus and Oseka, the goddess of Tides and nobody else seems to care. Coraln has asked you to give the water spirits some soothing water to see if it can soothe them.\n_You receive 4x \"A Vial of Soothing Water\"._\n_You may need more than 4 vials, so just say \"water\" to Corain to get more._\n\n---\n\nGive a Vial of Soothing Water to an Agitated Water Spirit 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nGive a Vial of Soothing Water to an Disturbed Water Spirit 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nGive a Vial of Soothing Water to an Angry Water Spirit 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nGive a Vial of Soothing Water to an Churning Water Spirit 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_You'll come across the water spirits as you make your way down Rubak Oseka, with the churning spirit being on the bottom level._\n_Occasionally, the spirit will reject the water (you'll receive it back) and attack you (hits for a max ~11,000). If this happens, you can either fade aggro or kill it (note that it sees invisibility). If faded, it will respawn non-aggro after about a minute. If killed, it has a fairly quick respawn._\nReturn to Coraln Seagrazer and speak with him 0/1 (Sarith, City of Tides)\nYou say, 'Hail, Coraln Seagazer'\nCoraln Seagazer says, 'You have done well this day. The spirits' souls call to me. They are at peace. Thank you, my friend.'\n_Reward:_\n205 platinum\nExperience\nEltarki's Diary - Depths of Thought\n- Eltarki's Diary - Depths of Thought [item=98071]",
    },
