        { id = 98071, name = "Depths of Thought\n- Eltarki's Diary - Depths of Thought", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Sarith, City of Tides [zone=808]\n**Who:**\n- Solphius Kelprunner [npc=38391]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Hadal Scrying Device [item=99358]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Rubak Oseka, Temple of the Sea [zone=809]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Rubak #2: Sacred Relics [quest=5459]\n- Rubak #3: Tides of Change [quest=5460]\n- Rubak #4: The Key to Freedom [quest=5461]\n- Rubak #5: Begin the Offensive [quest=5462]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Mon Nov 21 20:57:34 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is the first task in a series of five; a shared task (1-6 players) that begins with a Kedge named Solphius Kelprunner in Sarith, located in the northeastern part of the dock area (-35, -905, 0)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- No tasks\n\\- 73 Skill Level in Alaran\nYou say, 'Hail, Solphius Kelprunner'\nSolphius Kelprunner says 'The tides of battle turn quickly. The forces of Prexus are winning for now, but we must remain vigilant to keep our edge. In this, I believe you can [help].'\nYou say, 'How can I help?'\nSolphius Kelprunner says 'If you wish to serve Prexus, you must enter the temple of Rubak Oseka and gather information on those that dwell there, so that we may be better [informed] before we launch an offensive against them.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Oseka's Knowledge'.\nSolphius Kelprunner wants you to investigate some murals in Rubak Oseka.\nYou will need a scrying device before you can fully understand the murals. Kill Hadal in Rubak Oseka to obtain one.\nYou say, 'Informed?'\nSolphius Kelprunner says 'Religious murals line the walls of the temple interior. Unfortunately we have been unable to decipher them. It is said however that some of the Hadal may hold items that can decipher the murals. Obtain one of these items and decipher some of the murals.'\n\n---\n\nKill Hadal in Rubak Oseka to obtain a Hadal Scrying Device 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_Kill Hadal mobs (the fishman creatures) until one drops a \"Hadal Scrying Device\". This will open up the next four steps. Whoever loots the item must click on the four murals. These are the painting/picture-looking things you'll see on the center's walls as you make your way down the ramp._\n_Side Note: Whoever does the mural clicks for this task will be automatically granted a skill of 100 in the Hadal language (25 per click)._\nDecipher the first mural 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nUsing the Hadal Scrying Device, you are better able to decipher the mural. On Alaris, there was a city dedicated to the sea god, and it too was called Sarith. Sarith means \"Unbounded\" in the Alaran tongue. It was a huge city, obviously the safest port in the world. When Oseka arrived on Norrath, al did alir best to recreate the city that was dedicated to ali on Alaris. As a mortal, Oseka was a sea-fearing explorer, treasure hunter, and part-time pirate.\nDecipher the second mural 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nUsing the Hadal Scrying Device, you are better able to decipher the mural. Oseka has loved the sea ever since al was a child in Sarith, and always had a thirst for adventure and a cunning mind. Al became quite famous for alir exploits, carving out a name for aleself among the Alarans world-wide.\nDecipher the third mural 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nUsing the Hadal Scrying Device, you are better able to decipher the mural. As time progressed, Oseka gained a loyal set of followers, the best explorers and most notorious pirates of the surrounding seas. Chased by a few high profile members of authority, al always managed to slip away, quickly cobbling together devious tricks and traps to escape capture. Doing so gained ali the respect of those authorities as well, adding to alir legend.\nDecipher the fourth mural 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nUsing the Hadal Scrying Device, you are better able to decipher the mural. Oseka became a god by becoming a famous maritime explorer and a legendary pirate. Though never being one for rules, al did not have a problem with the Triumvirate in most situations, given alir free dominion over the ocean and tides. Alir hometown of Sarith, which al adored despite always being on the move, worshipped al and al rejoiced in it. Al also gained the devout worship of the Hadal, a mysterious underwater race that resided in alir temple of tides called Rubak Oseka. Not that alir free-spirited nature didn't come into conflict with the Triumvirate. And when they did clash, al was never shy about using alir devious mind to find loopholes and rules to bend the Triumvirate's laws.\nReturn to Solphius Kelprunner in Sarith and speak with him 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Note: With no lock point, players can be added to this task right up to its completion._\nYou say, 'Hail, Solphius Kelprunner'\nSolphius Kelprunner says, 'So the foolish Hadal and Alarans wish to resurrect their god, Oseka? Even if they did, they are no match for Prexus' forces. I think it's time to use their religious relics against them. Speak to me again if you are interested.'\n_Reward:_\n273 platinum\nEltarki's Diary - Depths of Thought\n- Eltarki's Diary - Depths of Thought [item=98071]",
    },
