      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Sarith, City of Tides [zone=808]\n**Who:**\n- Solphius Kelprunner [npc=38391]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Carving of Oseka [item=100830]\n- Conch of Whispers [item=100832]\n- Coral of Wisdom [item=100785]\n- Prexus-Infused Carving of Oseka [item=101082]\n- Prexus-Infused Conch of Whispers [item=101080]\n- Prexus-Infused Coral of Wisdom [item=101081]\n- Prexus-Infused Rune of the Sacred Ophidian [item=101083]\n- Rune of the Sacred Ophidian [item=100781]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Rubak Oseka, Temple of the Sea [zone=809]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Rubak #1: Oseka's Knowledge [quest=5458]\n- Rubak #3: Tides of Change [quest=5460]\n- Rubak #4: The Key to Freedom [quest=5461]\n- Rubak #5: Begin the Offensive [quest=5462]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Mon Nov 21 20:57:40 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is the second task in a series of five; a group task (3-6 players) that begins with a Kedge named Solphius Kelprunner in Sarith, located in the northeastern part of the dock area (-35, -905, 0)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- Completion of Oseka's Knowledge\n\\- 73 Skill Level in Alaran\nYou say, 'Hail, Solphius Kelprunner'\nSolphius Kelprunner says 'I want you to [collect] some religious relics from Oseka. I suspect all of these items are in the possession of various Hadal or Alarans.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Sacred Relics'.\nSolphius Kelprunner in Sarith wants you to gathersome sacred relics from the Alarans and Hadal in Rubak Oseka.\nYou say, 'Why do you want me to collect these things?'\nSolphius Kelprunner says 'Obtain the relics and return to me. I will reveal more about my plan then.'\n\n---\n\nObtain the Conch of Whispers 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nObtain the Coral of Wisdom 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nOptain the Carving of Oseka 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nObtain the Rune of the Sacred Ophidian 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_The above four items seem to drop randomly from Alarans and Hadal._\n_NOTE: These items are NOT pre-lootable._\nReturn to Solphius Kelprunner and speak with him 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, Solphius Kelprunner'\nSolphius Kelprunner says 'Excellent work. We will use these relics to attempt to turn the Alarans and Hadal to our side. I want you to take the relics to a nearby ally by the name of Aquarn the Tidalmaster. He will bless the relics in Prexus' name. Once he has blessed them, return to me.'\n_Aquarn the Tidalmaster is an elemental found nearby._\nGive the Conch of Whispers to Aquarn the Tidalmaster to have it blessed in the name of Prexus 0/1 (Sarith)\nGive the Coral of Wisdom to Aquarn the Tidalmaster to have it blessed in the name of Prexus 0/1 (Sarith)\nGive the Carving of Oseka to Aquarn the Tidalmaster to have it blessed in the name of Prexus 0/1 (Sarith)\nGive the Rune of the Sacred Ophidian to Aquarn the Tidalmaster to have it blessed in the name of Prexus 0/1 (Sarith)\nAquarn the Tidalmaster says 'I bless this relic with the all consuming waters of Prexus!'\n_You received \"Prexus-Infused\" versions of the same items._\n_NOTE: Keep this items on you for the next task._\nReturn to Solphius Kelprunner and speak with him 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, Solphius Kelprunner'\nSolphius Kelprunner says, 'Yes, I can feel the power of Prexus within the relics! Guard these relics with care. You will need them for the next stage of my plan. Speak to me again when you are ready.'\n_Reward:_\n273 platinum\nEltarki's Diary - Depths of Thought\n- Eltarki's Diary - Depths of Thought [item=98071]",
