      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Sarith, City of Tides [zone=808]\n**Who:**\n- Solphius Kelprunner [npc=38391]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 95\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Prexus-Infused Carving of Oseka [item=101082]\n- Prexus-Infused Conch of Whispers [item=101080]\n- Prexus-Infused Coral of Wisdom [item=101081]\n- Prexus-Infused Rune of the Sacred Ophidian [item=101083]\n- Vial of Ophidian Blood [item=100828]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Rubak Oseka, Temple of the Sea [zone=809]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Altar of Serpents [npc=38544]\n- Altar of Tides [npc=38545]\n- Altar of Whispers [npc=38546]\n- Altar of Wisdom [npc=38547]\n- Cursed Water Elemental [npc=39202]\n- a coral ophidian [npc=38556]\n- a revered ophidian [npc=38555]\n- a ringed ophidian [npc=38554]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Rubak #1: Oseka's Knowledge [quest=5458]\n- Rubak #2: Sacred Relics [quest=5459]\n- Rubak #4: The Key to Freedom [quest=5461]\n- Rubak #5: Begin the Offensive [quest=5462]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Mon Nov 21 20:57:53 2011\nModified: Sat Feb 8 15:50:13 2020 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is the third task in a series of five; a shared task (1-6 players) that begins with a Kedge named Solphius Kelprunner in Sarith, located in the northeastern part of the dock area (-35, -905, 0)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- Completion of \"Oseka's Knowledge\"\n\\- Completion of \"Sacred Relics\"\n\\- 73 Skill Level in Alaran\nYou say, 'Hail, Solphius Kelprunner'\nSolphius Kelprunner says 'So eager to help. Prexus will remember your contribution to this war. Head back to Oseka and seek out the sacred ophidians that dwell in the watery depths. You are to obtain several vials of their blood. Once you have the blood, place the relics at the various altars and sprinkle them with the ophidian blood. This will either anger, or convince the followers of Oseka to give up any false hope that Oseka can save them from the coming storm.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Tides of Change'.\nSolphius Kelprunner hopes that he can convince some of the Alarans and Hadal that worship Oseka to defect to Prexus' army. To accomplish this, you will need to place the artifacts, now blessed with Prexus' power, you stole earlier into several altars and pour the blood of Oseka's sacred serpents over them.\nObtain several vials of Sacred Ophidian Blood from the ophidians that inhabit the bottom of the temple of Rubak.\n\n---\n\nCollect vials of Ophidian Blood from the Ophidians in Rubak 0/4 (Rubak Oseka)\n_The ophidians are snakes found mostly in the bottom floor of the temple, and in greater numbers in the water under the bottom floor. The vial is a common drop._\n_Each of the next eight steps opens up one by one._\nGive the Prexus-Infused Conch of Whispers to the Altar of Whispers 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nGive a Vial of Ophidian Blood to the Altar of Whispers 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nGive the Prexus-Infused Coral of Wisdom to the Altar of Wisdom 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nGive a Vial of Ophidian Blood to the Altar of Wisdom 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nGive the Prexus-Infused Carving of Oseka to the Altar of Tides 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nGive a Vial of Ophidian Blood to the Altar of Tides 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nGive the Prexus-Infused Rune of the Sacred Ophidian to the Altar of Serpents 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nGive a Vial of Ophidian Blood to the Altar of Serpents 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_The altars are found in the side rooms adjacent to the main ramp. In each altar room are 3-4 trash mobs. Killing them isn't necessary to complete the task, but will make the turn-ins easier._\n_NOTE: Each time you complete a set of turn-ins, a Cursed Water Elemental spawns at the altar and attacks._\n_The Altar of Whispers is at 250, 150, 290._\n_The Altar of Wisdom is at 0, 250, 320._\n_The Altar of Tides is at -200, -100, 350._\n_The Altar of Serpents is at 0, -250, 375._\nReturn to Solphius Kelprunner in Sarith and speak with him 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, Solphius Kelprunner'\nSolphius Kelprunner says, 'So my plan only served to further infuriate the inhabitants of Rubak? Oseka's grasp on them is indeed powerful. So be it. They may be strong, but our army will not give up until Oseka and their minions have been utterly destroyed. Aquarn the Tidalmaster was looking for you. It is best not to keep him waiting. Go to him now and see how you can further serve Prexus.'\n_Reward:_\n205 platinum\nEltarki's Diary - Depths of Thought\n- Eltarki's Diary - Depths of Thought [item=98071]",
    },
