      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Sarith, City of Tides [zone=808]\n**Who:**\n- Aquarn the Tidalmaster [npc=38392]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Blue Gem [item=99359]\n- Green Gem [item=99360]\n- Orange Gem [item=100851]\n- Red Gem [item=99361]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Rubak Oseka, Temple of the Sea [zone=809]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- A Blue Orb [npc=38539]\n- A Green Orb [npc=38538]\n- A Red Orb [npc=38537]\n- An Orange Orb [npc=38536]\n- Silbek [npc=38548]\n- a priest [npc=38550]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Rubak #1: Oseka's Knowledge [quest=5458]\n- Rubak #2: Sacred Relics [quest=5459]\n- Rubak #3: Tides of Change [quest=5460]\n- Rubak #5: Begin the Offensive [quest=5462]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Mon Nov 21 20:57:57 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is the fourth task in a series of five; a shared task (1-6 players) that begins with an elemental named Aquarn the Tidalmaster in Sarith, located in the northeastern part of the dock area (around -35, -905, 0)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- Completion of \"Oseka's Knowledge\"\n\\- Completion of \"Sacred Relics\"\n\\- Completion of \"Tides of Change\"\n\\- 73 Skill Level in Alaran\nYou say, 'Hail, Aquarn the Tidalmaster'\nAquarn the Tidalmaster says 'Before we launch an attack against Rubak, there is one more task I need you to undertake. One of our operatives, a Kedge named, Silbek, has been captured and is to be sacrificed to Oseka, the Goddess of Tides. We need to get him [out] of Rubak.'\nYou say, 'How do we get him out of Rubak?'\nAquarn the Tidalmaster says 'Unfortunately it will not be so simple. He is being held under a powerful spell generated by four magical orbs. We have discovered, much to our fortune, that the Hadal priests sometimes carry colored gems that can disable these [orbs].'\nYou say, 'What about the orbs?'\nAquarn the Tidalmaster says 'If you were able to collect the gems, perhaps you can disable the gems and get Silbek out of there. Are you [up to] this most important of tasks?'\nYou say, 'I'm up to it'\nAquarn the Tidalmaster says 'I knew you would not disappoint me. Return to me after Silbek has been rescued.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Key to Freedom'.\nBefore an all-out attack can be carried out on the Temple of Rubak, Aquarn needs you to rescue a Kedge named Silbek who is to be sacrificed to Oseka.\nCollect a green, orange, red, and blue gem from the Hadal priests in the Temple of Rubak.\n\n---\n\nCollect a Green Gem 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nCollect an Orange Gem 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nCollect a Red Gem 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nCollect a Blue Gem 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_The gems drop randomly from \"a priest\" (Hadal model). Once you've looted the four gems, you'll have to turn them in to the colored orbs next to the pearl on the bottom floor of the temple._\n_NOTE: These are NOT pre-lootable. If you give a gem to the wrong colored orb, it will give it back to you._\nGive the Green Gem to the correct orb 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_The Green Gem goes to the Red Orb._\nGive the Orange Gem to the correct orb 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_The Orange Gem goes to the Blue Orb._\nGive the Red Gem to the correct orb 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_The Red Gem goes to the Green Orb._\nGive the Blue Gem to the correct orb 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_The Blue Gem goes to the Orange Orb. Upon this last turn-in, a Kedge named Silbek spawns._\nSpeak with Silbek 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_Task Window Says:_ You have disabled the orbs that had incapacitated Silbek! Speak with him before you leave the temple.\nYou say, 'Hail, Silbek'\nSilbek says 'You arrived just in time! The Hadal were going to sacrifice me to the ophidians in the name of Oseka. You have my thanks!'\nReturn to Aquarn the Tidalmaster and speak with him 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, Aquarn the Tidalmaster'\nAquarn the Tidalmaster says, 'I have received word or your success with rescuing Silbek. I am pleased. With your aid, the forces of Prexus are sure to be victorious. Speak with Tiljin of the Deep for your next assignment. He should be somewhere nearby.'\n_Reward:_\n273 platinum\nExperience\nEltarki's Diary - Depths of Thought\n- Eltarki's Diary - Depths of Thought [item=98071]",
    },
