      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Sarith, City of Tides [zone=808]\n**Who:**\n- General Serobi [npc=38395]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Alaran Language:** | 73\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Detonator Four [item=100026]\n- Detonator One [item=100023]\n- Detonator Three [item=100025]\n- Detonator Two [item=100024]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Rubak Oseka: Assault the Tower [zone=827]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Altar of Serpents [npc=39786]\n- Altar of Tides [npc=39785]\n- Altar of Whispers [npc=39783]\n- Altar of Wisdom [npc=39784]\n- General Serobi [npc=39787]\n- High Priest Xalziks [npc=38814]\n- a cold steel chest [npc=38812]\n- a whirlpool [npc=39788]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Rubak #1: Oseka's Knowledge [quest=5458]\n- Rubak #2: Sacred Relics [quest=5459]\n- Rubak #3: Tides of Change [quest=5460]\n- Rubak #4: The Key to Freedom [quest=5461]\n- Rubak #5: Begin the Offensive [quest=5462]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Mon Nov 21 21:13:45 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is a group mission that begins with General Serobi in Sarith. He's found in the northeastern part of the dock area at about 20, -1050._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- Completed \"Oseka's Knowledge\"\n\\- Completed \"Sacred Relics\"\n\\- Completed \"Tides of Change\"\n\\- Completed \"The Key to Freedom\"\n\\- Completed \"Begin the Offensive\"\n\\- 73 Skill Level in Alaran\n\n---\n\nYou say, 'Hail, General Serobi'\n_Without pre-requisites, you'll see:_\nGeneral Serobi says 'You are not yet ready for the task I have planned. Speak with Solphius Kelprunner, Tiljin of the Deep, or Aquarn the Tidalmaster if you wish to help.'\n_With pre-requisites, you'll see:_\nGeneral Serobi says 'I've been expecting you. With the explosive runes armed, now is the time to make our [move] against the Temple of Rubak Oseka.'\nYou say, 'Let's make our move'\nGeneral Serobi says 'Take these detonators and use them at the various altars in Rubak. They will detonate the explosive runes you armed. Hopefully we can do enough damage to the temple that we can get the attention of the High Priest. If the High Priest does appear, destroy him! Are you [ready] to undertake this most important of missions?'\n_You receive four detonators._\nYou have been assigned the task 'Assault the Tower'.\nYou are to enter the Temple of Rubak Oseka and use the four detonators to detonate the runed explosives you previously armed. It is hoped that enough damage is done to the temple, the High Priest will show himself and you can slay him.\n\n---\n\n_The steps will open up one at a time. You'll need to begin with the furthest altar, the Altar of Whispers, and make your way back up._\n_\\- The Altar of Whispers is at 250, 150, 290._\n_\\- The Altar of Wisdom is at 0, 250, 320._\n_\\- The Altar of Tides is at -200, -100, 350._\n_\\- The Altar of Serpents is at 0, -250, 375._\n_All trash mobs in the altar rooms will have to be killed before you can turn in a detonator. If you try to do a turn-in without doing so, you'll see:_\nYou can't put the detonator on the altar with those attendants watching!\nGive Detonator One unto the Altar of Whispers 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_Task Window Says:_ Give Detonator One unto the Altar of Whispers. It will self-detonate, causing the explosive rune you had previously armed to explode and damage the temple.\nGive Detonator Two unto the Altar of Wisdom 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nGive Detonator Three unto the Altar of Tides 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_NOTE: The task locks as you turn in the third detonator._\nGive Detonator Four unto the Altar of Serpents 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_Upon turning in the last one, the temple rumbles and you'll see:_\nThe temple shakes violently as the runed explosion is triggered!\nHigh Priest Xalziks shouts, 'Enough! You shall not damage our temple any further! The forces of Prexus shall be destroyed! If you wish to prove your true courage, I await you at the bottom of the temple, cowards!\nDefeat High Priest Xalziks 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_Task Window Says:_ The High Priest has shown himself just as General Serobi had hoped. Destroy him!\n_High Priest Xalziks spawns on the bottom floor. He hits for a max ~12,500 and casts no AEs. He does, however, spawn a whirlpool on a random person, complete with a damage aura (hits every two seconds):_\nRaging Vortex: Single Target, Cold (-900)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 6346\n_Note: You can pull Xalziks into this whirlpool to do extra damage to him. There's also an achievement for doing this five times._\n_As he reaches low health (you'll need to do about 1 million hp of damage to get to this point), you'll see:_\nHigh Priest Xalziks says, in Alaran, 'I have no time for your childish games. You are foolish to think you could have defeated me, for I am the embodiment of Oseka herself! Run back to your leader like the cowards you are and let them know that the forces of Oseka shall win this war!'\nSpeak with General Serobi in the Temple of Rubak 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\nYou say, 'Hail, General Serobi'\nGeneral Serobi says 'So, Oseka is using the High Priest's body to do her dirty work. It is most fortunate for you that he did not finish this battle. You are not yet ready to confront him; this much is clear, but we have learned much from this encounter. Take your reward from this chest and rest for now. There is still much work to be done. When you are ready to [leave] the temple, let me know and I will send you back to Sarith.'\nLoot the Cold Steel chest for your reward 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_Reward:_\n136 platinum\nEltarki's Diary - Depths of Thought\nPossible Chest Loot (1 Item + 1 Cantrip Per Task)\nBeasts' Domain Tangle\nDeathleaper's Pendant\nFur-lined Epaulets of the High Guard\nGlobe of the Ocean\nGotikan's Herb Pouch\nGravel of the Sacred Temple\nLunatic's Blade\nMiggles' Braxi-Down Cloak\nShell-Shield of the Sacred\nStonebark Bow\nGreater Alaran Cantrip\nMedian Alaran Cantrip\n- Eltarki's Diary - Depths of Thought [item=98071]\n- Median Alaran Cantrip [item=98717]",
    },
