      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Sarith, City of Tides [zone=808]\n**Who:**\n- General Serobi [npc=38395]\nRating:\n0/2**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(Average from 2 ratings)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Alaran Language:** | 73\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Loot\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Ancient Pearlescent Talisman [item=97983]\n- Fury of the Tides [item=98144]\n- Pearlescent Signet [item=98023]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Rubak Oseka: Time and Tides [zone=828]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Essence of Oseka [npc=39792]\n- General Serobi [npc=39790]\n- High Priest Xalziks [npc=38816]\n- High Priest of Oseka [npc=38815]\n- a devout templar [npc=39789]\n- a watery chest [npc=38813]\n- a whirlpool [npc=40063]\n- a zealot [npc=39791]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Assault the Tower [quest=5463]\n- Rubak #1: Oseka's Knowledge [quest=5458]\n- Rubak #2: Sacred Relics [quest=5459]\n- Rubak #3: Tides of Change [quest=5460]\n- Rubak #4: The Key to Freedom [quest=5461]\n- Rubak #5: Begin the Offensive [quest=5462]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Mon Nov 21 21:33:30 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n**NOTE: This is the quest entry for the group version of \"Time and Tides\". See this quest entry [quest=5540] for the raid version.**\n\n---\n\n_This is a group mission that begins with General Serobi in Sarith. He's found in the northeastern part of the dock area at about 20, -1050._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- Completed \"Oseka's Knowledge\"\n\\- Completed \"Sacred Relics\"\n\\- Completed \"Tides of Change\"\n\\- Completed \"The Key to Freedom\"\n\\- Completed \"Begin the Offensive\"\n\\- Completed \"Assault the Tower\"\n\\- 73 Skill Level in Alaran\n\n---\n\nYou say, 'Hail, General Serobi'\n_Without pre-requisites, you'll see:_\nGeneral Serobi says 'You are not yet ready for the task I have planned. Speak with Solphius Kelprunner, Tiljin of the Deep, or Aquarn the Tidalmaster if you wish to help.'\n_With pre-requisites, you'll see:_\nYou say, 'Hail, General Serobi'\nGeneral Serobi bows respectfully in greeting, 'You look well rested, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. This is good. You will need your strength for what lies ahead. While your efforts thus far have been commendable, it is clear now that it will take a much greater force to stop Oseka. Large or small, all help is needed. Tell me, do you have a [group] or a [raiding party] on hand, or perhaps you're willing to make another [move] against the Temple of Rubak Oseka?'\nYou say, 'I have a group'\nGeneral Serobi nods with understanding, 'Ah, a group. This will help immensely. To be able to possess the bodies of alir High Priests is a power unlike any I have ever witnessed. If the source of alir [strength] lies in Rubak, we shall find it, and use it against alir.'\nYou say, 'Strength?'\nGeneral Serobi says 'Just as Prexus derives power from the oceans of Norrath, Oseka must be sustained from something within Rubak. Finding this source of power, however, won't be an easy task. Oseka and alir High Priests are likely expecting an attack...' The General reaches within his robe and withdraws a water-filled crystal flask. 'Within this [vial], the tremulous waters of Prexus are contained. The vial may be small, but the strength within is boundless. One drop alone can embody the power of the sea.''\nYou say, 'What vial?'\nGeneral Serobi says 'A gift bestowed upon me by Prexus himself. While he cannot [travel] to the domain of Oseka, his power could, if contained. The Fury of the Tides, when unleashed near the heart of Rubak, may cause enough of a disruption for you to find the source of Oseka's power and use it against alir.'\nYou say, 'We'll travel there'\nGeneral Serobi hands you the crystal flask with great care. 'You hold the power of Prexus in your hands. When you are ready to [begin], I will lead you to the heart of Rubak.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Time and Tides'.\n_Everyone receives a \"Fury of the Tides\"._\nTravel to Rubak Oseka, Temple of the Sea, and find Oseka's source of power and use it against alir.\nDefeat devout templars in Rubak, and loot the talismans or signets which are the souce of their ancient power.\n\n---\n\nLoot ancient relics from templars within Rubak 0/6 (Rubak Oseka)\nDefeat devout templars 0/6 (Rubak Oseka)\n_Clear your way down to the bottom floor of the temple. As you're doing so, three people should each loot two items (dropped by the templars): \"Pearlescent Signet\" and \"Ancient Pearlescent Talisman\"._\n\n---\n\nTravel to the pearl at the heart of Rubak 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_Task Window Says:_ At the heart of Rubak the High Priests of Oseka gather.\n_On the bottom floor of the temple are 4x \"High Priest of Oseka\". They are non-aggro until the event is triggered._\n\n---\n\nRelease water from Fury of the Tides to interrupt the High Priests 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_Task Window Says:_ Using the Fury of the Tides, create a distraction large enough to interrupt the High Priests of Oseka.\n_NOTE: The task locks when you update this step._\n_When ready for a fight, someone needs to move into their vicinity and click the \"Fury of the Tides\", causing all four to activate._\nA drop of water spills from the vial, causing a tremulous wave of disruption.\n_The four mobs rush your party (one of the priests turns into \"High Priest Xalziks\")._\n\n---\n\nDefeat High Priests 0/3 (Rubak Oseka)\nDefeat Zealots 0/2 (Rubak Oseka)\n**In Summary...**\n\\- Burn down three High Priests as quickly as possible\n\\- Get out of the whirlpools as they spawn\n\\-\\-\\- NOTE: Whirlpools won't spawn as long as your DPS is focused on Xalziks\n\\- Kill the zealots before they reach the water\n\\- Once you have only High Priest Xalziks left, use the six click effects on it\n\\- Kill the newly spawned zealots before they reach the water\n**In Detail...**\n_The four mobs each hit for a max ~12,500. The High Priests of Oseka (which are mezzable) each cast \"Up From the Depths\":_\nUp From the Depths: PB AE 40', Magic (-900)\n1: Knockback (7) and Toss Up (2)\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 14200\n_High Priest Xalziks (which is not mezzable) casts \"Up From the Depths\" and \"Riptide\" (hits multiple targets at a time):_\nRiptide: Single Target, Magic (-900)\n1: 100% Chance to trigger: Tide Pull\n2: Unknown #343\n3: Decrease Hitpoints by 15050\n_\"Riptide\" triggers \"Tide Pull\" which is a one-tick pull-spell (will pull you towards the mob)._\n_During the encounter, you'll see emote warnings about a whirlpool spawn:_\n_Target Sees:_ A whirlpool begins to form around you.\n_Everyone Else Sees:_ Swirls of violent water and wind begin to form around \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.\n_This emote is a 9-second warning that a whirlpool is about to spawn on the targeted player. It comes with a large damage aura and pull effect._\n_NOTE: As long as your DPS is focused on \"High Priest Xalziks\", the whirlpools will not appear._\n_Additional emotes seen during the encounter (their effect, if any, is unknown):_\nA surge of water can be heard rushing up from the depths of Rubak.\nThe tide begins to turn.\n_As the fight goes on, \"High Priest Xalziks\" will turn into \"High Priest of Oseka\" and, consequently, one of the \"High Priest of Oseka\" will turn into \"High Priest Xalziks\". When this happens, there is no change in health. If you kill a High Priest while its name is \"High Priest Xalziks\", it still counts towards towards the task update._\n_If you kill \"High Priest Xalziks\" while other \"High Priest of Oseka\" are still alive, one of the remaining mobs will turn into \"High Priest Xalziks\"._\n_While all this is going on, non-aggro Hadal zealots will spawn and wander towards the water. These need to be killed before they reach the water, otherwise they turn into an add (\"a devout templar\"). If this happens, you'll see this emote:_\nA zealot has made the ultimate sacrifice, allowing another High Priest to appear.\n_Zealots spawn one at a time (about every 45 seconds) and can appear in any of the bottom three alcoves._\n\n---\n\nConfine Oseka's spirit in the body of High Priest Xalziks 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_Task Window Says:_ Use the Pearlescent Talismans or Pearlescent Signets to bind Oseka's essence into the body of High Priest Xalziks.\n_With the three High Priests dead, leaving Xalziks as the only remaining one up, the people who looted the talismans and signets need to click them on Xalziks. The clicks all need to be done within seconds of each other._\n_NOTE: The clicks won't work properly if there is still a \"High Priest of Oseka\" alive. \"High Priest Xalziks\" must be the only mob left._\n_If you try clicking on a regular High Priest, you'll see this failure emote:_\nOseka can only be confined while in the body of High Priest Xalziks.\n_Upon successful clicks, you'll see:_\nThe tides begin to calm, as a portion of Oseka's power returns to the pearl.\nZealots begin marching toward the water, in an attempt to free Oseka's spirit through their own death.\n_...And several zealots spawn and begin walking towards the water. They all must be killed before they reach the water. Once the zealots are dead, this step updates. The remainder of the task is non-combat._\n\n---\n\nHear Oseka's words and ensure alir essence returns to the pearl 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_Task Window Says:_ Unable to find a new host for alir spirit, Oseka's essence is forced to return to the pearl, but not without having the final word.\nHigh Priest Xalziks gurgles while struggling to form cryptic words, 'Your so-called Gods are weak; pathetic. Fear is easily trumped, as you proved by defeating one of your own lesser Gods. I suppose I should thank you for your unintentional gift.'\nHigh Priest Xalziks trembles as the remnants of life fade from its body, but the voice of Oseka continues, 'Do not think that you have seen the last of me. I may not be able to possess another mortal body, but I will assume my rightful place amongst my followers. This land will be reclaimed from the lesser gods, one way or another. I will not spend eternity confined in the depths of Rubak!' As Oseka's final words echo throughout Rubak, a brilliant light escapes the limp body of High Priest Xalziks and travels toward the pearl.\n_An \"Essence of Oseka\" appears and disappears into the pearl._\n\n---\n\nLoot the watery chest for your reward 0/1 (Rubak Oseka)\n_Task Window Says:_ Some treasures of Oseka are contained within this chest.\nAs a result of your heroic efforts, Oseka's spirit has returned to the pearl; no longer able to possess the mortal bodies of alir High Priests.\n\n---\n\n_Reward:_\n205 platinum\nEltarki's Diary - Depths of Thought\nPossible Chest Loot (1 Item + 1 Cantrip Per Task)\nBonecracker Belt\nFang-Tipped Ring\nGemstone of the Victorious\nNightleaper's Cloak of Hidden Malice\nRa`Argt, the Shell-Crusher\nSacred Shell of the Nautilus\nSharpened Rib Fragment of the Fray\nSilken Satchel of the Ambassador\nSuperb Katar of the Advisor\nMedian Alaran Cantrip\nGreater Alaran Cantrip\n- Bonecracker Belt [item=100267]\n- Eltarki's Diary - Depths of Thought [item=98071]\n- Fang-Tipped Ring [item=101240]\n- Gemstone of the Victorious [item=99995]\n- Greater Alaran Cantrip [item=99412]\n- Median Alaran Cantrip [item=98717]\n- Nightleaper's Cloak of Hidden Malice [item=100012]\n- Sacred Shell of the Nautilus [item=100900]\n- Sharpened Rib Fragment of the Fray [item=99548]\n- Silken Satchel of the Ambassador [item=100241]\n- Superb Katar of the Advisor [item=100737]",
    },
