      exp = "18",
      exp_name = "Veil of Alaris",
      min_lvl = 1,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "",
      repeatable = false,
      group_size = "",
      npc = "Wasinai",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Wasinai",
        "Undo WHAT damage?!",
        "Responsibility?",
        "What sentry stones?",
        "_Quest_",
        "undo",
        "responsibility",
        "sentry stones",
      },
      items_required = {
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 99795, name = "Music of the Mind\n- Eltarki's Diary - Music of the Mind", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Windsong Sanctuary [zone=813]\n**Who:**\n- Wasinai [ _Quest_]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Alaran Language:** | 81\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a contaminated wind elemental [npc=39452]\n- a polluted wind elemental [npc=39233]\n- a sentry stone [npc=39232]\n- an escaped swinetor prisoner [npc=39228]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Dec 1 22:20:07 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This solo task begins with Wasinai in Windsong Sanctuary, located at about 2700, 915, -27 (northwestern entrance to the inner area)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- No tasks\n\\- 81 Skill Level in Alaran\nYou say, 'Hail, Wasinai'\nWasinai says, in Alaran, 'Ever since you and the others from Antonica have arrived here, our land has not been the same. Be gone unless you are able to [undo] the damage you have caused to Windsong.'\nYou say, 'Undo WHAT damage?!'\nWasinai says, in Alaran, 'Your kind has caused an evil pollution to spread throughout Windsong. It taints and destroys my brethren and this land. It must be stopped, and since your kind has brought it upon us, it is your [responsibility] to do so.'\nYou say, 'Responsibility?'\nWasinai says, in Alaran, 'If you truly wish to help, I thank you. I am afraid it is too late for the elementals that have succumbed to the pollution. They must be destroyed. Do so, and then return to me.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Stop the Pollution'.\nAn Alaran named Wasinai believes that you and the other Norrathians are polluting the land. Perform the actions that Wasinai has asked of you to prove you are not to blame.\n\n---\n\nKill some polluted wind elementals 0/6 (Windsong Sanctuary)\n_These are found throughout the outer area of the zone._\nSpeak with Wasinai 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nYou say, 'Hail, Wasinai'\nWasinai says, in Alaran, 'It is unfortunate the polluted elementals had to be destroyed, but it was for the benefit of all. I also must apologize to you. As much as I dislike the presence of outsiders here, it is not your fault that the elementals have become polluted. It appears that one of my brethren captured the true culprit. It is a foul creature known as a swinetor. Unfortunately this beast has escaped and his unholy presence is what caused the pollution. Please find this escaped swinetor and kill it.'\nKill the escaped swinetor prisoner 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\n_\"an escaped swinetor prisoner\" spawns at about 2400, -430, -28 (northeastern part of the inner area)._\nSpeak with Wasinai 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nYou say, 'Hail, Wasinai'\nWasinai says, in Alaran, 'The swinetor is dead? You have done well. Unfortunately there is one more problem. A group of contaminated elementals are planning on attacking the [sentry stones]. I believe the sentry stones are trying to cleanse the pollution from the land and are angering the contaminated elementals. We cannot let them harm the stones. Please protect the stones and then return to me. I will ensure that you are rewarded for your efforts.'\nYou say, 'What sentry stones?'\nWasinai says, in Alaran, 'The sentry stones are sacred artifacts. They allow our god, Ryken to communicate with us. I have never seen one of the stones destroyed, and I do not want to know what would happen if one was.'\nLocate the first sentry stone 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nProtect the first sentry stone from the contaminated wind elementals 0/3 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nLocate the second sentry stone 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nProtect the second sentry stone from the contaminated wind elementals 0/3 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nLocate the third sentry stone 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nProtect the third sentry stone from the contaminated wind elementals 0/3 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nLocate the fourth sentry stone 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nProtect the fourth sentry stone from the contaminated wind elementals 0/3 (Windsong Sanctuary)\n\\- First: 1200, 950, -2 _(western part of inner area)_\n\\- Second: 2200, 745, -45 _(northwestern part of inner area)_\n\\- Third: 2080, -770, -30 _(northeastern part of inner area)_\n\\- Fourth: 1000, -715, -30 _(eastern part of inner area)_\n_For each sentry stone, you'll have three elemental adds to contend with. They'll spawn as you approach and/or hail the sentry stone. While they don't auto-aggro and are actually splittable, you'll likely aggro at least one of them after the trigger._\n_The elementals are casters (wizards); are mezzable, stunnable, and rootable; and each hit for a max ~12,500._\nSpeak with Wasinai 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nYou say, 'Hail, Wasinai'\nWasinai says, in Alaran, 'The land is on its way to healing. Thank you for what you have done. Please take this for your assistance in helping our land.'\n_Rewards:_\n375 platinum\nExperience\nEltarki's Diary - Music of the Mind\n- Eltarki's Diary - Music of the Mind [item=99795]",
    },
