      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Windsong Sanctuary [zone=813]\n**Who:**\n- Kolain [ _Quest_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Alaran Language:** | 81\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- First Piece of the Flute of Calming [item=100789]\n- Second Piece of the Flute of Calming [item=99767]\n- Third Piece of the Flute of Calming [item=101138]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Pillars of Alra [zone=812]\n- Resplendent Temple [zone=811]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Wisthir [npc=39453]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Dec 1 22:20:12 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This solo task begins with Kolain in Windsong Sanctuary, located at about 2125, 1165, -37 (the northwestern part of the inner area)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- No tasks\n\\- 81 Skill Level in Alaran\nYou say, 'Hail, Kolain'\nKolain says, in Alaran, 'Do not fear me, stranger. I care not about who you are or where you are from. I only care about my [duty] in this life, and it has been put on hold due to unfortunate circumstances.'\nYou say, 'Your duty?'\nKolain says, in Alaran, 'It is my job and my calling to play music that soothes the chaotic spirits of the wind. I cannot do that without my flute however. I awoke this morning and my flute was missing. Without it, the spirits of the wind will be in turmoil. I must get my flute [back]!'\nYou say, 'Get it back?'\nKolain says, in Alaran, 'You would help me? Perhaps the Norrathians are not as unseemly as others say. I know not where it could be, but perhaps if you spoke with the spirits of the wind, you could get some clues. The spirits see all.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Winds of Change'.\nKolain has asked you to help recover the Flute of Calming that is used to calm the spirits of the wind.\nExplore the northwest edge of Windsong Sanctuary for a clue about the first piece of the Flute of Calming.\n_NOTE: The items in this task are not pre-lootable by normal means (it won't automatically update), but it's been reported the steps will update if you hand the pre-looted items to an NPC (who will in turn, give it back)._\n\n---\n\nSearch the northwest edge of Windsong for a clue about the first piece of the missing flute 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\n_This step updates in the extreme northwest part of Windsong, at about 3260, 1050, -26._\nA gust of wind swirls around you. A wispy voice echoes in your mind. 'You seek to reconstruct the Flute of Calming. Yesss. Thisss must be done. I broke the flute into three piecessss in a fit of rage. I am not proud of thisss. Recover the piecessss. The spirits of wind need its calming melodiessssss. The first piece has fallen from Windsong to the Pillarsss of Alra below. You must get it back.'\nObtain the first piece of the Windsong flute from the Pillars of Alra 0/1 (ALL)\n_Task Window Says:_ The first piece of the Flute of Calming has fallen to the ground below Windsong Sanctuary in the Pillars of Alra.\n_Find \"First Piece of the Flute of Calming\" as a ground spawn in the Pillars of Alra. It spawns at about -980, 600, 1 (on the ground level, just southwest of the ramp leading up to the central island)._\nSearch the northeast edge of Windsong for a clue about the second piece of the missing flute 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\n_Task Window Says:_ Explore the northeast edge of Windsong Sanctuary for a clue about the second piece of the Flute of Calming.\n_This step updates in the extreme northeast boundary of Windsong (about 3230, -1275, -25)._\nA gust of wind swirls around you. A wispy voice echoes in your mind. 'The second piece of the Flute of Calming has fallen into the handssss of the Swinetor below the Resplendent Temple. They do not know the value of the item they possesssss, thinking it junk. Get it back for ussss.'\nObtain the second piece of the Windsong flute from a swinetor in the Resplendent Temple 0/1 (ALL)\n_Task Window Says:_ The second piece of the Flute of Calming is now in possession of the Swinetor below the Resplendent Temple.\n_This is a random drop off Ulork and Piq`a Swinetor mobs in the \"In-Between\" (underground caves) of the Resplendent Temple._\nSearch the south edge of Windsong for a clue about the third piece of the missing flute 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\n_This step updates in the south-central part of Windsong (about -150, 20, -40)._\nA gust of wind swirls around you. A wispy voice echoes in your mind. 'The third piece of the Flute of Calming has been taken by the filqua in Windsong Sanctuary. Find the filqua that has the piece and get it back.'\nObtain the third piece of the Windsong flute from a filqua in Windsong 0/1 (ALL)\n_Task Window Says:_ The third, and final piece of the Flute of Calming has been stolen by the filqua in Windsong Sanctuary.\n_This is a random drop from filquas in the inner area of Windsong._\nDeliver the first piece of the Windsong flute to Kolain 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nDeliver the second piece of the Windsong flute to Kolain 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nDeliver the third piece of the Windsong flute to Kolain 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nSpeak with Kolain 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\n_Be ready for a fight. Wisthir will go aggro about 20-25 seconds after the hail._\nYou say, 'Hail, Kolain'\nKolain says, in Alaran, 'You have done it! What happened? Why was the flute broken into pieces?'\nWisthir says, in Alaran, 'I can answer that. It was me. The music of the flute is so soothing. I want you to play only for me.'\nKolain says, in Alaran, 'But why? You know that the music I play is for all the spirits of the wind. I cannot play for you alone.'\nWisthir says, in Alaran, 'But I helped you recover the pieces and I am truly sorry for what I have done. Play the flute for me. Play only for me!'\nKolain says, in Alaran, 'I cannot do that, Wisthir. You know that. I am sorry.'\nWisthir says, in Alaran, 'The music must be played for me, and me alone!'\nKolain says, in Alaran, 'Help! You must defeat Wisthir! He has gone insane!'\nKill Wisthir 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\n_Wisthir hits for a max ~17,500._\nSpeak with Kolain 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nYou say, 'Hail, Kolain'\nKolain says, in Alaran, 'It is regrettable that Wisthir attacked us. Your assistance will allow me to play the flute once again however and calm the remaining spirits of the wind. I thank you for all you have done.'\n_Rewards:_\n375 platinum\nExperience\nEltarki's Diary - Music of the Mind\n- Eltarki's Diary - Music of the Mind [item=99795]",
    },
