      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Erillion, City of Bronze [zone=814]\n**Who:**\n- Druthur [npc=39313]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 95\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a faithful citizen [npc=39395]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Fri Dec 2 20:01:34 2011\nModified: Sat Feb 8 15:50:13 2020 | | **For an overview of the Veil of Alaris expansion, a task listing, and information about progression, spells, and armor, **click here**.**\n\n---\n\n_This is a kill task that begins with Druthur in Erillion, the City of Bronze (found at about -5, 390, -39 -- in the west-central jail block on the lower level of the main building)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- No tasks\n\\- 81 Skill Level in Alaran\nYou say, 'Hail, Druthur'\nDruthur says, in Alaran, 'Hah! I want no part in your dream of a world for lunatics and madmen. Begone!'\n_To get him to speak with you, talk to Oashim in the cell across the hall._\nYou say, 'Hail, Oashim'\nOashim says 'SCREEEEEEE!!' - From the opposite cell, you hear Druthur laughing uncontrollably, 'Hah! Come to give the oashim alis final meal before taking al to the carnifex, have you? And they said \\*I\\* was crazy! I'm not the one [imprisoning] vermin.''\nYou say, 'You're not imprisoning them?'\nOashim chitters softly.\nYou say, 'Who's imprisoning you?'\nDruthur says, in Alaran, 'Hmm?' It screws its eyes up and gives you a calculating look, 'Oh, goodness! I thought you were one of those nutcase guards. I apologize for the Oashim, al only shrieks like that at people al doesn't know. The city had ali locked up, for [wandering] the streets and since then al's had something of a grudge against strangers. Not that I blame al. They're mad - ALL of them!'\nYou say, 'Wandering?'\nDruthur says, in Alaran, 'Well, as the guards explained when I asked,' it switches to a tone of mock-arrogance, 'It is against our laws for vermin to roam the street. The oashim has broken the law, so al must be punished for alis [crimes].'\nYou say, 'What crimes?'\nDruthur says, in Alaran, 'As if public rodency wasn't enough,' it says, switching back to its normal voice, 'they're also charging al with vagrancy, loitering, and being visibly emaciated.' It stops to ponder this last crime for a moment, then shrugs, 'I suppose emaciation is considered acceptable by the [law], as long as it's well hidden when one is in public.'\nYou say, 'The law?'\nDruthur says, in Alaran, 'This one's fate is now sealed; al was doomed from the moment they caught al. Al will have alis trial, and then, be executed. Don't pine for al, though - I'll soon be [following], most likely, to keep the little critter company.'\nYou say, 'Following?'\nDruthur says, in Alaran, 'To tell the truth, I've grown rather fond of the fellow. I've named al Oashim.' It shakes its head sadly, 'It's too late to save either of us, and I for one do not regret my crimes, but if you want to save others from the same fate as Oashim, go slay the citizens of this 'fine' city. As for myself, I'd just appreciate some peace and quiet in my final hours.'\n_A task window pops up offering two tasks._\nYou have been assigned the task 'Ratting Out the Faithful'.\nIt seems there's nothing you can do to help Oashim; however, you may be able to prevent the same fate from befalling others by reducing the number of faithful citizens in the city.\n\n---\n\nKill 10 faithful citizens 0/10 (Erillion)\nSpeak with Druthur 0/1 (Erillion)\n_Rewards:_\n150 platinum\nExperience",
    },
