      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Shard's Landing [zone=867]\nRating:\n0/2**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(Average from 2 ratings)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 85\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Money\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Harbingers of Thule +100\n**Factions Lowered:**\n**Quest Items:**\n- Small Crystalline Shard [item=104875]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Master Hunter Jilare [ _Quests_]\n- Overseer Drent [ _Quests_]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Shard's #1b: Exploring Shard's Landing [quest=5989]\n- Shard's #2: Words of the Unspoken [quest=5979]\n- Shard's #3: Unusual Goral Coral [quest=5991]\n- Shard's #4: The Harbingers of Thule [quest=5992]\n- Shard's #5: Conquering Your Fears [quest=5993]\n- Shard's #6: The Believers [quest=5994]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Nov 27 21:54:16 2012\nModified: Sat Nov 1 17:39:17 2025 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This task is the first in a series of six. It's a solo task that you get from Overseer Drent in Shard's Landing._\nHail him to get the task. (dialogue needed)\nYou have been assigned the task 'Welcome to Shard's Landing'.\n_The locations listed below are for guidelines only. The actual ranges for updates are quite large._\n_See **this map** for locations pertaining to this task._\n\n---\n\nExplore the Harbinger's Outpost 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_This is the large crater in the middle of the zone._\nAs you make your way down from the walls of the crater you notice the great crystalline structure that acted as the catalyst for all that you see here. The leaders of this camp can be found just southwest of the crystal.\nSpeak to Overseer Drent 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Overseer Drent ( map) is found at 215, 100, 1 -- in a tent to the crystal's southwest (he also wanders to the fire)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Overseer Drent'\nOverseer Drent nods toward you, 'Greetings traveler and welcome to the outpost of the Harbingers of Thule. Normally I would offer a grand speech to sell you on the pressing importance of joining our ranks immediately, but we are pressed for time and I'm quite certain you've been through this same routine enough times that you understand what needs to be done. For now, I need you to become acquainted with the geography of these hills. Oh, before you go trekking off into the wilderness, speak to Master Hunter Jilare over there. She may have some work for you in the future.'\nSpeak to Master Hunter Jilare 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Master Hunter Jilare ( map is found at 245, 20, 1 (outside the same tent)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Master Hunter Jilare'\nMaster Hunter Jilare chortles, 'What is this prissy \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ doing around here at this hour?' Her tone becomes higher pitched and mocking, 'Come to save the world again, smash the baddies and grab their treasures?' She waves her hand dismissively and returns to her normal voice, 'Go run Boxboy Drent's little errands and get back to me if you survive. Then maybe, just maybe I'll have some work for you.'\n_This opens up the next 11 steps._\nExplore Magus Burlshin's Camp 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_This updates around /location -1450, -1100, 0 ( **map** \\-\\- southeastern valley, marked by a crystal druid ring)._\nMagus Burlshin's camp is situated very specifically on hallowed ground. Every active teleportation spire sits on land that resonates in this same manner. What is particularly interesting about this location is that both arcane and natural energy seems to converge here.\nExplore the Valley of the Naeya 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_This updates around /location -920, -1400, 5 ( **map** \\-\\- southeastern valley)._\nThe naeya here are generally not aggressive, save for the Alpha Naeya who is fiercely territorial. Although these creatures are unlikely to attack unless provoked, they are very social and will come to the aid of their kin at a moment's notice.\nExplore Banescale's Den 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_This updates around /location 800, -1250, 3 ( **map** \\-\\- entrance of the eastern valley)._\nThe snakes in this area appear to be of three varieties: the Slatescales which typically rest on the rocks scattered throughout the area, the Ivyscales which try to camouflage themselves by hiding under brush and foliage, and finally the aggressive Banescales that appear more frequently in this den and occasionally throughout the rest of the mountains.\nExplore the Village of the Forsaken 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_This updates around /location 420, -1880, 1 ( **map** \\-\\- eastern valley)._\nThe noxious stench of excrement and rotting flesh overpower any other details worth mentioning about this ramshackle 'village'. Overseer Drent begins speaking, 'The inhabitants here refer to themselves as 'The Forsaken'. All of our initial attempts at establishing diplomatic relations with the group have resulted in less than favorable results.' In fact, you think you spot the remains of one or two harbinger envoys as you survey the ground. Drent continues, 'The less hostile Alarans to the west refer to this group as 'The Unworthy', though they refuse to explain why...'\nExplore Greenscale Nest 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_This updates around /location 650, 1180, 1 ( **map** \\-\\- due west of the crater, a group of wyverns)._\nThe wyverns in this area seem particularly interested in the crystalline shards that have landed near their nests. This interest has changed their behavior dramatically. They have become aggressively territorial and remain on guard at all hours now. Exercise caution when wandering near any wyverns in these hills.\nExplore Pyrebeak's Peak 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_This updates around /location -275, 705, 150 ( **map** \\-\\- southwest of the crater, in the mountains)._\nThe Icebeak kangons make their roost on these snowcapped hills. This species of kangon is typically not aggressive, but you should exercise caution should their grand matriarch Pyrebeak make an appearance...\nExplore Corruption's End 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_This updates around /location -1200, 830, 10 ( **map** \\-\\- southwestern valley)._\nOverseer Drent's voice becomes clear in your mind, 'At the heart of this valley is the water supply that sustains the packs of goral and panthers that have made these hills their home. It is believed that the water is the reason these creatures have recently shown signs of mutation. All beasts here are aggressive and territorial, so you should exercise caution when travelling here.'\nExplore Worntooth's Run 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_This updates around /location 2050, -350, 1 ( **map** \\-\\- north of the crater, among the grendlaens)._\nThe Worntooth grendlaen make their home in this very small plot of land just west of Cragfeast Rock. What is particularly interesting about these creatures is the immense weight of their hides. It is almost as if these living creatures were formed out of stone.\nExplore Cragfeast Rock 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_This updates around /location 1860, -1300, 10 ( **map** \\-\\- northeastern valley)._\nCragfeast Rock is the name given to this valley where a pack of Verdantbeak kangons live symbiotically with a group of selyrah. The herbivorous kangon seem to keep to themselves while the omnivorous selyrah seem to be attracted to the crystalline shards that have landed in the valley.\nExplore the Infested Plain 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_This updates around /location 2025, 890, -34 ( **map** \\-\\- northwestern valley)._\nAlthough the Venomshell beetles can be found scattered throughout the hills, this small stretch of land appears to be their hotbed. Initial studies have suggested that the vegetation where the crystalline shards have landed seem to increase the potency of these beetles' venom.\nExplore Stonecoat's Plateau 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_This updates around /location 1500, 1600, 24 ( **map** \\-\\- southwest of the above step, in the mountains)._\nOverseer Drent's voice speaks to you with a hint of hesitation, 'The Frostcoat braxi that inhabit this small hillside are something our soldiers speak of in hushed words. Rumor says that these beasts are somehow smart enough to speak, but choose not to. I'm not convinced, but I'm not about to go challenging them to prove a suspicion...'\nExplore the Underground City 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_This updates around /location 450, 2100, -285 ( **map** \\-\\- entrance of the Alaran city in the southern part of the zone's northwest valley)._\nOverseer Drent's voice speaks with renewed resolve, 'Unlike the disheveled Alarans to the east, the inhabitants of this underground city have been far more welcoming to the arrival of people in the hills. We are still in the early stages of forming official diplomatic relations with this group, but we feel they will likely serve as important allies in our efforts to reinstate our father the Faceless to the pantheon... I need you to get acquainted with their city and then return to the outpost.'\nExplore the Council Chambers 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_This updates around /location -600, 2200, -402 ( **map**)._\nOverseer Drent continues, 'The appointed councilors meet in these halls twice daily, once midday between eleven of morning and four in the afternoon and again in the evening between eight and eleven of evening. Members of the council are signified by the heatless red flame of guidance that shines brightly from their left hand. Their meetings are conducted in absolute silence so we are still unsure what it is that they accomplish or discuss here.'\nExplore the Silent Hall 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_This updates around /location -400, 670, -750 ( **map** \\-\\- the large hall in the far eastern part of the underground city)._\nOverseer Drent's voice is quiet but clear in your mind, 'It is of absolute import that you do not speak to anyone in these halls. A non-clergyman making sound here is considered the greatest sacrilege to these people. It is interesting to think that the citizens and priests alike have chosen to call themselves 'The Believers'. From what we have gathered, the upper echelon of this society is marked by the pale ethereal orbs of power around their hands. We are still unsure what the dark flame that marks the others means. Take a moment to survey these halls, as something still does not seem quite right... If you find anything out of the ordinary, be discreet and return here as soon as possible.'\nLook for anything out of place 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\nSmall Crystalline Shard [item=104875] is a ground spawn ( **map**) that has a few spawn points in the silent hall. It appears as a small purple shard.\n30, 780, -747 _(northwest corner)_\n-120, 550, -747 _(northeast area)_\n-310, 790, -747 _(southwest area)_\nAs you survey the crystal shard you come to the realization that nowhere else in the city have you seen any sign that the Alarans have been collecting the crystals that litter the lands above this city... Perhaps Drent would be interested in this.\nReturn the crystal to Overseer Drent 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\nOverseer Drent takes the crystal and inspects it carefully before placing it aside, 'So you say you found this in their worship halls?' The Iksar furrows his brow, 'Troubling news, none of our other scouts have reported finding any crystals within the City of The Believers. We were under the impression that they were indifferent to our efforts...' The Overseer changes to a less grave expression, 'Still, you've done well, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. I would like to extend the open invitation of the Harbingers to you. There is still much to be done here if we are to reinstate our father to the pantheon but I am sure with the help of adventurers like you we will restore Norrath to its previous balance! I suggest you speak with Councilman Nostulia or Hunter Jilare for your next assignments, though I could always use more scouts to relay more detailed information about the area.'\nYour faction standing with Harbingers of Thule got better.\nNow that you are familiar with the general layout of Shard's Landing you can be of use to the Harbingers. Speak to Councilman Nostulia for your next training assignment, Master Hunter Jilare if you are interested in proving your worth as a hunter or Overseer Drent if you would like to gather more information about the various geographical points of interest.\n_Rewards:_\n225 platinum\nExperience (2% at Level 100 and 3 AAs)\n_Note: This task is not repeatable._",
    },
