      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Shard's Landing [zone=867]\n**Who:**\n- Councilman Nostulia [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/4**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(Average from 4 ratings)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 85\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Money\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Harbingers of Thule +25\n**Factions Lowered:**\n**Quest Items:**\n- Armsman's Missive [item=107396]\n- Believer's Private Notes [item=107442]\n- Council Minutes [item=107393]\n- Councilor's Memo [item=107376]\n- Gardener's Notes [item=107395]\n- Hand Copied Alaran Notes [item=107447]\n- Nondescript Clergy Memo [item=107443]\n- Nostulia's Quill [item=107448]\n- Page of a Citizen's Diary [item=107378]\n- Page of a Gladiator's Journal [item=107441]\n- Page of a High Guard's Diary [item=107386]\n- Sentry's Log [item=107427]\n- Simple Empty Tome [item=107446]\n- Tome of Blank Pages [item=107449]\n- Translated Notes [item=107450]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Shard's #1: Welcome to Shard's Landing [quest=5978]\n- Shard's #3: Unusual Goral Coral [quest=5991]\n- Shard's #4: The Harbingers of Thule [quest=5992]\n- Shard's #5: Conquering Your Fears [quest=5993]\n- Shard's #6: The Believers [quest=5994]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Nov 27 21:57:48 2012\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This task is the second in a series of six. It's a solo task that begins with Councilman Nostulia ( map) in Shard's Landing. He is found at /location 300, 85, 1 (southwestern part of the crater, in a tent north of Overseer Drent's location)._\n_In addition to being a progression task, this will also boost your Alaran language skill level to 100 (if it's not there already)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completed \"Welcome to Shard's Landing\"\nYou say, 'Hail, Councilman Nostulia'\nCouncilman Nostulia looks up, 'Oh yes, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_? Drent was just speaking about a rambunctious \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ that had shown some promise. I shall skip the pleasantries and get to the point, my job here is simple, I ensure that all of our recruits are ready and able to report on any and everything they see. To that end I need to know that you are fluent in their language. If you are willing to [prove] yourself ready to join our ranks then I have a simple task for you to complete.'\nYou say, 'I'll prove myself'\nCouncilman Nostulia says 'Very well, this should be an easy enough job.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Words of the Unspoken'.\nCouncilman Nostulia has tasked you with mastering the Alaran language.\nYour first order of business is to travel back to the Underground City. From there you will want to seek out some different pieces of text and then report back to him.\n\n---\n\n**Map Points**\n_Map points for ground spawns in this task (for your shardslanding.txt map file):_\nP -748.3299, 191.1828, -747.9532, 0, 0, 240, 1, believer's\\_private\\_notes\nP -1769.2292, 585.7079, -482.9475, 0, 0, 240, 1, clergy\\_memo\nP -1354.3511, 50.3915, -502.9690, 0, 0, 240, 1, gladiator's\\_journal\nP -1386.8800, -233.6790, -440.4068, 0, 0, 240, 1, sentry's\\_log\nP -966.6017, -161.6083, -502.4304, 0, 0, 240, 1, armsman's\\_missive\nP -2120.5300, 1191.9147, -602.8653, 0, 0, 240, 1, gardener's\\_notes\nP -1769.5480, 924.5905, -467.1320, 0, 0, 240, 1, council\\_minutes\nP -2252.6782, -7.3468, -296.9900, 0, 0, 240, 1, high\\_guard's\\_diary\nP -2345.6379, 279.4736, -297.5374, 0, 0, 240, 1, citizen's\\_diary\nP -1710.8660, 721.6621, -502.8739, 0, 0, 240, 1, councilor's\\_memo\n\n---\n\nTravel back to the Underground City 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_This updates as you enter the city (connected from the zone's northwestern valley)._\nObtain a Councilor's Memo 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ Just east of the council chambers is where many of the councilmen and citizens live. See if you can find a memo or diary from one of them.\n_\"A Councilor's Memo\" is a ground spawn on a table in this area (/location -715, 1710, -500 -- bottom level, second residence to your left if coming from the chambers)._\nObtain a Page of a Citizen's Diary 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ North of the council chambers is another living barracks, see if you can find any personal writings from one of the citizens.\n_\"Page of a Citizen's Diary\" is a ground spawn on a table in this area (/location -280, 2350, -295 -- upper level, first residence to your left if coming from the chambers)._\nObtain a Page of a High Guard's Diary 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ In the barracks north of the council chambers on the northern side are four rooms that the High Guards inhabit. See if you can find any writings of theirs there.\n_\"Page of a High Guard's Diary\" is a ground spawn on a table in this area (/location 5, 2250, -292 -- upper level of the residence to your right if coming from the chambers)._\nObtain a page of Council Minutes 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ In the barracks east of the council chambers are the houses of many councilmen. See if you can find any official documentation about their meetings.\n_\"Council Minutes\" is a ground spawn on a table in this area (/location -925, 1765, -465 -- upper level, first residence to your right if coming from the chambers)._\nObtain A Gardener's Notes 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ To the south of the council chambers is the indoor garden of believers. This area produces nearly all the food to sustain the city and may have some detailed documentation that would be worth examining.\n_\"A Gardener's Notes\" is a ground spawn in this area (/location -1200, 2120, -602 -- just to your right upon entering the area, if coming from the chambers)._\nObtain an Armsman's Missive 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ In the northeastern section of the Underground City is the armory. See if you can find any text of interest in that area.\n_\"An Armsman's Missive\" is a ground spawn on a table at /location 165, 975, -500 (on your map, this is the large room northwest of the Silent Hall)._\nObtain a Sentry's Log 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ Just east of the city's entrance is a barracks where a number of miners are housed. They are under constant supervision from the enforcers and taskmasters in the city. See if you can find anything of interest in that area.\n_\"A Sentry's Log\" is a ground spawn on a table in the open area east of the city's entrance (/location 230, 1375, -442 -- central part of this area)._\nObtain a Page of a Gladiator's Journal 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ Our understanding of the society is that there are several distinct castes, the lowest being 'the conscripted'. Many of them are housed as gladiators that perform for the entertainment of the citizens. See if you can find any writings by these warriors in their barracks southeast of the city gates.\n_\"Page of a Gladiator's Journal\" is a ground spawn on a table in the open area just northeast of the arena (/location -50, 1350, -502 -- in the north-central part of this area)._\nObtain a Believer's Private Notes 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ The devout worshippers are a curious group. We understand very little about their form of worship. See if you can find anything of use in the silent hall.\n_\"A Believer's Private Notes\" is a ground spawn in front of a bench at about -190, 750, -747 in the Silent Hall (northeastern part of the city -- in the west-central part of the Hall)._\nObtain a Nondescript Clergy Memo 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ Reports have stated that a number of clergy stand watch in the arena. See if you can find any texts of note by this group.\n_\"A Nondescript Clergy Memo\" is a ground spawn at /location -585, 1770, -482 (in the arena which is the large area just northeast of the council chambers -- ground spawn along the south-central wall of the arena)._\nReport back to Councilman Nostulia 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ Now that you have collected a wide variety of texts, report back to Councilman Nostulia and he will give you further instructions.\nYou say, 'Hail, Councilman Nostulia'\nCouncilman Nostulia says 'Ah, so you've collected the texts?' He takes a moment to look over the pieces of paper you present him, 'Very well, this will be a rather simple lesson, which I assume you find to be the best kind of lesson.' He smirks, 'Take this tome and piece together the papers into a master document, copy them -exactly- as written. After you've done that, translate the paper into common and return the perfectly translated work to me. I will not accept anything less than a perfect translation!' The wizened erudite hands you a tome full of blank pages and a quill.'\n_You receive a container: \"Simple Empty Tome\"_\nCopy the notes exactly as written 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Combine the 10 texts inside the container to produce a \"Tome of Blank Pages\" (container) + \"Nostulia's Quill\" + \"Hand Copied Alaran Notes\"._\nYou slowly copy the elaborate symbols that make up the Alaran language onto a series of blank pages until a perfect replica is made.\nYou have fashioned the items together to create something new: Hand Copied Alaran Notes.\nYou have fashioned the items together to create something new: Nostulia's Quill.\nYou have fashioned the items together to create something new: Tome of Blank Pages.\nTranslate the notes into Common 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_In the Tome, combine the Quill and Copied Notes until the step updates and you produce \"Translated Notes\" (as you do this, your Alaran will progress to 100)._\nYou review your work to find a number of glaring errors.\nYou review your work to find a handful of minor errors.\nYou review your work and find one or two simple mistakes.\nYou review your work and realize you've misspelled something.\nAfter several minutes of careful translation you review your work and find it immaculate! You have a clear understanding of the Alaran language.\nYou have fashioned the items together to create something new: Translated Notes.\nDeliver the Translated Notes to Councilman Nostulia 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ Deliver the Translated Notes to Councilman Nostulia so he can assess your success.\nCouncilman Nostulia looks over the paper carefully then looks back up at you, 'Well, you've proven to be quicker learner than I had anticipated. I suppose some minor congratulations are in order. You are now fully qualified to speak to the natives. I have another simple task for you should you be up for it, though I think Engineer Eilisia may also be interested in your talents.'\nYour faction standing with Harbingers of Thule got better.\nAlthough his methods felt somewhat patronizing, you feel inspired by the haste in which Councilman Nostulia was able to help you master the Alaran language. Whether or not you have any real use for their native tongue is another matter though...\n_Rewards:_\n262 platinum, 5 gold\nExperience (11% regular exp at Level 88 and 3 AAs at any level)\n_Note: This task is not repeatable._\n- Fragment of Legendary Alaran History [item=100964]",
    },
