      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Shard's Landing [zone=867]\n**Who:**\n- Engineer Eilisia [npc=41273]\nRating:\n0/3**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(Average from 3 ratings)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Money\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Harbingers of Thule +50\n**Factions Lowered:**\n**Quest Items:**\n- Corrupted Goral Sample [item=107079]\n- Crystallized Coral Sample [item=104846]\n- Crystallized Flesh Sample [item=107325]\n- Crystallized Water Sample [item=104847]\n- Empowered Crystal of the Heart [item=107328]\n- Heart Crystal Condenser [item=107326]\n- Infected Panther Sample [item=106535]\n- Mineral Extractor [item=105285]\n- Simple Chemical Filter [item=105286]\n- Simple Chemical Suspension [item=104845]\n- Small Crystal of the Heart [item=107327]\n- Undamaged Naeya Pelt [item=106516]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Magus Burlshin [ _Teleportation_]\n- a blighted prowler [npc=41375]\n- a coralspine goral [npc=41390]\n- a corrupted coralspine [npc=41391]\n- a wild naeya [npc=41426]\n- an elder naeya [npc=41440]\n- an elder prowler [npc=41441]\n- corrupted coral [npc=45533]\n- envoy`s supply box [npc=41490]\n- supply barrel [npc=41488]\n- supply box [npc=41489]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Shard's #1: Welcome to Shard's Landing [quest=5978]\n- Shard's #2: Words of the Unspoken [quest=5979]\n- Shard's #4: The Harbingers of Thule [quest=5992]\n- Shard's #5: Conquering Your Fears [quest=5993]\n- Shard's #6: The Believers [quest=5994]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 28 09:47:31 2012\nModified: Mon Feb 3 09:07:31 2025 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This solo task begins with Engineer Eilisia ( map) in Shard's Landing. She is located in one of the tents in the crater's southwest section._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completed \"Welcome to Shard's Landing\"\n\\- Completed \"Words of the Unspoken\"\nYou say, 'Hail, Engineer Eilisia'\nEngineer Eilisia says 'Well, well, if it isn't the famed \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ I have heard so much about. Really making a name for yourself in our ranks, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Today just happens to be your lucky day. I'm in need of assistance with a data gathering project and you are just fit enough for the job. Let me know if you are [interested] in assisting me.' The gnome looks back down at her notes after what you think was a quick wink in your direction.'\nYou say, 'I'm interested'\nEngineer Eilisia says 'Perfect, a \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ like you should have no problem completing this task.' She begins to detail a list of tools you will need to acquire and specific sample types she wants you to obtain...'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Unusual Goral Coral'.\nEngineer Eilisia is spearheading an initiative to study the nature of the Heart of Fear and she needs your help.\nYou will need a specialized tool to collect a fear crystal sample from the coral that grows in the pond at Corruption's End. Search the barrels and boxes around our camp to find a Mineral Extractor.\nOne of our envoys was recently sent out with a shipment of various chemical filters. Find out what's become of him and ask for a Simple Chemical Filter. The envoy was last seen heading northeast to scout out the pack of grendlaens that live in Worntooth's Run. You will need this to properly obtain a water sample from Corruption's End.\nMagus Burlshin has a number of 'interesting' items. Go speak to him and see if he is willing to part with something capable of melting flesh but preserving stone.\n\n---\n\nLocate a Mineral Extractor from the supply holds in our camp 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Supply barrels and supply boxes are found in the tents in the Harbinger's camp. /open those until you receive the Extractor._\nYou rummage through the box's contents but fail to find a Mineral Extractor. Perhaps one of the other containers will have it.\nYou have already checked this box. You may have more luck finding a Mineral Extractor if you check in one of the other containers.\nYou rummage through the barrel's contents but fail to find a Mineral Extractor. Perhaps one of the other containers will have it.\nYou reach into the barrel and uncover a Mineral Extractor!\n\n---\n\nObtain a Simple Chemical Filter from one of our envoys 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_\"envoy`s supply box\" ( map) is located at 1815, -500, 7 (northeast of the crater just over a hill in Worntooth's Run). /open it to receive a \"Simple Chemical Filter\"._\nYou dig through the remains of the broken box and uncover one usable Simple Chemical Filter hidden underneath a scrap of wood!\n\n---\n\nObtain a Simple Chemical Suspension from Magus Burlshin 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Magus Burlshin ( map) is found at -1450, -1095, 0 (zone-in area, marked by the big crystal shard and a tent)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Magus Burlshin'\nMagus Burlshin listens as you quickly recount the instructions that Eilisia gave you. The erudite nods, 'A chemical suspension...' He smiles, 'I would be happy to part with one of my precious concoctions, for a fair price. You see, the tent I have been staying in since I moved out to these hills is in constant need of repair and so I think this would be a fine opportunity for a trade. Bring me some materials to patch up my tent and I will part with the Simple Chemical Suspension that you seek.'\n\n---\n\nGather a few Undamaged Naeya Pelts 0/3 (Shard's Landing)\n_Kill 3 naeya mobs to receive 3x \"Undamaged Naeya Pelt\"._\n\n---\n\nDeliver the Undamaged Naeya Pelts to Magus Burlshin 0/3 (Shard's Landing)\nYou say, 'Hail, Magus Burlshin'\nMagus Burlshin says 'Just a few materials to patch up my tent. Hardly an inequitable trade for what you are after.'\n_Hand them in:_\nMagus Burlshin looks over the pelts and smiles, 'These will do nicely, thank you. Oh, right, you were after the suspension.' He digs through his bags and produces a small, tightly-sealed urn. He holds the object out with both hands and leaves you with this warning, 'Be quite careful with this solution, the acidity of the suspension is easily capable of ridding you of limbs if you are careless.'\n\n---\n\nUse the Mineral Extractor to gather a sample from the coral at Corruption's End 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ The coral that grows in the pond at Corruption's End has been infused with fear crystal dust. Use the Mineral Extractor to obtain a sample so we can analyze how this substance behaves after being metabolized in simple animal life.\n_In the southwestern valley of the zone is a pond. There is a \"corrupted coral\" spawn under the water. Target it and right-click the Mineral Extractor (-1390, 715)._\nThe coral in this pond looks to be infused with small bits of fear crystal. You will need to use a Mineral Extractor to filter out a sample.\nYou extract a strain of fear crystal that was growing inside of the coral.\n\n---\n\nUse the Simple Chemical Filter to gather a water sample from Corruption's End 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ The pond at Corruption's End is rich with fear crystal particles. Use the Simple Chemical Filter to collect a handful of this material. It will be important to analyze how the substance behaves after being distilled in a body of water.\n_Same location as above, click the Simple Chemical Filter._\nYou finish collecting a mineral sample.\nYou filter out a sample of fear crystal dust from the pond water.\n\n---\n\nGather several Corrupted Goral Samples from Corruption's End 0/3 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ The goral at Corruption's End have been ingesting bits of fear crystal. 'Obtain' some of their flesh.\n_Kill three gorals to receive their samples._\n\n---\n\nGather several Infected Panther Samples from Corruption's End 0/3 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ The panthers at Corruption's End have also been ingesting fear crystal. 'Obtain' some of their flesh.\n_Kill three prowlers to receive their samples._\n\n---\n\nDistill the animal samples in the Simple Chemical Suspension 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ Use the Simple Chemical Suspension to extract the fear crystal particles from the animal flesh. It is important that we analyze how the substance reacts after being metabolized by complex animal life.\n_Combine the above six samples in the Simple Chemical Suspension to produce a Crystallized Flesh Sample._\nYou place the samples of corrupted animal flesh in the Simple Chemical Suspension. After a few moments the flesh dissolves and all that remains is a condensed shard of fear.\n\n---\n\nReturn to Engineer Eilisia with the samples 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ Eilisia would like to review the samples you have collected so far. Return to the Harbinger camp and speak with her.\n_Hail her and receive a Heart Crystal Condenser._\nYou say, 'Hail, Engineer Eilisia'\nEngineer Eilisia looks up and gives you a wide smile, 'So you've collected the requested samples of fear crystal that have been metabolized by three different sources?' She looks over the small reconstructed crystals you have collected. 'Perfect!' She reaches into her bag and hands you a small arcane looking container. 'You will need to take the metabolized crystal samples and unite them into a single shard. Take this piece over to the Heart of Fear and see if we can harness any sort of reaction.'\n\n---\n\nCombine the samples in the Heart Crystal Condenser 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ Eilisia is pleased with the data you have helped gather with your samples. She now requests that you combine the discrete samples into a single shard. You can do this with the Heart Crystal Condenser she has provided you with.\n_Combine the three Crystallized Samples in the condenser._\nYou place the three differently metabolized shards in the condenser and begin the refining process. After a few moments the samples merge into a single glowing shard. It radiates with a faint power that the crystals surrounding Shard's Landing do not seem to possess.\n\n---\n\nRelease the essence of the Small Crystal of the Heart to the Heart of Fear 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ The crystal you have created radiates with a faint light that the otherwise lifeless stone surrounding the area does not. Bring this crystal sample near the Heart of Fear that rests in the center of the Harbinger's camp to see if you can harness any sort of reaction.\n_Stand on the giant crystal in the middle of the crater for this update (don't fall in the hole!). This is a location update_\nYou make your way toward the Heart of Fear and hold the small shard above your head. It emits a subtle glow but little else. You feel that something is missing. Speak to Engineer Eilisia to see what she has to say about this.\nYou look up at the lifeless chunk of crystal but feel nothing special from its presence.\n\n---\n\nAsk Engineer Eilisia why the crystal has had no effect 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ The crystal's reaction was rather unimpressive. See what Eilisia has to say about this.\nYou say, 'Hail, Engineer Eilisia'\nEngineer Eilisia listens as you explain that there was no significant reaction from your crystal. She looks down and sighs, 'I was afraid of this. You see, every time we collect new samples I have a lingering hope that the various ways in which nature and animals metabolize the substance will reveal a new method to empower the fear shards. Obviously we are surrounded by the blasted stuff, but unless it is empowered it will not react to the Heart of Fear. This is the reason we have sent teams around the globe to collect the remnants of this substance. It's not for a lack of material, but for a lack of correctly attuned material.' She begins to whisper as she explains the process of attuning the crystal you hold in your hand...\n\n---\n\nCapture a Sentient Soul using the Small Crystal of the Heart 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ It seems that Eilisia has higher expectations for the naturally metabolized crystal. Although she was hesitant to admit it, there is a known way to empower the crystal shards in order to provoke a reaction from the Heart of Fear.\nSeek out an Alaran living in the hills, a member of either The Forsaken or The Believers will do. You will need to weaken their physical form, and then use the crystal to capture their soul. This will be enough to empower the crystal.\n_Fight an Alaran (can be most types except for nameds, their PHs, or thralls) to at least 25% and right-click the crystal while basically standing right on top of them to receive an Empowered Crystal of the Heart._\n_Note: Alarans summon._\na forsaken believer grasps its chest and falls over dead as \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ drains its soul away!\nYou raise the Small Crystal of the Heart and drain your target's soul!\n\n---\n\nRelease the essence of the Empowered Crystal of the Heart to the Heart of Fear 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Task Window Says:_ Take the Empowered Crystal of the Heart back to the Heart of Fear to harness a more potent reaction.\n_Again, do this on the large crystal in the center._\nYou raise the Empowered Crystal of the Heart above your head. A blinding flash sends you tumbling to the ground as the crystal is ripped from your hand and absorbed into the Heart of Fear. The voices of the forsaken fill your ears like innumerable raindrops crashing against the ground on a stormy night. The cries of anguish, the growls of disgust and the roars of terror haunt you... Some awesome presence, some great and godly force seems to beckon you to continue your journey and so you find the will to pick yourself up off of the ground and return to Engineer Eilisia.\n\n---\n\nReport your success to Engineer Eilisia 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\nYou say, 'Hail, Engineer Eilisia'\nEngineer Eilisia listens intently as you recount how the attuned crystal flew from your hand and evoked visions of nightmarish suffering. She offers her hand to yours as a gesture of comfort, 'This is why I knew I could count on a powerful \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ such as yourself. A lesser being would have fallen dead or never returned here after such an experience!' She retracts her hand and quickly scribbles down a few notes, 'I owe you my thanks for your efforts today. The data you have helped us collect will be of immense value as we continue to study the nature of the Heart of Fear.' She looks away and returns to her notes.\nYour faction standing with Harbingers of Thule got better.\nAlthough she did not quite find the words to articulate it, you feel that your work with the Harbingers to uncover the nature behind the Heart of Fear will be invaluable in their efforts to reinstate the Faceless. Your reputation among the Harbingers continues to grow. In fact, Director Idris Manaar is ready to speak with you now.\n_Rewards:_\n337 platinum, 5 gold\nExperience (about 3% regular exp at 96 and 4 AAs)",
    },
