      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Shard's Landing [zone=867]\n**Who:**\n- Bodhessel the Caller [ _Quest_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 85\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Money\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Forsaken Believers +50\n**Factions Lowered:**\n- Heralds of the Unspoken -100\n- The Believers -1\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a citizen [npc=41374]\n- a council advisor [npc=41393]\n- a council judicator [npc=41394]\n- a council overseer [npc=41395]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 28 17:39:52 2012\nModified: Mon Feb 24 07:41:44 2025 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\nThis task begins with Bodhessel the Caller [npc=41282] ( map) in Shard's Landing at location +470,-1925 (in the Forsaken Village in the zone's east valley).\nPre-Requisites:\n\\- Level 85\n\\- No tasks\nYou say, 'Hail, Bodhessel the Caller'\nBodhessel the Caller says 'Tell me, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, have you ever forgotten your [purpose]? Have you ever wandered the wilderness to find your way back [home]?'\nYou say, 'Back home?'\nBodhessel the Caller gazes past you, their hate-filled eyes boring into the mountain beyond, 'Our home is here. It has been three heaps and twelve legs since I was last [underground]. Riddance is good, but we are not enemies.'\nYou say, 'Underground?'\nBodhessel the Caller frowns as they look down at their ragged clothes, 'I do not look right anymore. Hope has won the clothing war, but only once, I swear. The Underground City is the dwelling of The Heralds of the Unspoken! Surely you have heard of [Ali].'\nYou say, 'What purpose?'\nBodhessel the Caller raises their arms to the sky and stares above, 'Purpose? Per pus. You are right: pus is gross, but not frightening. We sow fear in service of Fear itself. Do you know [Ali]?'\nYou say, 'Ali?'\nBodhessel the Caller says 'You will know Ali soon enough, no mind. Sleep while you can. But they must not sleep. We can stop their sleep before it gets too deep. If it gets deep, they will rise too high. Will you [help] me?'\nYou say, 'I will help'\nBodhessel the Caller says 'Oh, good. Then we will not kill you. Just scare you to death!' Bodhessel cackles for a good long while before catching itself, 'We have left that city. I did not understand, but then I did. We were lifted up, shaped by the horror to complete the circle. Everyone in that city is the same: others fear them, but they fear no one. That is furious. Fearious. We will make them all fear you, [agreed]?'\nYou say, 'Agreed!'\nBodhessel the Caller says 'Do you sleep? They sleep in peace. They should have nightmares. You and I will be their nightmares. Go to where they sleep. Go through the mouth. Or is it the nose? Either way, kill all those. Give them fear and be blessed with it yourself, child \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Fear Begins at Home'.\nBodhessel wants you to kill Alaran in the nearby cult compound that it was exiled from. It is clearly insane, but it seems to have influence among the other exiles and may be able to put in a good word for you. Search for an entrance in the canyon to the west.\n\n---\n\n1\\. Find the Underground City 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\nThis is the area that connects to the zone's northwestern valley (labeled on this map for a different task).\n2\\. Kill Alaran in the housing and council area 0/10 (Shard's Landing)\n3\\. Return to Bodhessel the Caller 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Rewards:_\n150 platinum\nYou gain experience!!\nYour faction with Forsaken Believers has been adjusted by 50.\nYour faction with Heralds of the Unspoken has been adjusted by -100.\nYour faction with The Believers has been adjusted by -1.\nFragment of Legendary Alaran History [item=100964]\n- Fragment of Legendary Alaran History [item=100964]",
    },
