      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Shard's Landing [zone=867]\n**Who:**\n- Keeper Nenth [ _Quest_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Harbingers of Thule +?\n**Factions Lowered:**\n**Quest Items:**\n- Garden-Variety Skull [item=107529]\n- Grease-Blackened Scroll [item=107532]\n- Strange Glass Shard [item=107528]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Ashki the Forsaken [npc=41452]\n- Lera the Forsaken [npc=41469]\n- Selya the Forsaken [npc=41471]\n- a poorly crafted vase [npc=41500]\n- a well-groomed oashim corpse [npc=41485]\n- an eerily familiar plant [npc=41501]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 28 17:40:38 2012\nModified: Sat Sep 27 09:07:47 2025 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\nThis is a solo task that begins with Keeper Nenth [npc=41283] ( map) in Shard's Landing. This is a Carnifex mob located at -500, 1615, -502 (this is the arena of the Underground City -- the tunnel area that extends from the zone's northwestern valley).\nPre-requisites:\n\\- Level 85\n\\- No tasks\nYou say, 'Hail, Keeper Nenth'\nKeeper Nenth stares at you in surprise, 'What could One want of us, that they would dare to disturb our silent meditation? It seems unlikely that the Silent One would have sent such a noisy messenger in our hour of [need].'\nYou say, 'Your need?'\nKeeper Nenth coos to itself, clearly delighted with your interest in its plight, 'Clearly One has not been sent to our aid - and yet, that may not stop One from working such miracles as a messenger may. If One would but hear our [plea], perhaps an agreement may be reached?'\nYou say, 'What plea?'\nKeeper Nenth sighs, covering its heart with one hand, 'Sore has been our heart of late over the fate of those poor wretches known as the forsaken. They who rejected our love are loved all the more strongly and might yet be saved from an even worse [fate].'\nYou say, 'What fate?'\nKeeper Nenth says, in Alaran, 'Among the forsaken, three poor souls stand out. It is said they make treasures of rubbish and guard them closely, foregoing both food and rest. In their madness all sight of hope has been lost, leaving only the most pitiful of existences. One might [free] them of their burdens by relieving them of that which they guard so closely.'\nYou say, 'How would we free them?'\nKeeper Nenth says, in Alaran, 'If One were to seek out those known as Ashki, Lera, and Selya, the cause of their hearts' ache might be found. By retrieving the source of each one's misery, One might redeem them from their fate.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Coveted Rubbish'.\nKeeper Nenth has asked you to aid in the ridding of forsaken Alarans of their unnatural possessions.\n\n---\n\n1\\. Speak to Ashki and learn of its obsession 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\nNote: There are see-invis KoS NPCs inside NPC houses.\nAshki the Forsaken [npc=41452] ( map) spawns at about -20, -1560, 5 (the middle hut of the three west huts, in the Forsaken Village in the zone's east-central valley).\nYou say, 'Hail, Ashki the Forsaken'\nAshki the Forsaken says, in Alaran, 'Hush! You'll scare my beloved pets, and I don't want them [running] around and messing up their fur while I'm grooming them.'\nYou say, 'Running?'\nAshki the Forsaken says, in Alaran, 'Well, admittedly they don't run much anymore, since I broke their necks. \\*chuckle\\* You see, they kept trying to run away, and I [couldn't let them] do that, now could I?'\nYou say, 'Couldn't let them?'\nAshki the Forsaken smiles faintly, 'Let's just say, they're my precious pets. I couldn't live without them.' It resumes brushing one of the dead oashim, humming softly.\n2\\. Search the dead oashims' corpses for the object which causes Ashki's unrest 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\nFind well-groomed oashim corpses [npc=41485] arond Ashki's house and /open them until you loot a Grease-Blackened Scroll [item=107532].\n3\\. Speak to Lera and learn of its obsession 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\nLera the Forsaken [npc=41469] ( map) spawns in the house at about -210, -1630, 10 (the southwest hut in the Forsaken Village in the zone's east-central valley).\nYou say, 'Hail, Lera the Forsaken'\nLera the Forsaken says, in Alaran, 'Can't you see I'm busy trying to repair my gardening tools right now? Honestly! How am I supposed to keep my garden free of weeds if my tools keep [breaking] like this?'\nYou say, 'Breaking?'\nLera the Forsaken says, in Alaran, 'Well, it's not like I mistreat my tools, or anything, but for some reason they keep getting dented and chipped. Maybe the dirt out back is too rough? Is that even possible?? My [plants] seem to be managing alright, but my poor tools just can't seem to take it.'\nYou say, 'Your plants?'\nLera the Forsaken says, in Alaran, 'Hmph! It's none of your business what kind of plants I'm growing. So kindly let me get back to my work - oh! - and stay out of my garden! If you trample my poor plants, there'll be hell to pay!'\n4\\. Search the \"plants\" in the garden for the object which causes Lera's unrest 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\nFind eerily familiar plants [npc=41501] (these are actually bone piles around Lera's house) and /open them until you loot a Garden-Variety Skull [item=107529].\n5\\. Speak to Selya and learn of its obsession 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\nSelya the Forsaken [npc=41471] ( map) is found at 50, -1920, 1 (the middle house of the eastern set of houses in the Forsaken Village in the zone's east-central valley).\nYou say, 'Hail, Selya the Forsaken'\nSelya the Forsaken looks up in alarm, 'Please be careful where you step! Just think [what] would happen if you were to knock over one of my vases and it broke!'\nYou say, 'What would happen?'\nSelya the Forsaken says, in Alaran, 'Oh... er, it would break. Yes! And it would be irreplaceable! These are all my own work, you know, and each one is absolutely priceless, so be very careful!' It sinks back against the wall, apparently stressed just at the thought of broken vases, and mutters to itself, 'Perhaps pottery was a bad idea, after all.'\n6\\. Destroy vases to find the object which causes Selya's unrest 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\nFind poorly crafted vases [npc=41500] around Selya's house and /open them until you loot a Strange Glass Shard [item=107528].\n7\\. Deliver a Grease-Blackened Scroll to Keeper Nenth 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n8\\. Deliver a Garden-Variety Skull to Keeper Nenth 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n9\\. Deliver a Strange Glass Shard to Keeper Nenth 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n10\\. Speak to Keeper Nenth 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\nOn these last 3 hails, you'll need to wait for the animation to be over with and right on top of them for the hails to give you credit. You can also hail while invis, and even hail Lera through the wall.\n11\\. Deliver Nenth's message to Ashki 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n12\\. Deliver Nenth's message to Lera 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n13\\. Deliver Nenth's message to Selya 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n14\\. Return to Keeper Nenth 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n_Rewards:_\n225 platinum\nFaction with Harbingers of Thule\n2% lvl exp and 3 AA's",
    },
