      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Breeding Grounds [zone=871]\n**Who:**\n- Foreman Sukar [npc=41317]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Ashen Elixir [item=108462]\n- Dragon Egg Incubator [item=108449]\n- Glass Disk [item=47171]\n- Glowing Lava Rock [item=108440]\n- Mana Battery - Class One [item=11460]\n- Planar Alloy [item=108594]\n- Planar Energy Shard [item=104840]\n- Platinum Bar [item=14324]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Shard's Landing [zone=867]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Asupi Muksap [ _Quests_]\n- Craftkeeper Irus Tindlefoot [ _Tradeskill Components_]\n- Eyska Va`Ker, the Broodmother [npc=41319]\n- a Chetari deathbender [npc=42154]\n- a Chetari hoarder [npc=42156]\n- a Chetari scavenger [npc=42157]\n- a Chetari seeker [npc=42158]\n- a chetari bruiser [npc=42153]\n- a chetari defender [npc=42155]\n- a dragon egg [npc=42160]\n- a magma fiend [npc=42168]\n- a magma guardian [npc=42169]\n- a young ashwing [npc=42177]\n- an elder ashwing [npc=42185]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Breeding Grounds #1: A Chilling Rescue [quest=6074]\n- Breeding Grounds #3: Eggs As Bait [quest=6076]\n- Raid Expedition: A Feast for Zalikor [quest=6079]\n- Raid Expedition: Velishan's Revenge [quest=6080]\n- The Rise of the Ancients [quest=6077]\n- Zalikor's Lair [quest=6078]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 28 22:44:14 2012\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This task is the second in a series of three. It is a solo task that begins with Foreman Sukar ( map) at the zone-in of the Breeding Grounds (-20, 0, 4)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n_\\- Level 85_\n_\\- Completed \"A Chilling Rescue\"_\nYou say, 'Hail, Foreman Sukar'\nForeman Sukar says 'The excavator you rescued claimed that he and the crew were recovering broken egg shells near a nest of frozen dragon eggs when suddenly one of them began to hatch. The noise drew the attention of an elder [frostwing] who immediately tossed them into the water with one swipe of her wing. Without hesitation the dragon released her icy breath on top of the water, creating a frozen grave for the crew trapped below.'\nYou say, 'Tell me about the frostwing'\nForeman Sukar says 'The frostwing are ice dragons that dwell within the Breeding Grounds. Like many of the inhabitants here, not much is known about their history, though we do know that a specific sect of frostwing call themselves the Va`Ker. We have made a lot of progress in our relationship with these dragons. It is surprising to me that the Va`Ker are initiating attacks. Something isn't right... I implore you to [speak] to their leader, Eyska, on my behalf.'\nYou say, 'I will speak to her'\nForeman Sukar nods with understanding. 'Very well. Be cautious, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. While my crew has worked hard to establish an amicable relationship with the Va`Ker elders, it seems this delicate alliance has been recently rattled.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Treading Lightly'.\nForeman Sukar doesn't understand why the Va`Ker have been attacking his crewmembers. He has asked you to speak with their leader, Eyska, in hopes that you will be able to repair whatever damage has been done.\n\n---\n\nFind and speak to Eyska Va`Ker, The Broodmother 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nEyska Va`Ker, the Broodmother [npc=41319] ( map) is found at location 415, 500, 27 (end of the tunnel that extends from the zone's western-most cavern). Note: Two KOS drakes flutter at her side.\nYou say, 'Hail, Eyska Va`Ker, The Broodmother'\nEyska Va`Ker, The Broodmother scowls down at you, scraping her sharp claws across the ice in a threatening gesture. 'I will assume that since you speak for them, you belong to them; so repeat my warning to your masters: any who trespass within these caverns will meet their death. My brethren foolishly agreed to let your kind study our surroundings, so long as you kept away from our young. You betrayed your words by slaughtering my unborn children, and that grotesque act will not go unpunished! Now leave my chambers and do not return, or I shall spill your guts over this icy floor!'\n\n---\n\nReturn to Foreman Sukar 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Task Window Says:_ You should let Sukar know that Eyska claims his crew has been slaughtering her children.\nYou say, 'Hail, Foreman Sukar'\nForeman Sukar's face is filled with disbelief, 'The Broodmother claimed we have slaughtered her unborn children? This cannot be true. I handpicked the excavation crew myself. Each and every member had the utmost respect for dragonkind, and wouldn't dream of causing harm to the eggs within these walls. There must be another [hand] at work here.\nYou say, 'What's at hand?'\nForeman Sukar says 'Someone or something is destroying the dragon eggs, but I cannot fathom who. I suppose the quickest way to find out what is happening is to set up a scenario where we can witness the events ourselves. We can collect un-hatched eggs and place them around the Breeding Grounds as bait. Surely whoever is killing the unborn dragons won't be able to resist this lure. Before egg collection can begin, you'll need to create an [incubator]. The preservation of the future hatchlings is imperative! Also, you'll need to have Asupi mix an [Ashen Elixir] for you.'\nYou say, 'What about the Ashen Elixir?'\nForeman Sukar says 'If you've noticed, the dragon eggs within the Breeding Ground seem to respond to even the slightest movement. If you travel too close to the egg, it will hatch. This poses a problem, you see, since you'll need to be very close to the egg to place it in the incubator. Asupi is a Paebala who relies on his stealth to travel the caverns, scavenging for food. He has perfected a potion that will make you as quiet as a mouse, and as light as a drake made of ash. While he will mix this elixir for you at no cost, he does require some materials.'\nYou say, 'And the incubator?'\nForeman Sukar says 'Most of the necessary items can be found within the Breeding Grounds, though some will need to be fashioned using materials found or purchased elsewhere. While I am quite versed in dragon history, I know little to nothing of smithing. If you are anything like me, and lack the skills the fashion the incubator yourself, Irus Tindlefootin in Shard's Landing will be able to make one if you give her the proper materials and compensate her for her efforts.'\n\n---\n\nAcquire a Dragon Egg Incubator 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nRecover pristine ashwing scales 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nRecover a drop of Chetari blood 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Task Window Says:_ Foreman Sukar has decided the best way to determine who or what is killing the Va`Ker is to collect dragon eggs to use as bait. You may craft a Dragon Incubator by combining Glowing Lava Rock, Planar Alloy, a Glass Disk, and a Mana Battery (Class One) at a forge. Additionally, you can give the needed items to Irus Tindlefoot in Shard's Landing, and she can craft one for you. Glowing Lava Rocks can be found on magma dragons.\nThe two \"Recover...\" updates are not actual items - they are only kills (random updates from any \"ashwing\" and \"chetari\" mob, respectively). Note that ashwings are uncommon spawns as static mobs, but can be spawned with some frequency by stepping on eggs.\nFor the incubator, this is a no-fail smithing combine:\nMana Battery - Class One [item=11460] \\+ Glowing Lava Rock [item=108440] \\+ Planar Alloy [item=108594] \\+ Glass Disk [item=47171] = Dragon Egg Incubator [item=108449]\nThe Mana Battery - Class One [item=11460] is vendorbought or crafted (tinkering); the Glowing Lava Rock [item=108440] drops from magma dragons in the Breeding Grounds (found in the northeastern lava cavern); and the Planar Alloy [item=108594] (jewelcraft) and Glass Disk [item=47171] (jewelcraft) are crafted.\nAlternatively, you can hand in the following items to Craftkeeper Irus Tindlefoot [npc=41363] ( map) in Shard's Landing (in one of the tents in the crater's southwest):\n\\- Mana Battery - Class One [item=11460]\n\\- Glowing Lava Rock [item=108440]\n\\- Platinum Bar [item=14324]\n\\- Planar Energy Shard [item=104840]\n\\- Glass Disk [item=47171]\n\\-\\-\\- 10 platinum\nYou say, 'Hail, Craftkeeper Irus Tindlefoot'\nCraftkeeper Irus Tindlefoot shares a forced smile as she winces, 'Ah, a welcome customer. Hail to you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.' Her tone becomes slightly sarcastic, 'My 'brilliant' husband has insisted that we set up shop out here in this 'lovely' location to sell 'useful' wares to craftsmen travelling through. Please survey our wares to see if you are in need of anything.' She continues speaking in a whisper, 'I don't see why I couldn't just sell my own baked goods and save you the trouble of having to make these things yourself.' She shakes her head slightly still wincing and forcing a fake smile.\n_She gives you a Dragon Egg Incubator [item=108449] in exchange for the above items._\nNOTE: using the Alternatively, way to obtain the Dragon Egg Incubator did not update my task but if you take the Dragon Egg Incubator to Foreman Sukar (The Breeding Grounds) and this will update your task correctly.\n\n---\n\nSpeak to Asupi Muksap 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Task Window Says:_ Asupi Muksap will mix you an Ashen Elixir if you collect the required ingredients first.\nAsupi Muksap [npc=41340] ( map) is located around 200, -350, -99 (from the zone-in area, head east into the narrow tunnels and to the northwestern-most room in those tunnels).\nYou say, 'Hail, Asupi Muksap'\nAsupi Muksap uses his filthy paws to retrieve the necessary items from your grasp. With whiskers twitching, he places a few drops of chetari blood in a liquid-filled vial before crushing, then sprinkling in the drake scales. After a quick shake, he hands you the now cloudy vial with some advice, 'Drink before you go near any dragon eggs and you will not wake the unborn whelps within. Go near without drinking, and you'll be sorry... or dead. Probably dead.'\nYou receive an Ashen Elixir [item=108462]. Use this buff for the next step.\n\n---\n\nUse the incubator to collect dragon eggs (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Task Window Says:_ Locate dragon eggs around the Breeding Grounds and use the incubator to collect them.\nWith the buff on, walk over a dragon egg and click it. Note: If you lose the buff, you can return to Asupi for another Elixir. Failure to do this step without the buff will result in broken eggs.\nNote: Pets and mercenaries also break eggs.\nThe dragon egg shrinks into nothing as the incubator rattles and feels slightly heavier than before.\n\n---\n\nReturn the Dragon Egg Incubator to Foreman Sukar 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Task Window Says:_ Give the Dragon Egg Incubator to Foreman Sukar.\nForeman Sukar gives the incubator a quick inspection before nodding with approval. 'These eggs should work well as [bait].'\nYou used a special incubator to collect dragon eggs around the Breeding Grounds to use as bait.\n_\"bait\" leads into the next task._\n337 platinum, 5 gold\nExperience\nHere are the optional steps for those interested:\n(Opt) Give a Glowing Lava Rock to Irus Tindlefoot 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n(Opt) Give a Platinum Bar to Irus Tindlefoot 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n(Opt) Give a Planar Energy Shard to Irus Tindlefoot 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n(Opt) Give a Glass Disk to Irus Tindlefoot 0/1 (Shard's Landing)\n(Opt) Give a Mana Battery - Class One to Irus Tindlefoot 0/1 (Shard's Landing)",
    },
