      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Breeding Grounds [zone=871]\n**Who:**\n- Glimkar [npc=41318]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Bone Dust [item=107900]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Breeding Grounds: The Rise of the Ancients [zone=889]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Dartmor [npc=42663]\n- Drazankyr [npc=42661]\n- Dregankor [npc=42658]\n- Droolbrood the Necrotic [npc=42660]\n- Falzikor [npc=42656]\n- Glimkar [npc=42653]\n- Gorianar [npc=42654]\n- Halzifryn [npc=42659]\n- Nalarindor [npc=42657]\n- a chetari hoarder [npc=42662]\n- a dracolich [npc=42655]\n- a treasure chest - The Rise of the Ancients [npc=42474]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Breeding Grounds #1: A Chilling Rescue [quest=6074]\n- Breeding Grounds #2: Treading Lightly [quest=6075]\n- Breeding Grounds #3: Eggs As Bait [quest=6076]\n- Raid Expedition: A Feast for Zalikor [quest=6079]\n- Raid Expedition: Velishan's Revenge [quest=6080]\n- Zalikor's Lair [quest=6078]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 28 22:44:19 2012\nModified: Fri Sep 27 06:46:27 2024 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is a group mission that begins with Glimkar ( map) in the Breeding Grounds, found at location 655, 430, -34 (southeast part of the zone's western-most cavern)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completed \"A Chilling Rescue\"\n\\- Completed \"Treading Lightly\"\n\\- Completed \"Eggs As Bait\"\nYou say, 'Hail, Glimkar'\nGlimkar says 'Eyska Va'Ker has spoken of you. It is her wish that you destroy the ones responsible for eating our young. We will strike their lair without hesitation or remorse and cleanse their taint from this place. Are you [prepared] to take up arms against them?'\nYou say, 'We are prepared'\nGlimkar says 'We shall [depart] at once then! When we arrive, we will meet up with my brother, Gorianar.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Rise of the Ancients'.\nA group of terrorwings and fearwings are using the power of the fear crystals to summon long dead dragons to take over the Breeding Grounds and must be stopped!\nYou say, 'Depart'\nGlimkar says 'See you on the battlefield.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered The Breeding Grounds.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Gorianar 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_NOTE: The mission locks upon hail._\nYou say, 'Hail, Gorianar'\nGorianar says 'Brother! I have troubling news. The fearwings and terrorwings are raising the bones of long dead dragons to fight for them. They plan on conquering all the other flights! They must be stopped. Recruits; you must find their necromancers, and defeat the dracoliches they have raised. I would also like a sample of bone dust from any of the dracoliches you take down. If you feel you are not brave enough however, I can arrange for you to [depart] this place.'\n\n---\n\nKill some dracoliches 0/10 (The Breeding Grounds)\nLoot Bone Dust from dracoliches 0/10 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_You will get the above step updates done as you move along in the zone._\n\n---\n\nDefeat Falzikor 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Falzikor ( map) is in the room next to the zone-in. Falzikor casts a rear AE (\"Mighty Tail Swipe\")._\nMighty Tail Swipe: Directional 200', Magic (-960)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 19000\n\n---\n\nDefeat Nalarindor 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Nalarindor ( map) is found in the fear area (treasure room in the north part of the zone). He casts a single-target random fear (\"Visions of Terror\"; 1 tick)._\nVisions of Terror: Single Target, (-960)\n1: Fear up to level 200\n\n---\n\nDefeat Dregankor 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Dregankor ( map) is found deep in the basement._\n_He casts a single-target random DOT called \"Poisonous Breath\" (33,000 hp/tick; 3,000 end/tick for 3 ticks). 10 seconds after this spell lands on a player, it goes viral on anyone within 40' range of that player._\nPoisonous Breath: Single Target, Disease (-960)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 33000 per tick\n2: Decrease Endurance by 3000 per tick\n3: Increase Poison Counter by 80\n\n---\n\nDefeat Halzifryn 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Halzifryn ( map) is also found in the basement, in the room south of Dregankor's room (you'll be encountering Halzirfryn before Dregankor). During the fight, he buffs himself with \"Shield of Bones\" (60,000/tick regen, which gets dispelled after 20 melee attacks or spells are absorbed)._\nShield of Bones: Self 0', Magic (-960)\n1: Block Melee or Spells (20)\n2: Increase Hitpoints by 60000 per tick\n\n---\n\nGive the Bone Dust to Gorianar 0/10 (The Breeding Grounds)\nSpeak with Gorianar 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Gorianar ( map) is back at the zone-in._\nYou say, 'Hail, Gorianar'\nGorianar says 'This bone dust is tainted with the power of fear. Take the bone dust and keep it safe. My scouts have informed me that the leader of the necromantic dragons has appeared. He must be destroyed. Seek out Drazankyr and show him no mercy.'\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Drazankyr 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Drazankyr ( map) can be found in the northeastern magma cavern (head east from the zone-in through the Chetari tunnels, then north from there)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Drazankyr'\nDrazankyr says ''Welcome. I've been expecting you.\" An astonishingly fast blur whizzes past you as the ancient dragon speaks. A crafty chetari appears next to Drazankyr. You notice that the chetari has stolen the bone dust from you. \"Ah, Dartmor. You are just in time.\" The chetari hands the bone dust to the dragon. \"Nice work as always, Dartmor. Now it is time to show these pitiful fools my true power.\" Drazankyr throws the bone dust up into the air. It swirls and grows in a raging tornado. The grounds beneath you begins to quake as a massive undead dragon claws itself from the ground. \"Say hello to Droolbrood!''\n_This triggers the spawn of \"Droolbrood the Necrotic\" next to Drazankyr._\nDroolbrood the Necrotic roars and charges!\nDefeat Droolbrood the Necrotic 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Droolbrood the Necrotic casts a random single-target charm called \"Enslave the Living\"._\nEnslave the Living: Single Target, Magic (-960)\n1: Charm up to level 200\nDroolbrood the Necrotic has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nDroolbrood the Necrotic's corpse crumbles to the ground.\nDrazankyr shouts, 'Such a shame. I guess I will have to end your pathetic lives myself!'\n_Drazankyr attacks after Droolbrood is killed._\nDrazankyr lets forth a blast of fire and charges!\nDefeat Drazankyr 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Drazankyr casts a random single-target melee/spell silence called \"Baleful Roar\"._\nBaleful Roar: Single Target, Magic (-960)\n1: Amnesia (Silence vs Melee Effect)\n2: Silence\nDrazankyr has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nDrazankyr's corpse falls to the ground smoldering.\nDartmor shouts, 'You may have killed my master, but you won't kill me! Come and find me if you think you are so brave!'\n\n---\n\nDefeat Dartmor 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Dartmor ( map) spawns in the southernmost room of the Chetari tunnels._\nDartmor has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nDartmor's corpse falls to the ground.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Gorianar 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nYou say, 'Hail, Gorianar'\nGorianar says 'You have done well this day. The Breeding Grounds are safe once again and you have the thanks of me and my kin. Please take what you wish from the nearby chest. When you are ready to [leave], just let me know.'\nLoot the chest for your reward 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Rewards:_\n450 platinum\nExperience\n_Possible Chest Loot [npc=42474] (1 Item + 1 Dreadmote per task):_\nBelt of the Expansive Mind\nBlazing Hammer of Destruction\nCrystallized Dragon Breath\nEternity Band\nFire of Osalur\nGlowing Eternal Shard\nGosik's Wing\nNecklace of Zalifur\nNefori's Horn\nQuake Fist\nLesser Dreadmote\nMedian Dreadmote\nGreater Dreadmote\nGlowing Dreadmote",
    },
