      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Beasts' Domain [zone=810]\n**Who:**\n- Yioan [npc=41323]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Aphomat's Soul [item=108120]\n- Atbius' Soul [item=108131]\n- Erotoz's Soul [item=108128]\n- Mystical Soul Combiner [item=108135]\n- Nucleus of Fear [item=108139]\n- Obapeth's Soul [item=108121]\n- Soziel's Soul [item=108134]\n- Xartabta's Soul [item=108123]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Evantil: Fear Not [zone=891]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Aphomat [npc=42733]\n- Atbius [npc=42737]\n- Erotoz [npc=42736]\n- Garnalan [npc=42739]\n- Obapeth [npc=42734]\n- Soziel [npc=42738]\n- Waleni [npc=42732]\n- Xartabta [npc=42735]\n- a rotting chest - Evantil: Fear Not [npc=42150]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Evantil #1: Fun With Fungus [quest=6081]\n- Evantil #2: What A Mess [quest=6082]\n- Evantil #3: Forbidden Fruit [quest=6083]\n- Evantil #4: Searching for a Cure [quest=6084]\n- Evantil: Heart of the Oak [quest=6086]\n- Raid Expedition: Heart of the Oak [quest=6087]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 28 23:02:29 2012\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This group mission begins with Yioan in Beasts' Domain. This is an Alaran found at -620, 2755, 10 (due south of Kalda and Mea Treg who are in the zone's northwestern corner)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completed \"Fun with Fungus\"\n\\- Completed \"What a Mess\"\n\\- Completed \"Forbidden Fruit\"\n\\- Completed \"Searching for a Cure\"\nYou say, 'Hail, Yioan'\nYioan says, in Alaran, 'The vials of brain fluid you have given me have been put to good use. The elixir I was able to create from researching them does not work exactly as I had hoped, but I believe it can help with preventing those who consume the fear fruit from becoming addicted. You have already done much for me and my people, but I ask that you please help me further. I want you to [test] the elixir. If you wish, we can discuss the [wretched].'\nYou say, 'How can we test it?'\nYioan says, in Alaran, ''I will not lie to you; this will be very dangerous, but you have proven to me that you are strong. Before you depart to Evantil, you will need to use the elixir I created. It will protect you from becoming addicted to the fear fruit.\" Yioan hands you the elixir. You carefully swallow a sample of it. It tastes horrible, but does not appear to have any harmful effects. Yioan continues, \"When you are ready to depart to Evantil, please let me [know]. When you arrive, find the shaman known as, Waleni. Waleni was once part of our tribe, but is now part of the wretched. Waleni should be able to guide you further.''\nYou have been assigned the task 'Fear Not'.\nYioan in the Beasts' Domain has made an elixir from the vials of brain fluid you previously collected. The elixir is said to prevent one from becoming addicted to the fear fruit. Yioan wants you to test the elixir by consuming some fear fruit and then speaking with one of the wretched alarans in Evantil, named Waleni.\nYou say, 'What do you know!'\nYioan says, in Alaran, 'I await your safe return.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Evantil - The Vile Oak.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Waleni 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nYou say, 'Hail, Waleni'\nWaleni says, in Alaran, 'I have foreseen your coming. You are the ones that can help my people. The fear fruit induces visions when consumed, but these are not mere visions. They are apparitions from the Plane of Fear. These spirits have made it known that we are their eternal slaves, and they delight in torturing us. You must [destroy] them.'\n_Note: The task locks at this point._\nYou say, 'We will destroy them'\nWaleni says, in Alaran, ''You will need to consume this fear fruit before you will be able to see the visions of fear.' Waleni gives you a large fear fruit. You reluctantly eat it and immediately a feeling of absolute fear overcomes you. Thankfully Yioan's elixir has made it so you will not become addicted. \"Seek out the visions of fear throughout Evantil, destroy them, and take their souls. Return to me when you have done so. If you need to return to Yioan in the Beasts' Domain, I can [transport] you there.''\n_Task Window Says:_ Waleni wants you to kill six visions of fear that only appear to those who have consumed fear fruit. Waleni hopes that by defeating those visions, the wretched can be saved from the vile effects of the fear fruit. Defeat Aphomat, Obapeth, Xartabta, Erotoz, Atbius, and Soziel, and collect their souls.\n\n---\n\nKill the Vision of Fear known as Aphomat 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_Aphomat is a large Amygdalan found in the southeastern part of the zone (next to the Shard's Landing portal). He hits for a max ~15,500, and is pure melee._\n_NOTE: Recently (April 2013), it's been reported he casts \"Wave of Fear\" **(any confirmation about this or any casting by other nameds here besides Xartabta?**):_\nWave of Fear: PB AE 40', Disease (-850)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 81000 per tick _(1 tick)_\nLoot Aphomat's Soul 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n\n---\n\nKill the Vision of Fear known as Obapeth 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_Obapeth is a large parasite found in the northeastern part of the zone. It hits for a max ~15,500, and is pure melee._\nLoot Obapeth's Soul 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n\n---\n\nKill the Vision of Fear known as Xartabta 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_Xartabta is a large tentacle terror found in the northwestern part of the zone. It hits for a max ~15,500. Every 30 seconds, it casts \"Fearsome Tentacles\" on a random target (2-tick spell slow/interrupt; hp/mana drain):_\nFearsome Tentacles: Single Target, Cold (-920)\n1: Increase Spell Haste by 20%\n2: Interrupt Casting (60% chance)\n3: Decrease Hitpoints by 65000 per tick\n4: Decrease Mana by 8000 per tick\nLoot Xartabta's Soul 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n\n---\n\nKill the Vision of Fear known as Erotoz 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_Erotoz is a spectre found in the canyon in the western part of the zone. It hits for a max ~15,500, and is pure melee._\nLoot Erotoz's Soul 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n\n---\n\nKill the Vision of Fear known as Atbius 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_Atbius is a giant evil eye found on the third floor of the tree (the ant area). It hits for a max ~15,500, and is pure melee._\nLoot Atbius' Soul 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n\n---\n\nKill the Vision of Fear known as Soziel 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_Soziel is a ghoul found in the southeastern part of the tree top. It hits for a max ~15,500, and is pure melee._\nLoot Soziel's Soul 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Waleni 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nYou say, 'Hail, Waleni'\nWaleni says, in Alaran, 'Well done. Now you need to take this mystical soul combiner and combine all six of the souls within it. When you obtain the nucleus of fear, give it to me. If you lose your [mystical soul combiner] I can give you another one.'\n_You receive a Mystical Soul Combiner._\nGive the Nucleus of Fear to Waleni 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_In the container, combine the souls to produce a Nucleus of Fear. Hand this to Waleni._\nSpeak with Waleni 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_This triggers the spawn of Garnalan (not auto-aggro, but is KOS and spawns right next to Waleni -- you can sometimes avoid aggro if you move away very fast after hailing)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Waleni'\nWaleni says, in Alaran, 'I had my doubts you would be so easily fooled into handing me such power. With the nucleus of fear in my possession, I can now destroy all those that wish to take the fear fruit from us. The wretched will rule this land and destroy all those that oppose us! Garnalan, take care of our guests, please.'\n\n---\n\nDefeat Garnalan 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_Task Window Says:_ Waleni has gone mad with power and summoned a creature named Garnalan to kill you! Defeat Garnalan!\n_Garnalan hits for a max ~21,500. It is pure melee._\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Waleni 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nYou say, 'Hail, Waleni'\nWaleni says, in Alaran, 'Please don't hurt me! The power of the nucleus overcame me and I did not know what I was doing. I will destroy the nucleus, I promise! Thank you for your help. Perhaps now the effects of the fear fruit will wane, and my people will be able to join our tribe back in the Beasts' Domain some day. Please loot this chest for your reward. When you have received your reward and are ready to [leave], let me know.'\nLoot the treasure chest for your reward 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_Rewards:_\n375 platinum\nExperience\n_Possible Chest Loot (1 Item + 1 Dreadmote per task):_\nBand of the Earthmother\nBlack Chitin Shoulders\nBow of Grasping Vines\nEnthralling Orb\nFrostbitten Band\nMace of Life Draining\nOaken Spine Guard\nRuaabri's Fist\nSticky Dagger\nTainted Saver of Lives\nThe Queen's Diseased Heart\nLesser Dreadmote\nMedian Dreadmote\nGreater Dreadmote\nGlowing Dreadmote\n- Band of the Earthmother [item=109074]\n- Black Chitin Shoulders [item=108130]\n- Bow of Grasping Vines [item=108783]\n- Enthralling Orb [item=108621]\n- Frostbitten Band [item=108146]\n- Glowing Dreadmote [item=106497]\n- Greater Dreadmote [item=106464]\n- Lesser Dreadmote [item=106476]\n- Mace of Life Draining [item=108259]\n- Median Dreadmote [item=106509]\n- Oaken Spine Guard [item=107902]\n- Ruaabri's Fist [item=108148]\n- Sticky Dagger [item=108098]\n- Tainted Saver of Lives [item=108261]",
