      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Beasts' Domain [zone=810]\n**Who:**\n- Yioan [npc=41323]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Related Zones:**\n- Evantil: Heart of the Oak [zone=892]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Impacted Molar [npc=42765]\n- Molar [npc=42764]\n- Nest Protector [npc=42775]\n- Yioan [npc=42776]\n- a campfire [npc=42770]\n- a dessicated saporling [npc=42766]\n- a drop of sap [npc=42769]\n- a mantrap [npc=42773]\n- a reward chest - Evantil: Heart of the Oak [npc=42763]\n- a spore cloud [npc=42774]\n- a spore sprout [npc=45579]\n- a tanglefoot flower [npc=42768]\n- an aggressive ant [npc=42772]\n- an aggressive vinemaw [npc=42767]\n- an ant soldier [npc=42771]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Evantil #1: Fun With Fungus [quest=6081]\n- Evantil #2: What A Mess [quest=6082]\n- Evantil #3: Forbidden Fruit [quest=6083]\n- Evantil #4: Searching for a Cure [quest=6084]\n- Fear Not [quest=6085]\n- Raid Expedition: Heart of the Oak [quest=6087]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 28 23:02:32 2012\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This group mission begins with Yioan in Beasts' Domain. This is an Alaran found at -620, 2755, 10 (due south of Kalda and Mea Treg who are in the zone's northwestern corner)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completed \"Fun with Fungus\"\n\\- Completed \"What a Mess\"\n\\- Completed \"Forbidden Fruit\"\n\\- Completed \"Searching for a Cure\"\n\\- Completed \"Fear Not\" (mission)\nYou say, 'Hail, Yioan'\nYioan says, in Alaran, 'We have discovered much about the effects of the fear fruit. Now I would ask you to go into the heart of the great tree and see if you can stop, or at least slow, the influence of the fear shard on Evantil. I have discovered that there is a beast guarding the shard. It is a nest, of sorts, infested with ants. This beast bathes in the power of the shard and its ants infest the tree and pollinate the fruit with fear. [Kill the nest] and the ants, if you can, and I am sure that the influence of fear will be reduced. If this is too dangerous for you, another [test] of the elixir would help me understand the [wretched] better.'\nYou say, 'Kill the nest?'\nYioan says, in Alaran, 'It is dangerous and you most certainly will need a lot of assistance. You have proven yourself brave already, so if this proves too dangerous, you should not feel obliged to assist us. But if you have enough allies to mount a true raid and are [willing], simply let me know. If you have only a smaller group, there is may be something you can do to [assist].'\nYou say, 'We will assist you'\nYioan says, in Alaran, 'I am pleased to hear this. When you and your allies are [ready] to go, tell me and I shall transport you to Evantil. Be wary, though. It may know of your presence and employ hearty defenses to prevent your entry.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Evantil: Heart of the Oak'.\nIn order to reduce the effect of the fear shard on the great oak, you have been asked to destroy the beast that houses the ants at the heart of the oak. Those ants are the key to the 'pollination' of the fruit with the power of fear.\nGetting past the defenses into the tree will require defeating the molars. Yioan reminded you that trees generally do not like fire.\nYou say, 'Ready!'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Evantil - The Vile Oak.\n\n---\n\nDestroy the Nest Protector and the aggressive ants in the Heart of the Oak 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n**Part 1: The Molars**\n_Run up the ramp and into the tree to trigger the event. (Whoever triggers it will be ported to the zone-in, but can run back.)_\nThe tree seems to come to life with a great exhalation. Embers spring to life in old campfires as leaves swirl around your feet.\n_At the top of the ramp leading into the tree are two treants: \"Molar\" and \"Impacted Molar\". You need to kill the two treants while also killing the adds that spawn. The Molars each hit for a max ~18,000; are permanently rooted; do not summon; and are only susceptible to melee damage and fire-based nukes/DOTs._\n_As long as the Molars are alive, adds will be spawning and auto-aggro'ing your group (these adds have cross-zone aggro and will seek you out wherever you may be). You'll get one add every 60-90 seconds. Adds hit for a max ~12,500._\n_To help deal with the adds and the Molars, you can get a fire damage proc by running over one of the two campfires across the canyon. The buff is called \"Up In Flames\", but also has a DOT component to it. This buff is not necessary if you have enough DPS on your own._\nUp In Flames: Single Target, Unresistable (0) _(90 seconds)_\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 4000 per tick\n4: Add Proc: Touch of Flame rate mod 150\n_Note that if you try to pass the Molars while they are still alive (or any adds are still alive), you will be ported to the zone-in:_\nA great gust of moldy wind flings you from the heights.\n_You can melee the Molars without being kicked away, but have to stay in front of them._\n_In addition to the Molars and adds, you will also have oozes called \"a drop of sap\" spawning in the area. These are non-aggro and not killable, and have an aura around them, so you will want to avoid stepping in them:_\nSapping Strength: Single Target, Unresistable (0) _(3 ticks)_\n1: Decrease Spell Haste by 50%\n2: Limit: Combat Skills Not Allowed\n3: Decrease Movement by 80%\n4: Inhibit Melee Attacks by (50%)\n_If the Molars are left idle, you'll get emotes warning of a reset:_\nThe molars blocking the entrance to the great tree grow strong as they stand idle.\nA creaking sounds preceeds a great, warm wind. All of your efforts are swept away and things return to normal within the great oak.\n_Once the Molars and all adds are dead, you can move up into the tree._\nImpacted Molar has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nMolar has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nThe unnerving breathing from the great tree stops. Things become eerily quiet.\n**Part 2: The Nest Protector**\n_The main encounter here, \"Nest Protector\" spawns on the second floor of the tree (see this image for The Ant Queen \\-\\- the Nest Protector is found in the larger of the two rooms on the tree's second floor)._\n_Along the way to this location, you'll see numerous ants (\"an ant soldier\"). These don't see invisibility and don't factor into the task's progression, so you can invis past them if you want. You can also clear them as they don't have many hitpoints and don't hit too hard (~7,000). Don't pull them from a distance, however, as they will sometimes warp around. If they aggro the Nest Protector and you are not there to engage it, the task will reset to the beginning._\n_In the group mission, the Nest Protector has a standard aggro range, so you can set up and prepare just outside its room._\n_The Nest Protector hits for a max ~16,000 and single-target rampages. It casts:_\nForceful Explosion: PB AE 35', Magic (-800)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 20000\nLife Harvest: Single Target, Poison (-950)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 34000\n_It spawns adds (1x \"an aggressive ant\" at a time: mezzable; stunnable; hits for a max ~10,000). You will get one add on engage and more adds as the fight goes on. It's not confirmed whether these adds are timed or if they are based on the health of the Nest Protector, but as few as 10 adds and as many as 12 (in total) have been reported, so they may be timed. If they are timed, they appear at a rate of one every 10-15 seconds (perhaps up to a maximum number of spawns alive at once). These adds have a fair amount of hitpoints, so crowd control appears to be the best option, rather than killing them as they spawn._\n_Oozes occasionally spawn, with the aura \"Sappy Slime\":_\nSappy Slime: Single Target, Unresistable (0)\n1: Decrease CHA by 40\n3: Decrease Movement by 40%\n_There is an aura that circles the perimeter of the room, \"a spore cloud\". If you get caught in it, you get the debuff \"Pollination\" which leads to \"Explosive Sneeze\":_\nPollination: Single Target, Poison (-800)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 1500 per tick _(4 ticks)_\n2: Increase Disease Counter by 50\n3: Trigger Effect: Explosive Sneeze on Fade _(knockback + nuke for 17,500 hp)_\n_Around the room are five flower mobs called \"a mantrap\". These will target random players and pull them to their location, inflicting them with \"Flowery Grasp\" (holds them in position and an indefinite silence). In order to free the player, that particular mantrap needs to be killed (mantraps have relatively few hitpoints). Note that these instantly respawn._\nFlowery Grasp: Single Target, Unresistable (-10000)\n1: Slow Push (-300)\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 5000 per tick\n3: Amnesia (Silence vs Melee Effect)\n4: Silence\n_Kill the Nest Protector and all aggressive ants to update this task step. Note: The task locks upon the death of the last ant or the Nest Protector (whichever is killed last)._\n**About Wipeouts & Resets**\n_If you wipe out on the Molar phase, you will need to drop the task and get a new one (the auto-aggro adds keep spawning even after Molars reset, effectively preventing in-zone CR)._\n_If you wipe out while the Nest Protector is still alive, you will have to repeat the entire task (including the Molars)._\n_If you wipe out after the Nest Protector is dead, but aggressive ants are still alive, the event does NOT reset (they simply keep leashing themselves to the room). You can CR and move in to kill the ants after rezzing and rebuffing._\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Yioan 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_For all your effort, you get a simple \"well done\":_\nYou say, 'Hail, Yioan'\nYioan says, in Alaran, 'Well done! Thank you for your assistance.'\nOpen the chest for your reward 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_Rewards:_\n450 platinum\nExperience\n_Possible Chest Loot (1 Item + 1 Dreadmote per task):_\nFear Infused Charcoal\nFear Laden Brace\nJom'Agurd\nLiquid Crystal Mask\nOaken Spine Guard\nPetrified Mask\nShard Spattered Cord\nThe Defiler's Rebuke\nVeil of Thorns\nYunaizarn's Fang\nLesser Dreadmote\nMedian Dreadmote\nGreater Dreadmote\nGlowing Dreadmote\n- Fear Infused Charcoal [item=107661]\n- Fear Laden Brace [item=109027]\n- Glowing Dreadmote [item=106497]\n- Greater Dreadmote [item=106464]\n- Jom'Agurd [item=108262]\n- Lesser Dreadmote [item=106476]\n- Liquid Crystal Mask [item=108998]\n- Median Dreadmote [item=106509]\n- Oaken Spine Guard [item=107902]\n- Petrified Mask [item=108174]\n- Shard Spattered Cord [item=109919]\n- The Defiler's Rebuke [item=108629]\n- Veil of Thorns [item=109236]\n- Yunaizarn's Fang [item=107897]",
