      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Grelleth's Palace, Chateau of Filth [zone=872]\n**Who:**\n- Reena Kedson [npc=41324]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Gorvna the Jailer [npc=42141]\n- Kelmur the Quartermaster [ _Palace Quartermaster_]\n- Pulq the Beastmaster [ _Palace Beast Feeder_]\n- Sherri Ganes [npc=42147]\n- a palace guard [npc=42129]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Grelleth's #1: Rise of the Swinetor [quest=6088]\n- Grelleth's #2: Dirty Tactics [quest=6089]\n- Grelleth's #3: Double Trouble [quest=6090]\n- Grelleth's #4: Halt of Decay [quest=6091]\n- Grelleth's #6: The Art of War [quest=6093]\n- Raid Expedition: Grelleth, Her Majesty the Queen [quest=6096]\n- The Machinations of Kotul [quest=6094]\n- The Queen's Decree [quest=6095]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 29 05:26:47 2012\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This task is the fifth in a series of six. It's a shared task (1-6 players) that begins with Reena Kedson ( map) in Grelleth's Palace, the Chateau of Filth. She is located at 1200, 265, 0 (zone-in area)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completed \"Rise of the Swinetor\"\n\\- Completed \"Dirty Tactics\"\n\\- Completed \"Double Trouble\n\\- Completed \"Halt of Decay\"\nYou say, 'Hail, Reena Kedson'\nReena Kedson says '\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_? Nice to see you. I hope you're here to help us out. These Fear Shards are causing more trouble than we expected. Still, I've had enough of these Alaran gods. We have enough trouble with the Norrathian ones. Let's put an end to this together, as one people. And we have a [plan].'\nYou say, 'What plan?'\nReena Kedson says 'It's simple. In theory. First, gather [information] on our enemies. Second, we'll have to take out the [scouts] and any other [defenses]. Then, after we gain [access], we'll have to deal with the palace [forces], and recover any [clues] as to their further plans.'\nYou say, 'What about the forces?'\nReena Kedson says 'We're ready for our first real attack. We need to take out a few of the more powerful swinetor that Grelleth commands, and, if possible, Zurel as well. Zurel is the eldest daughter and taking her out would be just the break we need. Sherri has a list of others we need to take care of as well. Go talk to her when you can, and we'll be ready.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Raw Aggression'.\nZurel, a skilled warrior in control of the soldiers that serve Grelleth, now no longer has any external defenses. Bring the fight directly to her most valued minions to leave her without a coordinated attack force.\nSherri has information on the targets. Speak to her at the expedition camp.\n\n---\n\nAttend Sherri Ganes' briefing 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\n_Hail Sherri Ganes ( map), also in the expedition camp._\nYou say, 'Hail, Sherri Ganes'\nSherri Ganes says 'Reena sent you? Great, let's get started. We know Zurel runs the palace defenses with an iron fist. With Wuran's wards down, she's going to be relying even more on her top swinetor. That includes Gorvna, the jailer, who guards the expedition members they've captured among others. Kelmur, the quartermaster, who has succeed in collecting way too many quality Alaran weapons. And Pulq, the Beast Master, who organizes the creature oriented palace defenses. Take them out, along with as many palace guards as you can. We'll be dealing with the other targets while you remove those three.'\n\n---\n\nTake out palace guards 0/3 (Grelleth's Palace)\nEliminate Gorvna the Jailer 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\nEliminate Kelmur the Quartermaster 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\nEliminate Pulq the Beastmaster 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\n_Task Window Says:_ Eliminate the swinetor Zurel feels is key to the palace defense. Gorvna can likely be found near the jail. Kelmur oversees weapon maintenance so look for racks of weapons. Pulq was last seen near the filthy water pits in the palace by a scout.\n_Gorvna ( map) is located on the second floor jail at about 6175, 730, 290 (northwestern part of the palace's second floor). She casts \"Filth Blast\":_\nFilth Blast: Unknown(32) 100', Disease (-900)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 22500\n_Kelmur ( map) is located on the top floor at 5870, -270, 400 (in the large room south of the throne room). He casts \"Swinetor Tackle\":_\nSwinetor Tackle: Single Target, (-200)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 25000\n_Pulq ( map) is located in the lower floor of the palace at about 5625, -300, -30 (eastern part of the basement that leads into the large circular room). He casts \"Whip & Spin\":_\nWhip & Spin: Single Target, (-200)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 25000\n2: SpinStun\n\n---\n\nReport to Reena 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\nYou say, 'Hail, Reena Kedson'\nReena Kedson says 'Great to see you back alive. This means we're almost ready for an all-out attack. But there is one thing we need to make sure of, first. We have to make sure we find out what they're up to, to make certain they aren't expecting us. If we don't take out Grelleth's son Kotul, and especially Grelleth herself, we may just be delaying another swinetor uprising. Knowledge is strength, as Jaris is fond of saying.'\nYour first strike has eliminated several key Swinetor. However, Zurel is still at large and the fight is not over.\nReena Kedson says 'Where is Relco? I can't keep watching him to keep him out of trouble.'\n_Rewards:_\n150 platinum\nExperience",
    },
