      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Grelleth's Palace, Chateau of Filth [zone=872]\n**Who:**\n- Ain Kavus [npc=41325]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Related Zones:**\n- Grelleth's Palace: The Queen's Decree [zone=894]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Ain Kavus [npc=42711]\n- Grelleth, her Majesty the Queen [npc=42710]\n- Kotul [npc=42720]\n- Lelri [npc=42717]\n- Lelri`s Remains [npc=42723]\n- Lelro [npc=42716]\n- Lelro`s Remains [npc=42722]\n- Reena Kedson [npc=42714]\n- Relco Finn [npc=42712]\n- Sherri Ganes [npc=42713]\n- Turo [npc=42715]\n- Turo`s Remains [npc=42721]\n- Wuran [npc=42718]\n- Wuran`s Remains [npc=42724]\n- Zurel [npc=42719]\n- Zurel`s Remains [npc=42725]\n- a palace guard [npc=42727]\n- a pile of refuse [npc=42465]\n- a priest of decay [npc=42730]\n- a reanimated servant [npc=42726]\n- an assassin [npc=42728]\n- an elite soldier [npc=42731]\n- an oashim swarmling [npc=42729]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Grelleth's #1: Rise of the Swinetor [quest=6088]\n- Grelleth's #2: Dirty Tactics [quest=6089]\n- Grelleth's #3: Double Trouble [quest=6090]\n- Grelleth's #4: Halt of Decay [quest=6091]\n- Grelleth's #5: Raw Aggression [quest=6092]\n- Grelleth's #6: The Art of War [quest=6093]\n- Raid Expedition: Grelleth, Her Majesty the Queen [quest=6096]\n- The Machinations of Kotul [quest=6094]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 29 05:26:55 2012\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is a group mission that begins with Ain Kavus ( map) at location 1185, 265, 0 (the zone-in area)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completed \"Rise of the Swinetor\"\n\\- Completed \"Dirty Tactics\"\n\\- Completed \"Double Trouble\n\\- Completed \"Halt of Decay\"\n\\- Completed \"Raw Aggression\"\n\\- Completed \"The Art of War\"\n\\- Completed \"The Machinations of Kotul\" (mission)\nYou say, 'Hail, Ain Kavus'\nAin Kavus says '\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, it is good to see you alive and well. Our first assault on the Chateau of Filth has proved very effective. Thanks to you we have driven back Grelleth's forces and wounded her armies. If you are ready to bring this battle to a close then an [organized assault] with a handful of allies or the force of a full [raid] should finish this. If you wish to organize a [strike force] again then that is an option as well.'\nYou say, 'Let's do an organized assault'\nAin Kavus says 'Let me know when you are [ready] to depart.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Queen's Decree'.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n**Task Steps**\nLet Ain Kavus know that you are 'ready' to depart 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\nConfront Queen Grelleth 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\nDefeat Turo 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\nDefeat Lelri and Lelro 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\nDefeat Wuran 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\nDefeat Zurel 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\nDefeat Kotul 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\nDefeat Grelleth 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\nDefeat all of Grelleth's remaining minions 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\nClaim your rewards from Grelleth's pile of refuse 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n**Summary**\n\\- Say 'ready' to zone in.\n\\- Say 'fight' to Grelleth to trigger the event.\n\\- Grelleth is permanently rooted and does not summon, so you can back away from the throne to fight.\n\\- The encounter:\n\\-\\-\\- 100%: 2x \"a palace guard\", then another 2x \"a palace guard\" after the first two are dead.\n\\-\\-\\- 98%: Turo.\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Spawns 1x \"an assassin\" at 70% and 40%.\n\\-\\-\\- 87%: Lelri and Lelro.\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Spawn timed adds: 4x \"an oashim swarmling\" at unknown intervals.\n\\-\\-\\- 82%: Wuran.\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Spawns 1x \"a priest of decay\" at 70% and 40%.\n\\-\\-\\- 72%: Zurel.\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Spawns 1x \"an elite soldier\" at 70% and 40%.\n\\-\\-\\- 62%: Kotul.\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Spawns \"Turo`s Remains\" at 92%.\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Spawns \"Lelri`s Remains\" and \"Lelro`s Remains\" at 82%.\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Spawns \"Wuran`s Remains\" at 72%.\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Spawns \"Zurel`s Remains\" at 62%.\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- The \"Remains\" adds retain their earlier abilities and mechanics, but hit for less and have less hitpoints.\n\\-\\-\\- 52%: Grelleth powers up, becomes unrooted, and starts summoning.\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- From this point until her death, every 90 seconds, she does an emote that requires you to switch tanks.\n\\-\\-\\- 21%: 1x \"a reanimated servant\" spawns.\n\\-\\-\\- 19%: 1x \"a reanimated servant\" spawns.\n\\- Kill the queen and all adds to win the event.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n**In Detail**\nLet Ain Kavus know that you are 'ready' to depart 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\nYou say, 'Ready!'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Grelleth's Palace, the Chateau of Filth.\n_Make your way into the throne room where you will see Queen Grelleth (non-aggro), a few sleeping guards, and some expedition NPCs._\n\n---\n\nConfront Queen Grelleth 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\n_Task Window Says:_ Queen Grelleth will not give you the privilege of battle without a proper introduction.\n_Approach Grelleth (not aggro until triggered) and speak with her (\"fight\" to initiate the event)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Grelleth, her Majesty the Queen'\nGrelleth, her Majesty the Queen sniffs the air, 'My god, children what is the awful stench that has approached our throne!? This miserable pest couldn't be the dinner offering this silly expedition has brought us could it? Tell me pest, do you intend to put up a [fight] or are you a [willing sacrifice]?'\n_It is not advisable to offer a sacrifice:_\nYou say, 'I am a willing sacrifice'\nGrelleth, her Majesty the Queen claps her hands together cheerfully, 'Excellent!' She leans forward and cuts \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_'s head clean off!\nYOU were injured by a trap.\nYou have been knocked unconscious!\nYou died.\n_So, instead:_\nYou say, 'We want a fight'\nGrelleth, her Majesty the Queen recoils in confusion at your response, 'You enter my domain, threaten my babies and challenge me to battle? Who in the world do you think you are!? You... you miserable, greedy, insolent sack of revolting flesh! CHILDREN, OUR FEAST HAS ARRIVED!'\nGrelleth, her Majesty the Queen begins stomping the ground beneath her violently as she moves in to crush her next foe.\n_Grelleth goes aggro and remains aggro through the entire event, although she is permanently rooted for the time being. Note that she does not summon, so you can leave her be and stay outside her melee and spell range. From this point to her death, she casts these two spells (she will have other spells in her arsenal, later in the event):_\nExecution: Single Target, (-1200)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 12308 to 15385 (random)\nQueen's Swing: PB AE 100', (-1200)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 15385 to 16923 (random)\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 3077 to 3231 (random) per tick\n_Upon event trigger, 2x \"a palace guard\" spawn and attack. Kill them:_\na palace guard has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nThe palace guard begins squealing frantically as its blood pools on the floor.\nThe sleeping palace guards spring to their feet now that their companions have been slain.\n_Two more guards attack. Kill them, then DPS the Queen to 98% to spawn Turo._\n\n---\n\nDefeat Turo 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\n_Task Window Says:_ Turo the youngest and his horde of assassins is your first obstacle.\nGrelleth stomps her feet and begins shouting, 'Turo! Son!? Get out here now!' From the back of the room you hear the scraping of wood and the march of quiet footsteps.\n_Turo hits for a max ~13,000. He casts \"Crazy Blade\" on whoever is second highest on aggro (nuke up to 55,000 and 13,000 DOT for 3 ticks); AEs \"Smogscreen\" (200' range nuke for 20,000 + melee inhibitor for 3 ticks); casts \"Knife Whirl\" on random single target (nuke for 61,000); and casts \"Slick Toss\" on random single target (nuke for 65,000 + knockback + silence for 1 tick)._\nCrazy Blade: Single Target, (-10000)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 52308 to 55385 (random)\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 13847 per tick\nSmogscreen: PB AE 200', (-10000)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 15385 to 21539 (random)\n9: Decrease Accuracy by 75%\n10: Decrease Chance to Hit by 70% with All Skills\nKnife Whirl: Targeted AE 20', (-10000)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 60000 to 61539 (random)\nSlick Toss: Single Target, (-10000)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 65385\n2: Silence\n3: Amnesia (Silence vs Melee Effect)\n_He also spawns a single add (\"an assassin\") at 70% and 40%. These adds hit for a max ~10,000 and proc \"Diseased Blade\" on their tank (nuke for 21,000 hp + 13,000 hp/tick DOT for 3 ticks). If one of these adds is up for 90 seconds or longer, they buff themselves with \"Fear Shard Fury\" (increases their DPS)._\nDiseased Blade: Single Target, (-10000)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 15385 to 21539 (random)\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 12308 to 13846 (random) per tick\nFear Shard Fury: Self 0', Unresistable (0)\n3: Increase All Skills Damage Modifier by 35%\n4: Increase All Skills Minimum Damage Modifier by 115%\n_Kill Turo and his adds, and bring Grelleth to 87% to spawn Lelri and Lelro._\nan assassin has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nThe assassin says some rather nasty curse words before falling to the ground.\nTuro has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nTuro looks toward his mother and cries out for help before falling over dead.\n\n---\n\nDefeat Lelri and Lelro 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\n_Task Window Says:_ The twins Lelri and Lelro and their pet oashim are your next challenge.\nGrelleth roars, 'Lelro, Lelri! Mommy needs you. Come out here and rip these miserable intruders limb from limb!' From the back of the room you hear the scraping of wood and the slow drudging of footsteps.\n_Lelri and Lelro each hit for a max ~13,000. They must be kept balanced in health (within 20%) or they heal each other._\n_If they fall out of balance, you'll see an emote like this (and both will heal about 10%):_\nLelri looks fearfully at his brother and tosses him a potion of healing.\n_The twins also spawn waves of oashim adds (four at a time; fairly weak). You'll see this emote when they appear:_\nLoud squeaking begins echoing from every corner of the hall.\n_Note that when you kill one twin, the other one powers up:_\nEnraged by the death of his brother, Lelro begins swinging with reckless abandon.\n_Kill the twins and then bring Grelleth to 82% to spawn Wuran._\nan oashim swarmling has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nan oashim swarmling lets out a shrill squeak.\nLelri has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nLelri sighs in disappointment, 'At least I was mother's favorite!'\nLelro has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nLelro wipes the blood from his eyes, 'Wuran's gonna get you!' With that he falls to the ground and stops moving.\n\n---\n\nDefeat Wuran 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\nGrelleth calls out sweetly, 'Wuran, you've always been mommy's favorite. Come on out here and deal with these mean intruders for her!' A loud thud echoes off the door in the back of the room before it opens.\n_Wuran hits for a max ~13,000. He casts \"Rotting Flesh\" on a random target (a targeted AE, 15' range; 35 disease counters; nuke for 27,000 hp + 60-second melee slow + 3,000 hp DOT)._\n_He casts \"Touch of Decay\" on the tank (nuke for 32,000 hp + AC/stat/Aggro reduction + melee slow for 5 ticks)._\n_Also, every 30-40 seconds, he buffs Grelleth with \"Boon of Decay\" (increases her damage output for 6 ticks)._\nRotting Flesh: Targeted AE 15', Disease (-1000)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 23077 to 27692 (random)\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 2000 to 3077 (random) per tick\n3: Increase Disease Counter by 35\n4: Inhibit Melee Attacks by (25%)\nTouch of Decay: Single Target, Disease (-10000)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 30769 to 32308 (random)\n4: Inhibit Melee Attacks by (15%)\n9: Decrease Stats by 600\n10: Unknown #416 (100/-1300/0)\n11: Decrease Agro Multiplier by 20%\nBoon of Decay: Single Target, Unresistable (0)\n3: Increase All Skills Damage Modifier by 35%\n4: Increase All Skills Minimum Damage Modifier by 120%\n_Wuran spawns an add (\"a priest of decay\") at 70% and 40%. Adds hit for a max ~10,000. They cast \"Stench of Decay\" on a random single target (targeted 10' range AE; 30 disease counters; DOT for 5,000 hp + melee slow + casting level decrease for 90 seconds)._\nStench of Decay: Targeted AE 10', Disease (-10000)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 5385 per tick\n2: Increase Disease Counter by 30\n4: Inhibit Melee Attacks by (20%)\n9: Decrease Stats by 400\n10: Decrease Effective Casting Level by 20\n11: Negate Spell Mana Cost Effect\n_Kill Wuran and his adds, then bring Grelleth to 72% to spawn Zurel._\na priest of decay has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\na priest of decay begins deteriorating at an alarming rate.\nWuran has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nWuran stumbles back on his broken legs, 'Mom! MOM! MOMMY!'\n\n---\n\nDefeat Zurel 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\n_Task Window Says:_ Zurel is the apple of her mother's eye and also the most dangerous child of the royal family.\nGrelleth sighs and confesses, 'I guess I should have raised these miserable leeches to fight better.' She then raises her hand to her mouth and calls out, 'Zuuuuuuurel! Mommy could really use your help about now!' An unnerving female roar booms out through the hall after Grelleth's request.\n_Zurel hits for a max ~13,000. She casts \"Axe Spin\" (PB AE 80' range nuke for 33,000 + knockback); \"Axe Blade\" on random single target (nuke for 41,000 + AC reduction); and \"Grapple Chain\" on second-highest on aggro (pull effect)._\nAxe Spin: PB AE 80', (-10000)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 30308 to 33231 (random)\n2: Knockback (2) and Toss Up (2)\nAxe Blade: Single Target, (-10000)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 41539\n10: Decrease AC by 600\n11: Negate AC Limit Modifier Effect\nGrapple Chain: Targeted AE 10', (-10000)\n2: Slow Push (-200)\n_She spawns an add (\"an elite soldier\") at 70% and 40%. These adds cast \"Wild Swing\" (PBAE 40' range nuke for 28,000) and buff themselves with \"Ignore Pain\" when low in health (reduces damage taken)._\nWild Swing: PB AE 40', (-1000)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 27693 to 28462 (random)\n_Kill Zurel and her adds, then bring Grelleth to 62% to spawn Kotul._\nan elite soldier has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nan elite soldier writhes around as if it were still fighting.\nZurel has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nZurel glares at you defiantly before drawing her axe across her own throat.\n\n---\n\nDefeat Kotul 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\n_Task Window Says:_ Kotul the brilliant, exercise caution when doing battle with him.\nGrelleth looks panicked as she yells, 'K..Kotul? Are you still there son?'An ominous silence follows her words as the door opens and a cloaked swinetor makes its way into the hall.\n_Kotul hits for a max ~13,000 and flurries. Every 30-40 seconds, he buffs Grelleth with \"Boon of Decay\" (increases her damage output for 6 ticks; the same buff Wuran cast earlier)._\n_Kotul spawns undead versions of the previous mini bosses:_\n92% (Turo)\n82% (Lelri and Lelro)\n72% (Wuran)\n62% (Zurel)\n_These are weaker versions (hit for slightly less and have less hitpoints), but they retain their earlier abilities, spells, and mechanics._\n_At 92%:_\nKotul extends his forked spear into the ground and rakes together some fresh body parts. He waves his hand over them and shouts, 'Arise little brother, mother said your work is not yet done!'\nTuro`s Remains lumbers awkwardly toward \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.\nTuro`s Remains has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nTuro`s Remains crumbles to pieces.\nKotul shouts, 'Turo you worthless sack of vomitous refuse! I hope your afterlife is spent over a campfire spit!'\n_At 82%:_\nKotul grabs an armful of bones and a few hunks of flesh and throws them on the ground. His incantation seems terribly informal, 'Lelri, Lelro... Dinner's ready!'\nLelro`s Remains lumbers awkwardly toward \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.\nLelri`s Remains lumbers awkwardly toward \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.\nLelro`s Remains has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nLelro`s Remains falls to the ground.\nLelri`s Remains has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nLelri`s Remains falls to the ground.\nKotul growls, 'You idiots! I thought between the two of you, you would manage to come up with half a brain's worth of strategy here! Mother should have had you executed at birth in the same fashion as your dimwitted father!'\n_At 72%:_\nKotul frowns as he picks up half of a freshly severed Swinetor head. He sighs, 'Well Wuran, you're at least easier to deal with than your portly sister.' He kicks the repulsive hunk of flesh through the dirt and a skeleton forms underneath it.\nWuran`s Remains lumbers awkwardly toward \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.\nWuran`s Remains has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nWuran`s Remains breaks apart.\nKotul lets out a surprisingly loud sigh, 'I should have smothered you before your first birthday, Wuran...'\n_At 62%:_\nKotul bends down and picks up a dripping hunk of flesh. He begins to retch when he realizes it's his sister's leg. He throws the blubbery meat against the wall and a skeleton forms around it.\nZurel`s Remains lumbers awkwardly toward \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.\nZurel`s Remains has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nZurel`s Remains begins oozing putrid liquids.\nKotul roars, 'Fine! If my worthless siblings can offer us no assistance then I guess it's up to me to protect you mom!'\n_Kill all the adds to unlock Kotul's health. Kill Kotul, then move on to Grelleth._\nKotul has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nKotul looks back at his mother one last time before his skin begins melting off his body. All that is left of the necromancer after a few seconds is a mass of congealed entrails.\n_NOTE: Kotul's death locks the task._\n\n---\n\nDefeat Grelleth 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\nDefeat all of Grelleth's remaining minions 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\n_Task Window Says:_ Now that you have put an end to her children, Grelleth is ready to give you the privilege of battle! Defeat Grelleth and all her remaining reinforcements.\n_At 52% health, Grelleth becomes unrooted:_\nGrelleth snarls and grinds her teeth, 'Very well, it is time to show you how I earned this crown!' She tosses her hand-axes to the ground and takes hold of a mightier weapon.\nYour allies look toward the newly empowered queen and make a dash for the door!\n_She gains an ability called \"Fearsome Bellow\" (targeted 30' range AE; nuke for 40,000 hp + stat decrease for 8 ticks):_\nFearsome Bellow: Targeted AE 30', Unresistable (-10000)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 39562\n9: Decrease Stats by 100\n_This AE is preceded by an emote (occurs every 90 seconds; flashes up on screen and in text):_\nGrelleth prepares to strike \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ with a powerful attack! Someone else should take her attention.\n_When you see this emote, you have 15 seconds to switch tanks. Once you switch tanks, you'll see this:_\nGrelleth, her Majesty the Queen is forced to turn to a new target!\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ suddenly has someone's complete attention.\n_You still need the new tank to keep aggro, however, because she will still perform a \"check\" at the end of 15 seconds. If her target is different from whoever was tanking at the original emote, you'll see this success emote (flashes on screen):_\nGrelleth has lost her focus on \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.\n_At this point, it's safe for the original tank to take aggro again._\n_If you fail to do the tank switch, you will see this:_\nGrelleth unleashes a powerful attack on \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nGrelleth, her Majesty the Queen drives her foot through her victim's skull leaving nothing but a pulpy mass.\n_...And she casts \"Fearsome Bellow\" (each time she manages to cast this, she also increases her damage output by 10%._\n_In addition to all of the above, she also spawns two health-based adds: 1x \"a reanimated servant\" at 21% and 19% health (these adds are mezzable)._\n_NOTE: If you wipe out, the event does not reset. The Queen does, however, regenerate to 100% and retains the abilities she had at whatever health you left her at (so, if you wipe out at 30%, she will regenerate to 100%, but will be unrooted, summon, and will do the tank emote from the start). Any adds you have already killed will not respawn. Any adds that were alive at the time of the wipeout will remain up (they are NOT auto-aggro, so you can CR in the zone)._\n_Kill the Queen along with all adds to win the event._\nGrelleth, her Majesty the Queen has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nGrelleth, her Majesty the Queen falls to the floor with clenched fists. She looks around the room at the remains of her brood before whispering, 'My beautiful babies, how could this have happened?' Her eyes close and after a few heavy heaves her breath ceases.\nFrom the back of the room you hear the familiar sound of scraping wood. The inner sanctum door opens revealing a massive pile of refuse with a few shiny objects sticking out of it. You are now welcome to claim your... 'prizes'.\n\n---\n\nClaim your rewards from Grelleth's pile of refuse 0/1 (Grelleth's Palace)\n_Task Window Says:_ The door in the back of the hall has opened revealing a pile of refuse with a few shiny treasures sticking out of it. Go claim your rewards!\nYou sift through the pile of putrid waste to find a few articles of treasure. Thoughts of your latest conquest are fresh in mind as you begin to wonder how it was the great 'queen' was so easily defeated. The dread fear that this victory may have been nothing but a hollow illusion and that the real queen may be safely residing in another castle of filth sets upon you... but you are happy enough to claim the spoils of this charade and be on your way.\n_Rewards:_\n225 platinum\nExperience\n_Possible Chest Loot (1 Item + 1 Dreadmote per task)_\nBloodstained Neckguard\nCloak of Champions\nComponent Shoulders\nCooling Pad\nCrystalized Scream\nFilth-Covered Shiv\nHammer of the War Machine\nIceblade Knuckles\nInfused Thread\nWar Weilded Grotesque\nMedian Dreadmote\nGreater Dreadmote\nGlowing Dreadmote\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n**Extra Stuff: Your Allies**\n_In addition to the Queen and her many adds, you'll also see a few expedition members in the zone. While not a whole lot of practical help, you will have some moral support from them as they assist you in attacking._\n_These NPCs are not a part of the task's progression. You don't have to interact with them, and whether they survive or retreat, has no bearing on the task's outcome._\n**Reena Kedson**\nYou say, 'Hail, Reena Kedson'\nReena Kedson says 'It is a shame it has come to this.'\n_When aggro'd:_ Reena Kedson holds her nose as she charges into the fray.\n_When retreating:_ Reena Kedson strains her voice to shout above the din of battle, 'It must be the stench that's getting to me. I must retreat for now.'\n**Ain Kavus**\nYou say, 'Hail, Ain Kavus'\nAin Kavus smiles, '\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_! You're not a moment too soon! The wretched fiend has shown her disgusting face but refuses to give us the pleasure of battle without what she calls 'a proper feast' present.'\n_When aggro'd:_ Ain Kavus points its blade toward its next foe.\n_When retreating:_ Ain Kavus staggers back and shouts, 'Strike at these swine with all the fervor within you! I must make my leave.'\n**Sherri Ganes**\nYou say, 'Hail, Sherri Ganes'\nSherri Ganes snarls angrily, 'Wretched pigs don't even have the decency to die quiet! Go let 'er know it's time for us to eat bacon!'\n_When aggro'd:_ Sherri Ganes grins from ear to ear as she dives into the fight.\n_When retreating:_ Sherri Ganes coughs up a bit of blood as she staggers toward the exit. She calls back to you with a rather confident boast, 'Little piggies make the best bacon. Bring me what's left of their carcasses when you're done here!'\n**Relco Finn**\nYou say, 'Hail, Relco Finn'\nRelco Finn stands at attention and salutes you crisply, 'Right on time, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_! Our remaining allies are up ahead in a standoff with the trash queen. Should you need to make a hasty retreat just use the door behind you there.' The halfling points at the rickety wooden door.\n_When aggro'd:_ Relco Finn sighs loudly before charging into battle.\n_When retreating:_ Relco Finn grabs his arm and sighs as he begins limping away from the battle, 'Looks like you'll have to win this one without me.'",
