      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Evantil, the Vile Oak [zone=873]\n**Who:**\n- Aranu [ _Quest_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Delicate Pearlescent Growth [item=108532]\n- Fearbreeder Offspring Stomach [item=107905]\n- Grimy Pearlescent Growth [item=108506]\n- Large Pearlescent Growth [item=108502]\n- Oddly Shaped Pearlescent Growth [item=108503]\n- Slimy Pearlescent Growth [item=108505]\n- Small Pearlescent Growth [item=108504]\n- Swirled Pearlescent Growth [item=108501]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a gibbering breeder offspring [npc=42204]\n- a gibbering fear breeder [npc=42205]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 29 09:24:02 2012\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is a solo task begins with Aranu ( map) in Evantil, the Vile Oak. This is an Alaran located at 120, 440, 15 (at the base of the tree, west-central side)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- No tasks\nYou say, 'Hail, Aranu'\nAranu says, in Alaran, 'Hello, wanderer. Stay your weapons; I have no interest in harming you. I have come here to try to find a cure for the horrible effects the fear fruit are having on my people. I believe I just might have [found something] that may work.'\nYou say, 'You found something?'\nAranu says, in Alaran, 'The evil magic that leaks into the surrounding land from the vile oak has produced some horrible mutations in the creatures that live here. The strangest has to be the gibbering fear breeder. It is an elusive creature whose offspring look nothing like the adults at all. In fact, they look very similar to small eyeballs. I assume this is to try to scare off any predators that would try to eat them; not that their adult form is any more pleasing. Inside of the stomachs of these offspring is something [wonderful].'\nYou say, 'What was wonderful?'\nAranu says, in Alaran, 'While the offspring of the gibbering fear breeder are still young and in eyeball form, pearl-like growths are formed within their stomachs. There are many different types of these growths and I have found that when ground into powder form, they can offer some temporary relief from the addictive fear fruit. I need more samples however. Can you [help] me? Perhaps if I can get enough samples, I can create a more long lasting form of relief from the effects of the fear fruit.'\nYou say, 'I will help'\nAranu says, in Alaran, 'Thank you. Your kindness will not be forgotten. Collect [fearbreeder offspring stomachs] from fearbreeder offspring and return them to me. I have become quite adept at scraping the growths from the stomachs without damaging them.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Strong Stomachs Needed'.\nAranu needs you to collect some fearbreeder stomachs so that the valuable, pearl-like growths that form inside their stomachs can be extracted to help make a substance that can help provide relief from the effects of the fear fruits.\nKill gibbering offspring breeders or gibbering fear breeders and give the fearbreeder offspring stomachs to Aranu. Aranu can extract the growths from the stomachs for you. You will need to collect some swirled pearlescent growths, large pearlescent growths, oddly shaped pearlescent growths, small pearlescent growths, delicate pearlescent growths, slimy pearlescent growths, and grimy pearlescent growths.\n\n---\n\nCollect some swirled pearlescent growths 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nCollect some large pearlescent growths 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nCollect some oddly shaped pearlescent growths 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nCollect some small pearlescent growths 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nCollect some delicate pearlescent growths 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nCollect some slimy pearlescent growths 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nCollect some grimy pearlescent growths 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_Kill gibbering fear breeders (both adults or offsprings will do) and collect Fearbreeder Offspring Stomachs. Give a stomach to Aranu, and in return, he'll give you a random Pearlescent Growth. Turn in the Growth to update the task._\nGive the swirled pearlescent growths to Aranu 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nGive the large pearlescent growths to Aranu 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nGive the oddly shaped pearlescent growths to Aranu 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nGive the small pearlescent growths to Aranu 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nGive the delicate pearlescent growths to Aranu 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nGive the slimy pearlescent growths to Aranu 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nGive the grimy pearlescent growths to Aranu 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nSpeak with Aranu 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_Rewards:_\n375 platinum\nExperience (5 AAs)",
    },
    {
      id = "6147",
      title = "A Feat of Drunken Strength",
      exp = "19",
      exp_name = "Rain of Fear",
      min_lvl = 1,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "",
      repeatable = false,
      group_size = "",
      npc = "Gimthra",
      loc = { y = -185.0, x = 345.0, z = 20.0 },
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Gimthra",
        "Dragons...",
        "What treasure?",
        "What about the weird bugs?",
        "Wimpy druids?",
        "Cut that tree down?",
        "An axe?",
        "dragons",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "the materials to Gimthra 0/1 (Evantil", count = 1 },
        { name = "the snake and the flower to Gimthra 0/1 (Evantil", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Evantil, the Vile Oak [zone=873]\n**Who:**\n- Gimthra [npc=41345]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Anorak [npc=42232]\n- a corrupted sapling [npc=42192]\n- a fear blossom [npc=42195]\n- a frightening fear blossom [npc=42201]\n- a hungry binaesa [npc=42208]\n- a hungry fear blossom [npc=42209]\n- a tainted sapling [npc=42221]\n- a tree binaesa [npc=42222]\n- a wandering sapling [npc=42225]\n- an arboreal binaesa [npc=42230]\n- living sap [npc=42233]\n- oozing sap [npc=42234]\n- vile sap [npc=42235]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 29 09:24:07 2012\nModified: Fri Jan 31 10:25:07 2025 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is a solo task that begins with Gimthra ( map) in Evantil, the Vile Oak. She is found at -185, 345, 20. This is at the very base of the tree (southwest corner, on the inside of the \"gorge\" that surrounds the tree's south side)_\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- No tasks\nYou say, 'Hail, Gimthra'\nGimthra tips her mug to the sky and chugs. After a few seconds, she carelessly tosses the metal tankard to the ground and wipes the dripping foam from her lips with her arm. She reeks of beer as she looks up at you and grins. 'You here for the [dragons]?'\nYou say, 'Dragons...'\nGimthra doesn't wait for your response. She cuts you off and starts walking around you in a wide, wobbly circle, waving her arms while she rants, 'Yeah, they told me there'd be dragons here too!' Gimthra starts pantomiming her descriptions as she continues, 'Giant, scaly beasts with big wings, twenty rows of teeth, and at least fifty-foot torch radius on the flames it can shoot from its mouth. I came here for dragons, I came here for [treasure], I came here for glory! Instead I get a bunch of [weird bugs]. No thanks.\nYou say, 'What treasure?'\nGimthra's eyes darken and she tears off her bracer and throws it as far as she can, 'Dragon treasure! I was told there would be mountains of treasure the size of...' Gimthra's voice trails off as she loses focus and struggles to think, '...well, mountains, I guess. Lots of mountains of treasure!' Gimthra's eyes light up and she stumbles towards you. 'Can you imagine if there were mountains of treasure here? Those [wimpy druids] told me there was never any treasure here. You think they're hiding it?'\nYou say, 'What about the weird bugs?'\nGimthra laughs and puts her arm around your shoulder, 'Well, all bugs are kind of weird, you know? But these bugs are, uh, extra weird. There's like all-white snakes and some wolves made out of trees or something and, oh, there's these little floating eyeballs that are super weird!' Gimthra holds you at arm's distance, steadying herself by holding onto you, and looks you in the eyes, 'How have you not seen these, Gnome? They're like everywhere. You've seen those [wimpy druids] at least, right? I hope I'm not hallucinating all this.'\nYou say, 'Wimpy druids?'\nGimthra picks up her tankard and fills it with beer at the nearest keg while she talks, 'They're just to the east near the base of this big tree. But there's not much use talking to them. All they care about is that stupid tree. They think it's such a big deal.' Gimthra takes on a mocking tone as she mimics the druids, 'Stop hassling us about dragons and treasure, Gimthra. Go away so we can hug our tree, Gimthra.' She spits out some beer on the ground and takes another swig before looking back at you, 'I mean, come on! The tree isn't even that big! I could totally [cut that tree down] in like two chops of an axe.'\nYou say, 'Cut that tree down?'\nGimthra jumps at you and puts her finger in your chest while shouting at you with her beer-heavy breath, 'What? You don't think I can't do it? You don't think I can cut down this little wimpy tree? I've cut down trees twice its size without breaking a sweat. I'll do it right now, I'll prove it to you. Go get me an [axe]!'\nYou say, 'An axe?'\nGimthra says 'Yeah, an axe, dummy. Does it look like I'm carrying an axe big enough to chop down this tree? Go get me some piles of scrap metal and wood. I'll make the axe myself and then chop this tree down, dwarf-style.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'A Feat of Drunken Strength'.\nYou met a drunk dwarf who insists she can cut down the massive tree that sits in the middle of the region. You don't see any way that she could possibly succeed, but it might be entertaining to watch her try.\nShe challenged you to bring her wood from the treants that wander around the outskirts of the area so she can build an axe. She'll also need some metal scraps. You can find them suspended inside saps and oozelings around outcroppings close to the tree.\n\n---\n\nCollect pieces of wood from treants 0/5 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nCollect metal scraps from saps 0/3 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_Treants are all over the outer area of the zone. Oozes are in the chasm and top-side as well._\nGive the materials to Gimthra 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_Hail her and follow through dialogue, then say \"a pet snake\" for the update._\nFind a pretty flower 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_These are the flower mobs that are found wandering about the same area. There is no item involved here. It's a random update on kills._\nSteal an animal trap from the wretched living in the tree 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_Go up the ramp that leads into the tree entrance (the ramp is southeast of Gimthra's camp, nearby the main cluster of quest NPCs). The animal trap is a ground spawn next to the Alaran at the top of this ramp (in the first room). It's along the wall and is bright orange in appearance. (-225, -95, 241)_\nFight a snake until it passes out, then throw the trap on it while it's unconscious 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_Fight snakes until you get a proper update message._\nGive the snake and the flower to Gimthra 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\nAsk the gnome nearby for help 0/1 (Evantil, the Vile Oak)\n_Hail Anorak ( map), who stands nearby._\n_Rewards:_\n262 platinum, 5 gold\nExperience (3 AAs)",
    },
