      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Breeding Grounds [zone=871]\n**Who:**\n- Kesar [npc=41339]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Chetari Brain [item=107990]\n- Pickle Juice [item=108190]\n- Pickled Chetari Brain [item=108189]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a Chetari deathbender [npc=42154]\n- a Chetari hoarder [npc=42156]\n- a Chetari scavenger [npc=42157]\n- a Chetari seeker [npc=42158]\n- a young dragon [npc=42178]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 29 09:34:56 2012\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is a shared task (1-6 players) that begins with Kesar ( map) at the zone-in of the Breeding Grounds (-20, 0, 4)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- No tasks\nYou say, 'Hail, Kesar'\nKesar says 'Hello. Care to take a shot at [training] a dragon? It is both rewarding and terrifying at the same time!'\nYou say, 'Training?'\nKesar says 'Don't worry; it's not that difficult. Are you [interested]?'\nYou say, 'I'm interested'\nKesar says 'Excellent! First thing we will need to do is get some treats for the young dragons. You can't teach them if they aren't motivated. Take this pickle juice and collect some chetari brains. Place a chetari brain inside the pickle juice to make a pickled chetari brain. The dragons here just love them. If you need [more pickle juice] just let me know.'\n_You receive \"Pickle Juice\" (single-slot container)._\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Dragon Whisperer'.\nKesar has offered you the chance of learning the basics of training dragons.\n\n---\n\nKill chetari and collect their brains 0/4 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Brains can drop from four types of Chetaris:_\na Chetari deathbender\na Chetari hoarder\na Chetari scavenger\na Chetari seeker\n_Once looted, combine them one at a time in the \"Pickle Juice\" container to produce \"A Pickled Chetari Brain\"._\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Kesar 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nYou say, 'Hail, Kesar'\nKesar says 'Did you make some pickled chetari brains? I hope so. Approach one of the three young dragons that are not being trained at the moment and give them a pickled chetari brain to continue.'\nGive a young dragon a Pickled Chetari Brain 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nTeach a young dragon to sit 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Target the young dragon next to Kesar and tell it to \"sit\" (you may need to repeat this a few times)._\nGive a young dragon a Pickled Chetari Brain 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nTeach a young dragon to stand 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Target the young dragon next to Kesar and tell it to \"stand\" (you may need to repeat this a few times)._\nGive a young dragon a Pickled Chetari Brain 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nTeach a young dragon to play dead 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Target the young dragon next to Kesar and tell it to \"play dead\" (you may need to repeat this a few times)._\nGive a young dragon a Pickled Chetari Brain 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nTeach a young dragon to NOT breathe fire 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Target the young dragon next to Kesar and say to it \"do not breathe fire\" (you may need to repeat this a few times)._\n_Your exchange might look something like this:_\nYou say, 'Sit'\nThe young dragon sits down. You have successfully taught the young to sit!\nYou say, 'Stand'\nThe young dragon sits down. You have failed to teach the dragon to stand up. Try again!\nYou say, 'Stand'\nThe young dragon breathes fire. You have failed to teach the dragon to stand up. Try again!\nYou say, 'Stand'\nThe young dragon stands up. You have successfully taught the young to stand up!\nYou say, 'Play dead'\nThe young dragon plays dead. You have successfully taught the young to play dead!\nYou say, 'Do NOT breathe fire'\nThe young dragon breathes fire. You have failed to teach the dragon to not breathe fire. Try again!\nYou say, 'Do NOT breathe fire'\nThe young dragon does not breathe fire. You have successfully taught the young to not breathe fire!\nSpeak with Kesar 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Once done, hail Kesar._\nYou say, 'Hail, Kesar'\nKesar says 'I was watching how you handled the dragons. Not too shabby for a first time dragon trainer. A living dragon trainer is a successful dragon trainer as they say. You are by no means a master dragon trainer yet, but you at least know the basics now. Please take this for your hard work.'\n_Rewards:_\n187 platinum, 5 gold\nExperience (2 AAs + 1-2% exp in Level 96)",
    },
