      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Breeding Grounds [zone=871]\n**Who:**\n- Asupi Muksap [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Fear Fungi [item=106597]\n- Tainted Dragon Flesh [item=109024]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a pile of dragon bones [npc=42173]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 29 09:35:01 2012\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is a solo task that begins with Asupi Muksap ( map) in the Breeding Grounds. He is located around 200, -350, -99 (from the zone-in area, head east into the narrow tunnels and to the northwestern-most room in those tunnels)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- No tasks\nYou say, 'Hail, Asupi Muksap'\nAsupi Muksap's whiskers twitch as he speaks to you with a surprising command of the common tongue, 'Hail to you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Tell me, do you have a discerning [palette]?\nYou say, 'Palette?'\nAsupi Muksap says 'While the Paebala and [Chetari] share somewhat of the same diet, our tastes are much more refined than our primitive counterparts. They choose to feed off the rancid corpses of dragons, while we prefer to feast on finer [delicacies].'\nYou say, 'What about the Chetari?'\nAsupi Muksap's eyes squint as his voice drops to a more serious tone, 'Chetari are the filthy ratmen that followed us here from the Necropolis. They breed like rabbits, polluting any area they inhabit. Those mindless scavengers already outnumber the Paebala, and will soon deplete the [food supply] with their insatiable appetite for decomposing dragon flesh.\nYou say, 'Food supply?'\nAsupi Muksap says 'Unlike Dragon Necropolis, this cavern breathes new life rather than constant death. We must sustain ourselves on the flesh of dragons, but a dragon corpse is often hard to come by. We are few, and they are many, which is why the Paebala look for [allies] in adventurers like you. Someone with your skills can bring those large beasts to the ground, take their spoils, and leave the corpse for us to feed on.'\nYou say, 'What allies?'\nAsupi Muksap says 'A true ally would [help] us get rid of the Chetari. I can say with certainty that Norrath would be better off without them. Of course I don't expect you to get your hands dirty...' The ratman flashes a quick smile, revealing tiny, pointed teeth. 'The Chetari's insatiable hunger will be the cause of their demise. You will simply lead them to it.'\nYou say, 'I will help'\nAsupi Muksap nods in approval, and begins to disclose his plan, 'The best way to quietly reduce the Chetari population is to poison their food supply, but it's not as simple as pouring poison into their food. The scavengers will be able to detect any additives to their food, so we need to start at the [source].'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Poisoning the Food Supply'.\nAsupi Muksap has asked you to help poison the Chetari's food supply. Asupi needs a few ingredients before he can mix the poison.\nYou say, 'Tell me about the source'\nAsupi Muksap continues, 'If you can poison the dragons before you kill them, then the meat that clings to their bones will also be tainted, but undetectable to the Chetari. I have the formula for the poison all figured out, I just need you to collect the ingredients. Fear Fungi grows in warm spots within the caverns. You can scrape volcanic ash from the wings of lava dragons. Once you have the required items, return to me and I will coat your weapons in poison.'\n\n---\n\nPick Fear Fungi from around the caverns 0/4 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_These are ground spawns from \"warm spots\" around the caverns._\nRecover volcanic ash from the wings of lava dragons 0/4 (The Breeding Grounds)\nDeliver the Fear Fungi to Asupi 0/4 (The Breeding Grounds)\nSpeak to Asupi 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nYou say, 'Hail, Asupi Muksap'\nAsupi Muksap begins to cast a spell.\nYour weapon is coated in poison.\nAsupi Muksap takes the items from you and begins to mix them together into a thick liquid that he then drips over your weapons. 'Be careful not to get any of this on your skin. It could have some negative side effects... Other than that, as long as your weapon remains coated, you should be able to poison any large, non-lava dragon you fight.'\nLoot Tainted Dragon Flesh from the corpse of a sickly dragon 0/2 (The Breeding Grounds)\nKill any two regular fear or ice dragons while you have the poison buff on you. This turns the dragon green and indicates that they are poisoned. Kill and loot from corpses.\nPlace the Tainted Dragon Flesh inside a pile of dragon bones 0/2 (The Breeding Grounds)\nThe piles of dragon bones are found throughout the Chetari tunnels (you'll probably need to clear the room first).\nReturn to Asupi 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nYou say, 'Hail, Asupi Muksap'\nAsupi Muksap's lips curl up into a mischievous grin. 'So the deed is done? Good, good. I'm sure those filthy Chetari will devour every last morsel of that tainted meat! You've helped more than you know.'\nYou have helped Asupi reduce the Chetari population by poisoning their food supply.\n_Rewards:_\n225 platinum\nExperience (3 AAs)",
    },
