      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Breeding Grounds [zone=871]\n**Who:**\n- Shamptan the summoner [npc=41341]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a dragon egg [npc=42160]\n- a fearwing hunter [npc=42777]\n- a phase spider [npc=42172]\n- a young ashwing [npc=42177]\n- a young fearwing [npc=42179]\n- a young flamewing [npc=42180]\n- a young icewing [npc=42181]\n- a young scalewing [npc=42182]\n- an elder fearwing [npc=42186]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 29 09:35:04 2012\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is a solo task that begins with Shamptan the Summoner ( map) in the Breeding Grounds at location 1175, 185, -39 (in the archway that opens up into the northern-most part of the zone)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- No tasks\nYou say, 'Hail, Shamptan the summoner'\nShamptan the summoner's bones rattle as they move, suspended in the air in the shape of a dragon. It turns its empty eye sockets to you and speaks without moving its jaw, 'These [new] black dragons shouldn't be here. Just like [you].'\nYou say, 'What new dragons?'\nShamptan the summoner says 'For countless years, our kind has used this mausoleum as a final resting place, a proper closing to the long chapters of dragon life. The flamewings, the icewings, they've earned their place here. But this [dark brood] are interlopers, assaulting our sacred grounds and feeding on the energies of our dead. This is not right, it must be [dealt with].'\nYou say, 'What do you mean, you?'\nShamptan the summoner says 'Me? I've been here since the beginning, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, and I earned my rest. But it is my job to keep guard over this masoleum and I will not stand idly by while these [usurpers] vandalize our home.'\nYou say, 'Usurpers?'\nShamptan the summoner says 'For countless years, our kind has used this mausoleum as a final resting place, a proper closing to the long chapters of dragon life. The flamewings, the icewings, they've earned their place here. But this [dark brood] are interlopers, assaulting our sacred grounds and feeding on the energies of our dead. This is not right, it must be [dealt with].'\nYou say, 'Dealt with?'\nShamptan the summoner says 'The dragons that created this masoleum were wise. They knew we would eventually be discovered here and they ensured [safety measures] were in place to protect it.'\nYou say, 'What safety measures?'\nShamptan the summoner says 'Ancient guardian dragons can be summoned to cleanse the mausoleum in times of trouble. I will need your [help], however, as I cannot move if I want to [remain unseen].'\nYou say, 'Dark brood?'\nShamptan the summoner says 'I don't know where they came from, and I don't care. They must be [eliminated].'\nYou say, 'Eliminated?'\nShamptan the summoner says 'The dragons that created this masoleum were wise. They knew we would eventually be discovered here and they ensured [safety measures] were in place to protect it.'\nYou say, 'Remain unseen?'\nShamptan the summoner says 'Inside this rune circle, I'm able to reveal myself to whoever I please. Outside of it, though, I'd be immediately spotted, and no doubt killed by the fearwings. Now, will you [help] me?'\nYou say, 'I will help'\nShamptan the summoner says 'Good. I'm sure the medallion we need is in one of the treasure piles around the center pillar of this room. Search the bins filled with gold until you find a medallion with a white crystal in it. '\nYou have been assigned the task 'A Desperate Summoning'.\nThe dragon mausoleum has been overrun by a corrupted brood of dragons called the fearwings. You found an animated dragon skeleton that claims to know a way to summon ancient guardians to cleanse the dragons' resting place.\n\n---\n\nFind the amulet 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Task Window Says:_ Search the treasure piles around the pillar in the center of the room for a crystal amulet.\n_North of Shamptan, around the pillar in the center, are boxes of treasure. Click on them until you get an update and emote._\nA chill runs up your arm as your fingers grip the amulet at the bottom of the bag and pull it out.\nAsk Shamptan what to do with the amulet 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nYou say, 'Hail, Shamptan the summoner'\nShamptan the summoner says 'I'm glad you found it so quickly. Now, hold the amulet out and I will prepare it.' A soft glowing light begins to pulsate inside the amulets crystal when you hold it out. 'The first part of the summoning ritual is [unsavory]. But it is important. You must [promise] me that you do it.'\nYou say, 'I promise...'\nShamptan the summoner says 'The amulet must be powered with the essence of youth from all four dragon broods. You must find a young ashwing, scalewing, flamewing, and icewing, [kill them], and absorb their power into the amulet.'\nYou say, 'Unsavory?'\nShamptan the summoner says 'The dragons wanted to ensure that this summoning would not be pursued lightly, so they placed a heavy price on it: a sacrifice of [their young].'\nYou say, 'Their young?'\nShamptan the summoner says 'The amulet must be powered with the essence of youth from all four dragon broods. You must find a young ashwing, scalewing, flamewing, and icewing, [kill them], and absorb their power into the amulet.'\nYou say, 'Kill them?'\nShamptan the summoner says 'It's not pleasant business, but someone must do it. To save the others.'\nEssence of a young flamewing absorbed 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nEssence of a young ashwing absorbed 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nEssence of a young icewing absorbed 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nEssence of a young scalewing absorbed 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Task Window Says:_ Take the empowered amulet and absorb the essence from each of the four broods. Find a young flamewing near the mausoleum and kill it to absorb its essence. Kill a young ashwing near the mausoleum to absorb its essence into the amulet. Kill a young icewing in the egg chamber to the west and absorb its essence into the amulet. Kill a young scalewing in the icy egg chamber and absorb its essence into the amulet. You may need to step on the eggs to lure the young out of hiding.\n_Note: The \"young\" spawns can be triggered in the \"egg\" rooms in the different parts of the zone. Upon triggering a spawn, you get two mobs which auto-aggro (even through invis)._\nBring the empowered amulet back to Shamptan the Summoner 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nKill a young fearwing in the mausoleum 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_Fearwings are found in the same area as the treasure updates earlier._\nKill a phase spider in the north tunnels 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\n_These are found in the tunnels extending from the treasure room._\nKill the elder fearwing guarding the dragon statue 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nPlace the amulet on the dragon statue 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nWhen you do this, you see the following in yellow:\nThe amulet fits into the round indentation at the top of the dragon statue. A dark beam shoots out from the front of it and a large, black dragon appears in the sky.\nInstead of a guardian, a massive fearwing dragon is summoned by the amulet. It flickers, seeming to shift in and out of existence as it looks down around the room with an evil glint in its eye. After a brief moment it bares its massive teeth and grunts, 'Fear this day, pathetic dragons of Norrath. The fearwings have come to undo you.'\nThe massive dragon laughs as it phases out of this plane and begins its genocidal hunt.\nFind Shamptan 0/1 (The Breeding Grounds)\nShamptan the summoner has slipped into the shadows without a trace. Without him, you have no idea how to stop the Fearwing Hunter before it can terrorize the dragons that call this home.\n_Shamptan the Summoner disappears, and this task is not repeatable._\n_Rewards:_\n337 platinum, 5 gold\nExperience (4 AAs)\n- Dark Invocation [item=57429]",
