      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Bixie Warfront [zone=941]\n**Who:**\n- Frislo [npc=44041]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Related Zones:**\n- Bixie Warfront: Saving Jacyll [zone=949]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Frislo [npc=45118]\n- General Vaxa [npc=45122]\n- Honeycomb Chest [npc=44823]\n- Jacyll [npc=45119]\n- Lieutenant Drix [npc=45123]\n- Lieutenant Vyzik [npc=45124]\n- Lieutenant Zizzix [npc=45125]\n- Pelzia the Crazed [npc=45120]\n- Warchanter Neezzee [npc=45121]\n- a glass wall [npc=45117]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Raid Expedition: Saving Jacyll [quest=7262]\n- The Bixies of War [quest=7260]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Oct 8 05:54:34 2013\nModified: Sat Sep 27 08:15:42 2025 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\nThis group mission begins with Frislo [npc=44041] ( **click for map image**) in the Bixie Warfront. He is a drakkin found in the Queen's Wet River bixie camp (from the Ethernere portal stone, head east up the ramp and just follow the ramp until you come to the queen's camp).\nPre-Requisites for Requesting:\n\\- Level 95\n\\- Completed The Bixies of War [quest=7260] (Bixie Warfront partisan task)\nYou say, 'Hail, Frislo'\nFrislo glares at you, 'So you're the one who failed to rescue my brother? The one who thought it would be a good idea to use explosives at the center of a hive full of crazed bixies?' The exasperated drakkin rolls his eyes, 'Do you have any idea what you've done? The hive is now swarming with more bixies than before! You need to [help] undo what you've done and free my brother from captivity.'\nYou say, 'How can I help?'\nFrislo takes a deep breath in an attempt to calm down, 'I suppose I can't completely discount your efforts, since at the very least, you were able to locate where Jacyll's being held. It'll take a lot more force to break him free, though. Whatever material the bixie's are using to imprison him won't shatter under your first alone. I hope you brought a solid [group] of allies, or perhaps a [raid]?'\nYou say, 'I have a group'\nFrislo says 'Let me know when your group is ready and we can [begin] this rescue.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Saving Jacyll'.\nFrislo needs your help rescuing his brother from the center of the bixie hive.\nYou say, 'Let's **begin**'\nFrislo nods. 'I'll run ahead and make sure the path is clear. Meet me at the center of the hive where Jacyll is being kept.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Bixie Warfront.\n\n---\n\n**Task Steps**\nMeet Frislo at the center of the hive where Jacyll is being held 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Frislo said he's clear the way to the central room where his brother is being held captive. Meet him there to begin the rescue.\nSpeak with Frislo 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Frislo appears anxious to speak with you.\nDestroy the translucent wall surrounding Jacyll 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ A thick wall of unknown material is keeping Jacyll trapped. Use magic and might to break the wall.\nDefeat Pelzia the Crazed 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The hive is attacking! Defeat Pelzia the Crazed before she kills you and your allies.\nDefeat Warchanter Neezzee 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The hive is attacking! Defeat Warchanter Neezzee before she kills you and your allies.\n_(Task locks upon Neezzee's death.)_\nDefeat General Vaxa and her Lieutenants 0/3 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The hive is attacking! Defeat General Vaxa and her Lieutenants before she kills you and your allies.\nSpeak with Frislo once again 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Frislo looks as though he has something to say.\nClaim your reward from the Honeycomb Chest 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Your efforts shouldn't go unrewarded. Break the Honeycomb chest and claim whatever is inside.\n\n---\n\n**The Event: Triggering & Pelzia the Crazed**\n_Head up to the top of the hive, and hail Frislo:_\nYou say, 'Hail, Frislo'\nFrislo points at the translucent cage surrounding his brother, 'Here! We need to use all our strength to destroy this wall!'\n_DPS \"a glass wall\" to 75%. At 75%, it locks health and \"Pelzia the Crazed\" spawns on the bottom floor (not auto-aggro):_\nYour aggressive actions have caused the hive to stir.\nFrislo looks around, unsure of what to do next. 'Do you hear that? That buzz? The bixies are swarming. They're going to attack!' He eyes his brother before peering back at your group, 'You need to stop them before they reach Jacyll!'\n_Pelzia the Crazed spawns in the entry room of the hive. She sees invisibility and has a fair-sized aggro range. She hits for a max ~16,750 and casts two AEs:_\nStinging Blade: Area PC 30', Unresistable (-1000)\n1: Stun (2.00 sec/200)\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 53200\nWing Bash: PB AE 500', Unresistable (-1000)\n1: Knockback (8) and Toss Up (2)\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 10640\n_Kill Pelzia the Crazed to update the task._\nPelzia the Crazed has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nFrislo shouts 'Quick! Come help break down this wall while the hive is quiet. We won't have long.'\n\n---\n\n**The Event: Warchanter Neezzee**\n_NOTE: The task locks upon Warchanter Neezzee's death._\n_DPS \"a glass wall\" to 50% to spawn \"Warchanter Neezzee\" in the same fashion and location as Pelzia._\nYour aggressive actions have caused the hive to stir.\nFrislo urges you to be silent, 'Do you hear that? That familiar buzz? Pelzia must have called for reinforcements before she died. I'll keep an eye on Jacyll. You head down to the main floor and kill off the bixies before they reach us.'\n_Warchanter Neezzee hits for a max ~16,750; and casts \"Spinning Blade\" and the random single-target spells \"Hush\" and \"Mind Sap\":_\nSpinning Blade: PB AE 50', Unresistable (-1000)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 44240\n2: SpinStun\nHush: Single Target, Unresistable (-1000)\n1: Silence _(1 tick)_\n2: Amnesia (Silence vs Melee Effect)\n3: Increase Curse Counter by 60\nMind Sap: Single Target, Unresistable (-1000)\n1: Decrease Mana by 4300\n2: Decrease Endurance by 2150\n_Kill Warchanter Neezee to update the task._\nWarchanter Neezzee has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nFrislo shouts 'Quick! Come help break down this wall while the hive is quiet. We won't have long.'\n\n---\n\n**The Event: General Vaxa and the Lieutenants**\n_DPS \"a glass wall\" to 25% to spawn \"General Vaxa\" and three lieutenants._\nYour aggressive actions have caused the hive to stir.\nFrislo groans as he hears the familiar buzzing, 'Are you kidding me? More bixies?!' The frustrated drakkin looks toward his brother, 'Don't worry, Jacyll. We'll get you out of here eventually.' Frislo nods in your direction, 'You know what to do. Slaughter those bixies!'\n_These four mobs are aggro-linked, so you'll have to handle them all at once. All four mobs cast the random single-target spell \"Venomous Sting\". This acts as a reverse-knockback, pulling the target towards the NPC casting it:_\nVenomous Sting: Single Target, Unresistable (0)\n1: Pull target towards caster (5)\n2: Add effect: Venomous Sting\nGeneral Vaxa hits for a max ~14,000. The lieutenants each hit for a max ~11,400 and are rootable/snareable and mezzable.\n_Kill these four mobs to update the task._\nGeneral Vaxa has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nLieutenant Drix has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nLieutenant Vyzik has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nLieutenant Zizzix has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nFrislo shouts 'Quick! The wall is about to break. Just a bit more brute force and my brother should be free!'\n\n---\n\n**Completing the Task**\n_Destroy the glass wall..._\nFrislo hugs his brother while giving gentle reassurance, 'It's okay, Jacyll. You're safe now, you're safe.' The relieved drakkin loosens his embrace and reaches for the drum that his brother is still clutching, 'You'll never have to play for these bixies again, I promise.' Frislo takes the drum and turns toward you.\n_Speak with Frislo..._\nYou say, 'Hail, Frislo'\nFrislo says 'Thank you for helping me rescue my brother. I'm sure it'll take a while for Jacyll to return to his normal self, though who knows? Maybe one day he'll be comfortable playing music again. For now however, I want this drum out of our lives. Please take it far away from here when you [leave], and ensure that it doesn't fall into the wrong hands.'\n_...And open the chest to complete the task._\nYou rescued Jacyll from the main hive in Bixie Warfront.\nYou say, 'Let's leave'\nFrislo hands you the drum in a gesture of trust and respect.\n_You receive \"Selo's Drum\"._\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Bixie Warfront.\n\n---\n\n**Loot and Rewards**\n_Task Rewards:_\nExperience\n187 platinum, 5 gold\n_Possible Chest Loot (1 item + 0-1 armor piece + 0-1 Rk. II spell):_\nBroadaxe of the Bixies\nEnchanted Honey Mask\nEngraved Butterfly Faceguard\nPollen Pod\nStriped Bandit Mask\nBracer of Latent Ether\nGloves of Latent Ether\nHelm of Latent Ether\nLeggings of Latent Ether\nSpell: Insidious Deflection Rk. II\nSpell: Mental Terror Rk. II\nSpell: Spirit Bolstering Rk. II\nTome: Phantom Assailant Rk. II\nAlso, when you say \"leave\" to Frislo, you receive \"Selo's Drum\".\n- Bracer of Latent Ether [item=113263]\n- Broadaxe of the Bixies [item=113374]\n- Enchanted Honey Mask [item=113745]\n- Engraved Butterfly Faceguard [item=113783]\n- Gloves of Latent Ether [item=113373]\n- Helm of Latent Ether [item=113264]\n- Leggings of Latent Ether [item=113265]\n- Pollen Pod [item=113461]\n- Selo's Drum [item=113761]\n- Spell: Insidious Deflection Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Spell: Mental Terror Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Spell: Spirit Bolstering Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Striped Bandit Mask [item=113977]\n- Tome: Phantom Assailant Rk. II [tradeable]",
