      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Bixie Warfront [zone=941]\n**Who:**\n- Snazlieu the Shadow [npc=44042]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 75\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Adventure\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 03:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Aggressive Antenna [item=113809]\n- Soggy Plant Parts [item=113805]\n- Tracking Bugs [item=113806]\n- Volatile Components [item=113868]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Bixie Warfront: Always Follow the Money [zone=953]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Amber Grillet [ _Captain of the Guard_]\n- Colonel Honeybags [npc=44779]\n- Cristonix [npc=44780]\n- Crolling Criztanus [npc=44782]\n- Crutchy [npc=44783]\n- Delancey [npc=44784]\n- Dreadmole [npc=44077]\n- Kelly [npc=44785]\n- Luncher [npc=44788]\n- Mush [npc=44786]\n- Snazlieu the Sneak [npc=44787]\n- a bitter thief [npc=44752]\n- a burrowing mole [npc=44753]\n- a conspirator [npc=44754]\n- a crash tester [npc=44755]\n- a delivery florist [npc=44756]\n- a greedy guard [npc=44757]\n- a honey bender [npc=44758]\n- a lifter [npc=44759]\n- a material handler [npc=44760]\n- a mounted target dummy [npc=44761]\n- a packager [npc=44763]\n- a packer [npc=44762]\n- a plant bundler [npc=44764]\n- a plant inspector [npc=44765]\n- a quality inspector [npc=44766]\n- a rabid ganker [npc=44767]\n- a raging bandit [npc=44768]\n- a reclaimer [npc=44769]\n- a riot cop [npc=44771]\n- a river guardian [npc=44770]\n- a rushed runner [npc=44728]\n- a rushed runner [npc=44772]\n- a smug scab [npc=45139]\n- a soggy plant part [npc=44773]\n- a striking factory worker [npc=44774]\n- a welder [npc=44775]\n- an alerted guard [npc=44776]\n- an industrialized mole [npc=44777]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Daily Task: Heroic Adventures [quest=7988]\n- Snazlieu #1: Espionage Starts at Home [quest=7263]\n- Snazlieu #3: Working Overtime [quest=7265]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Oct 8 06:00:30 2013\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n**About Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Heroic adventures in Call of the Forsaken scale in level: As low as **Level 75** and up to current maximum level.\n\\- Scale is based on the highest level player **present in the zone** and affects difficulty, loot quality, and mob levels.\n\\- There is some variation/randomization in the task steps you'll be assigned as you progress through the task.\n\\- Time of completion will vary by your group's makeup (anywhere from 30-90+ minutes).\n\\- Collection items appear as ground spawns midway through tasks (you'll see an emote indicating their appearance).\n\\- Named mobs (or their PHs) spawn midway through tasks (usually, but always, at the same time collection items appear).\n\\- These tasks have individual **3-hour lockout timers** (timer gained upon completion).\n**Experience in Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Mobs in these instances grant some experience, but the bulk of experience is **earned upon task completion**.\n\\- As of a patch in November 2014, less difficult tasks were tuned to reward less experience and more difficult ones were tuned to reward more.\n\\- For an added experience bonus, check out **Guard Hamarn's \"Daily Tasks\"** [quest=7988].\n\n---\n\n_This is a heroic adventure (1-6 players) that begins with Snazlieu the Shadow ( **map image**) in the Bixie Warfront. She is located a little ways north from the portal to the Ethernere Tainted West Karana._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Level 75\n\\- Completed \"Espionage Begins At Home\" (heroic adventure)\n\n---\n\n**TASK SUMMARY**\n\\- Say \"embark on an adventure\" to request the task and \"ready\" to zone in.\n**Step #1:**\n\\- Kill plant bundlers 0/5\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update\n\\- Collect soggy plant parts 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- DPS plant parts and loot them\n**Step #2:**\n\\- Plant tracking bugs on tired runners 0/5\n\\-\\-\\- Right-click \"Tracking Bugs\" on rushed runners (doing so will spawn two hostile bixies)\n\\- Kill delivery florists 0/5\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update\n**Step #3:**\n\\- Escort a late delivery bixie 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Speak with Crolling Crixtanus, and kill the waves of mobs that spawn (not auto-aggro)\n\\- Collect aggressive antennae 0/15\n\\-\\-\\- Kill raging bandits, reclaimers, and bitter thieves until you've looted 15 of these\n\\- Kill rioters in the residential area 0/10\n\\-\\-\\- Kill hostile bixies in the residential district\n**Step #4:**\n\\- Kill Cristonix and Luncher 0/2\n\\-\\-\\- Kill the named mobs Cristonix and Luncher (splitable)\n\\- Survive the guards' ambush 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- Kill 3 groups of mobs\n**\\- At this point in the task, collectibles spawn in the zone (ground spawns) and a named (or its PH) has a chance to spawn.**\n**Step #5:**\n\\- Kill factory workers 0/10\n\\-\\-\\- Kill any 10 hostile bixies in the factory\n\\- Destroy catapults 0/4\n\\-\\-\\- Collect 20 \"Volatile Components\" (dropped from mobs in factory), stand on top of catapults, and right-click the items.\n\\- Support striking workers 0/4\n\\-\\-\\- Speak with Kelly (adds spawn), Crutchy (defend from scabs), Delancey (kill him), and Mush (\"wants help with slogan\")\n**Step #6:**\n\\- Kill Colonel Honeybags 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill the named\n\\- Escape the factory riot and kill the approaching riot cops 0/5\n\\-\\-\\- Kill 5x \"a riot cop\"\n\\- As soon as the objective for Step #6 is done, the task completes.\n\n---\n\n**NAMED MOBS**\n_\"Dreadmole\" (or its PH) has a chance to spawn after the fourth step is completed. Known loot from this named:_\nBixie Summoner's Stone\nDigested Dread Ring\nHelm of Latent Ether\nMole Whisker Ring\n\n---\n\n**TASK IN DETAIL**\n========================================================================\nTRIGGERING THE TASK\n========================================================================\nYou say, 'Let's embark on an adventure'\nSnazlieu the Shadow says 'Very well. Let me know when you're [ready] to depart.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Always Follow the Money'.\nThe Stone Hive bixies have begun shuttling all of the supplies to a large cavern in the northern edge of the residential area. Wet River Hive scouts report that the bixies are building weapons of war at an increase rate. Follow runners into the cavern and see if you can locate, and sabotage, the bixies' production line.\nYou say, 'Ready!'\nSnazlieu the Shadow says 'Good luck... No, don't tell me your name. It's easier this way.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Bixie Warfront.\n========================================================================\nSTEP #1\n========================================================================\nKill plant bundlers 0/5 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ You found a group of bixies that are bundling plant parts floating down the river so they can be carried in larger quantities. Put an end to their nefarious bundling of vegetation!\n_If You Get This Step: Kill update._\nCollect soggy plant parts 0/6 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The bixies appear to be using this honey river to float supplies down from the surface hive. Perhaps this is what's corrupting them. Smash some of the floating plants and grab some samples to test back at camp.\n_If You Get This Step: Attack the soggy plant parts as they flow down the stream of honey (cannot be stunned or snared, so have to DPS them while they'e mobile). Loot form them \"Soggy Plant Parts\". If you don't have enough DPS to destroy them on their first go-around, they do appear to respawn at the beginning at the same health you left them._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #2\n========================================================================\nPlant tracking bugs on tired runners 0/5 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ It looks like some of the bixies are carrying supplies from the river to another location. Place a tracking bug on some of them to find out where they're taking the supplies.\n_If You Get This Step: You receive \"Tracking Bugs\" in your inventory. You'll need to find \"a rushed runner\" and right-click the \"Tracking Bugs\" on them (a good place to catch them is at the end of the honey river). Doing this spawns 2x \"an alerted guard\" which attack (hit for a max ~12,000; mezzable; stunnable)._\nTwo shiny tracking bugs leap from your hands and race towards the rushed runner, latching onto its clothing.\n=====================\nKill delivery florists 0/5 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: There are a lot of bixie florists running around from the bottom of the honey river through the residential area. They are non-aggro and run back and forth into the town. You have to damage them while in this state until they get to 45% at which point they become aggro._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #3\n========================================================================\nEscort a late delivery bixie 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Not all of the bixie runners have been able to make it through the volatile street below. You found one particularly anxious bixie, who asked for help reaching its destination. Protect it along its entire route so that you can discover where they're taking all of these supplies.\n_If You Get This Step: Speak with Crolling Criztanus and follow her down the path. As she moves along, waves of 3x \"a rabid ganker\" spawn and attack her. These hit for a max ~11,000, and are mezzable and stunnable._\nYou say, 'Hail, Crolling Crixtanus'\nCrolling Crixtanus points his finger at you aggressively and shouts, 'You there! Stop whatever you're doing and [help] me deliver these weird plants to the other side of town.'\nYou say, 'We'll help'\nCrolling Crixtanus says 'I've been delivering small bits of dead plants to the residents of this particular strip for literally days without problem. Now they've all gone insane and started attacking me! These people need their plant parts. Are you [ready]?'\nYou say, 'Ready!'\nCrolling Crixtanus brushes off his arms, plucks at its wings, gets a good grip on the plant parts, and zooms ahead of you.\nCrolling Crixtanus says 'Here come the greedy freaks! Arm yourselves!'\na rabid ganker bares its teeth as it readies its first attack.\nCrolling Crixtanus slaps you with the big plant part, 'Less talking, more guarding!'\na rabid ganker's corpse shudders as it crumples on the ground.\na rabid ganker has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nCrolling Crixtanus haphazardly tosses the plant parts onto the doorstep and says, 'They deserve a slightly bruised plant after all that work. Time for a break!'\n=====================\nCollect aggressive antennae 0/15 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill raging bandits, reclaimers, and bitter thieves until you've looted 15x \"Aggressive Antenna\"._\n=====================\nKill rioters in the residential area 0/10 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The bixies in the street below have started rioting! Take down any overaggressive bixies you encounter in the area.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill 10 KOS bixies in the residential area._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #4\n========================================================================\nKill Cristonix and Luncher 0/2 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The riot was apparently organized by a local bandit leader, Cristonix. She's confronted you on the east edge of the street. Kill her and her bloody pet.\n_If You Get This Step: Head further down the path where you'll find Cristonix and Luncher. Luncher is a standard mob for the zone. Cristonix has a lot of hitpoints and casts \"Frozen Cyanin\". Neither are rootable/snareable (\\*update: Cristonix is snarable (by a lvl 105 wizard) and Luncher is immune to changes in runspeed), but they are stunnable and mezzable. They are NOT aggro-linked (CAN be split from one another)._\nCristonix says 'This neighborhood belongs to the Spider Stomper clan!'\n=====================\nSurvive the guards' ambush 0/6 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says: As you tried to leave out the east side of the row of homes, you were ambushed by a pack of guards not interested in quelling the riot. Survive their ambush and turn the tables on them._\n_If You Get This Step: Kill three waves of mobs (non-nameds are snareable/rootable):_\n_Wave 1:_\n_1x \"a greedy guard\"_\n_1x \"a conspirator\"_\n_Wave 2:_\n_3x \"a conspirator\"_\n_Wave 3:_\n_1x \"Amber Grillet\"_\n_========================================================================_\n_STEP #5_\n_========================================================================_\n_Kill factory workers 0/10 (Bixie Warfront)_\n_Task Window Says: You discovered that the runners are carrying supplies to what appears to be a large factory, where the bixies are building some catapults and training moles. Clear the floor to stop production._\n_If You Get This Step: From the residential area, head east and circle around the large rock (a named or its PH can spawn in this area at this point in the task), and enter the factory. Kill 10 bixies in the factory._\n_=====================_\n_Destroy catapults 0/4 (Bixie Warfront)_\n_Task Window Says: You discovered that the runners are carrying supplies to what appears to be a large factory, where the bixies are building catapults. Some have already been completed. Kill workers to find volatile components that you can use to destroy finished catapults._\n_If You Get This Step: Collect 20x \"Volatile Components\" (dropped from bixie mobs inside the factory). Stand on top of a completed catapult, and right-click these items (one click takes 5x \"Volatile Components\" and destroys one catapult)._\n_=====================_\n_Support striking workers 0/4 (Bixie Warfront)_\n_Task Window Says: You found where all the raw materials were being taken to: a military factory north of the housing section. It appears that the workers are on strike at the moment, keeping catapults and other weapons of war out of the hands of the bixie military. Speak with four prominent strikers inside the factory to find out how you can help each of them._\n_If You Get This Step: Speak with named striking workers Kelly (3 riot cops spawn and attack; kill them), Crutchy (4-5 mobs spawn from the opening and attack; kill them), Delancy (kill him), and Mush (\"wants help with slogan\")._\n_For Mush:_\n_You say, 'Hail, Mush'_\n_Mush looks at you suspiciously and asks, 'You [care] about the workers, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_?'_\n_You say, 'Yes... I care...'_\n_Mush nods and says, 'Maybe you wouldn't mind proving it by helping us make some [picket signs]?'_\n_You say, 'Picket signs?'_\n_Mush says 'Yeah, we gotta make some signs to show why we're [striking] and try to persuade some of those lazy lumps down in the village to support us!'_\n_You say, 'Striking?'_\n_Mush says 'Alright, which phrase do you like better for our signs? [MORE PAY MORE WORK MORE WAR] or [HONEYBAGS EATS CHILDREN]?'_\n_You say, 'HONEYBAGS EATS CHILDREN'_\n_Mush gives you a weird look and asks, 'Are you sure? Alright, well you heard the Gnomework, strikers. Write 'em up! Now, let's plan a [backup slogan].'_\n_You say, 'Backup slogan?'_\n_Mush says 'Sure, we can't be guaranteed that the first one you picked will catch on. Which do you like better between these: [TIME TO FIRE HIM] or [FIRE HIM TO TIRE!]--wait a second.'_\n_Mush looks around the group and says, 'Who wrote this last one? It doesn't even make sense. Charlie, was this one yours? I told you not to write anything. You're illiterate!'_\n_You say, 'TIME TO FIRE HIM'_\n_Mush says 'Yeah, that's the clear choice. Write it up, boys! Thanks for the help, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'_\n_For Crutchy:_\n_You say, 'Hail, Crutchy'_\n_Crutchy looks a bit scared as you approach and says nervously, 'Oh, hey there, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. [What can I do for you]?'_\n_You say, 'What can I do for you?'_\n_Crutchy smiles and looks at his friends near him, 'Oh, you want to help us? Well that's a wonderfully pleasant surprise. We've had some trouble with [scabs getting violent] recently.'_\n_You say, 'Scabs getting violent?'_\n_Crutchy looks down at the floor, 'Oh, you know. Scabs are the ones coming into the factory to work while we strike. Mr. Moneybags is paying them good money. But sometimes they [hurt] us...'_\n_You say, 'Hurt?'_\n_Crutchy holds his arm gingerly, and you notice for the first time that his wings are really torn up, 'I wouldn't mind having a little [help] if they come back to beat us up some more.'_\n_You say, 'I'll help'_\n_Crutchy points to the western factory entrance and whispers, 'H-here they come now. Please help us, Slahr.'_\n_When the scabs appear, you can just sit the whole thing out if you don't feel like fighting them. If you get aggro and can lose it, they will eventually despawn and you can hail Crutchy again for the update._\n_a smug scab says 'Lookie here. Little Crutchy found some friends. Pathetic.'_\n_a striking factory worker says 'Soak 'em for Crutchy!'_\n_a smug scab says 'Lookie here. Little Crutchy found some friends. Pathetic.'_\n_a striking factory worker says 'Soak 'em for Crutchy!'_\n_a smug scab says 'Lookie here. Little Crutchy found some friends. Pathetic.'_\n_Kill or mez these mobs (mez causes them to despawn). Once they've been handled, hail Crutchy again:_\n_You say, 'Hail, Crutchy'_\n_Crutchy shakes his fist in the direction that the fleeing scabs ran and shouts, 'And don't you come back!'_\n_Crutchy gives you an enthusiastic hug and says, 'Ah man, you were great, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Thanks for helping us out there!'_\n_For Delancey:_\n_You say, 'Hail, Delancey'_\n_Delancey jumps when you speak to him. He clearly didn't see you approaching. He glances over to the group of bixies he was [staring] at and says, 'Oh, yes? What do you want?'_\n_You say, 'Staring?'_\n_Delancey backs away from you slightly and protests in a hushed tone, 'No! Of course I wasn't staring at them. I was just, um, well, you see... Have you ever [been in love]?'_\n_You say, 'Been in love?'_\n_Delancey looks very pleased with himself, 'Yes, I'm in love! That's why I'm staring at that [group of bixies]. Love!'_\n_You say, 'What group of bixies?'_\n_Delancey stumbles in his speech and looks around as he thinks, 'Yes, I can't be in love with all of them, can I? Well, I'm in love with [that one]!'_\n_You say, Tthat one?'_\n_Delancey says 'Yes, the one with the [wings].'_\n_You say, 'Wings...'_\n_Delancey looks very frustrated and looks around frantically. He finally snaps and starts pushing you, 'You can't tell them I'm spying for Colonel Honeybags! He pays too well!'_\n_Kill Delancey for the update._\n_For Kelly:_\n_You say, 'Hail, Kelly'_\n_Kelly throws a piece of plant stalk at the [riot cops] on the ledge above._\n_You say, 'What about these riot cops?'_\n_Kelly smiles at you and puts his arm around your shoulder as he shouts up at the riot cops playfully, 'Yeah, look at those flitter-flatterers up there! Think they're so tough with [Moneybags]!'_\n_You say, 'Moneybags?'_\n_Kelly laughs and says, 'Old Moneybags owns this place. You've probably seen him around before. Thinks he's better than us, flying around while we [work] on the ground.'_\n_You say, 'Work?'_\n_Kelly starts shouting again, 'That's right! We work ourselves to the bone while they just sit up in their fancy offices drinking honey! It's time we show them who has the real [power] here!'_\n_You say, 'Power?'_\n_Kelly leans into you, smiling, and asks, 'You want to have a little [fun], \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_?'_\n_You say, 'Fun?'_\n_Kelly punches you playfully, and turn to the riot cops on the ledge and shouts, 'Hey, you! Ugly riot beaters up there! You're pathetic!'_\n_Kelly picks up pieces of plant stalk, hands some to you and starts throwing them at the riot cops._\n_a riot cop says 'That does it, Kelly! You've had this coming for a long time.'_\n_a riot cop says 'That does it, Kelly! You've had this coming for a long time.'_\n_a riot cop says 'That does it, Kelly! You've had this coming for a long time.'_\n_Kill the three riot cops, and hail Kelly again:_\n_You say, 'Hail, Kelly'_\n_Kelly laughs and puts his arm around you, 'Oh, that was brilliant, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_! We've got to tell the others about this.'_\n_Once you've done all four mini-tasks, this step updates._\n_========================================================================_\n_STEP #6_\n_========================================================================_\n_Kill Colonel Honeybags 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)_\n_Task Window Says: The factory owner, Colonel Honeybags, has shown up to personally put an end to the strike once and for all. Help the striking workers by taking down Honeybags._\n_If You Get This Step: Upon completion of the previous step, Colonel Honeybags spawns on the side of the factory opposite its entrance. The Colonel doesn't cast any special spells, but has a significant amount of hitpoints (5-6 times that of regular zone mobs) and hits for a max ~19,000 (this is in the Level 100 version of the task; no rampage; no flurry)._\n_Colonel Honeybags shouts across the entire factory, 'What flower-brain is causing this disruption to my production line? We have deadlines to meet!'_\n_Colonel Honeybags has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!_\n_This completes the task._\n_=====================_\n_Escape the factory riot and kill the approaching riot cops 0/5 (Bixie Warfront)_\n_Task Window Says: The striking factory workers have started a riot! Get out of the factory alive, and take out the riot police approaching from the west to ensure that the rioters succeed in trashing the factory. That will ensure the hive's war machine slows down._\n_If You Get This Step: Kill 5x \"a riot cop\" to complete the task._\n_\n---\n_\n_**TASK REWARDS**_\n_\\- a varying amount of platinum_\n_\\- a varying amount of experience_\n_\\- a varying number of Marks of Valor (currency used to buy group gear)_\n- Bixie Summoner's Stone [item=113767]\n- Digested Dread Ring [item=113239]\n- Helm of Latent Ether [item=113264]\n- Mark of Valor [item=113459]\n- Mole Whisker Ring [item=114052]",
