      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Bixie Warfront [zone=941]\n**Who:**\n- Clayton Teek [ _Daily Adventures_]\n- Naturalist Yrelia [ _Heroic Adventures_]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 75\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Adventure\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 03:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Bixie Fire Blower [item=113666]\n- Colorful Venom [item=114071]\n- Magister Knife [item=116160]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Bixie Warfront: The Great Hunt [zone=955]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Arachnox, the Dread Widow [npc=44075]\n- Charlbroiled Chanon [npc=44937]\n- Flace Woon [npc=44939]\n- Gralice [npc=44940]\n- Mosscreeper [npc=44607]\n- a creaky treant [npc=44913]\n- a crispy critter [npc=44914]\n- a freed hunter [npc=44915]\n- a kabab topper [npc=44916]\n- a late-night snack [npc=44917]\n- a lurker [npc=44918]\n- a meat stick [npc=44919]\n- a poisonous creeper [npc=44920]\n- a resilient egg pile [npc=44921]\n- a salivating arachnid [npc=44922]\n- a shroomed treant [npc=44923]\n- a special of the day [npc=44924]\n- a spider hunter [npc=44925]\n- a squirming egg sac [npc=44926]\n- a walking salad [npc=44927]\n- a web spinner [npc=44928]\n- a whole lot of garnish [npc=44929]\n- a wiggling cocoon [npc=44930]\n- a wild poisoner [npc=44931]\n- an agitated widow [npc=44932]\n- an appetizer [npc=44933]\n- an egg tender [npc=44934]\n- an encroaching spider [npc=44935]\n- an undying eater [npc=44936]\n- close enough to pork [npc=44938]\n- indigestion [npc=44941]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Daily Task: Heroic Adventures [quest=7988]\n- Yrelia #2: They've Gone Too Far This Time [quest=7267]\n- Yrelia #3: They're Everywhere! [quest=7268]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Oct 8 06:02:39 2013\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n**About Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Heroic adventures in Call of the Forsaken scale in level: As low as **Level 75** and up to current maximum level.\n\\- Scale is based on the highest level player **present in the zone** and affects difficulty, loot quality, and mob levels.\n\\- There is some variation/randomization in the task steps you'll be assigned as you progress through the task.\n\\- Time of completion will vary by your group's makeup (anywhere from 30-90+ minutes).\n\\- Collection items appear as ground spawns midway through tasks (you'll see an emote indicating their appearance).\n\\- Named mobs (or their PHs) spawn midway through tasks (usually, but always, at the same time collection items appear).\n\\- These tasks have individual **3-hour lockout timers** (timer gained upon completion).\n**Experience in Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Mobs in these instances grant some experience, but the bulk of experience is **earned upon task completion**.\n\\- As of a patch in November 2014, less difficult tasks were tuned to reward less experience and more difficult ones were tuned to reward more.\n\\- For an added experience bonus, check out **Guard Hamarn's \"Daily Tasks\"** [quest=7988].\n\n---\n\nThis is a heroic adventure (1-6 players) that begins with Naturalist Yrelia in the Bixie Warfront. She is located at about -790, -2120, 50 (up the ramp just east of the portal to the Ethernere Tainted West Karana).\nPre-Requisites for Requesting:\n\\- Level 75\n\\- No tasks\n\n---\n\n**TASK SUMMARY**\n\\- Say \"embark on an adventure\" to get the task and \"ready\" to zone in.\n**Step #1:**\n\\- Kill encroaching spiders near the hunting camp 0/4\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update\n**Step #2:**\n\\-\nSpeak with Gralice at the hunters' camp 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- \"final advance\" updates the task\n\\-\nSpeak with Charlbroiled Chanon at the hunters' camp 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- dialogue update\n**Step #3:**\n\\-\nDraw out and kill lurking spiders 0/8\n\\-\\-\\- In the tunnel to the east and onto the spider nest bridges, step over the small rock piles to spawn lurker spiders (kill update)\n\\-\nSquish egg sacs 0/12\n\\-\\-\\- Destroy egg sacs (spawns spiderling adds)\n**Step #4:**\n\\-\nFree spider hunters 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- Clear mobs from wiggling cocoons, then break them open\n\\-\nCollect colorful venom 0/10\n\\-\\-\\- This item drops from \"a poisonous spider\" (found in groups of 3-6; the large ones carry 1-2 bottles venom on them)\n\\-\nBurn undying spiders and resilient egg sacs 0/10\nTask Window Says: Some of the spiders in the nest have developed amazing resistance to traditional weapons and spells. The bixie hunters have developed a special tool for killing these undying spiders and their resilient egg piles. Weaken them, and then use the Bixie Fire Blowers to finish the job.\n\\-\\-\\- DPS undying spiders and resilient egg sacs (note: these spawn spiderling adds) to 10% and click the torch you received\n**\\- At this point in the task, collectibles spawn in the zone (ground spawns) and a named (or its PH) has a chance to spawn.**\nfile bixiewarfront\\_1.txt\nP 2297.5830, -121.8712, -49.2747, 0, 0, 0, 1, PH\\_or\\_Arachnox\\_the\\_Dread\\_Widow\nP 2569.0129, 131.7140, 12.8844, 0, 0, 0, 1, P\nP 2022.3705, 408.7396, 1.6057, 0, 0, 0, 1, P\nP 1966.0212, 194.0546, -32.8431, 0, 0, 0, 1, P\nP 2173.6765, -3.3280, -269.8212, 0, 0, 0, 1, P-on\\_floor\n**Step #5:**\n\\-\nFind an exit to the surface 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Make your way to the top of the spider ramps, and then through the tunnel to the surface\n**Step #6:**\n\\-\nSave Flace Woon from creaky treants 0/10\n\\-\\-\\- Speak with Flace to trigger the mini-event; if you look at a treant face-to-face, it stops attacking and remains immobile\n\\-\nKill Mosscreeper 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Clear the smaller treants to spawn Mosscreeper, then kill Mosscreeper\n\\-\nHunt wild beasts with Charlbroiled Chanon 0/15\n\\-\\-\\- DPS mobs to 10% at which point Chanon kills them\n\\- As soon as the objective for Step #6 is done, the task completes.\n\n---\n\n**NAMED MOBS**\n\"Arachnox, the Dread Widow\" (or her PH) has a chance to spawn after the fourth step is completed. Known loot from this named:\nLevel 100\nBixie Summoner's Stone\nFace of Dread\nSpidersilk Dread Mask\nLevel 95\nSignet of the Record Master\nLevel 90\nWarlord's Unholy Pendant\nLevel 85\n??\nLevel 80\n??\nLevel 75\n??\n\n---\n\n**TASK IN DETAIL**\n========================================================================\nTRIGGERING THE TASK\n========================================================================\nYou say, 'Hail, Naturalist Yrelia'\nNaturalist Yrelia's antennae twitch as she stares up through the rocky tunnel. A breeze from above carries the faint scent of [mildew and blood].\nYou say, 'Mildew and blood?'\nNaturalist Yrelia says 'There is war both above and below, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. The [wild beasts] grow restless under the [oppressive influence] of the bixies.'\nYou say, 'Wild beasts?'\nNaturalist Yrelia says 'Beetles, snakes, moles, and others giving into their most violent tendencies. But the biggest threat are the [spiders].'\nYou say, 'Oppressive influence?'\nNaturalist Yrelia says 'The Stone Hive Bixies may not have been friendly to outsiders invading their land...' Naturalist Yrelia gives you a knowing look before continuing, \"But they used to care for nature. Nurture it. Now they [aggravate and abuse] it.'\nYou say, 'What about the spiders?'\nNaturalist Yrelia says 'Wise, strong, and numerous is how you want to describe your allies, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, not your enemies. The spiders have a [large nest] near here, and I'm less certain with every passing minute that we can abide its presence.'\nYou say, 'How do they aggravate and abuse their nature?'\nNaturalist Yrelia says 'You've seen how they're acting recently. This isn't the Stone Hive bixies we've worked alongside for generations. These are monsters. Monsters with no aim but self-[destruction] and [foolish pride]'.\nYou say, 'What large nest?'\nNaturalist Yrelia says 'I've never seen spiders breed so quickly. I've only explored the first few caves I came across inside of the [massive underground complex], but in just those few rooms, I saw [hundreds of eggs] and hatchers tending to them.'\nYou say, 'What about this self-destruction?'\nNaturalist Yrelia looks at you with sadness and desperation in her eyes, \"Surely you've heard what their final plan is, right? To conquer Crescent Reach and slay the mighty dragons. Bixie hives are not typically known for their arrogance or stupidity. Will you [help] us stop them before they get themselves killed?\nYou say, 'And foolish pride?'\nNaturalist Yrelia says 'Our allies in the Stone Hive have a long history of flourishing alongside nature, encouraging its growth for a shared protection. Now, they plunder it for trophies and [bragging rights].'\nYou say, 'Tell me abou this massive underground complex'\nNaturalist Yrelia says 'It's better if you see it for yourself. Are you rested up and ready to [embark on an adventure]?'\nYou say, 'And the hundreds of eggs?'\nNaturalist Yrelia says 'Trust me, we do not want them to hatch, if they haven't already. How are you feeling? Are you ready to [embark on an adventure]?'\nYou say, 'Bragging rights?'\nNaturalist Yrelia says 'Hunting the massive spiders in the nearby nest has become a local sport. Returning with the corpse of a giant spider over your shoulder has become the highest sign of military prowess. Many return victorious every day, but even more are dying on the hunt and being left behind by their fellow hunters. There is no honor in a wasted death, and I fear the spiders' retaliation will be too much for the nearby bixie homesteads to bear. True strength comes from working alongside nature, not against it, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Will you [help]?'\nYou say, 'I will help'\nNaturalist Yrelia says 'The time for talking is done. Action is needed now. Will you [embark on an adventure] on behalf of us and our allies?'\nYou say, 'Let's embark on an adventure...'\nNaturalist Yrelia says 'Excellent. There's an urgent matter that suits you perfectly. Let me know when you're [ready] to confront it.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Great Hunt'.\nA group of paticularly bloodthirsty bixies have broken off from the hive to hunt deadly spiders that have nested nearby. Find these hunters and ensure that their crusade is successful, so that they don't accidentally trigger a backlash from the spider nest that'd surely wipe out the hive.\nYou say, 'Ready!'\nNaturalist Yrelia says 'May cool winds carry you and soft ground catch you. Fight well, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Bixie Warfront.\n========================================================================\nSTEP #1\n========================================================================\nKill encroaching spiders near the hunting camp 0/4 (Bixie Warfront)\nTask Window Says: You discovered a camp of savage bixies that have broken off from the hive and seem to be hunting spiders on the outskirts of the area. Prove your worth by slaying some spiders in front of them.\nIf You Get This Step: These mobs are located at the zone-in. They can have a lot of hitpoints and some of them AE rampage (hit for a max ~11,000).\n========================================================================\nSTEP #2\n========================================================================\nSpeak with Gralice at the hunters' camp 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\nTask Window Says: The spider hunters' camp appears to be ruled by Gralice, a particularly harsh-looking bixie hunter. Speak with her and find out what you can about their activities.\nIf You Get This Step: Follow through Gralice's dialogue, updating the step with \"final advance\".\nYou say, 'Hail, Gralice'\nGralice twitches towards you and grunts. She laughs cruelly and says, 'Pathetic! I could see the [fear] in your eyes.'\nYou say, 'Fear?'\nGralice says 'There's no point in denying it, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ You fear me, and you should. I am terrifying. I alone have [hunted] in these caves for weeks, and lived to [reign] over this camp.'\nYou say, 'Hunted?'\nGralice says 'We bixies have not always been respected for our military prowess. The world saw us as gardeners, nature-lovers, and honey collectors. Down here, in the new hive, we [prove them wrong].'\nYou say, 'You reign?'\nGralice roars at the top of her voice and nearby spider [hunters] cautiously shift away from her cautiously as she shouts, 'I am the queen of this camp. Do any dare defy me or my claim?'\nYou say, 'Prove them wrong?'\nGralice says 'Have you not seen the might of the bixie military yet, fool? Then I pity you, and welcome the \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ subjugation. The military is strong, but we, the spider [hunters], we are stronger.'\nYou say, 'What hunters?'\nGralice says 'There is no greater predator in this region than the vicious and powerful spiders. We hunters, the strongest bixies in the entire hive, have fought our way into this area, pouring out our blood for every inch of territory gained as we [push the spiders back].'\nYou say, 'Push the spiders back?'\nGralice raises her weapon into the air ahd shouts, 'We have pushed them all the way to their nest! The spiders lurk within, waiting for our [final advance]. And we will not disappoint!' The rest of the hunters cheer.\nYou say, 'Your final advance?'\nGralice gives you a wicked smile as she grabs your arm and says very sternly, 'You will be our forward scouts in this mission. Run into the nest, and fight your way to the top. We'll watch from here to see where they wait in ambush for us.'\n=====================\nSpeak with Charlbroiled Chanon at the hunters' camp 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\nTask Window Says: At the center of the spider hunters' camp is a jovial barbecue chef, Charlbroiled Chanon. The other hungers seem to respect her greatly. Speak with her and find out what you can about their activities.\nIf You Get This Step: This is a dialogue update; follow through the dialogues with Charlbroiled Chanon.\n========================================================================\nSTEP #3\n========================================================================\nDraw out and kill lurking spiders 0/8 (Bixie Warfront)\nTask Window Says: The hunters at the camp didn't seem to take you seriously, telling you to go to the nearby spider nest and simply wait for spiders to find you. You have the sneaking suspicion that they're right about the spiders finding you. Delve into the spider nest cautiously, and wait for lurking spiders to find you in the first tunnel.\nIf You Get This Step: As the task says, head into the east tunnel. In there, you'll see small piles of brown rocks on the ground. These signal the spawn locations of your kill targets. Run over a pile of rocks to spawn \"a lurker\", which attacks. Kill eight of these for the update. These mobs hit for a max ~13,000, AE rampage, and are stunnable/mezzable.\n=====================\nSquish egg sacs 0/12 (Bixie Warfront)\nTask Window Says: The hunters claimed to have killed most of the mature spiders in the caves in their most recent raids. Some reported that they suspect a new batch of spiders will hatch soon. They prefer to wait until the spiders are dangerous enough to kill some of their hunting party before starting a new raid. Smash the spiderlings in the egg sacs before they grow.\nIf You Get This Step: Destroy the egg sacs (note: spawns spiderling adds).\nLocation of \"Egg Room\": -142, -1968, -35.51\n========================================================================\nSTEP #4\n========================================================================\nFree spider hunters 0/6 (Bixie Warfront)\nTask Window Says: There are more mature spiders in this nest than hunters led you to believe. The nastiest of the bunch, the web spinners, seem to be capturing bixie hunters and preserving them for eating later. Find the web spinners, kill them, and free any captured bixie hunters that are still alive. Some of the cocoons have already been feasted on and you'll find nothing but corpses inside. Instead, look for wiggling cocoons which are much more likely to contain someone that can still be saved.\nIf You Get This Step: Head out of the spider tunnel and into the central nest area. On the bridges, around the caves, and inside the caves, you'll find cocoons called \"a wiggling cocoon\". To make these killable, you have to kill the \"a web spinner\" near it. With the web spinner dead, you can free the hunter trapped in the cocoon (these tend to have other spiders near them as well, but they aren't technically necessary to kill).\n=====================\nCollect colorful venom 0/10 (Bixie Warfront)\nTask Window Says: There are more mature spiders in this nest than the hunters led you to believe. The poisonous ones seem to be particularly nasty. Take out the packs of poisonous spiders and collect samples of their poison to develop an antidote with later.\nIf You Get This Step: This item drops from \"a poisonous spider\" (found in groups of 3-6; the large ones carry 1-2 bottles venom on them).\n=====================\nBurn Undying Spiders and Resistant Egg Sacks (0/10)\nTask Window Says: ?\nIf You Get This Step: With the \"Bixie Fire Blower\" you received in your inventory, DPS undying spiders and resilient egg sacs past 20% health, and then click the item to finish them off. Note that the egg sacs, while being DPS'd, spawn weak spiderling adds.\n========================================================================\nSTEP #5\n========================================================================\nFind an exit to the surface 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\nTask Window Says: You can see natural light coming from the top of this spider nest. Fight your way to the top and find a path that leads out to the surface.\nIf You Get This Step: Note that a named has a chance to spawn inside the zone at this point in the task. Make your way up to the top of the spider ramps and down the tunnel that leads to the surface.\n========================================================================\nSTEP #6\n========================================================================\nSave Flace Woon from creaky treants 0/10 (Bixie Warfront)\nTask Window Says: Flace Woon was incredibly relieved to find you in the forest clearing. He told you he's being attacked by angry treants. Help him kill the treants. Treants will freeze and stop attacking if you get close to them and look directly at them.\nIf You Get This Step: Speak with Flace Woon to trigger this mini event. Once triggered, the creaky treants surrounding the area move in and begin attacking Flace Woon. Don't worry about keeping her alive as she locks health at 10%. The treants each hit for a max ~12,500; are stunnable/mezzable; have a lot of hitpoints; and are social with each other (so if you aggro one, you aggro any nearby as well). They will initially focus their attention on Flace Woon, but you can draw their aggro from her. You can stop a treant from moving and from attacking by looking at it directly, face-to-face (you'll see an emote indicating it's become \"frozen in place\". As long as you keep looking at it, it will not attack back.\nYou say, 'Hail, Flace Woon'\nFlace Woon doesn't look at you while she speaks to you, 'Thank the gods you came, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. The treants here have been picking off our scouts one by one. I tried to help them, but they've cornered me here. We need to [kill them] once and for all.\nYou say, 'How do we Kill them?'\nFlace Woon says 'The treants won't move while you're looking at them! Try to keep vision on as many as possible while you fight them. Are you [ready]?'\nYou say, 'Ready!'\nFlace Woon says 'Here they come!'\na creaky treant has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nFlace Woon looks sad as she picks up a fallen leaf and tucks it into her pocket.\nThis completes the task.\n=====================\nKill Mosscreeper 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\nTask Window Says: You encountered Gralice, a stern spider hunger, as you were climbing out of the nest. She is eager for bloodshed, no matter who it is. Treant have taken over the courtyard in front of you and Gralice is itching for a fight. Try to keep her alive as she hunts the smaller treants. If you kill enough, Mosscreeper will no doubt arrive to defend his minions.\nIf You Get This Step: Clear the nine smaller treants to spawn Mosscreeper, which spawns with three additional treants. Mosscreeper, itself, has ~8 million hitpoints; hits for a max ~13,000; and casts \"Hold the Tree Line\" and \"Creeping Moss\":\nHold the Tree Line: Self 0', Unresistable (0)\n1: Block Melee or Spells (50), Max: 0\n2: Root\nCreeping Moss: Single Target, Disease (0)\n1: Illusion: New Treant\n2: Root\n3: Decrease Hitpoints by 4000 per tick (3 ticks)\n4: Increase AC by 1500\n**Keep Gralice alive or the task ends.**\n=====================\nHunt wild beasts with Charlbroiled Chanon 0/15 (Bixie Warfront)\nTask Window Says: You encountered a bixie spider hunter by the name of Charbroiled Chanon as you were climbing out of the nest. She seems obsessed with cooking everything she kills, and is eager to eat something beside spider meat. Help her hunt wild animals in the small forest clearing above the spiders nest. She'll be able to salvage top -quality inredients from anything you kill, but if you bring injured animals close to her, she'll eagerly help you finish them off.\nIf You Get This Step: DPS mobs to 10% at which point Charlbroiled Chanon kills them.\nCharbroiled Chanon spawns on the group immediately after completing the previous step, and will follow one group member around (like a pet).\nIf you hail her:\nUmbraeques says, 'Hail, Charbroiled Chanon'\nCharbroiled Chanon says, 'Oh, I just love hunting! You bring the beasties close to me when they're weak, and I'll kill them to ensure the tastiest parts are preserved.\nAny mob that's gets to 10% health near her will be killed instantly.\nWhen she kills a mob you see this:\nCharlbroiled Chanon says, 'I'll take it from here, team!'\n\n---\n\n**TASK REWARDS**\n\\- a varying amount of platinum\n\\- a varying amount of experience\n\\- a varying number of Marks of Valor (120-152 reported so far, currency used to buy group gear)\n- Bixie Summoner's Stone [item=113767]\n- Face of Dread [item=113226]\n- Mark of Valor [item=113459]\n- Signet of the Record Master [item=100822]\n- Spidersilk Dread Mask [item=113727]\n- Warlord's Unholy Pendant [item=93813]",
