      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Bixie Warfront [zone=941]\n**Who:**\n- Ambassador Crizlyna [npc=44043]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 75\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Adventure\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 03:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Murky Potion [item=113545]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Bixie Warfront: Assault the Main Hive [zone=958]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a Bixie Guardian [npc=44076]\n- a drunk chemist [npc=44835]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Oct 8 06:05:21 2013\nModified: Tue Feb 13 05:36:37 2024 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n**About Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Heroic adventures in Call of the Forsaken scale in level: As low as **Level 75** and up to current maximum level.\n\\- Scale is based on the highest level player **present in the zone** and affects difficulty, loot quality, and mob levels.\n\\- There is some variation/randomization in the task steps you'll be assigned as you progress through the task.\n\\- Time of completion will vary by your group's makeup (anywhere from 30-90+ minutes).\n\\- Collection items appear as ground spawns midway through tasks (you'll see an emote indicating their appearance).\n\\- Named mobs (or their PHs) spawn midway through tasks (usually, but always, at the same time collection items appear).\n\\- These tasks have individual **3-hour lockout timers** (timer gained upon completion).\n**Experience in Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Mobs in these instances grant some experience, but the bulk of experience is **earned upon task completion**.\n\\- As of a patch in November 2014, less difficult tasks were tuned to reward less experience and more difficult ones were tuned to reward more.\n\\- For an added experience bonus, check out **Guard Hamarn's \"Daily Tasks\"** [quest=7988].\n\n---\n\n_This is a heroic adventure (1-6 players) that begins with Ambassador Crizlyna ( **map image**) in the Bixie Warfront. She is located a short distance north from the portal to the Ethernere Tainted West Karana._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Level 75\n\\- No tasks\n\n---\n\n**TASK SUMMARY**\n\\- Say \"embark on an adventure\" to request the task and \"ready\" to zone in.\n**Step #1:**\n\\- Get instructions from Infiltrator Nallai 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- \"today\" updates the task\n**Step #2:**\n\\- Collect alluring flowers 0/10\n\\-\\-\\- loot 10 flowers from bixies outside the hive\n\\- Acquire royal guard-stamped passes 0/8\n\\-\\-\\- Kill or bribe (100pp) honey-addicted guards until you've collected enough passes\n\\- Find and drink a Bixie Illusion potion 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- \"a drunk chemist\" drops \"Murky Potion\"\n\\- Kill sneaky honey stealers 0/5\n\\-\\-\\- kill 5 of these mobs (note: they phase in and out of sight around the honey moat)\n**Step #3:**\n\\- Gain access to the main hive 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- speak with the keyholder at the front door of the main hive\n**Step #4:**\n\\- Kill fired bixie employees 0/13\n\\-\\-\\- kill 13 \"a fired \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\" mobs inside the hive\n\\- Debate philosophers 0/12\n> **Task Window Text:** The main hive seems to be filled with philosophers debating the meaning and value of war. There seems to be a lot of different opinions. Debate some and see if you can uncover some details about what's causing this hive-wide obsession with war.\n\\-\\-\\- Speak with and, if necessary, kill philosophers inside the hive.\n\\- Collect honeycomb chips 0/10\n\\-\\-\\- These are known to drop from mobs \"a cackling controller\" and \"a mind controlled slurper\".\n**\\- At this point in the task, a named (\"a Bixie Guardian\" or its PH) has a chance to spawn.**\n**Step #5:**\n\\- Debate the master philosopher 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- speak with and kill Jonnagnon the Dreamer\n\\- Kill the juiced warlord 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- kill Kritty the Crusher\n**\\- At this point in the task, collectibles spawn in the zone (ground spawns).**\n**Step #6:**\n\\- Collect creepily violent books 0/20\n\\-\\-\\- click book ground spawns to spawn mobs; ground spawns and mob kills should update\n\\- Collect weird chemicals 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- kill \"a volatile chemist\"; \"a training surgeon\"; and \"a confused patient\" until you've looted enough\n\\- Kill test subject moles 0/3\n\\-\\-\\- kill the three test subject moles\n\\- Kill mutating bixies 0/8\n\\-\\-\\- kill update (note that at 30%, they regen to 100% and strip themselves of debuffs)\n**Step #7:**\n\\- Obtain the first honeycomb 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- kill and loot Hexthresh\n\\- Stop the butterfly slaughter 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- complete mini event: prevent butterfly from being killed\n\\- Kill Kralynisia, the war alchemist 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill the named, Kralynisia\n\\- As soon as the objective for Step #7 is done, the task completes.\n\n---\n\n**NAMED MOBS**\n_\"a Bixie Guardian\" (or its PH) has a chance to spawn after the fourth step is completed. Known loot from this named:_\nLevel 100\nBixie Summoner's Stone\nGuardian's Combat Eyegear\nMetal Guardian Mask\nLevel 95\nVenomtooth\nLevel 90\n???\nLevel 85\n???\n\n---\n\n**TASK IN DETAIL**\n========================================================================\nTRIGGERING THE TASK\n========================================================================\nYou say, 'Hail, Ambassador Crizlyna'\nAmbassador Crizlyna smiles politely and nods to you while lowering herself until her front feet graze the ground, 'Well met, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. I trust you're here on [business]?'\nYou say, 'Business?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'Well, if you're here on vacation, you'll leave disappointed, I'm afraid.' Ambassador Crizlyna smirks, then adjusts her face to a somber grimace and continues, 'Have you heard about the [fate] befallen our poor [Stone Hive allies]?'\nYou say, 'What fate?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'Oh dear, yes. Our esteemed [bixie allies] in the Stone Hive have been corrupted by an evil force. They've turned from [wise protectors of nature] to savage beasts that [lash out] at anything that gets near! This has happened to most [clearly against their will].'\nYou say, 'What about your allies?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna smiles weakly, as if she's had to explain this countless times, 'You may have noticed our skin is a different color than the Stone Hive bixies. We're from the [West River Hive], located south of here along [Turnback River].'\nYou say, 'They were wise protectors of nature?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'Well, yes, of course.' She gives you a stern look and a strained smile, 'You wouldn't criticize our long-standing and respected allies while enjoying the hospitality of our well-protected [camp], would you?''\nYou say, 'How did they lash out?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'As the [Wet River Hive]'s primary ambassador to all of our esteemed allies, I've spent much of my life in the housing of other hives and tribes, ensuring our relations remain strong. Naturally, Her Highness brought me with her on this expedition to discover what our [Stone Hive allies] were up to. I've visited Queen Pelzia on many occasions, but this time, I found I was [not welcome].'\nYou say, 'What is the Wet River Hive?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'There are hundreds of bixie hives, some larger than others. Ours is the other major hive in the region, so we naturally sought an [alliance] with the Stone Hive bixies. Bixies need to work together to ensure mutual success in the face of an increasingly dangerous world filled with monsters, demons, and [gnomes].'\nYou say, 'Gnomes...?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'What?'\nYou say, 'What is the Turnback River'?\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'The river that runs throughout all of Antonica, of course. It's where all of this water around us comes from.' Ambassador Crislyna looks at you like she's concerned you might be a bit stupid, 'You didn't think it was raining in here, did you?''\nYou say, 'What about your camp?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna smiles naturally and resumes a more comfortable posture, 'Her Highness was most wise to personally investigate the [odd behavior] of our Stone Hive allies. Our [military escorts] have kept this camp safe for weeks while our scouts explore the area for [clues].'\nYou say, 'Why are you not welcome by the Queen?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'Their massive [underground hive] is completely surrounded by guards and workers, furiously stirring the honey, preparing for hunts, or getting into brawls in the street. Very unlike bixies to behave in such a brutish manner.' She pauses and looks at you, as if expecting a protest, but continues quickly, 'I was able to get halfway up the front steps before the [crazed guards] closed in.'\nYou say, 'What is this alliance?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'Mostly a non-aggression pact arrangement, with the standard trade arrangements, diplomat exchanges, and safe haven passage, et cetera. I'm sure the details would bore you. What you need to know is that the Stone Hive bixies are our trusted allies, and we will come to their aid in this, their [hour of need], so that...' She pauses to look at you directly, 'opportunistic outsiders won't try to take advantage of their vulnerable situation.''\nYou say, 'Tell me about the military escorts'\nAmbassador Crizlyna looks lustfully at a nearby guard, then catches herself and looks back you with a polite smile, 'Oh yes, I'm sure you've seen them around here. Strong, muscly types.'\nYou say, 'What about these clues?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'Well, you'll have to ask Her Highness, Queen Shulriya Fiume, if you want specifics regarding the more brutish activities. I keep to the [royal chambers] of our allies.'\nYou say, 'What underground hive?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'I'm sure you've seen the Stone Hive located above ground, just east of Blightfire Moors. If you haven't, I highly recommend you [visit] some time. It's quite beautiful. But they've built [another] down here.'\nYou say, 'What crazed guards?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'Their eyes were red, their muscles swollen. Completely consumed by the enraged effect of that [cursed drum]! They practically ripped my wings off as I flew through one of the [waterfalls] back into this cavern.'\nYou say, 'Visit? Me?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'Well, yes, our Stone Hive allies don't much like outsiders such as yourself. They're less tolerant of your violent nature and tendency to [ransack] every place you visit.'\nYou say, 'We don't ransack...'\nAmbassador Crizlyna gives you a patronizing smile and says, 'Let's just say there's a reason we haven't invited you back to our own hive quite yet. But your skills do have their uses, and we'd love for you to visit our allies' [underground hive], where your more forceful tactics are very much needed.'\nYou say, 'Another hive?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'A few months ago, our primary ambassador to the Stone Hive disappeared. When I arrived to investigate the matter, we discovered the Stone Hive bixies were [digging] underground at an alarming rate!'\nYou say, 'Tell me about the waterfalls'\nAmbassador Crizlyna looks proud and brushes some moisture off of her wings, 'While I respect and support all of our allies, being a [Wet River Hive] bixie certainly has its benefits. We embrace the water and the strength it brings us.'\nYou say, 'Digging?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'Well, they mostly used their trained moles for the digging, but the effect was the same. Within a few weeks, they'd dug a massive [cavern system] and filled it with the tools and trainings of [war].'\nYou say, 'What about their cavern system?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'It's marvelous what they've managed to build so quickly. Countless tunnels, dozens of caverns. Factories, dojos, training grounds, homes, and so much more. If they weren't using it all for a doomed [war], I'd applaud them for it.'\nYou say, 'A doomed war?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna sighs and shakes her head, 'I don't understand it. They've become obsessed with conquering Crescent Reach. This corrupting aggression has gotten the best of them, and they feel forced to prove their prowess by slaying dragons. They'll get themselves killed. We must [stop] that.\nYou say, 'Stop it?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'There is still much work to be done at the main hive if we are to ensure our and our allies' safety, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Let me know when you're [ready] to depart.'\nYou say, 'What's this cursed drum?'\nAmbassador Crizlyna's eyes get big for a moment before she composes her face into a fixed smile, 'Drum? I'm sorry, you must've misheard me. Please, I believe we've talked enough now. There is much to be done at the Stone Hive's underground hive. Are you willing to [embark on an adventure] to aid us and our allies? I hope so, after enjoying the safety and hospitality of our camp.'\nYou say, 'I'll embark on an adventure here...'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'Excellent. I believe you'll find there is much to be done in the hive. Let me know when you're [ready] to depart.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Assault the Main Hive'.\nThe Wet River Hive bixies have discovered the source of the Stone Hive's militaristic fury: a magical drum capable of influencing emotions. It's being constantly played at the center of the underground hive to keep bixies obsessed with war. Ambassador Crizlyna has recruited you to help Infiltrator Nallai weaken the hive's defenses for their primary strike force, which will try to sabotage or steal the drum.\nYou say, 'Ready!'\nAmbassador Crizlyna says 'Best of luck to you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. And do try to avoid hurting as many of our allies as you can. We may need them later.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Bixie Warfront.\n========================================================================\nSTEP #1\n========================================================================\nGet instructions from Infiltrator Nallai 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Follow Infiltrator Nallai's dialogues (\"today\")._\nYou say, 'Hail, Infiltrator Nallai'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'Thanks for coming, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. We're in the final stages of [our mission] and you're the only ones I [trust] to help me see it through.'\nYou say, 'Your mission?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'Our [spies] have identified a weak point in the [main hive]'s defenses. We need you to find a way in and [neutralize any threats] inside.'\nYou say, 'Why trust me?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'We've had our rough spots during these missions, but when honey hit the pool, you always had my back. I appreciate that.'\nYou say, 'What have your spies found?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'Thanks for your help in creating openings for our spies to enter the Stone Hive community, by the way. The integrated spies are providing the bulk of our intel, and only a few have [converted].'\nYou say, 'What about the main hive?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'After everything we've seen down here, I guess it's not surprising that the Stone Hive bixies have built another massive hive underground. It's just outside this building, and it's [packed with bixies].'\nYou say, 'Neutralize any threats?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'There's some weird types going in there. The hive seems to serve multiple purposes as a [science lab], [university], and a [government building].'\nYou say, 'Tell me about those converted'\nInfiltrator Nallai looks toward the doorway to make sure no one has snuck inside and whispers, 'You hear that powerful [drum], right?'\nYou say, 'What about science lab?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'I saw a lot of scientists running around inside and out [today]. Prepare yourself for some weird experiments. I doubt they're studying the effects of sleep in there.'\nYou say, 'What about the university?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'Bixies have typically studied the earth and nature, but the students I saw walking in [today] are obsessed with war. One of our spies debated espionage theories with their teacher for over an hour!'\nYou say, 'What about the government building?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'I don't want to get into the details of bixie physiology right now, but, yes, bixies still need a form of government. The senators I've seen walking around the hive aren't prone to diplomacy, if you know what I mean. Luckily, I haven't seen any out there [today].'\nYou say, 'And the drum?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'We believe that the drum is corrupting the Stone Hive bixies' emotions. It's driving them to insane levels of bloodlust, and bringing out their most savage instincts. We need to put an end to it. But before we can do that, we need to clear out the hive. That's what you're going to do [today].'\nYou say, 'Let's do it today'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'Your mission is simple, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Get inside that hive, assess the threats awaiting us, and eliminate anything that'll prevent our strike team from reaching the drum chamber after you.'\n========================================================================\nSTEP #2\n========================================================================\nCollect alluring flowers 0/10 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The bixies around the main hive seem to be obsessed with the local flora. If you can acquire some, the flowers may prove a valuable bargaining chip with the guards blocking your way into the main hive.\n_If You Get This Step: Simply kill mobs outside the hive until you've gotten all 10 updates._\n=====================\nAcquire royal guard-stamped passes 0/10 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill or bribe (100 platinum) honey-addicted guards until you've collected enough passes._\n=====================\nFind and drink a Bixie Illusion potion 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: \"a drunk chemist\" (spawns feigned death among the mobs outside the palace) drops \"Murky Potion\"._\n=====================\nKill sneaky honey stealers 0/5 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: These mobs phase in and out of visibility around the honey moat. Kill five of them to update._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #3\n========================================================================\nGain access to the main hive 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Two grumpy guards near the main hive entrance might be interested in your recent activities. Go speak with them.\n_If You Get This Step: Speak with the guards to open the door to the hive._\n_Without having completed the previous step, you'll see this:_\nYou say, 'Hail, a grumpy keyholder'\na grumpy keyholder looks at you with menacing eyes and grunts, 'You shouldn't be this close to the [hive], \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. You lookin' for a [fight]?'\nYou say, 'Let me in the hive!'\na grumpy keyholder says 'You want in the hive, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_? I'm still going to need to see some official papers or something like that to open the door for you.'\nYou say, 'I want a fight'\na grumpy keyholder spits in your face. 'You're not worth it, scum. Get out of here.'\n_Once on this step, you see:_\nYou say, 'Hail, a grumpy keyholder'\na grumpy keyholder snatches the bundle of flowers from your hands, shoves them in its face, and inhales deeply. It looks at you and says contently, 'How did you know these were my favorite? They normally only have these [inside].'\nYou say, 'I'd like inside now...'\na grumpy keyholder looks at the other hive gate guard and nods.\na grumpy keyholder says 'You want into the hive? We can make an exception for you. Besides, we weren't even paid this week.'\na grumpy keyholder inserts a small golden key into the door and the solidified honey chunk shoots up into the hive wall.\na grumpy keyholder says 'I doubt the crazies inside will be happy to see you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Give that pompous Jonnagnon a punch for me, eh?'\n========================================================================\nSTEP #4\n========================================================================\nKill fired bixie employees 0/13 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The main hive seems to be having some inner trouble. The scientists and supporting staff that are housed are getting kicked out. They're refusing to leave and the situation looks likely to escalate soon. Take out the potential rioters before they strike.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill 13 \"fired\" bixies inside the main hive._\n=====================\nDebate bixie philosophers 0/12 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Speak with and, if necessary, kill philsophers._\n=====================\nCollect honeycomb chips 0/10 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The bixies have captured drakkins from Crescent REach and have found a way to mind-control them! They're currently being forced to eat honey constantly inside the main hive. Kill the slaves or controllers and collect the honeycomb chips inserted into their necks.\n_If You Get This Step: These are known to drop from mobs \"a cackling controller\" and \"a mind controlled slurper\"._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #5\n========================================================================\nDebate the master philosopher 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The main hive bixies highly value the ability to debate the philosophies of war. The master philosopher has emerged from the higher levels of the hive. Debate him to prove your worth.\n_If You Get This Step: Jonnagnon the Dreamer spawns at the top of the steps._\nYou say, 'Hail, Jonnagnon the Dreamer'\nJonnagnon the Dreamer says 'Well met, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. I'm eager to discuss your opinions on war. Which school of thought do you belong to: [pacifism], [eschatological], [political], [realism], [cataclysmic], [just war], or [peace through strength]?'\nYou say, 'Just war...'\nJonnagnon the Dreamer says 'Very well, we can apply morals to war, if you insist. What aspect of war do you object to? The [killings], the [conscription], or the [costs]?'\nYou say, 'The killings...'\nJonnagnon the Dreamer says 'That's my favorite part of war! Allow me to show you why!'\n_Jonnagnon the Dreamer attacks; hits for a max ~15,000, AE rampages, and has a lot of hitpoints. Kill him to update this step._\nJonnagnon the Dreamer has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nA few points of shining light catch your eye.\n=====================\nKill the juiced warlord 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill Kritty the Crusher._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #6\n========================================================================\nCollect creepily violent books 0/20 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Click book ground spawns to spawn mobs (\"a raving writer\"; \"a book slapper\" - AE rampager). Ground spawns and mob kills should combine to update this step._\n=====================\nCollect weird chemicals 0/6 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill \"a volatile chemist\"; \"a training surgeon\"; and \"a confused patient\" until you've looted enough \"Weird Chemicals\"._\n=====================\nKill test subject moles 0/3 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Bixie scientists were conducting brutal experiments on restrained giant moles, but they broke out of their cages and have exacted revenge on their testers. Put these poor creatures out of their misery!\n_If You Get This Step: Head up the main steps and into the side rooms where you'll find the moles. These mobs will buff themselves with either \"Blinking\" (a short-term invulnerable buff), \"Bubbled\" (a rune)._\n=====================\nKill mutating bixies 0/8 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Bixie scientists in the higher levels of the main hive have been looking for ways to increase their strength. Things didn't seem to go well, and the lab appears to be overrun by bixies in different processes of mutation. Clear out the labs.\n_If You Get This Step: DPS \"a mutating bixie\" to 30% at which points it turns into \"a mutated bixie\", strips its debuffs, and regenerates to 100%. Kill the mutated bixie. (Repeat x8)_\n========================================================================\nSTEP #7\n========================================================================\nObtain the first honeycomb 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ At the peak of the main hive, an elder bixie sits inside of an archway, supposedly protecting the first honeycomb ever created on Norrath. If the bodies lying around him are any indication, however, he's become overzealous in his protection of it and has become violent.\n_If You Get This Step: Make your way up the hive and engage Hexthresh (hits for a max ~11,500; AE rampages; is stunnable)._\nHexthresh says 'Unpure eyes may not gaze upon the First Honeycomb and live. Begone, heathens!'\nHexthresh has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nHexthresh's corpse's final act is swallowing the honeycomb whole.\n_Loot the First Honeycomb to complete the task._\n=====================\nStop the butterfly slaughter 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Windo\n\n...[Walkthrough truncated for in-game performance]...",
