      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Dead Hills [zone=942]\n**Who:**\n- Gribble Grobblenobber [ _Heroic Adventures_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 75\n**Maximum Level:** | 130\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Adventure\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 02:37:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Diseased Blood [item=56910]\n- Healing Salve [item=56909]\n- Liquid Ooze [item=56907]\n- Ritual Supplies [item=56911]\n- Xulous Ritual Tome [item=56908]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Dead Hills: Disrupting the Ritual [zone=965]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Deathcaller Vyzol [npc=45170]\n- Gribble Grobblenobber [npc=45171]\n- Ritualist Zorous [npc=45172]\n- Warpriest Poxxil [npc=44100]\n- a captive gnome [npc=45437]\n- a ceremonial fire [npc=45173]\n- a diseased pusling [npc=45164]\n- a failed attempt [npc=45165]\n- a living ooze [npc=45174]\n- a recovering test subject [npc=45179]\n- a risen construct [npc=45166]\n- a sickly test subject [npc=45178]\n- a xulous elder [npc=45175]\n- a xulous elite [npc=45167]\n- a xulous guard [npc=45436]\n- a xulous lorekeeper [npc=45413]\n- a xulous ritualist [npc=45176]\n- a xulous warpriest [npc=45177]\n- an undead adventurer [npc=45168]\n- blood supply [npc=45169]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Daily Task: Heroic Adventures [quest=7988]\n- Gribble #1: Into the Hills [quest=7277]\n- Gribble #2: Scouting Ahead [quest=7278]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Oct 8 06:23:38 2013\nModified: Fri Jan 23 05:55:25 2026 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n**About Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Heroic adventures in Call of the Forsaken scale in level: As low as **Level 75** and up to current maximum level.\n\\- Scale is based on the highest level player **present in the zone** and affects difficulty, loot quality, and mob levels.\n\\- There is some variation/randomization in the task steps you'll be assigned as you progress through the task.\n\\- Time of completion will vary by your group's makeup (anywhere from 30-90+ minutes).\n\\- Collection items appear as ground spawns midway through tasks (you'll see an emote indicating their appearance).\n\\- Named mobs (or their PHs) spawn midway through tasks (usually, but always, at the same time collection items appear).\n\\- These tasks have individual **3-hour lockout timers** (timer gained upon completion).\n**Experience in Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Mobs in these instances grant some experience, but the bulk of experience is **earned upon task completion**.\n\\- As of a patch in November 2014, less difficult tasks were tuned to reward less experience and more difficult ones were tuned to reward more.\n\\- For an added experience bonus, check out **Guard Hamarn's \"Daily Tasks\"** [quest=7988].\n\n---\n\n_This is a heroic adventure (1-6 players) that begins with Gribble Grobblenobber ( **click for map**) in the Dead Hills. He is located outside a tent in the dock camp just west of the zone-in point._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Level 75\n\\- Completed \"Into the Hills\" (heroic adventure)\n\\- Completed \"Scouting Ahead\" (heroic adventure)\n\n---\n\n**TASK SUMMARY**\n\\- Say \"stop\" to request the task and \"go\" to zone in.\n**Step #1:**\n\\- Use ooze to extinguish the ceremonial fires 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- Loot \"Liquid Ooze\" from living oozes and click them over \"a ceremonial fire\"\n\\- Destroy ritual tomes by tossing them in the fires 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- Kill ritualist mobs, the ritual tomes, and hand the tomes to the fires\n\\- Dig up graves and kill the undead that rest within 0/12\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update\n**Step #2:**\n\\- Kill all failed attempts 0/16\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update\n\\- Use ritual supplies to perform a counter ritual 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill xulous mobs around the graves until you've looted six ritual supplies, then right-click the items\n\\- Stop the xulous ritualists from carrying out the resurrection ritual 0/16\n\\-\\-\\- Kill 16 ritualist mobs\n**Step #3:**\n\\- Free gnomes from captivity 0/4\n\\-\\-\\- Kill Xulous mobs around the gnomes to free them\n\\- Cure the test subjects using healing salves from xulous warpriests 0/4\n\\-\\-\\- Kill xulous warpriests, loot \"Healing Salve\", right-click them on gnome test subjects\n\\- Taint the bloody supply boxes with diseased blood 0/4\n\\-\\-\\- Kill diseased puslings until you've collected 4 bloods, then hand the blood to the supply boxes\n**\\- The task locks upon completion of Step #3.**\n**Step #4:**\n\\- Defeat a risen construct 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update\n\\- Kill Ritualist Zurous 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update\n\\- Defeat Deathcaller Vyzol 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update\n**\\- At this point in the task, collectibles spawn in the zone (ground spawns) and a named (or its PH) has a chance to spawn.**\n**Step #5:**\n\\- Speak to Gribble Grobblenobber to return to camp 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update to complete the task\n\\- As soon as the objective for Step #5 is done, the task completes.\n\n---\n\n**NAMED MOBS**\n_Warpriest Poxxil (or its PH, \"a xulous elite\") has a chance to spawn after the third step is completed. You'll see this emote if Warpriest Poxxil spawns:_\nThe ground trembles as Poxxil appears.\n_Known loot from this named:_\nLevel 100\nMantle of Change\nSpellbinder's Scarf\nLevel 95\nClampgrit's Pronged Spear\nIrebound Band\nKelkos' Beaded Girdle\nPoleaxe of Order\nLevel 90\n???\nLevel 85\n???\n\n---\n\n!\n\n---\n\n**TASK IN DETAIL**\n========================================================================\nTRIGGERING THE TASK\n========================================================================\nYou say, 'Hail, Gribble Grobblenobber'\nGribble Grobblenobber says 'So the descendants of Bertoxxulous have made a home in the Dead Hills? I guess it makes sense. This place seems alive with filth and decay, allowing the xulous to thrive while they capture innocent adventures to use in their ritual sacrifices. We can't let them raise their behemoths. Can you imagine the amount of destruction an undead golem the size of a mountain could do? Ak`Anon would be obliterated with one step! We need to [stop] the ritual.'\nYou say, 'How do we stop it?'\nGribble Grobblenobber says 'I think this plan of you going ahead and me sticking behind has been working out pretty well. Why mess up a good thing? Just say when you're ready to [go], and I'll be right behind you.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Disrupting the Ritual'.\nGribble Grobblenobber would like your help with discovering what lies within the northwestern hills.\nYou say, 'Let's go'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered The Dead Hills.\n========================================================================\nSTEP #1\n========================================================================\nUse ooze to extinguish the ceremonial fires 0/6 (Dead Hills)\n_Task Window Says:_ Use ooze on the ceremonial fires to extinguish them.\n_If You Get This Step: Loot \"Liquid Ooze\" from living oozes and right-click them over \"a ceremonial fire\"._\n=====================\nDestroy ritual tomes by tossing them in the fires 0/6 (Dead Hills)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill xulous elders and loot 6x \"Xulous Ritual Tome\". After acquiring the necessary books, simply \"give\" (trade action) them to the ritual campfires to complete the step._\n=====================\nDig up graves and kill the undead that rest within 0/12 (Dead Hills)\n_Task Window Says:_ Click on graves to dig them up.\n_If You Get This Step: Around the ruins just ahead of the zone-in are clickable gravesites. Clicking on a grave spawns 2x \"an undead adventurer\" (these don't auto-aggro, but they do see invis). These mobs hit for a max ~12,000 (stunnable/mezzable/rootable)._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #2\n========================================================================\nKill all failed attempts 0/16 (Dead Hills)\n_Task Window Says:_ Slaughter all failed attempts that linger within the xulous ruins.\n_If You Get This Step: These are kill updates found in the clearing ahead. They hit for a max ~13,800 (stunnable/mezzable/rootable)._\n=====================\nUse ritual supplies to perform a counter ritual 0/1 (Dead Hills)\n_Task Window Says:_ Once you have enough supplies, right-click them to perform a counter ritual.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill xulous mobs around the graves until you've looted 6x \"Ritual Supplies\", then right-click the supplies to update the step._\n=====================\nStop the xulous ritualists from carrying out the resurrection ritual 0/16 (Dead Hills)\n_Task Window Says:_ Kill the ritualists before they being their behemoths back to life!\n_If You Get This Step: Kill 16 ritualist mobs._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #3\n========================================================================\nFree gnomes from captivity 0/4 (Dead Hills)\n_Task Window Says:_ Defeat the xulous surrounding captive gnomes in order to free them.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill \"a Xulous guard\" around each of the gnomes. These mobs hit for a max ~12,500 and are mezzable/stunneable._\n=====================\nCure the test subjects using healing salves from xulous warpriests 0/4 (Dead Hills)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill xulous warpriests, loot \"Healing Salve\", and right-click them on the gnome test subjects._\n=====================\nTaint the bloody supply boxes with diseased blood 0/4 (Dead Hills)\n_Task Window Says:_ Place diseased blood within the bloody supply boxes to ruin the ritual blood supply. Diseased blood can be found from diseased creatures.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill and loot \"a diseased pusling\" until you've gathered four \"Diseased Blood\" items, then give them to the supply boxes._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #4\n========================================================================\nDefeat a risen construct 0/1 (Dead Hills)\n_Task Window Says:_ A risen construct has appeared within the ruins.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill \"a risen construct\". This mob has a few more hitpoints than standard mobs in the zone, doesn't cast any AEs, and doesn't appear to do much more DPS than an average mob._\n=====================\nDefeat Ritualist Zurous 0/1 (Dead Hills)\n_Task Window Says:_ Ritualist Zurous has appeared within the ruins.\n_If You Get This Step: This appears to be a straight melee fight._\n=====================\nDefeat Deathcaller Vyzol 0/1\n_Task Window Says:_ Deathcaller Vyzol has appeared within the ruins.\n_If You Get This Step: There isn't anything special about Deathcaller Vyzol. He is a necromancer, and has a few more hitpoints than a typical mob._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #5\n========================================================================\nSpeak to Gribble Grobblenobber to return to camp 0/1 (Dead Hills)\n_Task Window Says:_ Speak to Gribble Grobblenobber at the start of the path to return to camp.\n_If You Get This Step: Hail update for task completion._\nYou say, 'Hail, Gribble Grobblenobber'\nGribble Grobblenobber says 'Interesting discoveries, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Let's talk [back] at the camp where it's safe.'\n_After having completed his task arc, he responds to hails as such:_\nGribble Grobblenobber says 'We may have stopped the xulous for now, but we can't let up! They still linger in the northwest, snatching up adventurers to use in their cruel experiments. We should continue to pummel their forces, so they don't have a chance to rebuild and continue the ritual. Are you [willing] to fight?'\n\n---\n\n**TASK REWARDS**\n\\- a varying amount of platinum\n\\- a varying amount of experience\n\\- a varying number of Marks of Valor (currency used to buy group gear)\n- Mark of Valor [item=113459]",
