      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Neriak Fourth Gate [zone=943]\n**Who:**\n- Prince Tarant Thex [ _Dreadguard_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Related Zones:**\n- Neriak Fourth Gate: Houses of Thex [zone=951]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Bloodguard [npc=45454]\n- Bone Crusher [npc=45130]\n- King Naythox Thex [npc=45127]\n- Nightmare Devourer [npc=45129]\n- Queen Cristanos Thex [npc=45128]\n- a power-loaded crystal [npc=45462]\n- a servant [npc=45452]\n- a treasure chest - Houses of Thex [npc=45126]\n- a voracious ghoul [npc=45486]\n- an energy pulse [npc=45453]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Neriak #1: The Missing Scroll [quest=7283]\n- Neriak #2: Fourth Gate Investigation [quest=7284]\n- Neriak #3: Cautious Recruitment [quest=7285]\n- Raid Expedition: Houses of Thex [quest=7287]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Oct 8 07:06:36 2013\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is a group mission that begins with Prince Tarant Thex ( **click for map**) in Neriak Fourth Gate._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completed \"The Missing Scroll\"\n\\- Completed \"Fourth Gate Investigation\"\n\\- Completed \"Cautious Recruitment\"\n\\- Must be illusioned as a Dark Elf\nYou say, 'Hail, Prince Tarant Thex'\nPrince Tarant Thex says 'You? I had not expected you to dare to return here. I should slay you for your impertinence, but I might have need of you. Are you here with just a small [group], or have you actually brought a [force] with you?'\nYou say, 'I have a group...'\nPrince Tarant Thex says 'Normally I would never involve outsiders in family matters, but these are unusual times. The king and queen have been at war for decades. Their battles have always been quiet and indirect. But recently both have seen [divinations] from some other realm, and that has changed things.'\nYou say, 'Divinations?'\nPrince Tarant Thex says 'I haven't seen them, and obviously they don't confide in me. What I know is that they have had visions of powerful creatures -- golems, actually -- from some other realm. They have been building these creatures and plan to use them to [defeat each other]. Perfect, really: They don't have to get directly into battle with each other and therefore don't risk looking weak if they lose.'\nYou say, 'Defeat each other?'\nPrince Tarant Thex says 'Fools. They want each other dead but won't take any real risks. Their hatred for each other is matchless, but their unwillingness to fail is just as great. I can't interfere; I can't risk the wrath of both of them. But they hate you immensely already, as any dark elf will. You could go and [defeat these golems]. As long as they both lose, then things won't change. If one of them gains control of the dark elves the world would certainly change in a way you would not appreciate.'\nYou say, 'We'll defeat these golems'\nPrince Tarant Thex says 'Good. Go then. I can send you to where they confront each other even now, as soon as you are [prepared].'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Houses of Thex'.\nThe prince has asked you to help defuse the upcoming conflict between the king and queen. To do this, he believes you will need to destroy both the golems they have created.\nYou say, 'I am prepared...'\nPrince Tarant Thex says 'Go then. I shall send a servant to return you if you need to flee or if by some miracle you manage to complete your task.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\n\n---\n\n**Task Steps**\nSpeak with King or Queen Thex 0/1 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\nKill both of the golems 0/2 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\nOpen the chest for your reward 0/1 Neriak Fourth Gate)\n\n---\n\n**Triggering the Event**\n_All mobs are non-aggro until the event is triggered. Speak with either the Queen or the King to trigger the event._\n_With the Queen, you see:_\nYou say, 'Hail, Queen Cristanos Thex'\nQueen Cristanos Thex shouts 'What are you doing here, scum? Go away. [What happens] here has nothing to do with you.'\nYou say, 'What happens?'\nQueen Cristanos Thex shouts 'This is of NO MATTER TO YOU! Begone! If you [interfere] in any way, I will destroy you and use your corpse as a scullery maid!'\nYou say, 'Me? Interfere?'\nQueen Cristanos Thex shouts 'That can be the only reason you are here. Fine, the king will have to wait. I will destroy you first!'\nKing Naythox Thex shouts 'In this one thing, wife, I will join in your hatred. But when they are slain we will finish what we started!'\n_With the King, you see:_\nYou say, 'Hail, King Naythox Thex'\nKing Naythox Thex shouts 'Well, it's you. I see you've come to witness the queen's [fall]. Please hold back your laughter at her suffering. I want her to hear mine.'\nYou say, 'Her fall?'\nKing Naythox Thex shouts 'Of course she will fail. That is her destiny. You just [sit aside] and watch. Do NOT interfere. I know you will wish to assist me, but I can't allow that. Her defeat must be at my hands.'\nYou say, 'We will not sit aside!'\nKing Naythox Thex shouts 'I said, stay out of this. If you [insist] on interfering, I won't hesitate to kill you first.'\nYou say, 'We insist!'\nKing Naythox Thex shouts 'Well then, my dear wife will have to wait.'\nQueen Cristanos Thex shouts 'No, husband. I will help you destroy them. This is NOT their affair!'\n_Once they're done shouting at each other, the two golems aggro (zonewide auto-aggro on anyone in the zone)._\n\n---\n\n**The Golems**\n_To complete the event, you have to kill both \"Bone Crusher\" and \"Nightmare Devourer\". There are no balancing or proximity requirements, and they have fairly long leash ranges (will warp back to spawn point if leashed)._\n_Due to their mechanics, you'll probably want to keep them separated from each other._\n_Each golem hits for a max ~12,500 and has some tricks._\n\n---\n\n**Bone Crusher**\n_Bone Crusher has a few emotes:_\nBone Crusher shouts 'Sooo cooooold!'\n\\-\\-\\- _5-second warning for the AE \"Cold Jolt\":_\nCold Jolt: PB AE 110', Chromatic (-850)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 53846\n2: Decrease Movement by 50%\n3: Inhibit Melee Attacks by (35%)\nGet the one called \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, my creation!\n\\-\\-\\- _10-second warning for the targeted AE \"Sonic Jolt\":_\nSonic Jolt: Targeted AE 75', Chromatic (-850)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 23076 per tick\n2: Increase Effective Casting Level by 85\n_As long as Bone Crusher is a live, auras called \"an energy pulse\" will appear from the cave behind King Naythox Thex. These auras will target a specific player, who should kite the aura around until it dissipates. The auras move at a very slow speed, so should be easy for any class to kite. Anyone caught in one of these auras will have \"Jolt\" chain-casted upon them._\nAn energy pulse moves toward \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.\n\\-\\-\\- _This is the emote that indicates the aura's target._\nJolt: Single Target, Chromatic (-900)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 20000\n2: Stun (0.05 sec)\n**There may be another emote missing here (what is it?)**, one which indicates the spawn of \"a power-loaded crystal\" which AEs \"Explosive Response\":\nExplosive Response: PB AE 45', Unresistable (-900)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 80000\n2: Knockback (5) and Toss Up (5)\n\n---\n\n**Nightmare Devourer**\n_Nightmare Devourer has an aura around it, \"Cartilage Decay\":_\nCartilage Decay: Single Target, Chromatic (-850)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 10000 per tick\n2: Decrease Movement by 25%\n_It also buffs itself \"Death's Echo\" throughout the event:_\nDeath's Echo: Self 0', Unresistable (0)\n1: Increase Chance to Reflect Spell by 20%\n_It has one emote-based spell attack._\nThe one called \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_! Take that one's essence, my pet!\n\\-\\-\\- _10-second warning for the targeted AE \"Grave Chill\":_\nGrave Chill: Targeted AE 75', Chromatic (-900)\n1: Decrease Mana by 2000 per tick\n2: Inhibit Melee Attacks by (70%)\n3: Decrease Attack Speed by 170%\n_Nightmare Devourer spawns health-based adds called \"a voracious ghoul\" ( **at what health points, specifically?**). Note that these adds despawn upon the event's completion._\n\n---\n\n**Completion**\n_Kill the two golems to complete the event._\nKing Naythox Thex shouts 'Impossible! I guess you knew you could not defeat me, Cristanos. If you must rely on outsiders to ensure your survival, then surely you and your followers are doomed. Come, it is time we retired.'\nQueen Cristanos Thex shouts 'What? You fool! My hatred for you grows even stronger! Come, we have plans to make.'\n_Rewards:_\nExperience\n225 platinum\n_Possible Chest Loot (1 item + 0-1 armor piece + 0-1 Rk. II spell):_\nBloodletting Epee\nDarklight Archon Earring\nDarklight Emblem\nMaster of Beasts Earring\nStud of Lost Life\nBracer of Latent Ether\nGloves of Latent Ether\nHelm of Latent Ether\nLeggings of Latent Ether\nSong: Brusco's Burning Call Rk. II\nSpell: Anticipated Interposition Rk. II\nSpell: Natural Unity Rk. II\nSpell: Permeating Ice Rk. II\nSpell: Remote Relentless Servant Rk. II\nSpell: Shout of the Bosquetender Rk. II\nSpell: Spiritual Unity Rk. II\nTome: Last Stand Discipline Rk. II\nTome: Sting of the Wasp Rk. II\n- Bloodletting Epee [item=113811]\n- Bracer of Latent Ether [item=113263]\n- Darklight Archon Earring [item=113786]\n- Darklight Emblem [item=113792]\n- Gloves of Latent Ether [item=113373]\n- Helm of Latent Ether [item=113264]\n- Leggings of Latent Ether [item=113265]\n- Master of Beasts Earring [item=113988]\n- Song: Brusco's Burning Call Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Spell: Anticipated Interposition Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Spell: Natural Unity Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Spell: Permeating Ice Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Spell: Remote Relentless Servant Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Spell: Shout of the Bosquestalker Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Spell: Spiritual Unity Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Stud of Lost Life [item=113932]\n- Tome: Last Stand Discipline Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Tome: Sting of the Wasp Rk. II [tradeable]",
    },
