Jan 22 03:43:32 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n**About Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Heroic adventures in Call of the Forsaken scale in level: As low as **Level 75** and up to current maximum level.\n\\- Scale is based on the highest level player **present in the zone** and affects difficulty, loot quality, and mob levels.\n\\- There is some variation/randomization in the task steps you'll be assigned as you progress through the task.\n\\- Time of completion will vary by your group's makeup (anywhere from 30-90+ minutes).\n\\- Collection items appear as ground spawns midway through tasks (you'll see an emote indicating their appearance).\n\\- Named mobs (or their PHs) spawn midway through tasks (usually, but always, at the same time collection items appear).\n\\- These tasks have individual **3-hour lockout timers** (timer gained upon completion).\n**Experience in Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Mobs in these instances grant some experience, but the bulk of experience is **earned upon task completion**.\n\\- As of a patch in November 2014, less difficult tasks were tuned to reward less experience and more difficult ones were tuned to reward more.\n\\- For an added experience bonus, check out **Guard Hamarn's \"Daily Tasks\"** [quest=7988].\n\n---\n\n_This is a heroic adventure (1-6 players) that begins with Lark D`Tradis ( **click for map image**) in Neriak Fourth Gate. She is located at 600, -1800, 67 (outside the tunnel due north of the bridge in the far northeastern part of the zone)._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Level 75\n\\- Completed \"The Toll Road\" (heroic adventure)\n\n---\n\n**TASK SUMMARY**\n\\- Say \"continue\" to request the task and \"ready to go\" to zone in.\n**Step #1:**\n\\- Clear a path to sealed library 0/7\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update (brainwashed Teir`Dal knights and wizards).\n\\- Clear a path to sealed library 0/7\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update (undead mobs).\n**Step #2:**\n\\- Obtain the library key from an ousted librarian 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill ousted librarians until you loot a key (each librarian has two aggro-linked guards).\n\\- Destroy the crystals that shield the library doors 0/4\n\\-\\-\\- Kill the four crystals (each has two aggro-linked guards).\n**\\- The task LOCKS at this point.**\n**Step #3:**\n\\- Attempt to enter the sealed library 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Click on the door (if a key was looted in previous step, the player with the key needs to click).\n**\\- At this point in the task, collectibles spawn in the zone (ground spawns) and a named (or its PH) has a chance to spawn.**\n**Step #4:**\n\\- Defeat Shirik's ethereal guard 0/12\n\\-\\-\\- Kill 12 undead mobs; these spawn one at a time and attack (up to three mobs can be up at a time).\n**Step #5:**\n\\- Defeat Shirik's constructed guardian 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- DPS the gargoyle to 8% health.\n\\- Defeat Diran D`Tradis 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Aggro's after previous step completed; spawns an add at 76%, 31%, and 6% (locks health until adds are killed).\n**Step #6:**\n\\- Speak with Lark 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update\n\\- As soon as the objective for Step #6 is done, the task completes.\n\n---\n\n**MAP**\n!\n\n---\n\n**NAMED MOBS**\n_\"Rilen D`Tradis\" (or its PH, \"a Teir`Dal captain\") spawns after the third step is completed. Known loot from this named:_\nAegis of Prince's Court\nBoots of Latent Ether\nGuardian Ornament\nTome: Last Stand Discipline Rk. II\n\n---\n\n**TASK IN DETAIL**\n========================================================================\nTRIGGERING THE TASK\n========================================================================\nYou say, 'Hail, Lark D`Tradis'\nLark D`Tradis says, in Dark Elvish, 'I find it strange that those red eyed madmen all spoke Elder Teir`Dal, such a dialect is rare to hear even in the royal houses. Stranger still is the resistance we're facing in finding my father, even in his most reclusive hours I was always able to speak to him..' She sighs, looking more worried by the moment, 'If you are ready to [continue] on toward the library, just let me know.''\nYou say, 'Let's continue'\nLark D`Tradis says, in Dark Elvish, 'Excellent, are you [ready to go] now?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Sealed Gate'.\nUsing the information you gathered on your previous outing, Lark is sure her father has barricaded himself in the central library. She's still unsure what foolish endeavor he has undertaken, but needs your help to reach him before he does anything to endanger himself.\nYou say, 'Ready to go!'\nLark D`Tradis says, in Dark Elvish, 'I shall meet you on the road. I believe it was this way...'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Neriak - Fourth Gate.\n========================================================================\nSTEP #1\n========================================================================\nClear a path to sealed library 0/7 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n**Task Window Says:** Using the information you've gathered on your previous outing, Lark is sure her father has barricaded himself in the central library. She's still unsure what foolish endeavor he has undertaken, but needs your help to reach him before he does anything to endanger himself.\nAnother group of soldiers stands guard on the road leading to the sealed library. There is nothing unsettling in their lifeless demeanor.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill update (brainwashed Teir`Dal knights and wizards)._\n=====================\nClear a path to sealed library 0/7 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ A small group of undead constructs has gathered to stand watch on the road leading to the library. Return their bones to the dust of the earth to gain safe entrance to the sealed chambers.\n_If You Get This Step: Standard kill update -- any undead mobs around the zone-in area count towards the step._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #2\n========================================================================\nObtain the library key from an ousted librarian 0/1 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill ousted librarians until you loot a key (each librarian has two aggro-linked guards)._\n=====================\nDestroy the crystals that shield the library doors 0/4 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ A powerful magical force emanates from the library doors. In the distance you spot a pillar of light feeding energy to the sealed chambers. Dispersing this power at its source will surely expedite your entry.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill the four resonating crystals in the area. Each has two aggro-linked \"a shield \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\" mobs that hit for a max ~14,000 (stunnable; mezzable; charmable, but very resistant). Note that the focuser is an enchanter and will have buffed both with haste, and will cast mez spells on players. The crystals themselves have a fair amount of hitpoints, but don't attack back._\nThe door feels hot to the touch and immobile as if held in place by some great force.\n_After the crystals are destroyed, you see:_\nA brief flash of light fills the cavern as the crystal shatters into tiny fragments.\n========================================================================\nSTEP #3\n========================================================================\nAttempt to enter the sealed library 0/1 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ Make your way back to the library door and attempt to open it.\n_If You Get This Step: Click on the door (if a key was looted in previous step, the player with the key needs to click). NOTE: Doing this leads to the trigger of three aggro mobs._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #4\n========================================================================\nDefeat Shirik's ethereal guard 0/12 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ A hoard of necromantic beasts has come to halt your ingress. It seems Shirik truly does not want anyone interfering with his plans!\n_If You Get This Step: After attempting to open the library door, three undead mobs spawn and attack (hit for a max ~12,000; single-target rampage; flurry; stunnable; mezzable). You'll have to kill 12 mobs here. Each time you kill a mob, another one rushes in and attacks, up to a total of 12._\nThe anguished cries of the dead fill the air as necromantic guardians run through the library doors.\n_Note that if you drop aggro, the mobs will stay up and idle._\n_WARNING: Right after this step completes, a short script unfolds and then a named becomes aggro in front of the library doors._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #5\n========================================================================\nDefeat Shirik's constructed guardian 0/1 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: After the previous step is completed, the gargoyle above the library aggro's and attacks. DPS it to 8% health to update the step._\n_It has four stances:_\n\\- Normal (lasts for first 25 seconds of the fight and does not repeat).\n_After the initial 25 seconds passes, the following three stances cycle:_\n\\- Enraged (lasts for 15 seconds)\n_\\-\\-\\- immune to ranged DPS; frequently AE rampages; hasted attacks._\n\\- Shielded (lasts for 10 seconds)\n_\\-\\-\\- rooted in place; susceptible to ranged attacks; for every nuke or DOT cast on it AND for every 2% damage to it, casts directional AEs for 61k dmg (left/right/rear)._\n\\- Weakened (lasts for 15 seconds)\n_\\-\\-\\- becomes unrooted; hasted attack speed._\n=====================\nDefeat Diran D`Tradis 0/1 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ Diran D`Tradis, Lark's elder half-brother, has been surveying your attempts to enter his father's fortress and has taken it upon himself to stop you. If saving Shirik means killing his power-crazed heirs, then so be it. Defeat him to gain entrance to the library.\n_If You Get This Step: Diran D`Tradis aggro's after a short script completes, following the previous step._\nThe sound of mockingly slow applause echoes out over the library.\nA calm voice speaks in Elder Teir`Dal, 'So much bloodshed for a such misguided cause. Tell me, sister, why put these fools up to this?'\nLark D`Tradis looks up toward the top of the library, 'Brother? W... why has father done all of this?'\nDiran D`Tradis glares down at his younger sibling with contempt, 'Always the fool, Songbird. Our dealings are none of your interest or concern. Must I slaughter your misguided allies to get you to leave us, or will cowardice simply overtake you again?'\nLark D`Tradis clenches her fist, choking back tears, 'Enough! You know better than anyone father will be killed for this revolt!'\nDiran D`Tradis leaps down from the library's catwalk, landing with surprising grace for a fully armored knight.\nDiran D`Tradis grins and calls out to you, 'Stop us, if you can!'\nDiran D`Tradis says, in Elder Teir'Dal, 'Make peace with your gods.'\n_Diran D`Tradis hits for a max ~21,000; single-target rampages; and flurries. He has a lot of hitpoints and spawns a single add at 76%, 31%, and 6% (locks health until adds are killed). The adds hit for a max ~12,000 and are stunnable. As an add spawns, you see this emote:_\nDiran D`Tradis calls fourth a loyal guardian to bolster his defenses. _(sic)_)\nDiran`s guardian has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nA disembodied voice says, 'Turn back.'\nDiran D`Tradis has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nDiran D`Tradis's corpse shouts, 'Sister, know well that you have damned our family!'\nLark D`Tradis says, in Dark Elvish, 'I am so sorry, brother...'\n========================================================================\nSTEP #6\n========================================================================\nSpeak with Lark 0/1 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ Speak with Lark to determine your next move.\n_If You Get This Step: Hail Lark to complete the task._\nYou say, 'Hail, Lark D`Tradis'\nLark D`Tradis does her best to contain her sobbing, 'Brother...' She takes a moment to regain a measure of her composure, 'Though we were never particularly famous, our family is known for two things throughout Neriak, green eyes and mastery of elemental magic. Strange as it may sound, we've never studied necromancy. I fear now that it is not my father we will find within the library but his captors.'\nWhatever lies within the sealed library will put an end to Lark's worries, one way or another...\n\n---\n\n**TASK REWARDS**\n\\- a varying amount of platinum\n\\- a varying amount of experience\n\\- a varying number of Marks of Valor (currency used to buy group gear)\n- Aegis of Prince's Court [item=114724]\n- Boots of Latent Ether [item=114720]\n- Guardian Ornament [item=115072]\n- Mark of Valor [item=113459]\n- Tome: Last Stand Discipline Rk. II [tradeable]",
