      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Neriak Fourth Gate [zone=943]\n**Who:**\n- Lark D`Tradis [npc=45653]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 75\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 03:00:00\n**Related Zones:**\n- Neriak Fourth Gate: Late Checkout [zone=981]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Bloody Tome [npc=45663]\n- Lark D`Tradis [npc=45920]\n- Rylit, Tarant`s Arcanist [npc=45921]\n- Shirik D`Tradis [npc=45923]\n- Shirik`s Corrupted Guardian [npc=45922]\n- a Teir`Dal arcanist [npc=45917]\n- a dormant book [npc=45913]\n- a heretic of hate [npc=45914]\n- a projection of hate [npc=45915]\n- a sorcerer of hate [npc=45916]\n- an agent of hate [npc=45918]\n- an assassin of hate [npc=45919]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Daily Task: Heroic Adventures [quest=7988]\n- Lark #1: The Toll Road [quest=7396]\n- Lark #2: The Sealed Gate [quest=7397]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Jan 22 03:44:37 2014\nModified: Thu Oct 24 20:38:25 2024 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n**About Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Heroic adventures in Call of the Forsaken scale in level: As low as **Level 75** and up to current maximum level.\n\\- Scale is based on the highest level player **present in the zone** and affects difficulty, loot quality, and mob levels.\n\\- There is some variation/randomization in the task steps you'll be assigned as you progress through the task.\n\\- Time of completion will vary by your group's makeup (anywhere from 30-90+ minutes).\n\\- Collection items appear as ground spawns midway through tasks (you'll see an emote indicating their appearance).\n\\- Named mobs (or their PHs) spawn midway through tasks (usually, but always, at the same time collection items appear).\n\\- These tasks have individual **3-hour lockout timers** (timer gained upon completion).\n**Experience in Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Mobs in these instances grant some experience, but the bulk of experience is **earned upon task completion**.\n\\- As of a patch in November 2014, less difficult tasks were tuned to reward less experience and more difficult ones were tuned to reward more.\n\\- For an added experience bonus, check out **Guard Hamarn's \"Daily Tasks\"** [quest=7988].\n\n---\n\n_This is a heroic adventure (1-6 players) that begins with Lark D`Tradis ( **click for map image**) in Neriak Fourth Gate. She is located at 600, -1800, 67 (outside the tunnel due north of the bridge in the far northeastern part of the zone)._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Level 75\n\\- Completed \"The Toll Road\" (heroic adventure)\n\\- Completed \"The Sealed Gate\" (heroic adventure)\n\n---\n\n**TASK SUMMARY**\n\\- Say \"continue\" to request the task and \"ready to go\" to zone in.\n**Step #1:**\n\\- Investigate the first floor of the library 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Location update.\n**Step #2:**\n\\- Defeat the Arcanist's guardians 0/12\n\\-\\-\\- Kill the dark elves and ghosts around the room.\n**\\- The task LOCKS at this point.**\n**Step #3:**\n\\- Defeat Shirik's Corrupted Guardian 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill Shirik's Corrupted Guardian.\n**\\- At this point in the task, collectibles spawn in the zone (ground spawns) and a named (or its PH) has a chance to spawn.**\n**Step #4:**\n\\- Clear a path to the upper floor 0/8\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update.\n**Step #5:**\n\\- Look for Shirik D`Tradis 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Location update and script trigger.\n**Step #6:**\n\\- Defeat Rylit, Tarant`s Arcanist 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Five ghosts; DPS 10% of each one's health at which point it will reveal itself as either 'fake' or 'real' (repeat x5 until 'real one' is dead).\n**Step #7:**\n\\- Speak with Lark 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update.\n\\- As soon as the objective for Step #7 is done, the task completes.\n\n---\n\n**NAMED MOBS**\n_\"Bloody Tome\" (or its PH, \"a hatestorm dervish\") has a chance to spawn after the third step is completed. Known loot from this named:_\nGuardian Ornament\nLongbow of the Royal Court\n\n---\n\n**TASK IN DETAIL**\n========================================================================\nTRIGGERING THE TASK\n========================================================================\nYou say, 'Hail, Lark D`Tradis'\nLark D`Tradis says, in Dark Elvish, 'I'm no longer convinced these traps and obstacles are my father's doing, all of this is unlike him. I fear someone or something is controlling him and my brothers. I just hope we can get to him in time. If you are ready to [continue] I'm sure the end to this journey lies in that library.'\nYou say, 'Let's continue...'\nLark D`Tradis says, in Dark Elvish, 'Excellent, are you [ready to go] now?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Late Checkout'.\nLark no longer fears that her father aims to bring about his own destruction. She is convinced someone or something is manipulating him and her family. Whatever it may be, the answer rests within the sealed library.\nYou say, 'Ready to go!'\nLark D`Tradis says, in Dark Elvish, 'I shall meet you on the road. I believe it was this way...'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Neriak - Fourth Gate.\n\n---\n\n3. Investigate the first floor of the library 0/1 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n\n\n\n\n\n> _Task Window Says:_ Though the flames at the entrance of the library have dissipated, the first floor is uncomfortably warm. However, the end of this story stands in the center of the room.\n\n\n\n_If You Get This Step: This is a location update._\n\n\n\na Teir`Dal arcanist says, in Elder Teir'Dal, 'So the songbird returns to the nest...'\n\n\n\n\nLark D`Tradis shouts, in Dark Elvish, 'What have you done to my father!?'\n\n\n\n\na Teir`Dal arcanist says, in Elder Teir'Dal, 'The old man has proved invaluable to my master. So easily drawing away the attention of the divided houses while we work.'\n\n\n\n\nLark D`Tradis shouts, in Dark Elvish, 'Answer me!'\n\n\n\n\na Teir`Dal arcanist says, in Elder Teir'Dal, 'We are not quite done with him, but your mercenaries are proving to be quite a distraction.'\n\n\n\n\nThe wizard raises his hands in the air and the hall begins to shake.\n\n\n\n\nA great shockwave throws you backwards against the wall.\n\n\n\n\n_Everyone is warped back to the zone-in and feigned death._\n\n4. Defeat the Arcanist's guardians 0/12 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n\n\n\n\n\n> _Task Window Says:_ The wizard who has been manipulating Shirik's gargoyle has shielded himself from intrusion. Defeat his guardians to destroy the shield preventing you from entering the center of the room.\n\n\n\n_If You Get This Step: Kill the dark elves and ghosts in the room (nothing particularly special about them; the dark elves are a bit harder than the ghosts)._\n\n\n\na Teir`Dal arcanist shouts, in Elder Teir'Dal, 'Fight all you want, you'll never save him!'\n\n\n\n\nAs the final guardian falls the shield protecting the center of the room dissipates.\n\n\n\n\na Teir`Dal arcanist shouts, in Elder Teir'Dal, 'Very well, Songbird. Let us see which of your father's creations shall survive this confrontation!'\n\n5. Defeat Shirik's Corrupted Guardian 0/1 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n\n\n\n\n\n> _Task Window Says:_ The powerful gargoyle has nowhere to run. Defeat it once and for all!\n\n\n\n_If You Get This Step: Kill Shirik`s Corrupted Guardian._\n\n\n\n_As with the previous heroic adventure, this corrupted guardian has the same four stances:_\n\n\n\n\\- Normal (lasts for first 25 seconds of the fight and does not repeat).\n\n\n\n\n_After the initial 25 seconds passes, the following three stances cycle:_\n\n\n\n\\- Enraged (lasts for 15 seconds)\n\n\n_\\-\\-\\- immune to ranged DPS; frequently AE rampages; hasted attacks._\n\n\n\n\\- Shielded (lasts for 10 seconds)\n\n\n_\\-\\-\\- rooted in place; susceptible to ranged attacks; for every nuke or DOT cast on it (including weapon procs) AND for every 2% damage to it, casts directional AEs for 61k dmg (left/right/rear)._\n\n\n\n\\- Weakened (lasts for 15 seconds)\n\n\n_\\-\\-\\- becomes unrooted; hasted attack speed._\n\n\n\n_NOTE: Each time Lark D`Tradis is hit by one of these retaliation AEs, the Corrupted Guardian gains 10% mitigation to spell and melee attacks (up to a maximum 50%)._\n\n\n\n_It hits for a max ~22,000; single-target rampages; and flurries. Note that this mob does not reset, so if you wipe out, you'll have to re-engage it from 100% in its current stance and with its current mitigations. You'll see emotes as the fight goes on:_\n\n\n\n**Shirik`s Guardian (Shielding) retaliates to \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_'s spell.**\n\n\\-\\-\\- _(response to a nuke, DOT, or proc in shielded form)_\n\n\n\n**Shirik's Guardian retaliates to your continued assault.**\n\n\\-\\-\\- _(response to 2% damage in shielded form)_\n\n\n\n**Lark D`Tradis winces as the gargoyle's breath surrounds her.**\n\n\\-\\-\\- _(Guardian gains 10% damage mitigation)_\n\n\n\n**Shirik's Guardian gains a measure of Lark's power.**\n\n\\-\\-\\- _(Guardian gains 10% damage mitigation)_\n\n\n\n**Shirik's Guardian glows red with rage!**\n\n\\-\\-\\- _(Guardian enters enraged form)_\n\n\n\n**Shirik's Guardian surrounds itself with a powerful shield.**\n\n\\-\\-\\- _(Guardian enters shielded form)_\n\n\n\n**Shirik's Guardian staggers, momentarily weakened.**\n\n\\-\\-\\- _(Guardian enters weakened form)_\n\n6. Clear a path to the upper floor 0/8 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n\n\n\n\n\n> _Task Window Says:_ ?\n\n\n\n_If You Get This Step: Standard kill updates._\n\n7. Look for Shirik D`Tradis 0/1 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n\n\n\n\n\n> _Task Window Says:_ ?\n\n\n\n_If You Get This Step: This is a location update and triggers a script._\n\n8. Defeat Rylit, Tarant`s Arcanist 0/1 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n\n\n\n\n\n> _Task Window Says:_ ?\n\n\n\n_If You Get This Step: Five ghosts; DPS 10% of each one's health at which point it will reveal itself as either 'fake' or 'real' (repeat x5 until 'real one' is dead)._\n\n\n\n_Note: One of the AE effects here has an Alcohol Tolerance check (unknown level required to prevent drunkedness)._\n\n\n\nThe Rylit, Tarant`s Arcanist casts \"Unease\" (slows spell casting), \"Misery\" (30k DOT and drunk if Alcohol Tolerance is below 330), \"Neglect\" (silence on melee skills), \"Turmoil\" (prevents detrimental casting), and \"Agitation\" (melee slow and snare). These are spell IDs 42016-42020.\n\n\n\n\nThese all last 3 ticks, and they are all targeted AEs (20'), so your group can mitigate problems if you spread out from each other. The drunk effect of \"Misery\" lasts MUCH longer than 3 ticks, so the further below the 330 checkpoint you are, the more ...miserable... a fight you'll be in for.\n\n\n\n\nHis projections (ghosts) can also cast these effects, but do so much less frequently.\n\n\n\n\n_Five ghosts of the arcanist: DPS them one at a time to 90%. As each reaches 90%, it reveals itself as a fake target or a real target. If it's a fake target, that single ghost despawns. If it's a real target, then all the ghosts despawn and the arcanist spawns in its place. DPS the arcanist to 75% to respawn the five ghosts._\n\n\n\n_Repeat this process again to 75% (arcanist to 50%), then to 50% (arcanist to 25%), then to 25% (arcanist to 0%), then to its death._\n\n\n\n_All ghosts cast random targeted AEs (you'll have one AE going off every 10 seconds). The arcanist also casts random targeted AEs (two casts at a time every 30 seconds AND one cast for every 4% health lost)._\n\n9. Speak with Lark 0/1 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n\n\n\n\n\n> _Task Window Says:_ ?\n\n\n\n_If You Get This Step: Hail Lark to complete the task._\n\n\n---\n\n**TASK REWARDS**\n\\- a varying amount of platinum\n\\- a varying amount of experience\n\\- a varying number of Marks of Valor (currency used to buy group gear)\n- Guardian Ornament [item=115072]\n- Longbow of the Royal Court [item=114729]\n- Mark of Valor [item=113459]",
