      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Neriak Fourth Gate [zone=943]\n**Who:**\n- Rozz T`Ver [npc=44573]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 75\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 03:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Elemental Ember [item=114836]\n- Rancid Rat Meat [item=114847]\n- Spider Egg Sac [item=116715]\n- Vial of Effusive Acid [item=115061]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Neriak Fourth Gate: Hate Hath No Fury [zone=983]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Belyea F`Lok [npc=46156]\n- Cazum J`Essina [npc=46157]\n- Cizzar Q`Tentu [npc=46158]\n- Dragoon C`Vex [npc=46159]\n- Dragoon D`Bious [npc=46160]\n- Dragoon D`Jerna [npc=46161]\n- Dragoon G`Stinn [npc=46162]\n- Dragoon Morran [npc=46163]\n- Dragoon N`Mare [npc=46164]\n- Dragoon Poxxol [npc=46165]\n- Dragoon R`Lor [npc=46166]\n- Dragoon S`Kan [npc=46167]\n- Dragoon Tolax [npc=46168]\n- Dragoon Torrex [npc=45664]\n- Guard D`Dbth [npc=46169]\n- Guard D`Estalian [npc=46170]\n- Guard D`Horn [npc=46171]\n- Guard Dmizza [npc=46172]\n- Guard H`Rugla [npc=46173]\n- Guard J`Ran [npc=46174]\n- Guard L`Orus [npc=46175]\n- Guard M`Rekkor [npc=46176]\n- Guard N`Tan [npc=46177]\n- Guard S`Nez [npc=46178]\n- Guard Tolax [npc=46179]\n- Guard V`Rett [npc=46180]\n- Isaya J`Risan [npc=46181]\n- Issia D`Unnar [npc=46182]\n- Isvan To`Biath [npc=46183]\n- Ithvol Kixl [npc=46184]\n- Narex R`Dev [npc=46185]\n- Nazia J`Axx [npc=46186]\n- Nerta S`Tai [npc=46187]\n- Rozz T`Ver [npc=46188]\n- Rysva T`Azzl [npc=46189]\n- Sol D`Unnar [npc=46190]\n- Tonn N`Mar [npc=46191]\n- Tralon L`Crit [npc=46192]\n- Trista Vi`Rix [npc=46193]\n- Vissa D`Estalian [npc=46194]\n- a darklight widow [npc=46145]\n- a dinner guest [npc=46146]\n- a diseased rat - Neriak Fourth Gate: Hate Hath No [npc=46147]\n- a palace courtier [npc=46149]\n- a palace guest [npc=46150]\n- a portrait of the king [npc=46151]\n- a royal apothecary [npc=46152]\n- a stone statue [npc=46153]\n- a visiting noble [npc=46154]\n- a warrior banner [npc=46155]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Daily Task: Heroic Adventures [quest=7988]\n- Rozz #1a: The King's Court [quest=7399]\n- Rozz #2: Royal Access [quest=7401]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Jan 22 03:47:50 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n**About Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Heroic adventures in Call of the Forsaken scale in level: As low as **Level 75** and up to current maximum level.\n\\- Scale is based on the highest level player **present in the zone** and affects difficulty, loot quality, and mob levels.\n\\- There is some variation/randomization in the task steps you'll be assigned as you progress through the task.\n\\- Time of completion will vary by your group's makeup (anywhere from 30-90+ minutes).\n\\- Collection items appear as ground spawns midway through tasks (you'll see an emote indicating their appearance).\n\\- Named mobs (or their PHs) spawn midway through tasks (usually, but always, at the same time collection items appear).\n\\- These tasks have individual **3-hour lockout timers** (timer gained upon completion).\n**Experience in Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Mobs in these instances grant some experience, but the bulk of experience is **earned upon task completion**.\n\\- As of a patch in November 2014, less difficult tasks were tuned to reward less experience and more difficult ones were tuned to reward more.\n\\- For an added experience bonus, check out **Guard Hamarn's \"Daily Tasks\"** [quest=7988].\n\n---\n\n_This is a heroic adventure (1-6 players) that begins with Rozz T`Ver ( **click for map image**) in Neriak Fourth Gate._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Level 75\n\\- No tasks\n\n---\n\n**TASK SUMMARY**\n\\- Say \"revenge\" to request the task and \"begin\" to zone in.\n**Step #1:**\n\\- Tear down portraits of the king 0/5\n\\-\\-\\- Clear guards away from the paintings, then click on the paintings.\n\\- Destroy statues of the king 0/3\n\\-\\-\\- Clear guards from the statues, then DPS the statues for the update.\n\\- Tear down warrior banners within the palace 0/5\n\\-\\-\\- These are the blue banners around the palace; clear guards from them, then click for the update.\n**Step #2:**\n\\- Kill all palace guests, courtiers, and nobles 0/12\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update: \"a palace guest\"; \"a palace courtier; \"a visiting noble\".\n\\- Poison dinner guests by tainting their food 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- Kill diseased rats until you've looted 6x \"Rancid Rat Meat\", then use the meat in the dining area.\n**\\- At this point in the task, collectibles spawn in the zone (ground spawns) and a named (or its PH) has a chance to spawn.**\n**Step #3:**\n\\- Slaughter guards near the king's bedchambers 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- Kill Dragoons in or around the king's bedroom chambers.\n**Step #4:**\n\\- Pour vials of acid into the king's bathing pool 0/4\n\\-\\-\\- Kill \"a royal apothecary\" until you've looted 4x \"Vial of Effusive Acid\", then use the acid in the bedroom's pool.\n\\- Place poisonous spider egg sacs within the king's bedchambers 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- Kill \"a darklight widow\" until you've looted 6x \"Spider Egg Sac\", then use the sacs in the bed chambers.\n\\- Set the king's bedchamber on fire 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill \"a fire elemental\" until you've looted 1x \"Elemental Ember\", then use it in the bed chambers.\n\\- As soon as the objective for Step #4 is done, the task completes.\n\n---\n\n**MAP**\n!\n\n---\n\n**NAMED MOBS**\n_Dragoon Torrex (or its PH, \"Guard V`Rett\") spawns after the second step is completed. Known loot from this named:_\nBracer of Latent Ether\nBraided Leather Cord\nBuckler of the Turncoat's Anguish\nEtched Gold Girdle\n\n---\n\n**TASK IN DETAIL**\n========================================================================\nTRIGGERING THE TASK\n========================================================================\nYou say, 'Hail, Rozz T`Ver'\nRozz T`Ver says 'In the aftermath of the construct battle, the king and queen are more at odds than ever. Her majesty has been banished from the palace, and all those loyal to her killed or imprisoned. It's left the queen quite bitter and paranoid. I'm afraid her lust for [revenge] will interfere with the greater goal of winning this war. Without ears and eyes in the palace, the queen cannot gain ground in this ongoing battle. She needs an ally on the inside; one to [recover] information about what the king has planned.'\nYou say, 'Revenge?'\nRozz T`Ver says 'If you could enter the palace and cause complete chaos, your destruction might satiate the queen's hunger for revenge, allowing her to focus on more pressing issues, like her husband's devious plans. If you're willing to wreak havoc within the palace, then you should [begin] at once.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Hate Hath No Fury'.\nEnter Darklight Palace and cause chaos and destruction, in the name of the queen.\nYou say, 'Let's begin!'\nRozz T`Ver says 'Make haste, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'\n========================================================================\nSTEP #1\n========================================================================\nTear down portraits of the king 0/5 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ Tear down paintings of the king hung on palace walls, but beware of guards!\n_If You Get This Step: Clear guards away from the paintings, then click on the paintings. Note that guards are mezzable, but immune to stuns, roots, and snares._\n=====================\nDestroy statues of the king 0/3 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ Attack statues of the king around the palace to destroy them, but beware of guards!\n_If You Get This Step: Clear guards from the statues, then DPS the statues for the update. Guards are mezzable, but immune to stuns, roots, and snares. If you attack a statue while guards around it are still alive, you see:_\nYour actions alert the nearby guards!\n_Note: The \"statues\" have odd aggro, and if they drop off aggro, they immediately regenerate to 100% health. It seems you can usually avoid this from happening if you stand in very close proximity range of it. (For mechanics purposes, the NPC you are attacking is actually a nameless invisible man in front of the statue.)_\n=====================\nTear down warrior banners within the palace 0/5 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ Tear down blue warrior banners hung from the palace walls, but beware of guards!\n_If You Get This Step: These are the blue banners around the palace; clear guards from them, then click for the update. Note that guards are mezzable, but immune to stuns, roots, and snares. If you click a banner while guards are still nearby, they aggro you._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #2\n========================================================================\nKill all palace guests, courtiers, and nobles 0/12 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill update: \"a palace guest\"; \"a palace courtier; \"a visiting noble\"._\n=====================\nPoison dinner guests by tainting their food 0/6 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ Place rancid rat meat on the table within the dining area and watch as dinner guests dine to their deaths! Rancid meat can be found on diseased rats that roam outside in front of the palace.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill diseased rats until you've looted 6x \"Rancid Rat Meat\", then use the meat in the dining area._\na dinner guest calls out to the other hungry guests, 'It's time to dine, friends! Look at this lovely meal the palace servant has brought us.'\nA dinner guest takes a small bite of the rancid meat and begins to convulse before dropping lifelessly to the floor.\na dinner guest died.\n========================================================================\nSTEP #3\n========================================================================\nSlaughter guards near the king's bedchambers 0/6 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ Kill all the king's guards that linger near his bedchambers.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill Dragoons in or around the king's bedroom chambers. These mobs hit for a max ~13,000, and are stunnable and mezzable, but not rootable/snareable. Note that a named (Dragoon Torex) has a chance to spawn as a roamer in the middle of all the Dragoon spawns here. This mob is considerably more difficult than trash mobs and does not count towards this step._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #4\n========================================================================\nPour vials of acid into the king's bathing pool 0/4 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ An acid bath is just what the king needs! Only royal apothecaries handle such corrosive substances.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill \"a royal apothecary\" until you've looted 4x \"Vial of Effusive Acid\", then use the acid in the bedroom's pool to complete the task. These mobs hit for a max ~13,000._\n_(Task completes here; there is no completion text.)_\n=====================\nPlace poisonous spider egg sacs within the king's bedchambers 0/6 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill \"a darklight widow\" that roam outside in front of the palace. until you've looted 6x \"Spider Egg Sac\", then use the sacs in the bed chambers to complete the task._\n_(Task completes here; there is no completion text.)_\n=====================\nSet the king's bedchamber on fire 0/1 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill \"a fire elemental\" until you've looted 1x \"Elemental Ember\", then use it in the bed chambers to complete the task._\n_(Task completes here; there is no completion text.)_\n\n---\n\n**TASK REWARDS**\n\\- a varying amount of platinum\n\\- a varying amount of experience\n\\- a varying number of Marks of Valor (currency used to buy group gear)\n- Braided Leather Cord [item=115052]\n- Buckler of the Turncoat's Anguish [item=114621]\n- Etched Gold Girdle [item=114717]\n- Mark of Valor [item=113459]",
