      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Bixie Warfront [zone=941]\n**Who:**\n- Battlebreaker Kraklest [ _Heroic Adventures_]\nRating:\n0/2**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(Average from 2 ratings)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 75\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 03:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Bixie Battle Plans [item=114642]\n- Bixie Bludgeon [item=114649]\n- Cliknar Gas Pouch [item=115059]\n- Cliknar Scout Head [item=114648]\n- Healing Honey Goo [item=115027]\n- Magical Bixie Stone [item=114641]\n- Ripped Bixie Wings [item=114643]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Bixie Warfront: Endless War [zone=976]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Battle Advisor Leginalk [npc=45759]\n- Captain Thwaksax [npc=45760]\n- Cruncher [npc=46388]\n- Firesting [npc=44079]\n- General Sagrinta [npc=45761]\n- Infiltrator Nallai [npc=45762]\n- Infiltrator Ynoxi [npc=53940]\n- Lieutenant Jinkx [npc=45763]\n- Lieutenant Relikk [npc=45764]\n- Medic Grulina [npc=45765]\n- Scout Jugzz [npc=45766]\n- a battlefield medic [npc=45730]\n- a bloodthirsty soldier [npc=45731]\n- a catapult engineer [npc=45732]\n- a cliknar defender [npc=45733]\n- a cliknar scout [npc=45734]\n- a cliknar swarmer [npc=45735]\n- a combat medic [npc=45736]\n- a corpse hacker [npc=45737]\n- a flesh chef [npc=45738]\n- a hardened soldier [npc=45739]\n- a hive guard [npc=45740]\n- a hungry rager [npc=45741]\n- a nest defender [npc=45742]\n- a proud guardian [npc=45743]\n- a scared soldier [npc=45744]\n- a scarred defender [npc=45745]\n- a skittering ambusher [npc=46331]\n- a skittering thief [npc=46330]\n- a sprinting gasser [npc=45746]\n- a strategist [npc=45747]\n- a tactician [npc=45748]\n- a trench clearer [npc=45749]\n- a trench cutter [npc=45750]\n- a trench filler [npc=45751]\n- a trench torcher [npc=45752]\n- a wounded soldier [npc=45753]\n- a young soldier [npc=45754]\n- an abusive sergeant [npc=45767]\n- an assault team soldier [npc=45755]\n- an explosive barrel [npc=45756]\n- an incapacitated soldier [npc=45757]\n- an injured cliknar [npc=45758]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Daily Task: Heroic Adventures [quest=7988]\n- Kraklest #2: The Thunder Gun Escape [quest=7409]\n- Kraklest #3: General Sagrinta's Last Stand [quest=7410]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Jan 22 03:56:03 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n**About Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Heroic adventures in Call of the Forsaken scale in level: As low as **Level 75** and up to current maximum level.\n\\- Scale is based on the highest level player **present in the zone** and affects difficulty, loot quality, and mob levels.\n\\- There is some variation/randomization in the task steps you'll be assigned as you progress through the task.\n\\- Time of completion will vary by your group's makeup (anywhere from 30-90+ minutes).\n\\- Collection items appear as ground spawns midway through tasks (you'll see an emote indicating their appearance).\n\\- Named mobs (or their PHs) spawn midway through tasks (usually, but always, at the same time collection items appear).\n\\- These tasks have individual **3-hour lockout timers** (timer gained upon completion).\n**Experience in Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Mobs in these instances grant some experience, but the bulk of experience is **earned upon task completion**.\n\\- As of a patch in November 2014, less difficult tasks were tuned to reward less experience and more difficult ones were tuned to reward more.\n\\- For an added experience bonus, check out **Guard Hamarn's \"Daily Tasks\"** [quest=7988].\n\n---\n\n_This is a heroic adventure (1-6 players) that begins with Battlebreaker Kraklest ( **click for map image**) in the Bixie Warfront (found at the bottom of the ramp, at the edge of the water, /location -915, -1885, -165)._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Level 75\n\\- No tasks\n\n---\n\n**TASK SUMMARY**\n\\- Say \"embark on an adventure\" to request the task and \"ready\" to zone in.\n**Step #1:**\nGet a bixie disguise from Iniltrator Nallai 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Dialogue update (\"bixie disguise\").\n**Step #2:**\n\\- Convince General Sagrinta to give you her battle plans 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill 5x \"a cliknar scout\" and turn in their heads.\n\\- Steal the bixie battle plans inside the hive 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Click on the explosive barrel in the room, then click on the scroll box on the center table.\n\\- Kill skittering cliknar to recover the stolen bixie battle plans 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill the mobs under the hive until you loot the item.\n**Step #3:**\n\\- Get in the northwest bixie trenches to avoid the cliknar bombers 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Get in one of the trenches to avoid the zone AEs.\n\\- Get in the northwest bixie trenches to avoid the cliknar swarm 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Get in one of the trenches to avoid the swarming mobs.\n\\- Get in the southwest bixie trenches to avoid the explosive seeds 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Get in one of the trenches to avoid the explosions.\n**Step #4:**\n\\- Loot cliknar gas pouches 0/5\n\\-\\-\\- Kill \"a sprinting gasser\" until you've looted 5x \"Cliknar Gas Pouch\".\n\\- Kill cliknar gassers in the trenches 0/10\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update.\n\\- Knock out young bixie soldiers 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- DPS young soldiers to under 40% health (note: spawns an add at 40%), then right-click the bludgeon.\n\\- Heal and defend injured bixie soldiers 0/5\n\\-\\-\\- Find a honeycomb in the middle area of the trenches in the western part of the zone, right-click it on injured bixies, then kill the spawned cliknar.\n**Step #5:**\n\\- Report to Scout Jugzz in the southeast cliknar trenches 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Speak with Scout Jugzz (located in a trench in southwestern part of the cliknar's side of the zone).\n\\- Report to Medic Grulina in the southeast cliknar trenches 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Speak with Medic Grulina in the western part of the cliknar trenches.\n**\\- At this point in the task, collectibles spawn in the zone (ground spawns) and a named (or its PH) has a chance to spawn.**\n**Alternate Step #5:**\n\\- Report to Infiltrator Ynoxi in the southeast cliknar trenches. 0/1\n\\- Bixie assault teams are trying to contain the cliknar army across the river, but have run into trouble. Fight or sneak your way across the river, and find Infiltrator Ynoxi in the southeast cliknar trenches to offer your aid. 0/1\nYnoxi is in the southeast trenches, west side, in the second cubby up from the bottom.\n**Step #6:**\n\\- Recover bixie wings from the cliknar soldiers in the southeast trenches 0/30\n\\-\\-\\- Kill and loot cliknar mobs in the eastern half of the zone until you've gathered 30 of their wings.\n\\- Defend incapacitated bixie soldiers in the southeast trenches 0/5\n\\-\\-\\- Speak with \"an incapacitated soldier\" to spawn 2x \"a hungry rager\"; kill the adds; repeat x5.\n\\- Save disarmed bixie soldiers in the southeast cliknar trenches 0/3\n\\-\\-\\- Kill cliknar mobs around disarmed bixies, then hail the bixies.\n**Optional for Step# 6:**\n\\- Kill cliknar soldiers in the southeast cliknar trenches\n**Step #7:**\n\\- Stop or aid the bixie assault in between the eastern cliknar trenches 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Aid or kill \"an injured cliknar\" (either way, kill off a wave of mobs: Either the Lieutenant + 4x soldiers, or 6x \"a nest defender\")\n\\- Find and protect scared bixies from cliknar aggression 0/7\n\\-\\-\\- In the northern part of the eastern half of the zone are scared soldiers; speak with them to either update the step or spawn a hostile mob (kill the mob if one spawns).\n\\- Help General Sagrinta slaughter 100 cliknar 0/100\n\\-\\-\\- Speak with the General, and then follow her and kill 100 mobs alongside her.\n**Step #8:**\n\\- Report to Infiltrator Nallai on the northern river camp 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Dialogue update.\n\\- As soon as the objective for Step #8 is done, the task completes.\n\n---\n\n**MAP**\n!\n\n---\n\n**NAMED MOBS**\n_Firesting (or its PH, \"a cliknar defender\") has a chance to spawn after the fifth step is completed. Known loot from this named:_\nBloody Bixie Belt\nQuivering Tendon\nSilken Trillium\nBoots of Latent Ether\n\n---\n\n**TASK IN DETAIL**\n========================================================================\nTRIGGERING THE TASK\n========================================================================\nYou say, 'Hail, Battlebreaker Kraklest'\nBattlebreaker Kraklest grunts and nods in respect as she scratches [blood] off of her shield.\nYou say, 'What's this blood?'\nBattlebreaker Kraklest says 'It's a mess out there, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. The conflicts we've seen so far are nothing compared to the [battlefield] ahead.'\nYou say, 'Battlefield?'\nBattlebreaker Kraklest says 'The Stone Hive managed to start a [war] while we searched for the cause of their madness.'\nYou say, 'What about the war?'\nBattlebreaker Kraklest says 'The [cliknar] came from all over, digging through the walls, floors, and ceilings of the entire complex. At the time, the Stone Hive welcomed the war and established a massive battlefield just south of here.'\nYou say, 'Cliknar?'\nBattlebreaker Kraklest says 'You've probably seen them before, but not like this. They're just as mad as the Stone Hive. The numbers of soldiers on both sides is near endless. They're throwing them into a massive [meat grinder].'\nYou say, 'Meat grinder?'\nBattlebreaker Kraklest says 'They're lack of respect for life, and for the honor of fighting, is disgusting. We need to [stop] the war before it decimates both sides.'\nYou say, 'How can we stop it?'\nBattlebreaker Kraklest says 'Prisoners of war, a struggling front line, and an isolated general: there are several situations that could use your help. Are you ready to [embark on an adventure]?'\nYou say, 'Embark on an adventure?'\nBattlebreaker Kraklest says 'Good. Let me know when you're [ready] to depart and I'll ensure you make it to the battlefield safely.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Endless War'.\nInfiltrator Nallai has escorted you to the front lines of the bixie-cliknar war that has spontaneously erupted. The bixies are taking heavy casualties and the fighting is getting dangerously close to civilian areas. Help the bixies push back the cliknar, so that the civilians can be spared. The bixies do not trust outsiders.\nYou say, 'Ready'\nBattlebreaker Kraklest says 'Be swift and strong, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. But most of all, be brave. It's a dark world you're stepping into.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Bixie Warfront.\n========================================================================\nSTEP #1\n========================================================================\nGet a bixie disguise from Iniltrator Nallai 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Speak with Infiltrator Nallai to receive a bixie disguise. The bixies won't trust you if you don't appear to be one of them. If you lose the disguise, you can speak with Infiltrator Nallai or use the Magical Bixie Stone in your inventory to regain it.\n_If You Get This Step: Speak with Nallai at the zone-in._\nYou say, 'Hail, Infiltrator Nallai'\nInfiltrator Nallai smiles and speaks quietly, 'It's good to see you again, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. You're my most-trusted agent after our mission to break Jacyll out of his cell. I'm going to need your [help] here again.'\nYou say, 'Help?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'As you know, the powerful war-drum that corrupted the Stone Hive affects more than just bixies. At the height of its strength, the war-drum attracted a nearby [cliknar] colony, who came in search of it.'\nYou say, 'What cliknar?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'You've probably encountered them before. Insectoid, antennae, and like to travel in huge packs. If not, well, you'll see them soon. The cliknar invaded the hive and, of course, the bixies rushed off to start a large-scale [war] with them.'\nYou say, 'War?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'We can't blame it all on the bixies. The cliknar were driven into just as blind of a bloodlust as the bixies were. But they've been killing each other at an alarming rate. The bixies are losing the war, but you're going to [hold off] the cliknar.'\nYou say, 'Hold off?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'The cliknar have pushed the battle line dangerously close to the main hive. If they make their way into the chamber with the main hive, countless [civilians] will be slaughtered. We can't let that happen.'\nYou say, 'Civilians?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'Yep, and you'll be posing as one, coming to aid the bixie army. It's the only way they'll trust you. Let me know when you're ready for a [bixie disguise]. I borrowed some [magic thingamajiggies] for this mission.'\nYou say, 'What magic thingamajiggies?'\nInfiltrator Nallai laughs and shows you a collection of small stones in her hand, 'I don't pretend to understand magic, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. But Queen Shulriya Fiume personally assured me these magical disguises will fool anyone.\nYou say, 'Give me a bixie disguise'\nYou're transformed into the form of a bixie soldier.\nInfiltrator Nallai rubs a stone between two fingers and throws it at you. When it hits, you transform into a bixie. You pick up the stone for later, if needed.\n========================================================================\nSTEP #2\n========================================================================\nConvince General Sagrinta to give you her battle plans 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Convince General Sagrinta, located in the hive on the western edge of the battlefield, that you're a messenger worthy of carrying her battle plans. If you can't convince her with words, she'll be persuaded by an offering of five cliknar heads, taken from the cliknar scouts beneath the hive.\n_If You Get This Step: Outside the entrance tunnel and beneath the hive are several mobs called \"a cliknar scout\" (hit for a max ~11,500). Kill them until you've looted five of their heads, then give them to General Sagrinta inside the hive._\nYou say, 'Hail, General Sagrinta'\nGeneral Sagrinta looks at you disapprovingly, 'I expected them to send someone stronger as my [messenger].'\nYou say, 'I am a worthy messenger!'\nGeneral Sagrinta says 'Well, you'll have to prove that you can survive a scuffle with the [cliknar] before I'll trust you with these battle plans.'\nYou say, 'What cliknar?'\nGeneral Sagrinta says 'There are some scouts directly beneath this hive. They think they we haven't noticed them. Prove you can [beat them in combat], and I'll be convinced your worthy to carry this letter.'\nYou say, 'Me? Beat them in combat?'\nGeneral Sagrinta says 'Yes, bring me five of their heads as proof and the job is yours!'\n_Upon hand-in:_\nGeneral Sagrinta says 'Well done, soldier.'\nGeneral Sagrinta says 'Guard these battle plans with your life, and return as soon as they've been delivered!'\n_You receive \"Bixie Battle Plans\"._\n=====================\nSteal the bixie battle plans inside the hive 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The bixies have left their battle plans in a scroll box on the center table inside the hive at the western edge of the battlefield. Get inside and find a way to distract the guards long enough to steal the battle plans.\n_If You Get This Step: Click the explosive barrel in the room to set off an explosion, then click the scroll box on the table in the middle of the room. In the bixie hive are several strategists, tacticians, and a Battle Advisor._\na strategist says 'We must tell the officers to send the new recruits immediately. We don't have time to wait for their training!'\na strategist says 'How can there possibly be so many of them? We've killed thousands and they just keep coming.'\na strategist mumbles to itself while shuffling through documents.\na tactician says 'We must take the western river ramp if we hope to succeed!'\na tactician says 'Get out of here, grunt! We've got serious thinking to do.'\nBattle Advisor Leginalk says 'Not now, grunt! We're busy planning where you should die. I mean fight.'\nYou can't steal the battle plans while the advisors are watching.\nBattle Advisor Leginalk says 'Hands off those battle plans, grunt! We're still working on them.'\n_Upon clicking the barrel, you see:_\nThe explosive barrel fulfills its destiny, and goes out in a blaze of glory.\na strategist says 'Ahhh!'\nBattle Advisor Leginalk says 'My face! Who detonated that explosive barrel? I'll have their head!'\na strategist says 'Why do we even keep that thing in here?'\na strategist says 'I can't see anything!'\nBattle Advisor Leginalk is blinded by the explosion!\nA tactician is blinded by the explosion!\nA strategist is blinded by the explosion!\nA strategist is blinded by the explosion!\nA strategist is blinded by the explosion!\nA strategist is blinded by the explosion!\nA strategist is blinded by the explosion!\nA strategist is blinded by the explosion!\nYou steal a copy of the bixie battle plans from the scroll box on the table.\nBattle Advisor Leginalk says 'Where'd the battle plans go? Did you eat them again, Sliz?'\na strategist says 'I ate before I came this time.'\n=====================\nKill skittering cliknar to recover the stolen bixie battle plans 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill the mobs under the hive (just next to the zone-in tunnel) until you loot a \"Bixie Battle Plans\" from one of them._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #3\n========================================================================\nGet in the northwest bixie trenches to avoid the cliknar bombers 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The battle plans reveal that the cliknar have been launching long-range explosives into the bixie camp. Get into the northwest bixie trenches to avoid drawing the attention of their bombers.\n_If You Get This Step: Upon completion of the previous step, if you're out on the battlefield, you start getting nuked for 25,000 to 50,000 dmg every few seconds. Get into a trench to update the task. (Note that if you leave the trenches, they'll continue bombing you.)_\nCliknar bombers lock on your position. Get in the trenches!\nExplosive bugs fall from the sky. Get in the trenches!\nYou have been spotted by cliknar bombers!\n=====================\nGet in the northwest bixie trenches to avoid the cliknar swarm 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The cliknar are beginning to swarm! You risk attracting their attention by walking above-ground. Get into the northwest bixie trenches to stay hidden as you move.\n_If You Get This Step: Upon completion of the previous step, if you're out on the battlefield, mobs called \"a cliknar swarmer\" spawn on top of you two at a time, attacking (hit for a max ~1,200). These mobs don't stay up long, but you'll want to get into the trenches before they DPS you down too far. They will follow you into them, but despawn soon enough._\nGet into the trenches to avoid the cliknar swarm!\n=====================\nGet in the southwest bixie trenches to avoid the explosive seeds 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Get in one of the trenches to avoid the explosions._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #4\n========================================================================\nLoot cliknar gas pouches 0/5 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Cliknar gassers are working their way through the bixie trenches, fumigating anyone they find. Fight through the west bixie trenches and rip the gas pouches from their lifeless bodies. The bixies may be able to use them to develop an immunity vaccine.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill \"a sprinting gasser\" until you've looted 5x \"Cliknar Gas Pouch\". These mobs hit for a max ~13,000 (backstab for much higher) and are mezzable/stunnable._\n=====================\nKill cliknar gassers in the trenches 0/10 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Cliknar gassers are working their way through the bixie trenches, fumigating anyone they find. Fight through the west bixie trenches and take down the cliknar gassers.\n_If You Get This Step: Standard kill update (10x \"a sprinting gasser\")._\n=====================\nKnock out young bixie soldiers 0/6 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Even adolescent bixies have been drafted into their army and sent to fight on the front lines! Weaken young bixie soldiers in the west bixie trenches and use the Bixie Bludgeon in your inventory to knock them out. They can only be knocked out after you've worn them down in combat.\n_If You Get This Step: Upon completing the previous step, you received a \"Bixie Bludgeon\" on your cursor. DPS \"a young soldier\" (found throughout the trenches -- hit for a max ~12,000; stunnable/mezzable) down to below 40%, then right-click the item. NOTE: \"an abusive sergeant\" (hits for a max ~5,000; stunnable/mezzable) spawns and attacks when the young soldier reaches 40% health._\na young soldier says 'P-p-please, I don't want to fight you!'\nan abusive sergeant says 'Dissent in the ranks? Don't let these wimps push you around, soldier!'\nYou bludgeon the young soldier's head, and it collapses to the ground, unconscious. The cliknar will ignore it now.\n=====================\nHeal and defend injured bixie soldiers 0/5 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Find a honeycomb in the middle area of the trenches in the western part of the zone, use it on injured bixies (which spawns a cliknar). Kill the cliknar, repeat x5._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #5\n========================================================================\nReport to Scout Jugzz in the southeast cliknar trenches 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The bixie army has walked into a trap! While they pushed their way into the enemy's trenches across the river, the cliknar army snuck behind them and cut off their retreat route across the bridge. Find a way around the cliknar-barricaded bridge, and find Scout Jugzz near the front of the southeast cliknar trenches.\n_If You Get This Step: Find Scout Jugzz in the southeastern cliknar trenches. He is a bixie in a dead-end down in the trench in the southwestern part of the cliknar's half of the zone._\nYou say, 'Hail, Scout Jugzz'\nScout Jugzz jumps as you speak. He clearly didn't notice you. He says quietly, 'Honey help us! We're in a heap of [trouble] over here!'\nYou say, 'Trouble?'\nScout Jugzz says 'You saw how dense the cliknar population was near the bridge, right? There's at least 700 of them, and they're as tall as mountains! They must be readying a full-scale assault on our hive! You saw the defenses there. We wouldn't stand a chance! We need to [strike] them hard now, in their own trenches to distract them!'\nYou say, 'Let's strike...'\nScout Jugzz tries to hide himself behind you and pushes you into the trenches. Here are my orders from the general. They're yours now! For the hive!\n=====================\nReport to Medic Grulina in the southeast cliknar trenches 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The bixie army is taking heavy losses across the river, but have secured the bridge. Run across the bridge, and find Medic Grulina in the southeast cliknar trenches near it.\n_If You Get This Step: Find Medic Grulina._\nYou say, 'Hail, Medic Grulina'\nMedic Grulina wipes blood from her hands and says slowly, 'Another one run into the slaughter, eh? I hope you fair [better] than the last pack.'\nYou say, 'Better?'\nMedic Grulina kicks the skull of the skeleton at her feet across the trench and mutters, 'It's blood for blood, and we're losing. I suppose you'll want [orders]?\nYou say, 'Orders?'\nMedic Grulina wipes her surgery knife on her skirt and says quietly, 'Here they are. Many good bixies died here today. Don't add to that count, okay?'\n========================================================================\nSTEP #6\n========================================================================\nRecover bixie wings from the cliknar soldiers in the southeast trenches 0/30 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Cliknar soldiers have begun collecting bixie wings as trophies. The most veteran warriors have hundreds of them. Kill the cliknar soldiers in the southeast cliknar trenches and take back their gruesome trophies.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill cliknar mobs in the eastern half of the zone until you've collected 30 of their wings. These drop from about every mob in the area, four at a time._\n=====================\nDefend incapacitated bixie soldiers in the southeast trenches 0/5 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ During the last retreat some bixie soldiers were left behind because they were unable to move due to injuries. Find the incapacitated bixie soldiers in the southeast cliknar trenches and speak with them. They will shoot up a flare to attract a medic to carry them out. Defend them until the medic arrives.\n_If You Get This Step: Throughout the cliknar trenches are bixie mobs feigned death, called \"an incapacitated soldier\". Speak with them to spawn 2x \"a hungry rager\" (hit for a max\n\n...[Walkthrough truncated for in-game performance]...",
