      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Bixie Warfront [zone=941]\n**Who:**\n- Battlebreaker Kraklest [ _Heroic Adventures_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 75\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 03:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Cliknar Poison Antidote [item=114850]\n- Explosive Seed [item=114646]\n- Surprisingly Aerodynamic Rock [item=115047]\n- Thunder Gun Toolkit [item=114644]\n- Unrefined Bixie Tools [item=114645]\n- Wakey-Wakey Honey Rub [item=114658]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Bixie Warfront: The Thunder Gun Escape [zone=977]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Engineer Friliim [ _The Thunder Gun_]\n- Gellwing, the Corpse Looter [npc=44080]\n- Infiltrator Nallai [npc=45808]\n- Kreppo the Curious [npc=45809]\n- Skruffz [npc=45810]\n- Skyrider Elena [npc=45811]\n- Sticky Feet [npc=45812]\n- a Thunder Gun fan [npc=45800]\n- a battlefield medic [npc=45771]\n- a bixie poisoner [npc=45772]\n- a blast technician [npc=45773]\n- a cackling kidnapper [npc=45774]\n- a captured mole mount [npc=45775]\n- a carcass carver [npc=45813]\n- a cliknar slaver [npc=45776]\n- a corpse hider [npc=45777]\n- a dead soldier [npc=45778]\n- a distracted guard [npc=45779]\n- a frenzied cliknar [npc=45780]\n- a grave digger [npc=45781]\n- a hive guard [npc=45782]\n- a hungry chef [npc=45783]\n- a hungry impaler [npc=45784]\n- a hungry nibbler [npc=45785]\n- a kleptomanic cliknar [npc=45786]\n- a meat eater [npc=45787]\n- a pit guard [npc=45788]\n- a poisoned soldier [npc=45789]\n- a poisoner [npc=45790]\n- a poisonous cliknar [npc=45791]\n- a prison ambusher [npc=45792]\n- a prison torcher [npc=45793]\n- a prison warden [npc=45794]\n- a rageblind slasher [npc=45795]\n- a rageblind torcher [npc=45796]\n- a rampaging bixie [npc=45797]\n- a rampaging cliknar [npc=45798]\n- a roasting mole [npc=45799]\n- a trap [npc=45801]\n- a wimpy cliknar [npc=45802]\n- a wounded soldier [npc=45803]\n- an enslaved prisoner [npc=45805]\n- an equipment case [npc=45806]\n- an escaped prisoner [npc=45804]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Daily Task: Heroic Adventures [quest=7988]\n- Kraklest #1: Endless War [quest=7408]\n- Kraklest #3: General Sagrinta's Last Stand [quest=7410]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Jan 22 03:58:52 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n**About Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Heroic adventures in Call of the Forsaken scale in level: As low as **Level 75** and up to current maximum level.\n\\- Scale is based on the highest level player **present in the zone** and affects difficulty, loot quality, and mob levels.\n\\- There is some variation/randomization in the task steps you'll be assigned as you progress through the task.\n\\- Time of completion will vary by your group's makeup (anywhere from 30-90+ minutes).\n\\- Collection items appear as ground spawns midway through tasks (you'll see an emote indicating their appearance).\n\\- Named mobs (or their PHs) spawn midway through tasks (usually, but always, at the same time collection items appear).\n\\- These tasks have individual **3-hour lockout timers** (timer gained upon completion).\n**Experience in Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Mobs in these instances grant some experience, but the bulk of experience is **earned upon task completion**.\n\\- As of a patch in November 2014, less difficult tasks were tuned to reward less experience and more difficult ones were tuned to reward more.\n\\- For an added experience bonus, check out **Guard Hamarn's \"Daily Tasks\"** [quest=7988].\n\n---\n\n_This is a heroic adventure (1-6 players) that begins with Battlebreaker Kraklest ( **click for map image**) in the Bixie Warfront (found at the bottom of the ramp, at the edge of the water, /location -915, -1885, -165)._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Level 75\n\\- Completed \"Endless War\" (heroic adventure)\n\n---\n\n**TASK SUMMARY**\n\\- Say \"embark on an adventure\" to request the task and \"ready\" to zone in.\n**Step #1:**\nSpeak with Iniltrator Nallai near the bridge 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Dialogue update.\n**Step #2:**\n\\- Get captured by cliknar kidnappers on the bridge 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Location update on the bridge.\n**Step #3:**\n\\- Revive and speak with Engineer Friliim in the prison 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Right-click the item received and speak with Friliim.\n\\- Convince Engineer Friliim to attempt an escape 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Dialogue update.\n**Step #4:**\n\\- Escape your curiously unguarded prison pit 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Head out of the pit and be ready for a possible mob ambush (two mobs, if any).\n\\- Find a rock to bash the cliknars guarding your prison pit with 0/2\n\\-\\-\\- Pick up the rock from the ground, target the distracted guards, and right-click the rock.\n**Step #5:**\n\\- Kill prison wardens 0/4\n\\-\\-\\- Kill the prison wardens roaming about the area (each spawns three low-difficulty adds every 20% health).\n\\- Free bixie prisoners 0/30\n\\-\\-\\- Kill 10x \"a cliknar slaver\" to free prisoners (three prisoners each); prisoners are aggro-linked with cliknar until the cliknar dies.\n\\- Kill cliknar prison guards 0/12\n\\-\\-\\- Kill 12x \"a pit guard\".\n**\\- At this point in the task, collectibles spawn in the zone (ground spawns) and a named (or its PH) has a chance to spawn.**\n**Step #6:**\n\\- Find Friliium's toolkit in one of the cliknar chests and give it to him 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Lead Engineer Friliium to equipment crates in the prison area (he'll keep warping to players in your group, similar to a mercenary).\n\\- Recover Friliium's toolkit from the kleptomanic cliknar and give it to him 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill \"a kleptomanic cliknar\" (wanders the eastern edge of the zone), loot the toolkit, and hand it in to Friliim.\n\\- Build some tools for Friliim at the nearby forge and give them to him 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill Kreppo the Curious in the far southeastern part of the zone, loot it, then right-click the item at the large forge.\n**Step #7:**\n\\- Free 6 captured mole-mounts 0/6\n\\-\\-\\- Kill hungry cliknar around the captured moles, then hail the moles.\n\\- Kill rageblind bixies 0/10\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update.\n\\- Taste-test roasted moles 0/10\n\\-\\-\\- Around the area are several roasts over fires with cliknar mobs around them; kill the cliknar, then click the roast.\n**Step #8:**\n\\- Find Sticky Feet in the southern trenches and free it from a trap 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Sticky Feet, found in the southwestern part of the cliknar trenches, is trapped; click on the trap to free it.\n\\- Find Friliim's sister in the southeast cliknar trenches 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill 2x \"a grave digger\" next to Skyrider Elena (found in the southwestern part of the cliknar trenches).\n\\- Help Friliim heal poisoned bixies in the southeast cliknar trenches 0/3\n\\-\\-\\- In the trenches, hail \"a poisoned soldier\" to spawn a cliknar; loot antidote from the cliknar; turn item in to Friliim.\n**Step #9:**\n\\- Take explosive seeds from cliknar technicians and activate them near the bridge 0/3\n\\-\\-\\- Kill blast technicians on the bridge, loot explosive seeds, and right-click them at the eastern end of the bridge.\n\\- Kill the stalwart cliknar guards that are fighting prisoners on the bridge 0/4\n\\-\\-\\- Kill update.\n\\- Keep Hepons the Merciless busy while bixies escape\n\\-\\-\\- Aggro Hepons until 15 bixie prisoners get across the bridge\n**Step #10:**\n\\- Talk with Engineer Friliim 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Dialogue update.\n**Step #11:**\n\\- Report to Infiltrator Nallai 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Dialogue update.\n\\- As soon as the objective for Step #11 is done, the task completes.\n\n---\n\n**MAP**\n!\n\n---\n\n**NAMED MOBS**\n_\"Gellwing, the Corpse Looter\" (or its PH, \"a frenzied cliknar\") has a chance to spawn after the fifth step is completed. Known loot from this named:_\nAbandoned Bulwark\nSilken Trillium\n\n---\n\n**TASK IN DETAIL**\n========================================================================\nTRIGGERING THE TASK\n========================================================================\nYou say, 'Embark on an adventure?'\nBattlebreaker Kraklest says 'Good. Let me know when you're [ready] to depart and I'll ensure you make it to the battlefield safely.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Thunder Gun Escape'.\nYou've been sent to infiltrate a cliknar prison in order to break a bixie engineer, nicknamed The Thunder Gun, out and escort him back to the hive.\nYou say, 'Ready'\nBattlebreaker Kraklest says 'Be swift and strong, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. But most of all, be brave. It's a dark world you're stepping into.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Bixie Warfront.\n========================================================================\nSTEP #1\n========================================================================\nSpeak with Iniltrator Nallai near the bridge 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ As always, Iniltrator Nallai has a plan to solve this problem. Speak with Iniltrator Nallai near the bridge on the bixie side of the battlefield to get your instructions.\n_If You Get This Step: Speak with Nallai at the zone-in._\nYou say, 'Hail, Infiltrator Nallai'\nInfiltrator Nallai smiles and says proudly, 'We're making real progress here, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_! The Stone Hive generals have agreed to accept the Wet River Hive's aid directly. No more disguises and [working from the shadows]!\nYou say, 'Working from the shadows?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'Well, actually, we'll be working from the shadows this time too. But this'll be the last time! Maybe. Probably not. Hey, there's [nothing wrong] with shadows!'\nYou say, 'Nothing wrong?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'There is something wrong, though. The bixie's best catapulteer, Engineer Friliim, who the troops refer to as The Thunder Gun, was captured by cliknar during their last offensive. They want us to [get him back].'\nYou say, 'How to we get him back?'\nInfiltrator Nallai chuckles and says, 'You're not going to like this, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. I need you to get [captured] by the cliknar.\nYou say, 'Captured...?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'It's the easiest way to find out where Engineer Friliim was taken, and get yourself there! Once you find him, [convince] him to trust you.'\nYou say, 'How do we convince him?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'It shouldn't be hard. He's in a cliknar prison! Break him out and [escort] him back here to me. I'll deliver him to the bixie generals and ensure we have a permanent ally here.'\nYou say, 'Escort him?'\nInfiltrator Nallai says 'Do whatever it takes to get him back here safely, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. You can try to rescue any others you find, but every one else is expendable.'\n========================================================================\nSTEP #2\n========================================================================\nGet captured by cliknar kidnappers on the bridge 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The bixies' most promising catapulteer, Engineer Friliim (nicknamed The Thunder Gun), was captured by cliknar and is being held in a prison behind enemy lines. Run onto the bridge and let the cliknar kidnappers capture you. They'll take you to the prison where you can meet up with Friliim and help orchestrate an escape.\n_If You Get This Step: This is a location update on the bridge. You'll be blinded and ported to the prison._\na cackling kidnapper says 'These ones are working with the bixies, which means they'll bring in good trade.'\na cackling kidnapper says 'Grab 'em!'\nYou've been kidnapped by cliknar!\nThe kidnappers bash you over the head!\nYou don't resist as the kidnappers knock you out and drag you back to a cliknar prison pit.\nYou awake in a cliknar prison pit.\nSkruffz says 'Welcome to the prison pits, friend!'\n========================================================================\nSTEP #3\n========================================================================\nRevive and speak with Engineer Friliim in the prison 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ You've been placed in the same prison pit as Engineer Friliim but he looks weak to move. Use the Wakey-Wakey Honey Rub Infiltrator Nallai apparently tucked into your backpack to revive him.\n_If You Get This Step: Click the item given to you on Friliim, then speak with him for the update._\nEngineer Friliim is unconscious. Infiltrator Nallai slipped a salve into your backpack to help with this situation. Find the Wakey-Wakey Honey Rub in your bags and use it to revive him.\nYou rub some of the pungent waxy substance under Engineer Friliim's nose, and he starts to stir.\nEngineer Friliim looks around groggily and says, 'Wha... Where... Ugh, that stuff smells horrible!'\nYou say, 'Hail, Engineer Friliim'\nEngineer Friliim holds his arm gingerly, but looks grateful. 'Thanks for the help, stranger. You up for a [prison break]?'\nYou say, 'Prison break?'\nEngineer Friliim says 'Yep, me and Skruffz were planning to break out before I, well, passed out like a wimp.'\nSkruffz looks embarrased and says, 'Don't worry, Friliim. I won't tell anyone back at camp about your pathetic collapse. And maybe you could forget about that whole [pebbles incident].' He winks at you.\nYou say, 'What pebbles incident?'\nEngineer Friliim chuckles and says, 'Don't worry, I'm sure he'll try it again soon. Come on, let's get out of here.'\n=====================\nConvince Engineer Friliim to attempt an escape 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Thankfully, you were taken to the same prison as Engineer Friliim. He looks quite scared, though. Speak with Engineer Friliim and convince him to escape from the prison with you.\n_If You Get This Step: This is a dialogue update._\nYou say, 'Hail, Engineer Friliim'\nEngineer Friliim says 'Welcome back to the land of the living, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Those cliknar gave you a good [beating].'\nYou say, 'A beating?'\nEngineer Friliim says 'They won't beat you any more. They haven't been too rough on us in here. Have they, Scruffz?'\nSkruffz says 'Nope, sometime they even throw rocks at us to eat! I [love it here]!'\nYou say, 'Love it here?'\nEngineer Friliim says 'Well, love is probably a strong word for it, but it's bearable. We can [wait out] the war in here.'\nYou say, 'Wait out the war?'\nEngineer Friliim says 'Look, I'm sure the generals want me back, but a jail break would be suicide without [my tools].'\nYou say, 'What about 'my tools'?'\nEngineer Friliim thinks for a little while and says, 'Yes, if we could reaquire my tools, we might stand a chance. Are you willing to [risk] it?'\nYou say, 'Let's risk it'\nEngineer Friliim smiles as he rolls up his sleeves. Then let's get out of here, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.\nEngineer Friliim says 'Skruffz, pack up your rocks, we'll eat them later!'\nSkruffz says 'Awww...'\n========================================================================\nSTEP #4\n========================================================================\nEscape your curiously unguarded prison pit 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ You can't see anyone guarding your prison pit. Cautiously try to walk out, and hope no one spots you. If they do, kill them.\n_If You Get This Step: Walk out of the prison. Sometimes, nothing spawns. Sometimes, you get ambushed by 2x \"a prison ambusher\" (hit for a max ~11,000; stunnable; mezzable; fully slowable). Sometimes, you get ambushed by 2x \"a rampaging bixie\" (hit for a max ~11,000; stunnable; mezzable; fully slowable; go non-aggro at 40% health). If mobs spawn, you have to deal with them for the update._\nFrenzied bixie warriors run forward and start to attack you without realizing you're prisoners.\na rampaging bixie recovers from its bloodlust and realizes you're on their side, 'Sorry, Thunder Gun! I don't know what came over me. I'll go take out some cliknar to help you get out of here alive!'\nEngineer Friliim shakes his head and says, 'These meatheads are more pain than they're worth!'\n=====================\nFind a rock to bash the cliknars guarding your prison pit with 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Your prison pit is guarded by two cliknar guards. Find a rock in the pit and use it to bash the guards' heads in. That should buy you time to escape.\n_If You Get This Step: Pick up a \"Surprisingly Aerodynamic Rock\" from the ground, target the distracted guards, and right-click the rock._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #5\n========================================================================\nKill prison wardens 0/4 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The cliknar prison is run by a small number of powerful wardens. Kill the cliknar wardens near the prison pit to shut down the whole system.\n_If You Get This Step: Pull and kill the cliknar prison wardens in the area. Each of these is a standard trash mob, except they spawn adds at 80%, 60%, 40%, and 20% health (3x \"a corpse hider\" - adds hit for a max ~2,100; have low hitpoints; and are mezzable and stunnable)._\nYou have slain a prison warden!\na prison warden's corpse says 'Let the hiders take my body, please. The prisoners will do terrible things to it.'\nEngineer Friliim says 'These cliknar are digusting! We may never get this stench off of us.'\n=====================\nFree bixie prisoners 0/30 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The cliknar have tons of bixie prisoners trapped here. Kill the cliknar guards near the prison pits to free the prisoners trapped inside.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill 10x \"a cliknar slaver\" in the area. Each has 3x \"an enslaved prisoner\" aggro-linked with it (mezzable, stunnable). The adds aren't too difficult in comparison to the cliknar and will drop aggro, updating the task, once the cliknar slaver dies._\na cliknar slaver has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\na cliknar slaver's corpse says 'How? ... You're just... a bug.'\nan enslaved prisoner says 'Thanks for everything, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'\nan enslaved prisoner says 'They're really dead? Wow. Thanks'\nan enslaved prisoner says 'I was holding back my punches.'\nan enslaved prisoner says 'No hard feelings, right?'\nan enslaved prisoner says 'Engineer Friliim! You're alive? Thank the honey!'\nan enslaved prisoner says 'You didn't lie about leaving no one behind, Thunder Gun! You're my hero!'\nan enslaved prisoner says 'Time to ditch these cliknar for good.'\n=====================\nKill cliknar prison guards 0/12 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ It looks like the cliknar prison guards have been killing most of their bixie prisoners. Kill the cliknar prison guards near the prison pits to stop their cruelty.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill 12x \"a pit guard\" (found throughout the prison pits in the area). These hit for a max ~14,250 and are stunnable and mezzable._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #6\n========================================================================\nFind Friliium's toolkit in one of the cliknar chests and give it to him 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Engineer Friliim needs to recover his toolkit, which he saw the cliknar put into an equipment case when he was kidnapped. Bring Friliim to equipment cases in the prison pits in the area until he finds one with his toolkit inside.\n_If You Get This Step: Lead Engineer Friliim around to equipment crates in the area. He'll follow your group around like a mercenary would, occasionally warping to your location. You need to position him about right on top of the crate before he'll notice it._\nEngineer Friliim spots a chest and runs to open it.\nEngineer Friliim says 'The case they put my toolkit into looked just like this one!'\nEngineer Friliim says 'Socks... antennae... there's nothing good in here!'\nEngineer Friliim says 'This case probably has my toolkit inside!'\nEngineer Friliim says 'Well, okay. I guess not. The next one probably does though!'\nEngineer Friliim says 'Okay, the first two were unlucky. This third equipment case will have my stuff!'\nEngineer Friliim kicks the equipment case away and grunts, 'Nothing.'\nEngineer Friliim says 'Fourth try's the charm?'\nEngineer Friliim says 'Eww, gross. I don't even want to touch that. It's definitely not my toolkit.'\nEngineer Friliim says 'Okay, this is getting tiresome. Just give me my stuff already!'\nEngineer Friliim says 'This isn't my stuff. It's not even stuff! It's just empty! Who keeps an empty equipment case?'\nEngineer Friliim says 'I'm about to go Thunder Gun all over this box if my toolkit isn't in here.'\nEngineer Friliim says 'You got off easy this time, box. The Thunder Gun is back in business!'\nEngineer Friliim puts on his toolbelt and grabs his favorite compactible weapons from it.\nEngineer Friliim says 'What do you-- wait, don't press that!'\nEngineer Friliim sighs and says softly, 'Yes you are, Scruffz. You'll always be a crazy little butterfly...'\n=====================\nRecover Friliium's toolkit from the kleptomanic cliknar and give it to him 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Engineer Friliim needs to recover his toolkit, which he saw a cliknar snatch from the pile when he was kidnapped. Kill the kleptomanic cliknar and return it to him. It wanders along the eastern edges of the trenches near the prison pits.\n_If You Get This Step: Find the mob called \"a kleptomanic cliknar\" (roamer along the eastern edge of the zone). Kill it, loot the \"Thunder Gun Toolkit\", and turn it in to Engineer Friliium. This mob has about twice the hitpoints of an average mob here, hits a bit harder, but not overly difficult. It's mezzable and stunnable._\na kleptomaniac cliknar has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\na kleptomaniac cliknar's corpse says 'Bury me... with... your stuff...'\n--You have looted a Thunder Gun Toolkit.--\nEngineer Friliim says 'Thanks, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_! I hope the cliknar didn't break anything.'\nEngineer Friliim puts on his toolbelt and grabs his favorite compactible weapons from it.\n=====================\nBuild some tools for Friliim at the nearby forge and give them to him 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Engineer Friliim lost his toolkit when he was kidnapped. He wants you to make him some rudimentary tools at the forge in the prison pits. Kill Kreppo the Curious, the cliknar blacksmith, to get Refined Bixie Tools. Then use them at the forge to build some new tools. Then give them to Friliim once you're done.\n_If You Get This Step: Find Kreppo the Curious in the far southeastern part of the zone, by a large forge. Kill it (average difficulty with about double the average hitpoints; stunnable; mezzable), loot the tools from its corpse. With the tools, stand in or near the cliknar forge where Kreppo was and right-click them to create \"Thunder Gun Toolkit\". Give this to Engineer Friliim to update the step._\nKreppo the Curious says 'You bring me more exotic weapons to experiment with? Perfect!'\nKreppo the Curious has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nKreppo the Curious's corpse says 'They're brilliant... I've never seen such brilliant weapons.'\nEngineer Friliim says 'Here are the schematics for my tools. Follow them exactly!'\nYou heat the unrefined tools in the forge, and work them against the stone walls to shape them per Engineer Friliim's instructions.\nEngineer Friliim says 'That actually looks pretty decent. Well done!'\n========================================================================\nSTEP #7\n========================================================================\nFree 6 captured mole-mounts 0/6 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The bixie army has been attempting to push the front line with mole riders. Many of the moles have been abandoned and captured by the cliknar, who plan to eat them. Kill the hungry cliknar surrounding moles in the southeast trenches, and tell the moles to flee the hive.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill \"a hungry \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\" cliknar mobs around captured moles, then hail the moles._\n=====================\nKill rageblind bixies 0/10 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The bixies in the southeast trenches nearby have gone into a blind-rage, and are killing anything that comes close, even bixie prisoners trying to escape. There's no better solution. You have to kill them.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill any 10 of the rageblind bixies all over the area (standard trash mobs)._\na rageblind torcher has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\na rageblind torcher's corpse says 'I've done nothing wrong, traitor.'\na rageblind slasher has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\na rageblind slasher's corpse looks at you, realizing for the first time that you're not a cliknar. 'What have I done?'\nEngineer Friliim says 'I wish we didn't have to kill our own, but those bixies were out of control. They shame our entire army.'\n=====================\nTaste-test roasted moles 0/10 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ The cliknar army has baited the southeast cliknar trenches with moles roasting over barbecue pits, some of which have been poisoned. Find roasting moles in the trenches, kill any cliknar around them, and then taste-test the meal to see if it's safe for prisoners to eat.\n_If You Get This Step: Arou\n\n...[Walkthrough truncated for in-game performance]...",
