      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Neriak Fourth Gate [zone=943]\n**Who:**\n- Noxhil V`Sek [npc=44050]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Related Zones:**\n- Neriak Fourth Gate: Hate Rising [zone=987]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Dreadguard conjuror [npc=45710]\n- Dreadguard swordsman [npc=45711]\n- Kavi V`Lask [npc=45712]\n- Lanys T`Vyl [npc=47249]\n- Prince Tarant Thex [npc=45714]\n- Xavier T`Ser [npc=45713]\n- a dark chest [npc=45705]\n- a spiteful lich [npc=45707]\n- a spiteful shade [npc=45708]\n- a spiteful specter [npc=45709]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Houses of Thex [quest=7286]\n- Neriak #1: The Missing Scroll [quest=7283]\n- Neriak #2: Fourth Gate Investigation [quest=7284]\n- Neriak #3: Cautious Recruitment [quest=7285]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Jan 22 04:41:56 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This group mission begins with Noxhil V`Sek ( **click for map image**) in Neriak Fourth Gate._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Level 95\n\\- Completed \"The Missing Scroll\"\n\\- Completed \"Fourth Gate Investigation\"\n\\- Completed \"Cautious Recruitment\"\n\\- Completed \"Houses of Thex\" (group mission)\n\\- Must be illusioned as a Dark Elf\n**Steps & Summary**\n\\- Say \"band\" to request the task and \"meet\" to zone in.\nGain entry to the library 0/1 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\nObtain the Scroll of G'Han 0/1 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\nOpen the chest 0/1 (Neriak Fourth Gate)\n\\- Note: The NPCs Kavi and Xavier have beneficial auras that mitigate spell and melee damage, so it's in your interest to keep them alive (they can be buffed and healed). (There is an achievement for allowing them to die, however.)\nFIRST PHASE:\n\\- Inside the instance, say \"ready\" to Prince Tarant Thex to begin the event.\n\\- After a short delay, two mobs spawn (\"a spiteful lich\" and \"a spiteful shade\").\n\\-\\-\\- \"a spiteful lich\" has a damage aura around it and is snareable/mezzable.\n\\-\\-\\- \"a spiteful shade\" casts a 10k spell damage shield when low in health (is mezzable).\n\\- There a minimum number of mobs that must be killed to progress the task, and until you meet that requirement, you'll always have at least two mobs up at a time.\n\\- Mobs called \"a spiteful specter\" spawn randomly upon lich and shade deaths. These also must be killed.\n\\- Specters will focus their DPS on the friendly NPCs (Kavi and Xavier).\n\\- Once you've completed this step, you'll have a short break.\nSECOND PHASE:\n\\- Meet Prince Tarant Thex in the upper floor of the library.\n\\- A script unfolds, and then he goes aggro along with two Dreadguard adds.\n\\- The Prince summons two Dreadguard adds every 20% health.\n\\- All adds must die before the event can be completed.\n\\- Dreadguard swordsmen are charmable.\n\\- Dreadguard conjurors cast AE damage spells.\n\\- Kill all adds and bring the Prince to 3% health for the win.\n\n---\n\n**Requesting the Task**\nYou say, 'Hail, Noxhil V`Sek'\nNoxhil V`Sek says 'The prince has informed me that the time is nigh for infiltrating the library. I will leave it up to you whether to proceed with a small [band] of friends or a large [force]. Otherwise, you may recruit a [group] for infiltrating the library or let me know if you are [interested] in keeping the scroll out of the hands of the King and Queen.'\nYou say, 'I have a small band'\nNoxhil V`Sek says 'Let us hope you are up to the task. I will arrange for you to [meet] with Prince Tarant when you are ready.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Hate Rising'.\nThe prince has agreed to help you gain entry to the library and help you acquire the Scroll of G'Han. He does not wish either the king or queen to have it as it would upset the balance of power in Neriak.\nYou say, 'We'll meet him there'\nNoxhil V`Sek says 'Success unto you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Neriak - Fourth Gate.\n\n---\n\n**PHASE ONE: Triggering the Event**\n_Speak with Prince Tarant Thex to begin the event (\"ready\"). He and his two cohorts will move to the library door, then two adds will spawn (1x \"a spiteful lich\" + 1x \"a spiteful shade\")._\nYou say, 'Hail, Prince Tarant Thex'\nPrince Tarant Thex says, in Dark Elvish, 'I have managed to obtain the key to the library, though its caretakers will likely discover it missing soon. I know not what we will find inside so be prepared for anything. Let me know when you are [ready] to enter. You may also [leave] if you are too cowardly to continue.'\nYou say, 'Ready!'\nPrince Tarant Thex says, in Dark Elvish, 'Very well. Let us proceed.'\n_The three NPCs path up to the library entrance, at which point you see:_\nPrince Tarant Thex leaps backwards as he shouts 'Get back, there's a spell on it!'\n\n---\n\n**PHASE ONE: The Spiteful Undead**\n_\"a spiteful lich\" is snareable and mezzable. It has an aura around it called \"Lich Touch\":_\nLich Touch: Single Target, Cold (-650)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 6500\n_It also casts \"Icy Rain\":_\nIcy Rain: Targeted AE 30', Cold (-999)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 15000\n_\"a spiteful shade\" is mezzable. It procs \"Shade Touch\":_\nShade Touch: Single Target, Cold (-999)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 1500\n_When low in health, they cast \"Shield of Spite\" on themselves:_\nShield of Spite: Self 0', Unresistable (-650)\n1: Spell Damage Shield (10158)\n_Occasionally, as you kill the above mobs, you'll get \"a spiteful specter\" spawn. These mobs focus their DPS on Kavi and Xavier, so if you're keeping them alive, be sure to pay attention to their health while a specter is up. The specters don't cast any AEs._\n_Kill a certain amount of \"spiteful\" mobs to progress the task._\nPrince Tarant Thex mutters to himself 'Nothing is ever easy when mother is involved.' He surveys the scene around him and says 'We must must move quickly now. I can give you a minute to rest but no more.'\n\n---\n\n**PHASE TWO: Encounter in the Library**\n_Next, find Prince Tarant Thex upstairs. A script will unfold:_\nPrince Tarant Thex shouts, in Dark Elvish, 'This is it!'\nPrince Tarant Thex says, in Dark Elvish, 'And now that I have it, you are no longer necessary.'\nPrince Tarant Thex shouts, in Dark Elvish, 'Dreadguards!'\n_Two Dreadguards enter the area (not aggro yet)._\nPrince Tarant Thex smiles as he says 'You see, I had no intention of allowing you to possess the scroll as I have already promised it to my love. Once I have silenced you, I will deliver it to her.'\nPrince Tarant Thex shouts, in Dark Elvish, 'Dreadguards, forward!'\n_All three mobs are now aggro._\n_\"Dreadguard conjuror\" casts two AEs:_\nMolten Beam: Area Hatelist 30', Fire (-999)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 15000\nMolten Rain: Targeted AE 30', Fire (-999)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 15000\n_\"Dreadguard swordsman\" casts no spells._\n_The Prince summons two additional Dreadguard adds (one of each type) every 20% health. All adds have to be killed before Prince Tarant Thex can be defeated._\n_Once all adds are dead and the Prince reaches 3% health, you've won the event._\n\n---\n\n**Event Completion**\n_The Prince falls to the ground, seemingly unconscious, and Lanys T`Vyl appears..._\nLanys T`Vyl steps out from the shadows.\nLanys T`Vyl says, in Dark Elvish, 'It looks like I arrived just in time to save you.'\nLanys T`Vyl quickly searches the prince.\nLanys T`Vyl says in a sultry, sarcastic tone, 'I'll be taking that, my prince.'\nLanys T`Vyl looks up from the wounded prince toward your party, 'As for the rest of you, I shall leave you with these paltry rewards. After all, you've earned them. Despite the fact that you were driven here by the ramblings of a madman, your assistance in obtaining the scroll has proven invaluable.'\nLanys T`Vyl speaks with uncharacteristic concern, 'You're like mad dogs, powerful but aimless. So eager to serve at the hand of any master that offers you your next meal. You do realize that if that madman gets his hands on this scroll it will mean the end of Norrath, don't you?'\nLanys T`Vyl says, in Dark Elvish, 'I don't often waste my sincerities on your lot, but I offer you this truth, it is imperative that this treasure not fall into the hands of the forsaken. I suggest you reflect upon your arrangement with Zebuxoruk and really question where your loyalties lie.'\n_Lanys T`Vyl gates out of the library while the Prince remains unconscious..._\n_Rewards:_\n225 platinum\nExperience\n_Possible Chest Loot (1 item + 0-1 armor piece + 0-1 spell per task):_\nCerulean Sash of the Spire\nElaborate Vine Pendant\nEnigmatic Teir`Dal Eye\nFlowing Crimson Wool Sash\nNotched Leather Waistguard\nPlundered Sceptre of the Court\nRough Leather Girding\nRoyal Bixie Scepter\nBoots of Latent Ether\nBracer of Latent Ether\nTunic of Latent Ether\nSpell: Aura of Divinity Rk. II\nSpell: Force of Abrogation Rk. II\nSpell: Insidious Deflection Rk. II\nSpell: Pillar of Ro Rk. II\nTome: Focused Clamor of Claws Rk. II\nTome: Focused Storm of Blades Rk. II\nTome: Reflex Rk. II\n- Boots of Latent Ether [item=114720]\n- Bracer of Latent Ether [item=113263]\n- Cerulean Sash of the Spire [item=115020]\n- Elaborate Vine Pendant [item=114863]\n- Enigmatic Teir`Dal Eye [item=115023]\n- Flowing Crimson Wool Sash [item=115017]\n- Notched Leather Waistguard [item=115039]\n- Plundered Sceptre of the Court [item=115115]\n- Rough Leather Girding [item=115099]\n- Royal Bixie Scepter [item=115126]\n- Spell: Aura of Divinity Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Spell: Force of Abrogation Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Spell: Insidious Deflection Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Spell: Pillar of Ro Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Tome: Focused Clamor of Claws Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Tome: Focused Storm of Blades Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Tome: Reflex Rk. II [tradeable]\n- Tunic of Latent Ether [item=114722]",
    },
