      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Argin-Hiz [zone=1004]\n**Who:**\n- Vasser Fayeil [ _Quests, Missions, Raid_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Chunk of Solenium [item=117822]\n- Keeper's Ring [item=117824]\n- Moltenite [item=117823]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Argin-Hiz: The Keeper's Ring [zone=1005]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Ashen Remains [npc=47332]\n- Faldern Yvell [npc=47312]\n- Faldern Yvell [npc=47333]\n- Nara Fayeil [npc=47334]\n- Nara Fayeil [npc=47274]\n- Vasser Fayeil [npc=47335]\n- a laborer [npc=47282]\n- an ember trooper [npc=47331]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Argin-Hiz #1: Burning Curiosity [quest=7612]\n- Argin-Hiz #2: The Reclusive Collector [quest=7613]\n- Argin-Hiz #4: A Dimming Light [quest=7615]\n- Burn Out [quest=7620]\n- Raid Expedition: Burn Out [quest=7621]\n- Rings of Fire [quest=7619]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Jul 15 23:45:37 2014\nModified: Sat Sep 27 08:33:55 2025 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\nThis solo task is the third in a series of four. It begins with Vasser Fayeil [npc=47269] ( **click for map image**) in Argin-Hiz.\nPre-Requisites:\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completed Burning Curiosity [quest=7612]\n\\- Completed The Reclusive Collector [quest=7613]\nSay \" **promise**\" to request the task.\n\n---\n\n!\n\n---\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Vasser Fayeil'\nVasser Fayeil examines his recently returned ring in detail, 'This band has seen better days. The metal is dull and the setting empty, but it still holds so much sentimental value.' The shopkeeper sighs, 'I realize I will need to part with this ring in order for you to do what you came here to do, but before I hand it over, can you [promise] me to help Nara escape before you enter Keeper's Hall? Once they find out we've aided you, they will come for her.\nYou say, 'I promise'\nVasser Fayeil forces a faint smile, 'Very well then. The ring won't do you much good in its current state. I'll have to repair it before it can be used to access Keeper's Hall. I can reshape the band with a chunk of solenium and fill the setting with moltenite. Both of these materials can be found within our mines, but are fairly rare. Return to me once you have the items and I can start to repair the ring.\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Keeper's Ring'.\nReparing the Keeper's Ring is your ticket to entering the Keeper's Hall.\n\n---\n\n1\\. Loot a Chunk of Solenium from laborers within the mines 0/1 (Argin-Hiz)\n2\\. Loot Moltenite from laborers within the mines 0/1 (Argin-Hiz)\nChunk of Solenium [item=117822] and Moltenite [item=117823] both drop off a laborer [npc=47282] found throughout the mines. You must be on this step for them to drop. They appear to be common.\n\n---\n\n3\\. Bring the Chunk of Solenium to Vasser Fayeil 0/1 (Argin-Hiz)\n4\\. Bring the Moltenite to Vasser Fayeil 0/1 (Argin-Hiz)\nVasser Fayeil takes the Chunk of Solenium from you and begins to work on repairing the band.\nVasser Fayeil takes the Moltenite from you and begins to cut and shape it so that it fits within the ring's setting.\n5\\. Speak to Vasser 0/1 (Argin-Hiz)\nYou say, 'Hail, Vasser Fayeil'\nVasser Fayeil puts the finishing touches on his work as he speaks, 'Unfortunately, I wasn't able to repair the ring. It was too damaged to recover. The good news is, after combining the materials you brought me with the smelted down band I was able to create two new rings. You may keep one, as promised, but I was hoping you could deliver the other to Nara before you help her [escape].\nYou receive 2x Keeper's Ring [item=117824]: one for the task, and one for you.\n**At this point, you now have access to the Keeper's Tower (the large structure in the northwestern part of the zone).**\nYou say, 'Escape? What?'\nVasser Fayeil frowns, his eyes filled with worry, 'You remember your promise, don't you? You said you'd help Nara flee this land. Please, you must help my daughter escape Argin-Hiz before the Keepers come for her.'\n\n---\n\n6\\. Deliver a Keeper's Ring to Nara Fayeil 0/1 (Argin-Hiz)\nNara Fayeil [npc=47274] ( **click for map image**) is found at the north end of the zone-in field.\nNara Fayeil fights back tears as she places the tiny band on her finger, 'I know it's not my mother's ring, but I can still feel her presence when I wear it.'\n7\\. Speak to Nara 0/1 (Argin-Hiz)\nYou say, 'Hail, Nara Fayeil'\nNara Fayeil smiles at you with hope in her eyes, 'You came back to help me flee this place, didn't you? Vasser said you'd be my escort beyond the forest. What about [Faldern]? Did he mention him, too?'\nYou say, 'Who is Faldern? There was no 'Faldern' in this deal'\nNara Fayeil says 'Faldern is one of my only friends here. We used to explore the forests together until the Keepers took him away to work the mines. I can't leave him behind to die. I promise he won't be any trouble. Just let him know that we plan to escape. That's all I ask.'\n\n---\n\n8\\. Find Faldern and fill him in on the escape plan 0/1 (Argin-Hiz)\nFaldern Yvell [npc=47312] is found in the far southern part of the mines (/loc 0, -1685, -226).\nYou say, 'Hail, Faldern Yvell'\nFaldern Yvell wipes his brow, 'Nara sent you, did she? I'm glad to know she's safe, but... she's not really thinking of escaping, is she? The Keepers would kill us both if we got caught!' Faldern sighs, 'But I guess I'd just die in these mines anyway. I might as well take the risk. Let's [meet] at Vasser's shop.\nArgin-Hiz is now available to you.\nAt this time, you are assigned an expedition. Say \"meet\" to zone into the instanced zone.\n\n---\n\n9\\. Meet Faldern and Nara at Vasser's shop 0/1 (Argin-Hiz)\nHere, you'll enter your very own expedition/instance. Lucky you.\nNote: In order to zone in, you have to be on this very step in the task (meaning, if you want help from other players, they must be on this step as well).\nThis task step updates upon entry.\n10\\. Escort Nara and Faldern safely out of the city 0/1 (Argin-Hiz)\n11\\. Kill any troopers that stand in your way 0/7 (Argin-Hiz)\nYou need to make it to /location -1400, 1000, -348 (about three-quarters the way through the zone-in field area). There are multiple an ember trooper [npc=47331] mobs in the area - clear these away. These hit for a max ~15,500 and are mezzable and stunnable.\nOnce the troopers are dead, hail Faldern Yvell in order to get him to follow you like a pet.\nYou say, 'Hail, Faldern Yvell'\nFaldern Yvell says 'Nara and I are ready to leave this place whenever you are. Just lead the way, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'\nThere are numerous creatures found in the zone-in field, but they don't aggro the NPCs and you can invis past them. Once you get to the update point, the NPCs stop.\nFaldern Yvell comes to a stop and screams, 'Nara, wait! Something's wrong...' The fire elf shivers as his skin turns a damp grey color. 'It's? so? cold.'\nNara Fayeil cries out as she rushes toward her friend, 'Faldren! Are you okay?'\nFaldern Yvell shivers and falls silently to the ground, his inner fire completely extinguished causing his body to turn to ash.\nFaldern Yvell says 'Please don't forget me. I tried...'\nFaldern Yvell died.\nAshen Remains [npc=47332] spawns (KoS, but NOT auto-aggro).\n\n---\n\n12\\. Defeat the Ashen Remains 0/1 (Argin-Hiz)\nIts melee power appears to be slightly less than that of the troopers you fought earlier. Like the other mobs, the Ashen Remains is mezzable and stunnable. It is recommended you pull it away from its spawn location as there are multiple animals that path by its location.\nAshen Remains has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nThe small shards of stone composing the dervish fall lifelessly to the floor.\n\n---\n\n13\\. Speak to Nara 0/1 (Argin-Hiz)\nYou say, 'Hail, Nara Fayeil'\nNara Fayeil sobs as she stands over the pile of ash, 'Faldern, no... How can this be?' The heartbroken fire elf looks up at you with teary eyes, 'How could he simply turn to ash? This isn't right.' Nara glances down at her warm skin, 'I should be ash, too, shouldn't I? We need to [return] to my father. He'll be able to make some sense of this.'\nYou say, 'I wish to return'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Argin-Hiz.\nYou appear back in the non-instanced version of the zone.\n\n---\n\n14\\. Return to Vasser to tell him what happened 0/1 (Argin-Hiz)\nYou say, 'Hail, Vasser Fayeil'\nVasser Fayeil tries to remain calm as you recount the events that took place when trying to escape, 'How can it be that Faldern turned to ash? Someone can't just die from leaving the city, can they? Have the Keeper's known this all along?' The shopkeeper's eyes light up, 'They have! Their rings, they must serve as some sort of protection. That explains why Faldern perished but Nara was able to survive leaving the city.'\nYou helped Vasser recreate rings that protect fire elves from turning to ash when they leave the city.\n_Rewards:_\nKeeper's Ring [item=117824]\n187 platinum, 5 gold\nExperience (about 3 AAs at Level 100)\n- Keeper's Ring [item=117824]",
