      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Degmar, the Lost Castle [zone=1019]\n**Who:**\n- Researcher Neckchi [npc=47722]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 105\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Second Stage Frangible Ore [item=121120]\n- Tiny Silver Hammer of Brell [item=121080]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a spectral apparition [npc=48069]\n- a spectral furor [npc=48070]\n- a spectral haunt [npc=48071]\n- a spectral librarian [npc=48072]\n- a spectral rager [npc=48073]\n**Era:** | !The Darkened Sea\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Oct 26 03:38:32 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**The Darkened Sea Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This solo task begins with Researcher Neckchi ( **click for map image**) at the zone-in of Degmar, the Lost Castle._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Minimum Level 95\n\\- No tasks\n_Say \"destroy\" to request the task._\nYou say, 'Hail, Researcher Neckchi'\nResearcher Neckchi says 'Oh, thank the gods, a sane person. You would not believe what I've been through. But you're obviously an adventurer, so perhaps you could [care] less what I've been through since you face adversity every day. Let me get to the point. I could use your help on a [task], and I can help [you] along the way.'\nYou say, 'I care!'\nResearcher Neckchi says 'Thank you! So few adventurers want to talk, and instead want to just get to it. I am in quite the [quandary].'\nYou say, 'What quandary?'\nResearcher Neckchi says 'The combine sent me here alone! Assuming all would be well within the habitat, and I could go about my [mission] in peace! But all is not [well]!'\nYou say, 'What was your mission?'\nResearcher Neckchi says 'I was sent through, all but blindly, to set up a return teleport device, and contact the dwarves for their help in repairing the dome in Katta Castrum. While I have no problems setting up the device, things did not go [well] with the dwarves.'\nYou say, 'All isn't well?'\nResearcher Neckchi says 'I thought it odd that this guard house was empty, but it gave me the space and privacy I needed to set up the return device. Once the device was active, I attempted to make contact, but not only was I immediately [attacked] by dwarves, I saw a [ghost]!'\nYou say, 'Attacked?!'\nResearcher Neckchi says 'Yes! They caught me by surprise and dragged me to their Commander. He would not even listen to my pleas that I was on a diplomatic mission. He accused me of being a spy to scout the Castle before an attack, and he threw me into his dungeon. I saw so many [ghosts] I thought I would go mad myself! Luckily, [Damton] Silverhammer over there freed me and protected me from the guards long enough to cast an evacuate spell and get us back here to the guard house.'\nYou say, 'A ghost!'\nResearcher Neckchi says 'Horrible things! The dead should remain dead! And when they pass through you... just, yuck! Please, I don't want to talk about ghosts any longer. Just thinking about them is terrible! Sorry, I know it's not rational, but I have phasmophobia and I just can't seem to conquer it.'\nYou say, 'Who is Damton?'\nResearcher Neckchi says 'She is a very nice dwarf. The only sane one that I've met, though she claims there are others. Speak with her and she may have more information for you.'\nYou say, 'You, can help me?'\nResearcher Neckchi says 'Getting right to the point, if you [destroy] some [ghosts] and retrieve two items from the ends of the [branches] in this oddly designed castle, I will give you a device that will teleport you back to this guard room.'\nYou say, 'What branches are you talking about?'\nResearcher Neckchi says 'Well, I'm not sure what insane person designed this castle, but there are very few cross passages. Other adventurers reported to me that there are only two main branches, and that once you get to the end of a branch, to return here, you have to come all the way back through the rooms you just exited. Because the [ghosts] don't rest for long, you have to fight your way back again. Very inconvenient and dangerous.'\nYou say, 'I'll destroy some'\nResearcher Neckchi says 'Very good. I've updated your journal with the task particulars, But I can give you more [details] if you wish.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Castle Travel'.\nResearcher Neckchi assumes that you do not like ghosts, despite the fact that you are braver than he. He will create a device for you that will teleport you back to the guard house if you retrieve the right items for him, and kill some ghosts along the way.\nYou say, 'Hold on... More details...'\nResearcher Neckchi says 'First off, destroy any aggressive [ghost] you cross paths with. That is the basic fee I charge for this device. You're welcome to kill any non-aggressive ghosts if you like. I wish those horrible things would stay dead. You should, of course, defend yourself against the dwarves, but don't kill them if you can avoid it. To make the device function, I will need a focus item from the rooms at the end of each branch. Adventurers have mentioned a [workshop] and a [chapel].'\nYou say, 'What is the workshop?'\nResearcher Neckchi says 'Within the workshop, I have heard of some delicate magical ore. A sample of this will be ideal for the focus. Previous adventurers have brought some back, and they told me that it's very sensitive to travel magic, so be sure that you do not use any magic that would cause you to travel, or it might disintegrate.'\nYou say, 'What is the chapel?'\nResearcher Neckchi says 'Within the chapel, you will find some small hammers used as a prayer focus for Brell. Please bring me one of these as the focus for that branch. Don't worry about chapel running out; they seem to have a vast supply of these hammers.'\n\n---\n\n!\nP 189.5671, 238.7247, 44.9989, 0, 0, 0, 1, ore\nP 193.3842, 201.5962, 44.9989, 0, 0, 0, 1, ore\nP 191.1917, 152.9781, 40.9989, 0, 0, 0, 1, ore\nP 157.3299, 143.2104, 44.9989, 0, 0, 0, 1, ore\nP 124.2548, 142.4542, 40.9989, 0, 0, 0, 1, ore\nP 89.8103, 148.3458, 40.9989, 0, 0, 0, 1, ore\nP 88.3539, 200.7745, 44.9989, 0, 0, 0, 1, ore\nP 100.9480, 273.1967, 42.6702, 0, 0, 0, 1, ore\\_(3)\nP 138.0611, 273.4642, 42.6702, 0, 0, 0, 1, ore\\_(4)\nP -131.7532, 160.7996, -10.5823, 0, 0, 0, 1, hammers\n\n---\n\nKill 8 ghosts 0/8 (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\nCollect 2 Tiny Silver Hammers of Brell 0/2 (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\nCollect 2 Second Stage Frangible Ores 0/2 (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\n_Kill any eight mobs with \"spectral\" in its name. In the Chapel, you can find hammer ground spawns (appear as small hammers around the dwarven statue). And in the Workshop, you can find ore ground spawns (appear as piles of ore with a hammer)._\n**NOTE: Ores are flagged as \"No Zone\" which means if you zone, they disappear from your inventory. (Hammers are not flagged this way.) You can COH around group members and it will NOT destroy ore.**\n\n---\n\nGive Researcher Neckchi the Tiny Hammer of Brell 0/2 (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\nGive Researcher Neckchi the Second Stage Frangible Ore 0/2 (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\nResearcher Neckchi is impressed with your bravery.\n_Rewards:_\nExperience\n75 platinum\n_You receive \"Degmar Relocation Device\" (teleport item that only works in Degmar - ports you to the gate room). It's non-combat cast only, with a 30-minute recast timer._\n_This task is repeatable with a 6-hour lockout timer from the time of request._\n- Degmar Relocation Device [item=119687]",
