      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Degmar, the Lost Castle [zone=1019]\n**Who:**\n- Damton Silverhammer [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 105\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Degmar's Commoners +225\n**Factions Lowered:**\n**Quest Items:**\n- Degmar Castle Ale [item=121349]\n- Fancy Drumstick [item=121347]\n- Fancy Fruitcake [item=121346]\n- Fancy Green Apple [item=121343]\n- Fancy Ham [item=121348]\n- Fancy Mushroom [item=121345]\n- Fancy Pumpkin [item=121344]\n- Fancy Red Apple [item=121342]\n- Fancy Turkey [item=121340]\n- Library Book [item=121338]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a librarian - Degmar - 1 [npc=48066]\n- a spectral librarian [npc=48072]\n- a spectral reveler [npc=48074]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Castle Crasher [quest=7748]\n- Castle Growth [quest=7749]\n- Castle Relic [quest=7757]\n**Era:** | !The Darkened Sea\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Oct 26 03:39:01 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**The Darkened Sea Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This solo task begins with Damton Silverhammer ( **click for map image**), located at the zone-in of Degmar, the Lost Castle._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Minimum Level 95\n\\- No tasks\n_Say \"fetch\" to request this task._\nYou say, 'Hail, Damton Silverhammer'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'Salutations, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ You look like the adventuring type and I wager you'd like work. I can use help gathering [supplies] and seeing if we can overturn my [banishment]. If you are the more conversational type, I can also tell you a little about Degmar's [Castle].'\nYou say, 'What supplies do you need?'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'While I have plenty of room to sleep, supplies are rather scarce. I will reward you if you [fetch] me some supplies.'\nYou say, 'I'll fetch some'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'Thank you. I've made notes of what I need in your journal, but I can give you more [details] if you like.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Castle Raid'.\nDamton has been banished to the guard house and would like for you to retrieve supplies for her from the castle.\nDefeat denizens of the library and collect library books from them, so she has something to entertain her. Go to the dining hall and collect food for her. The elvish ghosts in the hall will attack if you do not dance with them before you collect the food. Spend at least one minute dancing with them. Collect Degmar Ale from the brewery. The dwarfs in the brewery are likely to strenuously object.\nYou say, 'Give me more details...'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'I would like you to [fetch] some [books], [food], and [ale].'\nYou say, 'Ale?'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'The brewery can be accessed through the dining room. Once there, you can retrieve ale however you like, but you may find the bartenders and patrons a bit... possessive, with their ale. They will notice if any goes missing, so be prepared!'\nYou say, 'Where do I get food?'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'To gather food you will need to go west on the upper level of the foyer and through the merchant's quarters to the [dining] hall. While passing through the merchant quarters, if you feel you have time, and if you can find her, let Priestess Gli'helin know that I'm okay.'\nYou say, 'What about the dining hall?'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'You will find the food in the dining hall. Don't worry about depleting the supply as more food is generated magically. But be careful, the elven dancers in that room will want to dance with you, and if you do not appease them, they will attack. You don't need to show skill, just spend at least a minute in their presence.'\nYou say, 'What about the books?'\nDamton Silverhammer says '[Neckchi] over there is a fine conversationalist, but he is often busy, and even when I can get his attention he's likely to drone on and on about esoteric details of teleportation magic. Some books from the [library] will help me pass the time.'\nYou say, 'Tell me about the library'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'The library is immediately east of the foyer on the lower level. Most of the books on the shelves are so old that they'll crumble if you handle them. You will instead need to gain them from the library patrons. I encourage you to take them from the ghostly librarians, but I will not censure you if you take some from the crazy dwarves digging in the library. There is no telling what harm the madmen will cause with their digging.'\n\n---\n\n!\n\n---\n\n1\\. Kill 5 Librarians 0/5 (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\n2\\. Collect 2 Library Books 0/2 (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\n_Kill any mobs with \"librarian\" in their name (both live and undead count). Library books have a 50% drop rate if you're on this step. Note that undead librarians will use standard mez spells._\n\n---\n\n3\\. Dance with the revelers to appease them 0/1 (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\nYou can just stand between the tables for 1 minute and get the update.\n4\\. Collect 5 Fancy Foods 0/5 (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\nDon't take any food until the dancers have been appeased.\nOutside the party room is Herrul Bakewell. He sells the Fancy party foods (free), if he is kos to you invis/sneak.\n5\\. Collect 2 Degmar Castle Ales 0/2 (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\n_Head to the dining area where you'll find numerous tables set up along with a spread of food along the room's north wall. Before you pick at the food, you need to 'appease' the revelers in the room by dancing with them... To do this, all you need to do is move around in the room for at least 60 seconds straight. The task will update, and you'll see an emote:_\nThe revelers look at you and raise a glass in celebration.\n_You can now pick up five food items from the tables. (There are five types; any combination counts.) **NOTE:** These items are actual food; don't eat them!_\n_If you DON'T dance with the revelers before picking at the food, they aggro you. You can also draw auto mob aggro if you hang around in the room for more than five minutes without dancing. In this case, you start seeing emote warnings 60 seconds before they'll attack:_\nThe revelers look at you and frown.\nThe revelers look at you, disapointed that you have not reveled with them, and attack.\na spectral reveler says 'Why won't you dance?'\nYou have been slain by a spectral reveler!\na spectral reveler says 'See. You should be dancing.'\n_For the Degmar Castle Ales, head to the Brewery (just east of the dining room with the revelers) and pick up 2x \"Degmar Castle Ale\" from the bars in there._\n\n---\n\n6\\. Deliver a library book to Damton Silverhammer 0/2 (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\n7\\. Deliver 5 Fancy foods to Damton Silverhammer 0/5 (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\n8\\. Deliver Degmar Castle Ale to Damton Silverhammer 0/2 (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\n_Upon turn-in:_\nDamton Silverhammer is grateful for your assistance.\n\n---\n\n_Rewards:_\nExperience\n75 platinum\nFaction with Degmar's Commoners (+225)\n_This task is repeatable with a 6-hour lockout timer from the time of request._",
    },
