      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Degmar, the Lost Castle [zone=1019]\n**Who:**\n- Damton Silverhammer [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 105\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Degmar's Commoners +225\n**Factions Lowered:**\n**Quest Items:**\n- Degmar Ceremonial Hammer [item=121081]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a Degmar ambusher [npc=48058]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Castle Growth [quest=7749]\n- Castle Raid [quest=7747]\n- Castle Relic [quest=7757]\n**Era:** | !The Darkened Sea\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Oct 26 03:40:58 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**The Darkened Sea Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This solo task begins with Damton Silverhammer ( **click for map image**), located at the zone-in of Degmar, the Lost Castle._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Minimum Level 95\n\\- No tasks\n_Say \"resolve\" to request the task._\nYou say, 'Hail, Damton Silverhammer'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'Salutations, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ You look like the adventuring type and I wager you'd like work. I can use help gathering [supplies] and seeing if we can overturn my [banishment]. If you are the more conversational type, I can also tell you a little about Degmar's [Castle].'\nYou say, 'Tell me about this Castle'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'Three to five centuries ago, long before I was born, this castle and everyone inside were transported from the edge of Faydark to this underwater tomb. To protect Degmar from the pressure of the sea, the castle was encapsulated in an exceedingly strong magical barrier. No one, not even the Elven emissaries that were with us at the time could transport themselves out. The Commander Degmar of the time was very [wise].'\nYou say, 'How was he wise?'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'He integrated the elves into the population, treating them as equals, as family even. For many centuries we had peace. Unfortunately, what we did not realize is that the elves are uncomfortable in enclosed spaces, and after hundreds of years of claustrophic isoluation they went insane. A group of the elves started killing the dwarves off, one at a time, leaving evidence that implicated other dwarves. As you can imagine, [paranoia] ran rampant.'\nYou say, 'Paranoia?'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'The situation would have stabilized, except Commander Alast Degmar, an ancestor of the original Commander Degmar, caught an elf attempting to assassinate him. Alast Degmar was already paranoid that the elves were out to get him, and this proved his fears and sent him into a frothing rage. He killed every elf in the castle, though Priestess Gli'helin managed to escape the purge, and has managed to stay hidden since then. And even after slaying the elves, paranoia is still a [problem].'\nYou say, 'What kind of problem?'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'I hate to think of any more dwarf blood being shed, but many of my brothers and sisters are so far gone that they'll attack any stranger they see on sight, even if you are trying to help them. Do what you must, but spare as many as you can.'\nYou say, 'What happened with your banishment?'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'My banishment is a sad story. I can [explain] it if you wish, or you can just help me [resolve] it by reading the notes I'll jot down in your journal.'\nYou say, 'Yes, explain...'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'This [castle] has a long sordid history. Thankfully, I've managed to stave off the rampant paranoia that has affected the other dwarves in these past twenty years. When Neckchi was captured, and don't tell him this, it will just frighten him more, he was sentenced to be executed. I could not allow that to happen, so I [freed] him.'\nYou say, 'You freed him?'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'Yes. I freed him. I could not justify the judgment, handed down simply because Commander Degmar is paranoid. By doing this I earned the wrath of Commander Degmar. Luckily, he is so paranoid that he believes the teleport device to be a [bomb]. He ordered his men to clear out of the guard house, and banished me here as a traitor.'\nYou say, 'It's not a bomb, is it...'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'Of course it's not a bomb, but I let the commander think that so he does not send guards here to kill us. The influx of adventurers like you has only served to fuel his paranoia, and he sees you as invaders. But I ramble on. Let me explain the [task].'\nYou say, 'What about the task?'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'It's fairly simple, though dangerous. I'm sending you to the [armory] to retrieve a specific hammer that has [sentimental] value for Commander Degmar. When you go there, I've arranged to have a few enemies of mine [ambush] you. I think by the fact that I arranged the ambush, this will convince Commander Degmar that I'm not a traitor, and he will allow me to return. You must keep this confidential.'\nYou say, 'Where is the armory?'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'The armory is on the lower level. Take the east branch in the foyer, and go through the library and throne room to get to the armory.'\nYou say, 'What's sentimental about the hammer?'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'It's simple. It is his father's hammer. The hammer is unremarkable except for its family heritage. If I return it to him after the \"invaders\" steal it, it will help ingratiate me with Commander Degmar.'\nYou say, 'Ambush me, really?'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'Yes. I know I'm asking a lot for you to purposefully go into an ambush, and now that I think about it, since you're forewarned, it's not much of an ambush. But... I can tell that a \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ like you is a survivor and you'll be just fine. Please don't think me callous for asking you to kill my fellow dwarves. They are our enemies. If they no longer have a voice in Commander Degmar's ear, it will further cement my return.'\nYou say, 'I'll resolve all this'\nDamton Silverhammer says 'Thank you. I've placed the notes you will need in your journal. I'll [explain] more if you like.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Castle Crasher'.\nDamton Silverhammer has been banished and would like for you to clear her name. Go to the armory and survive the ambush. The armory is on the east branch from the foyer.\n\n---\n\n!\n\n---\n\nGo to the armory and approach the hammer 0/1 (Dregmar, the Lost Castle)\nKill 1 Ambusher 0/1 (Dregmar, the Lost Castle)\n_Updates at around -310, 125, -13 in the armory (through the eastern wing of the castle; down the hall leading west out of the throne room). Note: A mob will spawn here, so you'll probably want to clear the area of guards._\na Degmar ambusher says 'It will end poorly for you.'\n_Kill 1x \"a Degmar ambusher\" (of average difficulty for the zone; mezzable; social with other mobs in the room)._\n\n---\n\nCollect 1 Degmar Ceremonial Hammer 0/1 (Dregmar, the Lost Castle)\n_This is a ground spawn at the location of the ambush (appears as a hammer sitting on a crate)._\nDeliver 1 Degmar Ceremonial Hammer to Damton Silverhammer 0/1 (Dregmar, the Lost Castle)\nDamton Silverhammer is grateful for your assistance.\n_Rewards:_\nExperience\n37 platinum, 5 gold\nFaction with Degmar's Commoners (+225)\n_This task is repeatable with a 6-hour lockout timer from the time of request._",
    },
