      walkthrough = "**Level:** 70\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n\nThis is the fourth in a series of five tasks.\nCaptain Zheren may be found at -1225, +620.\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Zheren'\nCaptain Zheren says '______! Aren't you a sight for sore eyes! We set up this camp a few weeks ago to scout the lands controlled by Dyn`leth. We expected [opposition], but nothing like this.'\nYou say, 'What opposition?'\nCaptain Zheren says 'Dyn`leth's armies control almost every piece of land between the mines to the east and the temple to the north. We are vastly outnumbered. Any strength you can lend to our [cause] would be much appreciated.'\nYou say, 'What cause?'\nCaptain Zheren says 'We are the Crusade of the Scale! We will not rest until Dyn`leth is dead and the Scale of Veeshan has been reclaimed!'\nIf you have previously completed \"Dyn`Leth's Artillery\"..\nYou have been assigned the task 'Dyn`leth's Mine'.\nFrom the Ashengate Orders, Captain Zheren has learned that Dyn`Leth's forces hope to unearth the ancient dragon Vergalid from the mines below Sunderock. Zheren now wants you to slow the mining operations by any means necessary.\nKill 10 Green Legion Slavedrivers - Sunderock Springs\na Green Legion overseer also counts towards this tally.\nKill Overseer Vorsirus - Sunderock Springs\nCan be snared.  Will summon.  Comes with a friend, The Guardian of the Mines, who can also be snared but does not seem to start summoning until the Overseer is dead.\nKill 10 Skullcrush Slaves - Vergalid Mines\nAny Skullcrush mob will count.\nKill 10 Kickpick Slaves - Vergalid Mines\nAny Kickpick mob will count.\nKill 3 Green Legion Overseers - Vergalid Mines\nReport Back to Captain Zheren - Sunderock Springs\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Zheren'\nYour task 'Dyn`Leth's Mine' has been updated.\nYou have received a character flag!\nZheren salutes you as you return, 'Welcome back, my friend.  The enemy forces in the area are reeling from the blow you struck to their leaders.  Your deed has been a great service to our [cause]!'\nThis is a lead-in to the next quest in the series \"The Direwind Front\".\nYour faction standing with Crusade of the Scale got better.\nYour faction standing with Forces of Dyn'leth got worse.\nYour faction standing with Circle of the Crystalwing got better.\nYou gain experience!!\nReward Options:\nBelt of the Crusader\nShimmering Healer's Mantle\nCrusader's Luckstone\nRing of the War Runner\nYou have successfully been granted your reward for: Dyn`Leth's Mine\nSubmitted by: Lias Roxx, Defiant, ZekRewards:\n- Belt of the Crusader [item=52565]\n- Crusader's Luckstone [item=52567]\n- Ring of the War Runner [item=52568]\n- Shimmering Healer's Mantle [item=52566]\n[",
