      walkthrough = "**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n\nThis 23rd anniversary task starts with Giraga in The Rathe Mountains. Giraga can be found in the northeast corner of the zone at /waypoint 3332, -3464, 22. She is on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Giraga'\nGiraga says, 'Oh, hi dere! Dun worrie, I'm not going to smash you. I already know I wud win, ha! I am here to talk to da [sphinxes]. If dey keep confusing me with dey words, mebbe I will smash dem instead.'\nYou say, 'What do you need from the sphinxes?'\nGiraga says, 'Few days ago, I ask a great warrior from my town to train me to be strong like him. He laugh at me! Then he say, 'mebbe when fish fly.' I have never seen fish fly, but I heard dat da sphinxes are really smart. Wuz thinking dat dey wud know where I can [find] da flying fish.'\nYou say, 'Did they tell you where to find one?'\nGiraga says, 'Bah! Instead of telling me, dey give me this book. Dey said I need to solve da 'riddlez' inside. What in da Grobb is a [riddle]? I am reading da words, but I dun see anything about da flying fish.'\nYou say, 'A riddle is a puzzle. You need to figure out the answers.'\nGiraga says, 'I dun like puzzles. Why can't everything be easy? Dats why I think [mebbe] I shud smash da sphinxes. Smashing is easy. Den dey will give me da answers.'\nYou say, ''Mebbe' instead, I can help you figure them out.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Known Laws of Aviation'.\nGiraga says, 'Heh, you iz a nice person. Will you look at dis book? Dere are three riddlez inside. If you can't figure dem out, mebbe Volantpiscis can tell you what da words mean.'\nYour Location is 3312.79, -3448.83, 19.60\nNOTE: You get a book called Volantpiscis' Riddles (No Trade) with the riddles inside.\nIt reads:\nRiddle One: A book can take you many places: mountains, oceans, or a shore. a book can take you straight to me and I can take you to many more, at my center us a library filled with wisdon beyond compare. At my edges are stone monuments that can take you anywhere.\nRiddle Two: I'll never give up. I'll never surrender. I'm a real contender. Kill me once. kill me twice. I will not rest 'til Qeynos pays the price.\nRiddle Three: My eyes are a sight to behold; deep pools of yellow and gold. On Luclin you'll find me on the rpowl; thorugh darkness you might see my avian scowl.\nYou say, 'Hail, Volantpiscis'\nVolantpiscis says, 'Greetings. Are you here seeking knowledge? Or perhaps you are searching for [flying fish] as well?'\nYou say, 'I am helping Giraga find the flying fish.'\nVolantpiscis says, 'Very well. No knowledge is free. I am willing to help you and Giraga solve her problem, but you must do so using your wits. Such is our way. If you are truly perplexed, I am willing to give you a [hint]'\nYou say, 'I need a hint.'\nVolantpiscis says, 'Certainly. I am sympathetic to your plight of having small minds. Would you like a hint to riddle [one], [two], or [three]?'\nYou say, 'one'\nVolantpiscis says, 'The answer to this riddle is a location. It is a different plane than the one we're on, but there's a way you can travel directly between here and there.'\nYou say, 'two'\nVolantpiscis lets out a rumbling purr of amusement. 'There is a curious gnoll who lurks around northern Qeynos. He attacks the city relentlessly, but the guards always manage to catch him before he does any real damage. He is the answer.'\nYou say, 'three'\nVolantpiscis says, 'There are creatures on Luclin that are both bird and beast. The answer to this riddle is the name of the animal.'\n- 1. Say the answer to the first riddle to Giraga 0/1 The Rathe Mountains\nYou say, 'Plane of Knowledge'\nYour task 'The Known Laws of Aviation' has been updated.\nGiraga says, 'Wow, you iz reel smart. Dat makes sense!'\n- 2. Say the answer to the second riddle to Giraga 0/1 The Rathe Mountains\nYou say, 'Fippy Darkpaw'\nYour task 'The Known Laws of Aviation' has been updated.\nGiraga says, 'Wut's a Fippy Darkpaw? Never hurd of it, but you iz a geeneus so I think you iz right.'\n- 3. Say the answer to the third riddle to Giraga 0/1 The Rathe Mountains\nYou say, 'Owlbear'\nYour task 'The Known Laws of Aviation' has been updated.\nGiraga says, 'Oh my Grobb, dat is definitely da answer! Sounds tasty.'\n- 4. Tell Volantpiscis you have solved the riddles 0/1 The Rathe Mountains\nYou say, 'Hail, Volantpiscis'\nYour task 'The Known Laws of Aviation' has been updated.\nVolantpiscis says, 'I commend you on deciphering my riddles. The universe is vast, but clearly you are an adventurer of [merit] if you've learned enough to solve these puzzles.'\nYou say, 'Does this merit your help with our quest?'\nVolantpiscis says, 'I can create an enchanted flying fish for Giraga, but your work is not done. I require three items in order to do so, each related to the answers to the riddles. The items are: a [sterling silver sunfish], a length of rope with a [clove hitch knot], and one [tuft of owlbear feathers].'\nYou say, 'sterling silver sunfish'\nVolantpiscis says, 'The fish we seek is in the Plane of Knowledge. An angler by the name of Suzelle specializes in catching them, and she might be willing to give one to you.'\nYou say, 'clove hitch knot'\nVolantpiscis says, 'The guards in North Qeynos keep rope on hand to catch the pesky Fippy Darkpaw. Unfortunately for Fippy, they prefer using their swords to teach him a lesson. One of the guards might be willing to give you rope with the right kind of knot.'\nYou say, 'tuft of owlbear feathers'\nVolantpiscis says, 'You can find plenty of owlbears on Luclin; Hollowshade Moor seems to have a plentiful population. Dispatch of a few and bring back their feathers.'\n- 5. Find Angler Suzelle on the Plane of Knowledge 0/1 Plane of Knowledge\nNOTE: She is on Find, near the small bank.\nYou say, 'Hail, Angler Suzelle'\nAngler Suzelle says, 'Ahoy there! I could see that glimmer in your eye from afar, and I know exactly why you've come over here. You're here to [ask] me on a date, aren't you? I'm awfully flattered.'\nYou say, 'Actually, I'm here to ask about your wares.'\nAngler Suzelle's eyes go wide and her face flushes bright pink. 'I- I knew that! I was just playing around. Clearly your beaming smile is about fish, not me.' Suzelle awkwardly clears her throat. 'What [do you] want to know about?'\nYou say, 'Do you have a sterling silver sunfish?'\nAngler Suzelle says, 'I sure do! But I'm not selling it, if that's what you're asking about. I caught this one in the river this morning and I'm saving it for dinner. This is all I've got to [eat] today!'\nYou say, 'How about I buy you something else to eat?'\nYour task 'The Known Laws of Aviation' has been updated.\nAngler Suzelle c ocks an eyebrow. 'Are you sure you're not trying to take me on a date? This is an awfully roundabout way to do it. Truthfully, I am getting a little tired of eating seafood all the time. If you really want this fish, buy me a nice dinner. The baking supply merchants around here should sell what I want. I'd love a meat pie! Bring me a fresh one and I'll give you the sunfish.'\nYour Location is -396.68, 740.85, -121.47\n- 6. Give Angler Suzelle a new dinner 0/1 Plane of Knowledge\nChef Denrun told you, 'That'll be 2 silver 6 copper per Meat Pie.'\nYou purchased Meat Pie from Chef Denrun for  2 silver 6 copper.\n(Give the Meat Pie to Angler Suzelle,)\nYou have been given: Sterling Silver Sunfish\nYour task 'The Known Laws of Aviation' has been updated.\nAngler Suzelle sniffs the food and lets out a satisfied sigh. 'Hoo boy, doesn't this pie smell delicious? Here's the fish you want; you've more than earned it. And if you're ever looking to buy dinner again, I hang out here from time to time.' She winks at you.\n- 7. Speak to Guard Urli in North Qeynos 0/1 North Qeynos\nYou say, 'Hail, Guard Urli'\nGuard Urli says, 'H-hail, Bonzz. Might there b-be [something] I can assist you with today?'\nYou say, 'You seem nervous about something.'\nGuard Urli looks down at his feet. 'N-n-nervous? Me? N-no, of course not. I'm shaking because I'm b-brimming with excitement!' He gives you an extremely unconvincing smile. 'Today's my first day on the [job] a-and the captain prepared me for an important assignment.'\nYou say, 'Does your job entail using any rope?'\nGuard Urli tilts his head quizzically. 'Y-yes, how'd you know? The captain's lucky smoking pipe was stolen and eaten by one of these giant rats. He gave me some rope and told me to find the [rat], wrangle it, and get the pipe back.' His voice drops to a faint whisper. 'B-but I'm scared of rats....'\nYou say, 'Why don't you kill the rat?'\nGuard Urli says, 'I've been ordered not to. The captain doesn't want to risk his pipe being scratched or broken by a blade. It's made of a rare, expensive monster tusk! So he told me to tie the rat up and get it to [cough]  up the pipe. But... just thinking about those yellow, gnashing teeth makes me want to faint....'\nYou say, 'If I get it to cough it up, can you do me a favor?'\nYou have been given: Qeynos Guard's Rope\nYour task 'The Known Laws of Aviation' has been updated.\nGuard Urli says, 'H-hail, Bonzz. Might there b-be [something] I can assist you with today?'\nGuard Urli says, 'Would you really do that for me? Yes! If you can get the pipe back, I'm happy to help you with what you need! Take this rope. I'll be over here if you need me. Please try not to need me.'\nYour Location is 404.90, 28.27, 5.10\nItem Received: Qeynos Guard's Rope (Lore, No Trade).\n- 8. Use the guard's rope to wrangle the satiated rat 0/1 North Qeynos\nYour Location is 1047.31, -637.76, 5.09\nYou say, 'Hail, a satiated rat'\nA satiated rat regards you indifferently -- what would you like your tombstone to say? (Lvl: 121)\n(Give the Qeynos Guard's Rope to a satiated rat.)\nYou have been given: Captain's Smoking Pipe\nYour task 'The Known Laws of Aviation' has been updated.\nA satiated rat coughs and splutters when you get the rope around its neck. It takes no effort at all before the captain's pipe is coughed up. It's covered in disgusting, viscous saliva, but that sounds like a problem for Urli.\nItem Received: Captain's Smoking Pipe (Lore, No Trade).\n- 9. Hand the Captain's Smoking Pipe over to Guard Urli 0/1 North Qeynos\n(Give the Captian's Smoking Pipe to Guard Urli.)\nYou have been given: Clove Hitch Knot\nYour task 'The Known Laws of Aviation' has been updated.\nGuard Urli says, 'My friend, I have never been so relieved in my life. I'd sooner fight the entire Darkpaw clan than touch one of those nauseating pests. What is it you needed? A rope with a clove hitch knot? Easily done. Take this rope, and good luck with your quest!'\nItem Received: Clove Hitch Knot (Lore, No Trade).\n- 10. Hunt owlbears an take some of their feathers 0/2 Hollowshade Moor\nTargeted (NPC): an owlbear cub\nAuto attack is on.\nAn owlbear cub assails you with a deafening shriek!\nYou crush an owlbear cub for 318 points of damage. (Lucky Critical)\nYour task 'The Known Laws of Aviation' has been updated.\nThe owlbear's eyes seem to dim as its lumbering frame ceases moving.\nYou have slain an owlbear cub!\nTargeted (NPC): an owlbear fleshrender\nAuto attack is on.\nAn owlbear fleshrender assails you with a deafening shriek!\nAn owlbear fleshrender's corpse twitches as life fades from its round yellow eyes.\nYou hit an owlbear fleshrender for 1232 points of magic damage by Overdrive Punch.\nAn owlbear fleshrender is struck by heavy punch!\nYou have slain an owlbear fleshrender!\nYou have been given: Tuft of Owlbear Feathers\nYour task 'The Known Laws of Aviation' has been updated.\nNOTE: A Tuft of Owlbear Feathers (Lore, No Trade) should appear on your cursor.\n- 11. Give the sterling silver sunfish to the sphinxes 0/1 The Rathe Mountains\n(Give the Sterling Silver Sunfish to Volantpiscis.)\nYour task 'The Known Laws of Aviation' has been updated.\n- 12. Give the clove hitch knot to the sphinxes 0/1 The Rathe Mountains\n(Give the Clove Hitch Knot to Volantpiscis.)\nYour task 'The Known Laws of Aviation' has been updated.\n- 13. Give the tuft of owlbear feather to the sphinxes 0/1 The Rathe Mountains\n(Give the Tuft of Owlbear Feathers to Volantpiscis.)\nYour task 'The Known Laws of Aviation' has been updated.\n- 14. Speak once more to Volantpiscis 0/1 The Rathe Mountains\nYou say, 'Hail, Volantpiscis'\nYou have been given: Faux Flying Fish\nYour task 'The Known Laws of Aviation' has been updated.\nVolantpiscis says, 'looks at the items approvingly. 'Admirable work. Allow me a moment to enchant these items.' The sphinx closes its eyes and begins to hum. Before you, the feathers form wings on the fish's back. The length of rope slips around the fish's body and the knot tightens. 'Quickly, grab hold of that rope before the fish flies off. Giraga will have to use that as a leash.' The fish awkwardly flops around in the sky. Its [wings] beat quickly trying to keep its flailing body aloft.'\nYou say, 'wings'\nVolantpiscis observes the fish struggling in the air. 'More accurately, we attached the wings. It did not grow them. According to all known laws of aviation, there is no way that a fish should be able to fly. These wings are too small to get its slippery, flopping body off the ground. The fish, of course, flies anyways. Because fish don't care what we think is impossible.' Volantpiscis gives you a mysterious, toothy smile. 'Give this to Giraga. It should suffice her needs.'\nItem Received: Faux Flying Fish (Lore, No Trade).\n- 15. Give Giraga the Faux Flying Fish 0/1 The Rathe Mountains\n(Give the Faux Flying Fish to Giraga.)\nYour task 'The Known Laws of Aviation' has been updated.\nThe fish flops awkwardly in the sky. Its wings flutter uncomfortably fast, barely able to keep its body aloft. Giraga begins leading it away by its leash, but turns back and smiles at you. 'Thanks for da help. Yur a real pal. Next time sumbody tells me to solve sum riddlez, I'll find you to do it for me. If I can't find you, I'll just smash da person, hehe.' She waves and cheerily continues on her way.\nYou receive 225 platinum .\nYou receive alternate currency.\nReward(s):\n225 plat\n10 Commemorative CoinsSubmitted by: GOMNRewards:\n- Commemorative Coin [item=116720]\n[",
