      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 65\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n\nPrerequisite Task: 26th Anniversary: Diary of the Jade - The Search [quest=13315]\nThis Anniversary task starts with  Firiona Vie in Shadeweaver's Thicket near the Loda Kai Embassy building in the southwestern corner of the zone. She is on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Firiona Vie'\nFiriona Vie says, 'If the myths are to be believed the Jade Tiger statue is more than just a pretty object to be hidden away in some vault or worse be used in some nefarious way. The loss of the journal has set us back, but I trust Dreezil will be able to discover another way into the temple. While he does that we need to figure out how the [thief] even knew about the idol.'\nYou say, 'Maybe the thief overheard us talking to someone.'\nFiriona Vie says, 'I agree, that is possible. Did you get a good [look] at the culprit?'\nYou say, 'Yes, I got a good look at them.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Back to Square One'.\nFiriona Vie says, 'Good, maybe we should ask around the gallery to see if someone here knows something.'\nJust on the cusp of discovering how to reach the Jade Tiger statue, you has the Diary of the Jade stolen by a bandit, forcing you back to square one. While waiting for Dreezil to figure out another way into the temple, Firiona Via recommends you find out as much as you can about this 'Jade Bandit.' She suggests that you ask around the gallery to see if anyone can help identify who the thief is.\nSpeak with one of the servers to see if they know anything.\n- 1. Learn the first clue 0/1 Shadeweaver's Thicket\nan art gallery server is right inside of the entrance of the building Firiona Vie is standing in front of.\nYou say, 'Hail, an art gallery server'\nAn art gallery server says, 'Welcome, can I get you something or did you have a [question]?'\nYou say, 'question'\nAn art gallery server says, 'I do remember someone asking around about the artist. I didn't know anything, but I do remember hearing them asking one of the [guests] that seemed to know something.'\nYou say, 'guests'\nYour task 'Back to Square One' has been updated.\nAn art gallery server says, 'Yes, I only heard them briefly talking, but she may know something. I do not know her name, but I do remember her wearing a posh robe.'\n- 2. Learn the second clue 0/1 Shadeweaver's Thicket\na posh gallery guest is upstairs in the same building.\nYou say, 'Hail, a posh gallery guest'\nA posh gallery guest says, 'Oh, hello. The [artist]'s work is spectacular, isn't it?'\nYou say, 'Do you remember a halfling asking about the artist?'\nA posh gallery guest says, 'I do remember speaking to him. I believe he said his name was Boldven. I've heard the artist is extremely private, but like many others he was attempting to [meet] them.'\nYou say, 'Why was he trying to meet the artist?'\nYour task 'Back to Square One' has been updated.\nA posh gallery guest says, 'Why else? To get a glimpse behind the curtain, to see how the art takes shape. I told him it was unlikely he would be able to meet the artist, but I directed him to the event coordinator and wished him luck.'\n- 3. Lean the third clue 0/1 Shadeweaver's Thicket\nGo back down to the first floor and speak to a gallery coordinator.\nYou say, 'Hail, a gallery coordinator'\nA gallery coordinator says, 'Welcome to the Shadeweaver Jade Gallery. I hope you are enjoying yourself. Is there something that I can [help] you with?'\nYou say, 'I was hoping that you could help me find Boldven.'\nA gallery coordinator says, 'Boldven? Oh, I remember him. He was trying to meet the artist. I informed him that the artist doesn't just see anyone, but he was [confident] that they would want to see him.'\nYou say, 'He was confident? Why?'\nA gallery coordinator says, 'I'm not entirely sure, but I informed him that I would reach out to the artist, but it would take some time. He expressed a need to tend to an important matter and gave me a way to [contact] him.'\nYou say, 'contact'\nA gallery coordinator says, 'I'm not really all that comfortable sharing this information, but as it turns out the artist is interested in meeting him. I tried to contact him, but my messenger was unable to find his [associate].'\nYou say, 'associate'\nYour task 'Back to Square One' has been updated.\nA gallery coordinator says, 'Yes, we were to contact him was through an intermediary. An associate of his by the name of Vernan Finken, in Shar Vahl. I hope that helps.'\n- 4. Get the informant to talk 0/1 Shar Vahl\nVernan Finken is in Shar Vahl at /way -408, -466, -188, he is also on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Vernan Finken'\nVernan Finken stammers and wobbles. 'Oh, you got me a strong bitter drink? No!? Well, I got nothin' for you, so leave me be!'\nYou are looking for Owlbear Bitter Brew. It's sold by several Barkeeps in Shar Vahl.  Nearby is Barkeep Rawlf /way -459.34, -237.06, -187.27\nYou offered 1 Owlbear Bitter Brew to Vernan Finken.\nYour task 'Back to Square One' has been updated.\nVernan Finken says, 'That for me? Oh-why-thank-you-very-much. What's the [occasion]?'\nYou complete the trade with Vernan Finken.\n- 5. Speak with informant 0/1 Shar Vahl\nYou say, 'No special occasion, I'm looking for information.'\nVernan Finken says, 'Are you now? What makes you think that I [know] anything?'\nYou say, 'I was told you know Boldven.'\nVernan Finken says, 'Oh, I know him alright. He left me here with naught to my name. Why are you [looking] for him?'\nYou say, 'I'm looking for him because he took something from me.'\nVernan Finken says, 'Well, I think we may be able to [help] each other out then.'\nYou say, 'help'\nVernan Finken says, 'As it turns out I do know that good for nothin' snake and I know where to find him, but I'm gonna need [something] from you first.'\nYou say, 'something'\nVernan Finken says, 'Since bein' stranded here, I may have run into a slight gold [situation] that, judgin' by your... equipment you can help me with.'\nYou say, 'situation'\nVernan Finken says, 'Well, I wasn't left much gold and some of my habits are expensive, so after a while I was forced to borrow a little gold from some rough [individuals]. The last time that I needed cash I was forced to give them a keepsake as collateral. If you bring it back to me, I'll tell you what you want to know.'\nYou say, 'Where are these rough individuals?'\nYour task 'Back to Square One' has been updated.\nVernan Finken says, 'You can find them in Shadow Haven and, uh, do your best to resolve this peaceful like.'\n- 6. Speak with the debtor 0/1 Shadow Haven\nDaxan is located at /way 299, -347, -28 in Shadow Haven. He is on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Daxan'\nDaxan says, 'What do we have here? You don't look down on your luck, but I'm not one to turn away a hand in [need].'\nYou say, 'I only need the flask that Vernan gave to you as collateral.'\nDaxan says, 'Really? That weasel got you to come out here for him. Get lost, I don't have [time] for a wannabe adventurer in rented equipment.'\nYou say, 'You best make time.'\nYour task 'Back to Square One' has been updated.\nDaxan whistles. 'Oh, is that so? Pummel this moron and take their armor. I'm sure we can sell this fake crap for at least a little bit of gold.'\nMulder mumbles in a thick accent while cracking his knuckles.\nMack mumbles in a thick accent while cracking his knuckles.\n- 7. Defeat the thugs 0/2 Shadow Haven\nKill Mulder and Mack, they died to my pet before I could con them.\n- 8. Collect the informant's keepsake 0/1 Shadow Haven\nYou say, 'Hail, Daxan'\nYou have been given: Flask Keepsake\nYour task 'Back to Square One' has been updated.\nDaxan says, 'Wo, wo, wo! Alright, slow down. Take the stupid thing.'\n- 9. Deliver the keepsake to the informant 0/1 Shar Vahl\nYou offered 1 Flask Keepsake to Vernan Finken.\nYour task 'Back to Square One' has been updated.\nVernan Finken says, 'I didn't think you'd help me, but a deal's a [deal].'\nYou complete the trade with Vernan Finken.\n- 10. Gather the information from the informant 0/1 Shar Vahl\nYou say, 'deal'\nVernan Finken says, 'Alright, I'm gettin' to it. I met Boldven at the Golden Rooster in Highpass Hold. He was lookin' for someone to help him with a few odds and ends jobs. He was hush hush about where he was from, but one night after a job I got a little curious, so I [followed] him.'\nYou say, 'followed'\nYour task 'Back to Square One' has been updated.\nVernan Finken says, 'Yeah, I followed him through the pass to a small cabin in the southeast of Kithicor Forest. I didn't follow him to his door, but I saw his place. Now I'm gonna head off and find myself a drink.'\n- 11. Report back to Firiona Vie 0/1 Shadeweaver's Thicket\nYou say, 'Hail, Firiona Vie'\nYour task 'Back to Square One' has been updated.\nYou were able to track down information about the thief, getting a name and a known associate. After assisting the associate with a financial problem, you were able to convince them to provide the location of the thief's hideout.\nYou receive 5 silver .\nYou receive 2 gold .\nYou receive 2 platinum .\nYou received 10 Commemorative Coins.\nFiriona Vie says, 'You did exceptionally well in tracking down the Jade Bandit's hideout. I will need a moment to contemplate what our next step will be.'\n2 platinum, 2 gold, 5 silver\n10 Commemorative CoinsSubmitted by: GidonoRewards:\n[",
