      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n\nPrerequisite Task:  Stone Cold Summer: Write With Me [quest=13362].\nThis seasonal task is given to you by Inis Zidas [npc=60694] in Field of Bone at /way -1952, 2719, 7 in front of the ruins that lead to East Cabilis in the south western part of the zone.\nYou say, 'Hail, Inis Zidas'\nInis Zidas says, 'You found this broken ossuary in the [library]?'\nYou say, 'Yes, the library.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Patience, Purification, and Peace'.\nInvestigating the piles of bones rising to the surface in the Field of Bones has spurred an investigation into disturbed graves in Kaesora. Inis Zidas believes that laying this powerful spirit to rest will ease the turmoil in the Field of Bone. She wants you to repair he broken ossuary and return the remains to the library.\n- 1. Speak with Inis about the relics 0/1 The Field of Bone\nInis Zidas says, 'It's possible that these bothersome remnants belong in it. But before we could even try laying them to rest, the ossuary  would have to be purified, repaired and blessed in the way they were previously laid to rest. I don't know many one with that kind of [patience].'\nYou say, 'Do you have that kind of patience?'\nInis Zidas says, 'There is an island north of here. You would need to spend some time on it and let the wind and sounds of the water wash away the pain of those who disturbed this ones rest. Once the negative energies have settled, the ossuary to Klok [Toren]  in Cabilis East. She should be able to help you repair the box.'\nYou say, 'Taking the ossuary to Toren doesn't sound too hard.'\nYour task 'Patience, Purification, and Peace' has been updated.\nInis Zidas says, 'I am glad you feel that way. The ossuary will then need to be taken back to Kaesora's chapel to be blessed before the relics can be sealed and returned to their rest. Here take the Forgotten Talisman and don't forget to add the Blood of Chosooth into the ossuary.'\nYou are given: Forgotten Talisman\nYou are given: Broken Ossuary\n- 2. Visit the island that Inis mentioned 0/1 The Field of Bone\nHead north to the smaller island and wait until the broken ossuary feels more settled.\nThis is a location update around /way 3225, 2027, -146 on the small eastern island.\nThe wind and sound of the waves clear some of the weight from your shoulders.\nYour task 'Patience, Purification, and Peace' has been updated.\n- 3. Speak with Klok Toren about the Broken Ossuary 0/1 Cabilis East\nKlok Toren is in East Cabilis in the central part of the zone at /way 194, -301, 1.\nYou say, 'Hail, Klok Toren'\nYour task 'Patience, Purification, and Peace' has been updated.\nKlok Toren says, 'I am busy. Somebody had better [sent] you.'\n- 4. Give Klok Toren the Broken Ossuary 0/1 East Cabilis\nYou offered 1 Broken Ossuary to Klok Toren.\nYou have been given: Empty Ossuary\nYour task 'Patience, Purification, and Peace' has been updated.\nKlok Toren says, 'People can be so crude. This repair won't take long. Here, now keep moving.'\nYou complete the trade with Klok Toren.\n- 5. Return to the ruins of Xalgoz's chapel 0/1 Kaesora\nThis step updated in the building across from Xalgoz's chapel, upstairs at /way 80, 533, -266 .\nThe ossuary in your hands begins to hum with calming powering.\nYour task 'Patience, Purification, and Peace' has been updated.\nIMPORTANT: Do not seal the relics before completing this step !\nOtherwise, you will have to restart almost the entire quest line.\n- 6. Seal the relics in the Empty Ossuary 0/1 Kaesora\nPlace the Blood of Chosooth, Forgotten Talisman, and Ink Stained Hand in the empty ossuary and seal it.\nYou have fashioned the items together to create something new: Sealed Ossuary.\nYour task 'Patience, Purification, and Peace' has been updated.\n- 7. Return the Sealed Ossuary to the burial crypts 0/1 Kaesora\nThis step updated on outside of Xalgoz's chapel on the west side at /way -150, 657, -300 .\nYour task 'Patience, Purification, and Peace' has been updated.\nWhen I got the update a level 125 an abandoned librarian spawned and attacked.\n- 8. Defeat the abandoned librarian 0/1 Kaesora\nKill it ! It has very few health points and doesn't deal much damage.\nYour task 'Patience, Purification, and Peace' has been updated.\nYou gain party experience!\nAn abandoned librarian's corpse claws at the air as it returns to its rest.\n- 9. Let Inis know what you have done 0/1 The Field of Bone\nYou say, 'Hail, Inis Zidas'\nYour task 'Patience, Purification, and Peace' has been updated.\nYou have successfully investigated and returned the disturbed relics to their rest.\nInis Zidas says, 'The rumbling of the bones are slowly fading. The spirits whisper that one of the librarians has been laid to rest and you are to thank. I apricate the work you have done.'\nYou have successfully been granted your reward for: Patience, Purification, and Peace\nYou have completed achievement: Stone Cold Summer: Blood From A Stone\nYou have successfully been granted your reward for: Stone Cold Summer: Blood From A Stone (Placeable statue item named Faceless Hero of Kaesora)\nReward(s):\n6x - Sanguine Seltzer\nSubmitted by: larthRewards:\n- Sanguine Seltzer [item=151716]\n[",
