      walkthrough = "**Level:** 0\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n\nLaveer Krass regards you indifferently -- looks like quite a gamble. (Lvl: 130)\nLocation is -3326.38, -1315.82, -141.78\nADD to map westwastes_3.txt\nP -2778.4875, 1827.3354, 16.7969,  0, 0, 0,  1,  27th_Laveer_Krass\nP -2292.3022, -1269.2410, -59.9862,  0, 0, 0,  1,  Chase_Update\nP -1846.8904, -2126.1072, -50.3997,  0, 0, 0,  1,  cheif_dragon_elder\nP 729.7202, -1567.5175, -7.8657,  0, 0, 0,  1,  a_crystal_Prlon\nP 597.8863, -1385.4486, -20.7058,  0, 0, 0,  1,  a_crstal_Pylon\nP 581.5116, -1295.6477, -20.9038,  0, 0, 0,  1,  a_crystal_pylon\nYou say, 'Hail, Laveer Krass'\nLaveer Krass says, 'Now that we have some form of respite, let me introduce myself. My name is Laveer Krass. Now let's see [inside] this package here.'\nYou say, 'What is inside?'\nLaveer Krass says, 'Well, this was a bit underwhelming, considering the great lengths you took to get this package to me. There does not seem to be much inside except for an envelope and a [letter]. Give me a moment to read it.'\nYou say, 'What does the letter say?'\nLaveer Krass is visibly distraught. 'This is from my father. He composed music like myself, but I have not seen or heard from him for a long time. Last thing he told me, he was going out to find something, something of great importance. He was in such a rush that I thought it was one of his crazy fits, acting like a mad man. He was an old man in his late years and I did not think anything of it. His previous \"revelations\" came up unfruitful, but it seems this time was not like the others. He found what he was looking for, but apparently only part of it. He mentions another [group] as well that was seeking what he was looking for. They got to him, but he was able to [send] this to me before they captured him. So most likely the people pursuing both this package and yourself were those same people.'\nYou say, 'Who was this group?'\nLaveer Krass says, 'There does not seem to be any more info on the group that was pursuing you, but it looks like they have some sort of operation going on in the Western Wastes.'\nYou say, 'What did he send?'\nLaveer Krass says, 'The envelope seems sealed magically. I'll need time to unlock it. Would you mind seeing what is [happening] in the Western Wastes?'\nYou say, 'I'll check on what is happening.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Note Left Behind'.\nLaveer Krass says, 'Sounds good. I'll tidy up here and meet you in the Western Wastes. Come find me.'\nstep\nFind  Laveer some where in the Western Wastes                            The Western Waste\nNote: Laveer Krass is on /find\nYour Location is -1820.04, 2825.76, 16.47\nstep\nSpeak with Laveer                                The Western Waste\nLaveer Krass says, 'Keep your head down. Over in the distance there seems to be a group of people gathered up trying to break into the ice. There seem to be more past this first site. What I got from this lovely sleeping [drake] was that they are trying to find something.'\nYou say, 'Who is this drake?'\nYour task 'Note Left Behind' has been updated.\nLaveer Krass says, 'Ah, him. He was kind enough to give me a little information on what is happening over there. Seems like a subfaction of the Claws of Veeshan wants something in that ice. It seems to be related to what my father was looking into. This gentleman was able to recognize me,\nthinking I would be dead by now, but luckily you were there to help me. Anyways, my gut tells me what they have is what I need for breaking open this envelope. Be a good sport and procure any useful items and information you can get from them.'\nstep\nKill dragon expedation members                    0/5             The Western Waste\nNOTE only three  Veeshan expedition are up on track and expect  this to be a big bottle neck\nA Veeshan expedition officer  . (Lvl: 50)\nA Veeshan expedition worker   (Lvl: 50)\nstep\nCollect supplies for Laveer                           0/3        The Western Waste\nlooted a Ward Fragment from a Veeshan expedition surveyor's corpse\nstep\nReturn to Laveer and give him the items 0/3  The Western Waste\nNote:  Laveer Krass  is on /find\nYour Location is -1820.04, 2825.76, 16.47\nstep\nSpeak with Lavee The Western Waste\nYou have handed the wards to Laveer to use.\nLaveer Krass says, 'Thanks, these wards may help. I'll need time working on the envelope. I heard something while snooping around when you were getting these wards. Apparently, this group was also going to go somewhere else in the Western Wastes. There seems to be a very old group of\ndragons that have been holding onto something that those evil dragons want. Try and find them and get in contact with them. Maybe kill the group that went looking for them as well.'\nstep\nChase after the search party The Western Waste\nYour Location is 1269.24, 2292.30, -56.39\nstep\nClear out some of the search party        0/4   The Western Waste\nNOTE only three  Veeshan expedition are up on track and expect  this to be a big bottle neck\nA Veeshan expedition officer  . (Lvl: 50)\nA Veeshan expedition worker   (Lvl: 50)\nstep\nSpeak with someone in charge of this mysterious group         The Western Waste\nNote:  Chief dragon elder is on /find\nYou say, 'Hail, chief dragon elder'\nChief dragon elder says, 'Ah, a mortal. Why have you come? Are you [with] that band of hooligans out there?'\nYou say, 'I am not with them.'\nChief dragon elder says, 'Hmm, you are quite right. I did see you slay some of them. What an unruly bunch they are, an utter disgrace to all dragon kind. Now what do you [want]?'\nYou say, 'I want to see why they are after you.'\nChief dragon elder says, 'After us? Well, we old ancient fossils have been guarding something you can't possibly imagine. Since you are somewhat trustworthy and honorable in your prowess, I'll let you in on [who] we are.'\nYou say, 'Who are you guys?'\nChief dragon elder says, 'We are, some might say, fans of the musical arts. We have lived for so long that we collect and reminisce in the essence of hymns and notes. We look like this to fool the young ones. Plus, being in our original bodies would make it so we could not fit in tight spaces.\nBut enough of that. Did you also come here [seeking] some long lost artistry?'\nYou say, 'Not seeking, but helping someone.'\nChief dragon elder says, 'Ah, I see. Would perchance this mortal go by the name of [Laveer]?'\nYou say, 'Yes, his name is Laveer. How did you know that?'\nYou have been given: Activation Device\nYour task 'Note Left Behind' has been updated.\nYou hear the dragon elder laugh heartily as he walks back into his sanctum. Go out and kill the group that took from the dragon elders. Use the activation device you got from the dragon elder on crystal pylons in the crystal formations nearby. There should be expedition workers from the Claw\nof  Veeshan that have been guarding these pylons.\nChief dragon elder says, 'So, the hatchling sought to follow in their father's footsteps. Oh mortals, your lives are so fleeting. Just going off on a scent and risking it all for the pursuit of the ultimate piece. Well, you are in luck, mortal. We do have what your companion is looking for, but we only\nhave parts of it. That band of imbeciles killed three of our own and took their parts of what you are looking for. Kill them and return the parts to us. If you accomplish this, you may have the whole piece, but just maybe you won't. Now leave.'\nstep\nUse the activation device on the crystal                     The Western Waste\nYou say, 'Hail, a crystal pylon'\nYour Location is 1567.52, -729.72, -5.99\nYou offered 1 Activation Device to a crystal pylon.\nMOB will spawn  lvl 130  A Veeshan expedition leader\nnote: mulit a crystal pylon are around crystals\nstep\nCollect parts of the ultimate piece 0/3                           The Western Waste\nYou have looted a Note Part from a Veeshan expedition leader's corpse.--\nstep\nReturn to the chief dragon elder and give him the pieces 0/3     The Western Waste\nNote:  Chief dragon elder is on /find\nYou offered 3 Note Part to chief dragon elder\nstep\nReturn the activation device    The Western Waste\nYou offered 1 Activation Device to chief dragon elder.\nstep\nSpeak with the chief dragon elder         The Western Waste\nChief dragon elder says, 'Ah, mortal, welcome back. You have done a great deed here. Before you leave with the completed piece, I would like for you to answer this [riddle] of mine. I want to be sure handing this over is the right choice.'\nYou say, 'What is the riddle?'\nChief dragon elder says, 'Well, since you are so eager, here is the riddle. I am born of magic, heard by the soul. I can make you weep, or take control. I have no body, yet I can be trapped in your head. What am I?'\nstep\nSolve the riddle      The Western Waste\nANSWER   GNOS            (backwards)\nYou have been given: A Page of the Piece\nstep\nReturn to Laveer and hand him the part of the ultimate piece        The Western Waste\nNote:  Laveer Krass  is on /find\nYour Location is -1820.04, 2825.76, 16.47\nYou offered 1 A Page of the Piece to Laveer Krass.\nYour task 'Note Left Behind' has been updated.\nYou have found what you were looking for and handed it over to Laveer. His father's notes pointed to possibly the next part to completing the piece left by the gods. Seek out a songwriter at Kerra Ridge.\nrewards\n2 Platinum, 2 Gold, 5 Silver\nGilded Clavichord\n10x Commemorative CoinsRewards:\n[",
