      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 0\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n\nThis Anniversary task starts with Jharin Kevva in Toxxulia Forest. She is on find (CTRL-F).\nYou say, 'Hail, Jharin Kevva'\nJharin Kevva gives little attention to Jeffroex. 'Leave me. I have [important things] to attend to.'\nYou say, 'Important things like an ancient composition?'\nJharin Kevva perks up an ear as he turns from his notations towards Jeffroex, the quill in his hand finding a home in a tiny ink well beside his notebook and an old parchment. He gives the adventurer a slightly longer moment of scrutiny. 'Well, yes. And your curiosity has my attention. You have the look of a person who has [walked the Planes].'\nYou say, 'Yes, I have walked the Planes.'\nJharin Kevva says, 'A well-traveled person can give wonderful [insight] and perspectives.' He claps his hands together in anticipation. 'What do you think? Do you mind helping me out?'\nYou say, 'I can share my insight.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Linguistic Libretto'.\nJharin Kevva says, 'Spirits with us! Thank you, friend. So...' The Jharin's index finger traces along the table beside the parchment, a mere whisper across the wood and not daring to touch the weathered paper. 'An ancient composition I acquired, but specifically the lyrics and vocal cues. I can only guess the instruments or tune to accompany this ditty. While I can confirm what is jotted down here is a [language], I cannot fathom from where. It may be pre-historic.'\nYou say, 'Do you have any leads on the roots of the language?'\nJharin Kevva says, 'No, but the text draws me in all the same. I absolutely must translate this.' He furrows his feline brow, and his ears stay alert as he stands deep in thought for a moment. 'Aquatic. A mere guess based on the flowing style of [the lettering], and that the text has avoided bleed over these many years, but I believe it would be a good jumping off point.'\nYou say, 'Could I study the lettering?'\nMissing dialogue\nYour task 'Linguistic Libretto' has been updated.\n1. Get any lead you can manage from Jharin Kevva 0/1 (Toxxulia Forest)\n2. Kill 6 shiliskin in Undershore 0/6 (The Undershore)\n3. Search Malgrinnor in Undershore for examples of shiliskin text 0/2 (The Undershore)\n4. Kill 6 mermaids in Kedge Keep 0/6 (Kedge Keep)\n5. Search Kedge Keep for examples of mermaid text 0/2 (Kedge Keep)\n6. Search Cobalt Scar for examples of othmir text 0/2 (Cobalt Scar)\n7. Speak with Jharin Kevva about the language examples gathered so far 0/1 (Toxxulia Forest)\n8. Study the Copy of the Ancient Lyrics 0/1 (Toxxulia Forest)\n9. Update Jharin Kevva about your findings 0/1 (The Undershore)\n10. Take the Studied Copy of Ancient Lyrics to Maelin Starpyre in New Tanaan 0/1 (The Plane of Knowledge)\n11. Talk with Maelin about your findings and the work you're doing with Kevva 0/1 (The Plane of Knowledge)\n12. Deliver the Maelin-Notated Ancient Lyrics to Jharin Kevva 0/1 (Toxxulia Forest)\nNOTE: The mystery part of this needs the divine cypher achievement from PoP progression and then all trainable languages at 100 along with Alaran and Hadal at 100.\nRoF - Words of the Unspoken to quickly get Alaran to 100.\nVoA - Oseka's Knowledge to learn Hadal\nPop - PoP proggression  https://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/quest.html?quest=2638\nLooks like it's doing progression to Tier 2 - Plane of Torment\nIf Seer Mal Nae`Shi tells you the following, then you have probably successfully completed this part of the flagging sequence. The Cipher of the Divine Language appears on your arms for a brief moment then fades.\nNOTE On TEST: I was about to get the mystery. I did not had Hadal but I did had Alaran to 100 and all the other normal Languages to 100. I am not sure about my PoP Progression.\n- 2 Platinum, 2 Gold, 5 Silver\n- Music Box: First Dawn\n- 10 Commemorative Coins\nSubmitted by: larth ; Revamped by iventheassassinRewards:\n- Commemorative Coin [item=116720]\n[",
