      walkthrough = "**Level:** 40\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n\nJharin Kevva is located in Toxxulia Forest. She is on find (CTRL-F).\nYou say, 'Hail, Jharin Kevva'\nJharin Kevva gives little attention to Jeffroex. 'Leave me. I have [important things] to attend to.'\nMissing dialogue\nYou receive Jharin Kevva's Signet.\n1. Take Jharin Kevva's Signet to Pastseeker Rhondarra in New Tanaan 0/1 - The Plane of Knowledge\nPastseeker Rhondarra is located on the 4th floor of the Great Library in The Plane of Knowledge. /waypoint +120, +1056, +98\nYou say, 'Hail, Pastseeker Rhondarra'\nPastseeker Rhondarra says, 'Welcome, traveler! I have come to New Tanaan seeking knowledge of my ancestors that has not before been revealed to me by the spirits. I have found a couple of books that tell of the predecessors to the Vah Shir. You may borrow the books if you like, they will be returned by the magic of New Tanaan when you are through with them.'\nHand her Jharin Kevva's Signet.\nPastseeker Rhondarra says, 'So, Kevva's doing more homework, is he? And sending an adventurer on his errands.' The soft chuckle rumbles through her throat like a purr, the familiarity between the two Vah Shir apparent in her teasing amusement. 'Well, how can I help the two of you? Do you [need] a book from this great Library?'\nYou complete the trade with Pastseeker Rhondarra.\n2. Speak with Rhondarra about Kevva's request 0/1 - The Plane of Knowledge\nYou say, 'I need a story. An epic tale.'\nPastseeker Rhondarra says, 'There are thousands upon thousands of epic stories along these shelves. That is: unless you need [something] so old it's new.'\nYou say, 'That something is right.'\nPastseeker Rhondarra smiles a sharp, toothy smile, her eyes twinkling. 'Typical Kevva. It looks like I'm running you on some errands as well, then. I've business to handle here at the Library, but I know just the people to seek down to grow your collection of epic tales.' She pulls out a stylus from her pocket and a spare scrap of paper, commenting as she scribbles down names and generic locales, 'Talk to them. Ask them for their stories. Note down whatever you can. Our friend Kevva, and the whole of New Tanaan here, will both greatly appreciate your work in this.'\nYou receive Jharin's Pack.\n3. Find Lenik Gemborn 0/1 - Crystal Caverns\nBefore you move to him, kill mobs near the zone-in until you find and pre-loot a Ry`Gorr Toolbelt.\n--You have looted a Ry`Gorr Toolbelt from a Ry`Gorr watchman's corpse.--\nYou receive Ry`Gorr Toolbelt.\nLenik Gemborn is on find (CTRL-F). /waypoint -221, +187, -382\nYou say, 'Hail, Lenik Gemborn'\nLenik Gemborn says, 'Hello, and I hope you are well this fine day.'\nYou say, 'Tell me your story'\nLenik Gemborn says, 'Huh? Why me?' The Coldain dwarf seems genuinely confused. 'Historian Baenek is the one who holds our city's [knowledge]. Turn around, head down the ramp, and it's just a good few strides to his room from there.'\nYou say, 'I don't just want knowledge, but an epic tale of an equally epic adventure.'\nLenik Gemborn pauses with a furrow of his brow as he assesses Jeffroex. 'Bards are persistent, I can tell you that. Fine... Fine!' The Coldain lets out a puffed breath in exasperation. 'Your friend wins. But I need some payment. Get me a Ry`Gorr Toolbelt; I've no need for bloodied pieces of flesh, and mining picks are a silver a dozen. I just want proof of clearing a few out.\n4. Fulfill Lenik Gemborn's request 0/1 - Crystal Caverns\nIf you haven't pre-looted the toolbelt already, kill orcs in the mines until you find a Ry`Gorr Toolbelt.\nMissing dialogue\nLenik Gemborn says, 'Let me know if your bard friend finds it a worthy telling. I still think you should have gone to Baenek instead...'\nYou offered 1 Ry`Gorr Toolbelt to Lenik Gemborn.\nLenik Gemborn grips the Ry`Gorr Toolbelt in his hand, his stiff fingers crushing the hardy leather. 'Sorry. That was theraputic.' He tosses the toolbelt behind him, and the sound of heavy metal and leather slamming into the cold stone wall reverberates. 'If you want context... talk to Historian Baenek, because he has held onto our legacy more than any one man should.' He passes a few papers, written in fine text, towards Jeffroex. 'My story. I'd been gathering it for more than a few years... If you wanted an epic tale, you came to the wrong dwarf, but I can tell you that I hold the blood of [Glight].'\nYou complete the trade with Lenik Gemborn.\nYou receive Lenik's Story.\nMissing dialogue for the trigger phrase \"Glight\".\n5. Find Brinaghan the Reposed 0/1 - The Estate of Unrest\nBefore you move to her, pluck and pre-loot four white flowers (Sorrow of the Tranquil) from the garden and the hedge maze. They are quick respawning ground spawns.\n/waypoint +335, -47, +4 ; /waypoint  +324, -144, +4\n/waypoint +385, -257, +4 ; /waypoint  +345, -77, +4\nYou receive Sorrow of the Tranquil.\nYou receive Sorrow of the Tranquil.\nYou receive Sorrow of the Tranquil.\nYou receive Sorrow of the Tranquil.\nBrinaghan the Reposed is at the end of the basement. She is on find (CTRL-F).\n/waypoint +464, +62, -34\nYou say, 'Hail, Brinaghan the Reposed'\nBrinaghan the Reposed says, 'Go back. You... shouldn't be here...'\nYou say, 'Tell me your story'\nYour task 'Melic Memoirs' has been updated.\nBrinaghan the Reposed says, 'I... don't have an... epic... story. Wrong place. Wrong time. Nothing [more]'\nYou say, 'I think there is more to it.'\nBrinaghan the Reposed exhales a breath that comes out choked from lungs that don't truly function. 'Did... [Quellious] send you?'\nYou say, 'No, it wasn't Quellious.'\nBrinaghan the Reposed says, 'It's a... shame. Priest, then?... [Bard]?...'\nYou say, 'Yes, a bard sent me.'\nBrinaghan the Reposed says, 'Ha. Ha... ha.' Her laugh seems oddly genuine but an unfamiliar expression for her. 'Story time, then. Bring me... a few flowers... Sorrow of Quellious. Sorrow... Only blooms here,\nabove, since... Since...'\n6. Fulfill Brinaghan the Reposed's request 0/4 - Estate of Unrest\nIf you haven't pre-looted them already, pluck four white flowers (Sorrow of the Tranquil) from the garden and the hedge maze. They are ground spawns.\nYou offered 4 Sorrow of the Tranquil to Brinaghan the Reposed.\nBrinaghan the Reposed says, 'Yes...'\nBrinaghan the Reposed says, 'You found them... Fresh... Tranquil One, remember me.' She slowly pulls them close to her chest, taking a non-existant inhale. 'Letters... Never made it... home. Letters. Best story you can tell... To remember... Me...'\nYour task 'Melic Memoirs' has been updated.\nYou complete the trade with Brinaghan the Reposed.\nYou receive Brinaghan's Story.\n7. Find Kaelen Muris 0/1 - Barindu, Hanging Gardens\nKaelen Muris is on find (CTRL-F). /waypoint +375, -488, -123\nYou say, 'Hail, Kaelen Muris'\nKaelen Muris says, Missing dialogue\nYou say, 'Tell me your story'\nYour task 'Melic Memoirs' has been updated.\n8. Kill a few Discordians in Barindu 0/4 - Barindu, Hanging Gardens\n9. Fulfill Kaelen Muris' request 0/1 - Barindu, Hanging Gardens\n10. Find Perris Stormwalker 0/1 - Firiona Vie\nPerris Stormwalker is on find (CTRL-F).\nYou say, 'Hail, Perris Stormwalker'\nPerris Stormwalker says, Missing dialogue\nYou say, 'Tell me your story'\nYour task 'Melic Memoirs' has been updated.\n11. Kill the wandering golem 0/1 - Firiona Vie\nThe golem spawns behind Perris Stormwalker in the middle of the larger octagonal room in the ruins. If it doesn't spawn, you have to /camp and return, and hail him again.\n12. Fulfill Perris Stormwalker's request 0/1 - Firiona Vie\n13. Combine the collected stories and give them to Jharin Kevva 0/1 - Toxxulia Forest\nThe four stories are: Lenik's Story, Brinaghan's Story, Kaelen's Story, Perris' Story. Combine them in Jharin's Pack and hand the newly created item over to Jharin Kevva.\nYou receive ???.\nMissing dialogue and the name of the newly created item and the last two stories from Kaelen and Perris.\nYou receive Grand Organ of Hate.\n- 2 Platinum, 2 Gold, 5 Silver\n- Grand Organ of Hate\n- 10x Commemorative Coins\nSubmitted by: larth ; Revamped  by iventheassassinRewards:\n- Grand Organ of Hate, 10x Commemorative Coins, Mone\n[",
