      id = "8459",
      title = "Adalora's Items",
      exp = "01",
      exp_name = "The Ruins of Kunark",
      min_lvl = 40,
      max_lvl = 130,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = false,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "Unknown",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Taluran the Mindful",
        "Whose memory are you speaking of?",
        "What aid do you need?",
        "Tell me more of the locations of these items.",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "Ornately Carved Wooden Pendant", count = 1 },
        { name = "Plain Leather Wrap", count = 1 },
        { name = "Repaired Silver-Veined Staff", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 128221, name = "War Staff of the Righteous", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
        { name = "Inhabitants of Firiona Vie", change = 10 },
        { name = "Emerald Warriors", change = 7 },
        { name = "Storm Guard", change = 7 },
        { name = "Legion of Cabilis", change = -1 },
        { name = "Pirates Of Gunthak", change = -1 },
        { name = "Inhabitants of Firiona Vie", change = 10 },
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 40\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n\nThis is one of the finished Kunark quests added on the February 15, 2017, update.\nYou say, 'Hail, Taluran the Mindful'\nTaluran the Mindful says, 'Greetings. I am Taluran the Mindful. It's a pleasure to meet you. I wish that I had more time to speak, but I am here on a quest and to divert my focus would disgrace [her memory:Whose memory are you speaking of?].'\nYou say, 'Whose memory are you speaking of?'\nTaluran the Mindful says, 'Her name was Adalora. She was a monk of my esteemed order and follower of the teachings of Tranquility. She's been lost to us for many centuries. However, it is not her I seek, but the restoration of her legacy. I would venture into the lands of Kunark myself, but I [need the aid:What aid do you need?] of Kaelana and Levaios, which they cannot provide. Evidently they are consumed by searches of their own.'\nYou say, 'What aid do you need?'\nTaluran the Mindful raises a brow and studies _____ carefully, 'If you're offering your assistance, I will not turn it down. The first item I need is Adalora's Focus. It's a small wooden pendant, and has been separated and likely scattered throughout the lands. Before dismissing me to perform the duties needed by her people, Kaelana allowed me to read through her ancestor's journal, written by the Ivyshae who traveled with Adalora for some time. I was able to ascertain the [locations:Tell me more of the locations of these items.] of the pieces of the pendant.'\nYou say, 'Tell me more of the locations of these items.'\nTaluran the Mindful says, 'The separate pieces have been scattered across the Ruins of Kunark. The Ornately Carved Wooden Pendant can be found in the sprawling jungle that bears the dragon's name, still within the clutches of the monster that ended Adalora's life, one whose true name has been forgotten and replaced with an apt description -- the Tortured Wraith. The Runed Brass Disk is in the dusty depths of the Howling Stones. The final piece, Adalora's Oath, is in the grips of a deadly creature known as the Obsidian Wyvern.'\nHead to Trakanon's Teeth.\n- Loot Ornately Carved Wooden Pendant from Tortured Wraith in Trakanon's Teeth.\nHead to Howling Stones.\n- Loot Runed Brass Disk from golems in Howling Stones.\nHead to Skyfire Mountains.\n- Loot Adalora's Oath from Obsidian Wyvern in Skyfire Mountains.\nGo back to Firiona Vie.\n- Give Ornately Carved Wooden Pendant, Runed Brass Disk and Adalora's Oath to Taulran the Mindful.\nTaluran the Mindful says, 'Well done, ____. Now we must procure the staff of her legacy. Recover the Splintered Wooden Staff from the jungle, Dankglow Ivy Sap from the myconids, and gather Fine Silver Shards from the mines. Deliver all of these items, including the Plain Leather Wrap, to the monk known as Drethall. He is a strange man who challenges himself by meditating amongst choking smoke and dangerous monsters.'\nYour faction standing with Inhabitants of Firiona Vie has been adjusted by 10.\nYour faction standing with Emerald Warriors has been adjusted by 7.\nYour faction standing with Storm Guard has been adjusted by 7.\nYour faction standing with Legion of Cabilis has been adjusted by -1.\nYour faction standing with Pirates Of Gunthak has been adjusted by -1.\nReceive: Plain Leather Wrap.\nHead to Emerald Jungle.\n- Loot Splintered Wooden Staff from Festering Silverback in Emerald Jungle.\nHead to Old Sebilis.\n- Loot Dankglow Vine Sap from myconids in Old Sebilis.\nHead to Mines of Nurga.\n- Loot Fine Silver Shards from Tribal Mineralist in Mines of Nurga.\nHead to Burning Woods.\n- Give Plain Leather Wrap, Splintered Wooden Staff, Dankglow Vine Sap and Fine Silver Shards to Drethall.\nDrethall says, 'Ah, I see that Taluran has finally received some assistance after all these years of waiting. How fortunate for him, and the rest of us who wish to restore Adalora's legacy to our Order. Take this, ____, and return it to Taluran along with two additional items, Thin Strands of Silver Silk and Thin Strands of Golden Silk. Good luck to you, ____. May the fates smile fondly upon your endeavor.'\nReceive: Repaired Silver-Veined Staff.\nHead to Karnor's Castle.\n- Loot Thin Strands of Silver Silk from mobs in Karnors Castle.\n- Loot Thin Strands of Golden Silk from undead in The Hole.\nHead back to Firiona Vie.\n- Give Repaired Silver-Veined Staff, Thin Strands of Silver Silk and Thin Strands of Golden Silk to Taluran the Mindful.\nTaluran the Mindful says, 'Well done, _____. We've finally gathered all of Adalora's lost possessions and can now restore her legacy. I wish for you to wield this. Though it was once understood by only Adalora, its secrets have now been unlocked and we may continue her legacy throughout our Order.'\nYour faction standing with Inhabitants of Firiona Vie has been adjusted by 10.\nYour faction standing with Emerald Warriors has been adjusted by 7.\nYour faction standing with Storm Guard has been adjusted by 7.\nYour faction standing with Legion of Cabilis has been adjusted by -1.\nYour faction standing with Pirates Of Gunthak has been adjusted by -1.\nAny other faction hits for any of the other item turn ins?\n- War Staff of the Righteous\n- Kunark Archaeologist player title suffix if first per server\nSubmitted by: GidonoRewards:\n- War Staff of the Righteous [item=128221]\n[",
