        { name = "Venril Sathir", change = 5 },
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n\nThis is one of the finished Kunark quests added on the February 15, 2017, update.\nYou say, 'Hail, Vitratul K`Reil'\nVitratul K`Reil raises an eyebrow as he takes in the entirety of _____. He utters a disapproving 'hmph' before speaking in a calculated, callous tone, 'Good day to you. I am Vitratul K`Reil, and unless you have business to discuss, it would be best for your continued existence if you were to depart from my sight immediately. I have no interest in idle chatter when there are [greater concerns:What greater concerns?] more worthy of my attentions.'\nYou say, 'What greater concerns?'\nVitratul K`Reil draws in a deep breath and narrows his eyes, pausing for a moment to collect his thoughts before speaking again in a slow, regal tone, 'I come to this place in search of knowledge and power -- much like yourself, _____. Though I choose to refrain from the more vulgar, barbaric rituals of battle when the [true power I seek:What is the true power you seek?] lies in patience and study.'\nYou say, 'What is the true power you seek?'\nVitratul K`Reil chuckles softly, a faint, sinister smirk creeping into the corner of his lips, 'Ah, your inquiry is well earned. Of course, it can be answered -- but as with all things, _____, such knowledge comes with a price. If you wish to know what I'm seeking, then you shall [aid me:I will aid you.] and earn this knowledge and discipline.'\nYou say, 'I will aid you.'\nVitratul K`Reil straightens his posture, the sinister smirk washing away from his features, replaced by his default callous demeanor, 'And so you shall, _____. There are four scrolls that you shall retrieve for me, as your introduction to this study and discipline. The Scroll of Night which you may find in Talendor's domain, the Scroll of the Beguiler from the city enshrouded by mist, the Scroll of the Invoker from the sarnak stronghold, and the Scroll of the Conjuror from The Hole. Return only when you have all four of these scrolls, _____. I shall accept nothing less.'\nHead to Skyfire Mountains.\n- Loot a Scroll of Night from Nightwing in Skyfire Mountains.\nHead to City of Mist.\n- Loot Scroll of the Beguiler from A Spectral Beguiler in City of Mist.\nHead to Chardok.\n- Loot Scroll of the Invoker from a Di`zok Invoker or a Di`zok Channeler in Chardok.\nHead to Ruins of Paineel (The Hole)\n- Loot Scroll of the Conjuror from The Stone Caller in The Hole,\nHead back to The Overthere.\n- Turn in all 4 scrolls to Vitratul.\nVitratul K`Reil studies the scrolls carefully, taking in their words methodically and with great consideration before giving a subtle nod of approval, 'You have done well in this, _____. Now for your second task.' The necromancer hands you a scroll of fresh parchment covered with recently scribed words, the ink still shimmering and wet, 'These are the Words of Night. Take them to Nureya I`Rals once you have obtained a Thin Crystal Orb which can be found in the mines and an Essence of Night from the jungle. She will tell you what to do next once you have completed this task.'\nYour faction standing with Venril Sathir has been adjusted by 15.\nYou gain experience!\nYou receive Words of Night.\nHead to the Mines of Nurga.\n- Loot a Thin Crystal Orb in Mines of Nurga from Tribal Elder.\nHead to Trakanon's Teeth.\n- Loot a Essence of Night from The Night Warder in Trakanon's Teeth.\nHead to The Overthere.\n- Turn in the Thin Crystal Orb, Essence of Night and Words of Night into Nureya in The Overthere\nNureya raises one eyebrow as she scans the Words of Night, then she examines the pair of orbs carefully. Without a word, the beautiful Teir`Dal enchantress begins to chant in her haunting, otherworldy soprano. The pair of orbs in her hands radiate as she draws them together, where they meld into a single pitch black sphere that seems almost vulgar in Nureya's delicate hands. Slowly, she extends her arms toward _____, offering the orb, 'If you wish to continue your task, return this Orb of Night and the Black Orb of the Arcane to Vitratul. The latter can be found in the depths of Sebilis. My aid to you, Derresh, and he, ends here.'\nYour faction standing with Venril Sathir has been adjusted by 10.\nYou gain experience!\nYou receive Orb of Night.\nHead to Old Sebilis.\n- Loot Black Orb of the Arcane from a froglok krup enchanter.\nHead back to The Overthere\n- Turn in Orb of Night and Black Orb of the Arcane into Vitratul.\nVitratul K`Reil raises his chin ever so slightly as he clasps one of the black orbs into each of his hands. His azure eyes roll back into his skull as he utters an eerie chant. The pair of orbs pulse and radiate brilliantly in a blinding aura of unholy energies, their pulse in perfect tempo to the pounding of the necromancer's voice. As Vitratul's chant grows louder and swifter, he joins the orbs together, melding them into one solid, round object. When the chanting ceases, the necromancer returns his gaze to you and offers the strange pulsating shield. 'This is the reward for your discipline and the answer to your questions about true power.'\nYour faction standing with Venril Sathir has been adjusted by 5.\nYou gain experience!\n- Arcane Orb of the Dark\n- Kunark Archaeologist player title suffix if first per server\nSubmitted by: GidonoRewards:\n- Arcane Orb of the Dark [item=128105]\n[",
    },
