      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 50\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n\nThis is one of the finished Kunark quests added on the February 15, 2017, update.\nKuughrak Bonecrush says, 'What?! What do you want, Goblin? Can't you see that Kuughrak is busy?' Kuughrak pauses and glances around, as if lost or in deep thought for a moment, 'Well, Kuughrak would be busy if Kuughrak had knowledge of what to do, but Nureya finds it funny to keep Kuughrak waiting for so long. Maybe if Kuughrak had [assistant], waiting would not be so long.'\nYou say, 'perhaps I could be of assistance?'\nKuughrak Bonecrush narrows his eyes and snorts as he studies _____, 'Fine, Kuughrak doesn't have the patience to argue with that. If you want to be of any use and not irritate Kuughrak further, you will bring me Elyrian's Journal and the Earthen Steel Hammer. Your first step will be to find Dajrool. Ask him about the journal. And bring him this note along with a Petrified Wooden Handle held by the forest giants. The goblin will know what to do -- and he will do it because he fears Kuughrak!'\nYou receive Note to Dajrool.\nHead to Burning Woods.\n- Kill a forest giant ancient in Burning Woods and loot Petrified Wooden Handle.\nHead to Firiona Vie.\nDajrool is a goblin wandering in Firiona Vie, he dies often due to attacking Drachnids. He has a quick respawn of a few minutes.\nYou say, 'Hail, Dajrool Waggletongue'\nDajrool Waggletongue squints his left eye and chatters his teeth before speaking sharply in a high pitched, scratchy voice, 'What? What do you waaaaant, _____?! Hrm? I clearly see that all you provide is bit of... Hrm... nausea from hiiiideous face and that... rrreeepulive stench wafting about you! Go away before you make me ill... though it may be too late.' Dajrool curls his lip and smacks his tongue as if having a foul taste in his mouth.\n- Turn in the Petrified Wooden Handle you looted from a Forest Giant and the note Kuughrak gave you to Dajrool.\nDajrool Waggletongue reads the note, chattering his pointed teeth as he scans each line. He then utters an incomprehensible curse in his scratchy, high-pitched tenor before addressing _____, 'Very well! You brought stiff woodstick needed for hammer! Here! Take hammer and go! And tell obtuse, clumsy, stupid Kuughrak to leave Dajrool alone!'\nYou receive Earthen Steel Hammer.\nYou say, 'journal'\nDajrool Waggletongue chatters his teeth for a moment and then ***** his head, 'So what of it, _____? You want journal? Well... nothing in this world is given without payment. I tell you what, _____. You do [something for me:What can I do for you as payment?], yes? And I... I will give you journal.'\nYou say, 'What can I do for you as payment?'\nDajrool Waggletongue says, 'Aaah! Of course you will, if you want journal, _____. I ask only one thing... and that is that you bring me ornate bracer that sniffling, wretched sarnak... even more wretched and rrreeepulsive than you, _____, stole from me. You will find thieving, dragon-lizard where sarnak gather. I believe that... parents would call him Rusdai. Yes... Rusdai the thieving little whelp that took bracer. Go, Dark Elf. Bring me bracer and I give you journal... good as new.'\nHead to Chardok.\n- Find Rusdai, kill and loot Ornate Steel Bracer.\nPut this in your chardok_2.txt map file for Rusdai's location.\nP 112.6636, 289.4477, -289.0581, 127, 0, 0, 2, Rusdai\nHead back to Firiona Vie.\nFind Dajrool. Give him the Ornate Steel Bracer.\nDajrool Waggletongue gives a hoarse, throaty chuckle and stashes the bracer in his taut loincloth, 'Good! Good, _____. Now, I keep my side of bargain. Here is journal. Oh... yes, there is one more thing I conveniently did not mention and that is journal is incomplete. Imbecile whelps in Nurga thought they could kill me... but they failed! You have journal... but missing pages there in Nurga still. Consider information courtesy for fine job in getting bracer. If you kill Nurga whelps, then good. If not, then fine... but go now! I cannot stand Dark Elf stench anymore.'\nDarjool gives you Torn Journal.\nHead to Mines of Nurga.\n- Kill goblins in Mines of Nurga and loot Elyrian's Journal Pg. 15, Elyrian's Journal Pg. 17, Elyrian's Journal Pg. 18, Elyrian's Journal Pg. 22.\n- Combine these pages in the Torn Journal Dajrool gave you.\nYou have fashioned the items together to create something new: Elyrian's Journal.\n- Give Kuughrak the Elyrian's Journal and Earthen Steel Hammer.\nKuughrak Bonecrush says, 'Good! For such a puny _____ you have done well. Well, puny compared to Kuughrak anyway! Now that I have the hammer and journal, I do not need Nureya as much. But we still need her magics. Here, _____. Elyria's journal says that we need the Spectral Blade of Mist and the Rusty Mithril Sword. Give those blades to Nureya along with this note. She will know what to do next, and she will do it because she, like Dajrool, is afraid of the mighty Kuughrak!'\nReceive: Commision for Nureya.\nHead to City of Mist.\n- Kill Mist Reaver or Lady Ixtariz and loot Spectral Blade of Mist.\nHead to Kedge Keep.\n- Kill Phinigel Autropos in Kedge Keep and loot Rusty Mithril Sword.\n- Give Nureya the Commission for Nureya, the Spectral Blade of Mist, and the Rusty Mithril Sword.\nNureya raises one eyebrow as she reads through the commission, then she examines the two blades carefully. Without a word, the beautiful Teir`Dal enchantress begins to chant in her haunting, otherworldy soprano. The pair of blades in her hands radiate as she draws them together, where they meld into a single elegant weapon that seems almost vulgar in Nureya's delicate hands. Slowly, she extends her arms toward ____, offering the blade, 'It can be improved and Kuughrak can assist you with this. Return the weapon to him, along with the spikes of a fire wurm and the spine of a shambling froglok. My aid to you, ____, and he, ends here.'\nYour faction standing with Venril Sathir has been adjusted by 10.\nYou gain experience!\nReceive: Enchanted Mithril Blade.\nHead to Skyfire Mountains.\n- Loot a Fire Wurm's Spikes from any wurm in Skyfire.\nHead to Old Sebilis.\n- Loot a Undead Froglok Spine from a dar ghoul knight in Old Sebilis.\nGo back to The Overthere.\n- Give Kuughrak the Enchanted Mithril Blade, the Fire Wurm's Spikes, and the Undead Froglok Spine.\nKuughrak Bonecrush says, 'Aaaaah... yes, this is what Kuughrak needed to make blade. Here, ____. Kuughrak has forged weapon for you. Use it in the name of Kuughrak.' The Ogre pounds his fist hard against his chest in pride, 'It is a good blade and will make your prey nice and dead.'\nYour faction standing with Venril Sathir has been adjusted by 10.\nYou gain party experience!\nYou gain party experience!\n- Kuughrak's Blade\n- Kunark Archaeologist player title suffix if first per server\n- Kuughrak's Blade [item=128222]\n[",
